1 |text lot people get hung this films tag children film and that certainly though one made for adults takashi miike uses the fantasy genre particularly the children fantasy genre springboard into the wild territory that the great yokai war the setup simple boy selected play the hero this years annual festival only discover his role much more real than could have imagined what follows hallucinatory grotesque whimsical and often funny journey through the world japanese folklore but wait there also evil villain the lose who wants destroy the world however the villain here not mere demon the demon spirit the accumulated resentment those things which humans use and discard usuing chamber made out pure liquid hate resentment the villain transforms the vibrant colorful yokai spirits into soulless ten foot tall makeshift robots which chainsaw for arms and eyes like burning coals those whove played the video game sonic the hedghog might remember certain robotnik performing similar procedures the cute and cuddly who sonic had then liberate the hero this film actually the least interesting character essentially playing the straight man world gone suddenly mad though does through the typical heroes trials more often than not cowers many the yokia themselves who seem truly defenseless against the murderous robots some spirits being umbrellas with eyes talking walls creatures whose soul purpose life count beans course this magical world miike yokai war even beans take magical power when one believes them several ways this film subverts the normal conventions children fantasy few any the characters are heroic their victory being combination happenstance almost arbitrary faith and desire party the yokai spirits only rally together and lay siege the villains hideout after they mistake the end the world invasion earth for great yokai festival and even then only dance and party also the film ends not with the usual celebratory all well that ends well fantasy ending but with final scene showing our hero years older with adult job now unable see the yokai spirits his youth who then despondently turn the villain who being spirit can never really die this ending with yokai spirit who the spitting image pokemon pikachu warns not just leaving behind our childhood selves but the horrors over consumption the villain resentment caused when humans longer have reverence for the world and the objects around them japanese folklore nearly every object has some kind spirit and when they are used and discarded consumer societies without reverence they become soulless vengeful machines not unlike those seen modern video games suggesting that though our imaginations and myths not ever really die but can become deformed this one the first scripts miike has contributed and believe shows there tightness conceptually that sometimes gets swept under the rug his exuberance for visual playfulness though focused mostly the story since lots users here seem write off want say that visually kaleidescope cgi stop animation costume and live puppetry that works remarkably well there dreamlike quality lot the film and the miyazaki comparisons are warranted are the neverending story and labrynth comparisons though this film sharper and more adult than either the yokai are beaten brutalized and turned into machines living hate who believe even kill few humans deformed aborted calf with mans face born and dies the films grotesque opening while sexual undercurrent the women with the long neck licking the face our boy hero another characters persistent memory touching the thigh young scantily clad water spirit boy seem linger bit too long for most western tastes especially when considering this children film however these are slight enough catch adult attentions while minor enough not traumatize any children bad grims fairy tales before revisions did much worse far more often all and all this one miikes most accessible and engaging ventures yet with enough visual drama and great performances the yokai spirits have humanism and absurd humor them thats laugh out loud funny times appeal audiences all ages and steady conceptual undercurrent strong enough draw adult audience who have presumably brought their children else come out sense nostalgia for the long lost fantasy films their youth the latter group the film seems address the most fervently asking that they not just continue passive consumption the world around them but show reverence those spirits within them which seemed much closer reality childhood another beautiful funny and truly original film from thrilling director who hasn come close his apex instant classic
