1 |text found grey garden gripping film amazingly intimate look too eccentrics who basically have the right idea forget society and live delapidated house with heating and huge brood cats and raccoons persuing their own interests rather mundainly all the while chattering the camera big edie and little edie are the two crazies that the mazles bros have chosen document they seem like characters out fellini film only stranger that makes any sense old edie almost fully bedridden pile papers clothes and dirty dishes growing around her little edie even more interesting she prances around the house always wearing baboushka like headdress around her head completely covering her hair never see her hair throughout the film nor ever get hint that she still has much age fifty eight though she still beautiful and full life grey gardens get the sense that both these women lives have become much less than what they once were little edie probably the sadder the two while her mother her earlier years got married made family lived luxuriously and even made some recordings the scene where she sings along with recording tea for two she made decades ago one the films best scenes edie left her promicing career model take care her ailing mother she still longed find her prince charming anything little edie still little girl full dreams glamour and fame and domestic and romantic bliss that have yet fulfilled highlights the film include the opening moments where little edie explains her outfit the camera the tea for two sequence the birthday party the climactic argument the grocery deliver scene and the scene the attic the whole thing incredibly candid and unpretencious and made all the more remarcable since all real suggest seeing grey gardens back back with the kenneth anger short puce moment the criterion dvd but worth every penny
