1 |text having been driven out the house and into the theater the sweltering heat could not have been more pleased the road perdition directed sam mendes american beauty destined become one the greatest movies all time perhaps just getting old perhaps just seen the same themes recycled time and again but this movie indeed different the story opens with young michael sullivan facing out the sea contemplating the duality his father legacy one the best men ever live one the most evil this duality snakes its way throughout the movie the story revolves around crime boss john rooney paul newman and michael sullivan tom hanks the young man rooney once took and who now serves his personal angel death rooney tied blood his own son but tied love and loyalty michael young michael intrigued the stories reads steals away his father car one night while dad goes off work with connor rooney heir the family business connor lets the situation get out hand and what was meant only warning turns into murder witnessed michael upon the discovery that young michael has seen what should not have seen the plot set motion conflicting loyalties collide soon michael the run with his young son pursued contract killer harlen the reporter maguire jude law will disclose further details order avoid any potential spoilers however strongly encourage viewers examine the many dualities that present themselves the movie problems between sons and fathers michael john rooney son connor between the world home and the world work between good and evil between those who pretend men god and those who really are between clean money and dirty between the town perdition and perdition hell and along the way savor the visual brilliance cinematographer conrad hall nominations oscars for best cinematography rain pouring off fedoras shots through mirrors especially swinging doors tommy gun flashes from out the shadows absent any sound not only has year old hall given perhaps the best cinematic product his career but year old paul newman offers one his best performances ever yes may getting old but seen lot and this fresh and invigorating the road perdition presents lasting and loving tribute the gangster genre films the 40s dark comic book figures lurking the darkness villains and heroes american film general see
