1 |text taiwanese director ang lee whose previous films include sense and sensibility and the ice storm turned the american civil war for his latest feature based novel daniel woodrell follows the exploits group southern guerrillas known bushwhackers they fight their northern equivalents the jayhawkers the backwater missouri one might expect there plenty visceral action but the focus the tension that the war put the young men who fought many whom were fighting against their former neighbours and even family jake roedel tobey maguire such man rather boy only seventeen when the war reaches missouri the son german immigrant but instead following his countrymen and becoming unionist joins his lifelong friend jack bull chiles skeet ulrich and rides with the bushwhackers despite lack acceptance because his ancestry and unwillingness participate the murder unarmed union men remains loyal the cause does his friend daniel holt jeffrey wright black slave freed another bushwhacker and fighting for the south lee handles the subject with aplomb never rushing the deep introspection that the plot demands favour action and this lends the film sense the reality war long periods boredom and waiting interposed with occasional flashes intensely terrifying fighting the action unglamorised and admirably candid recognising that both sides committed great number atrocities the performances are superb with maguire and wright both courageous and dignified and coming irish actor jonathan rhys meyers particularly chilling cold blooded killer while skeet ulrich enjoyably suave and arrogant lee never flinches from the reality war but his actors admirable job showing the good that comes from the growth friendship the demonstration courage and wider scale the emancipation oppressed peoples ride with the devil beautiful and deeply compassionate film that regularly shocks but always moves the audience
