ury deeply concerned with the meaning borders and with those who are the victims the confusion between nations the waiting room facing the albanian border the refugees political other outcast the rest humanity wait they may stuck against political border but unfortunately they still carry with them and hang deeper ancestral borders those the languages the customs and the races although angelopoulos political views are well known the film steers clear any political discourse regarding the causes the refugees plights the process angelopoulos forces meditate the concepts geographical cultural political and personal borders angelopoulos considers himself historian twentieth century greece and likes bring lessons from the hellenic myths into his discussions this film does some border crossing himself between the greek and italian cultures drawing from combined homeric and dantesque tradition odysseus travel alexander telemachus search story about aging greek politician odysseus who disappeared never heard again this political man brilliant orator unexpectedly and inexplicably left the comfort his bourgeois existence his wife and his brilliant career live anonymously refugee camp with the lowest the low became poet exile wondering how change the world course the politician not alexander father but the politician stands before alexander like father figure odysseus with homer telemachus alexander grows person during his odyssey course would wrong try and see the film retelling homer odyssey contemporary context angelopoulos draws odysseus travels only structuring and thematic elements for his film angelopoulos ending odysseus more like the dante odysseus does not leave for ithaca but goes carrying suitcase and alexander telemachus suspended between returning his home and his career embarking voyage somewhere else states much voice over the beginning the film paraphrasing few lines from dante inferno and don forget that the time for voyage has come again the wind blows your 