1 |text this film does not fail engage and move even 2008 audience only familiar with modern over produced sound and computer enhanced techniques the experience the movie goer 1922 who could only see this cinema with others their big screen must have been truly profound and thoroughly satisfying experience one has ask could film maker today make two hour silent movie and make interesting and achieve the same structure tempo and balance this movie has silent film making was pure art had hold the attention through its structure direction and acting there was padding out with more words computer generated distractions poorly made uninteresting silent movie unwatchable this film needs put into context for those who might disconcerted with the mention christian themes this not christiany film not selling anything these themes along with reference current moral standards often appear this era also church going sundays was national past time christianity was given most households thus the film only depicting normal life was then the themes would have rung true and deep the time most odd given the strong support good christian thinking this particular movie and not preaching religion anyone only highlighting the difference between hypocrites and the honest that 1922 pastor open debate with representative from the film industry with large crowd denounced pickford example immorality along with some other individuals named times 1922 maybe they should have watched this movie that also came out 1922 and learned some lessons the pastor complained that since the film industry had started church attendance had dropped 500 000 the film representative the debate however made the following observations that saloon attendance had also dropped that there were far more pastors prison than actors fact and that selecting few examples from among the many was not representative the whole thus there was ongoing battle between church and the film industry during the early days film this wonderful film about being honest and true family friends and willing make sacrifices mary pickford naive honest feisty full happiness and joy faithful humorous and silently sacrificing though poor and uneducated she represented the perfect character this however not thrust down our throat but revealed bit bit through the film this reminiscent some modern chinese films where characters are slowly languidly revealed over the course film and this tempo that creates stronger connection with the character has smooth even tempo for the first half that builds all the elements for the last section the last minutes are great film making and has appreciated was achieved without the benefit sound running dialog was achieved through deft acting and great directing sometimes surprising realize that the end the film you haven hear word spoken but feels like you have heard everything the supporting cast put great performances especially gloria hope jean hersholt and lloyd hughes the final few minutes are typical pickford understated humor she goes outside under the pretext sweeping the snow near perfect balance and ending this special type touching humor that should not underestimated chaplin used this device often and copied some from pickford another special observation made about silent films and especially pickford films that the star often has hold the camera for much the movie without the audience becoming jaded bored with the actors over exposure that pickford usually thoroughly the center attention through most her movies but the people still couldn get enough her testament her fine acting ability
