1 |text peckinpah did with straw dogs and kubrick with clockwork orange director john boorman delivers effective film about man violent side deliverance arguably definitive horror film the 1970s burt reynolds jon voight ned beatty and ronny cox portray four atlanta businessmen who decide take canoe trip down the wild cahulawassee river northern georgia before dammed into what reynolds calls one big dead lake but the local mountain folk take painfully obvious dim view these city boys carousing through their woods and the following day continuing down the river beatty and voight are accosted and sexually assaulted the film infamous squeal sequence two vicious mountain men bill mckinney herbert cowboy coward thus what started out nothing more than lark through the appalachians has now turned into nightmare which our four protagonists come see the thin line that exists between what think civilization and what think barbarism james dickey adapted the screenplay from his own best selling book and the result often gripping and disturbing shocker often known for its squeal and dueling banjos sequences deliverance also quite pulse pounding ordeal with the four leading men superb their roles and mckinney and coward making for two the most frightening villains all times must see film for those willing take chance
