1 |text riding giants brilliant documentary that dives deep into the world one the most under appreciated sports and brings the surface very human and raw emotion that only director stacy peralta could capture everything from the structure the players the amazing stock footage even the style which this was filmed only reinforced the beauty and power behind the sport surfing all the surfing films that have seen endless summer billabong odyssey and step into liquid this was the most consistent and relevant beginning with the early ages surfing brief history lesson lasting all the way till laird infamous ride riding giants goes further into the mind heart and soul the sport than any these other documentaries how does this giving the whole story from start finish without fictionalizing jig jagging from wave wave begin this film was structurally sound the other films that have seen about surfing you sometimes find yourself jumping from new person new person wave wave event event without any knowledge why who riding giants have very small cast veterans and newbies this allows you really deeper into the mind each one also instead just riding waves are handed more history and more personal insight the world than before this what really attracted this film was impressed that instead showing all these big waves because big wave movie listen stories and see first hand what these surfers had overcome get those waves loved the information about the beach bums father surfing still floored the amazing tales greg noll and his early adventures into the harsh deep blue then see him person talking about what was going his mind only added more fuel the fire the straightforward structure that peralta followed allowed follow and walk away with more knowledge the sport than with any the earlier films peralta shows much emotion and passion that you cannot help but amazed what these brave people have done and where the sport going add immaculate structure some intense and creative cinematography and you have darn near perfect film using techniques that last saw the kid stays the picture riding giants creates some scenes that almost feel they are jumping out the screen while isn that flat dimensional feeling that you get when you put two pictures top each other this film worked created more depth the scenes and really added not just the shock value man these waves were huge but also the danger that these guys constantly faced broke differently they maneuvered wrong these waves would kill them some did die but didn stop the sport only created more excitement and more passion better this love the ocean and sport that leads final point the human element many earlier adventures the world surfing documentaries left with beautiful waves but very little about the people the films knew that people were watching for the waves would basically from wave wave wave and the maybe short second about the person this film was the direct opposite peralta created this masterpiece still giving the waves but devoting much more attention onto the surfers and the immortal question why they this everyday what rushes through their minds what pushes them further and the bonds that are formed while out there the wild blue yonder felt like after watching this film that not only knew more about big wave surfing but also about the emotional side the sport this was element not developed the other films and pushed riding giants whole new personal level overall this film was brilliant never have witnessed much passion devotion and love wrapped structurally sound film from beginning end was impressed would very happy this film won the oscar this year for best documentary and see new rebirth the surfing world and open more doors for films this nature grade out
