rse every second worthy for barrymore beauty
1 |text absolute masterpiece film goodnight tom has swiftly become one favourite films all time nobody should miss out seeing this film just too good tom perfectly portrayed john thaw the harsh old man who becomes soft father figure when william beech nick robinson sent him for evacuation almost like the town mouse and the country mouse truly heart wrenching film the director knew exactly how turn book into film and has done extremely well the film was excellently shot that the emotions the characters and what was happening made the audience feel range emotions from love fear and these emotions could turn six pence set time turmoil during world war two this film also shows the difference between the cities and the countryside they are almost like different countries absolute must see those who don are missing out truly amazing and brilliant film
1 |text umi miteita the sea watching was akira kurasawa swansong film his adaptation his favored novelist shugoro yamamoto story into screenplay intended film was his final mark left brilliant career director kei kumai pays homage both kurosawa and yamamoto presenting this visually stunning transformation word image set 19th century japan the story explores the lives the women geisha house whose sole purpose life earn money pleasuring men the house run older couple who are genteel and the geishas are enchanting group women who know their trade and take pride their careers each has reason for turning the life geisha oshin nagiko tono supports her family who live neighboring village kikuno misa shimizu has customers both good and evil whom she manages sustain with her stories her higher caste oshin befriends endangered samurai falls love with the gentle fellow only find that must not marry out his caste and leaves his pleasures with oshin marry his promised betrothed oshin heart bruises easily but always supported emotionally and physically monetarily kikuno and the other geishas handsome samurai ryosuke masatoshi nagase enters oshin life and develops the first trusted and devoted relationship with her kikuno beset problems deciding whether accept the humble love old man who wishes marry her and coping with rich but abusive customer all the while the sea watching and typhoon destroys the geisha house and street oshin and kikuno sit atop the roof waiting for the promised rescue ryosuke the manner which the story ends one sacrifice love and devotion the sea watching and will find protection for true love the photography kazuo okuhara breathtakingly beautiful night scenes with glowing lanterns and colorful geisha interiors are matched with recurring glimpses the sea both calm and turbulent the acting bit strained for edo art but the characters are well created and keep the story credible the one distraction which definitely not something kurosawa would have condoned the tacky western music score that sounds like cheap soap opera filler except for the isolated moments when real japanese music authentic instruments graces the track but the end there enough kurosawa influence imbue this film with his brand dreamlike wonder that will always maintain his importance world cinema grady harp
