1 |text when one thinks 1950s science fiction films one thinks the sort schlocky black and white films that were parodied the old mystery science theater 3000 television show yet while there were far more films like plan from outer space and robot monster than good films the 1950s did have some very good not great science fiction films like the day the earth stood still the incredible shrinking man invasion the body snatchers war the worlds and the thing from another world yet the best the bunch for its literacy and production values was undoubtedly mgm first big foray into level science fiction forbidden planet released 1956 was minute color film directed fred wilcox that featured then state the art special effects and was endowed with very good screenplay cyril hume from screen treatment called fatal planet irving block and allen adler who adapted aspects william shakespeare the tempest into the film drew raves when was released for its oscar nominated special effects its all electronic music score louis and bebe barron although credited electronic tonalities avoid music guild fees vivid matte paintings inspired chesley bonestell and the famed monster the moti which was animated animator joshua meador loan from the walt disney studio even more famous was the appearance robby the robot his first role either film television later would appear the film the invisible boy included this dvd bonus well several appearances the 1960s sci shows the twilight zone night gallery and lost space with whose own robot often confused and cameo appearance the 1984 film gremlins the tale simple but elegantly constructed and filled with humorous asides that leaven the forced love story aspect the film the 23rd century the united planets cruiser 57d flying saucer led commander adams leslie nielsen yes was once leading man type before his police squad days route the planet altair investigate what happened the crew the bellerophon sent the planet twenty years earlier after year journey there they encounter the lone survivor the party doctor edward morbius walter pidgeon the prospero stand philologist his gorgeous blond daughter altaira anne francis the miranda character pre 1960s miniskirt and robby the robot the domestic servant who the calibanian counterpart morbius warns the crew mysterious force that killed the bellerophon party their first year yet was immune xc2 x85 all all technically good film especially with some rear projections and matte paintings and the absurdity the adult reactions timmy and robby exploits borders dalian surreal absurdity yet manifest that the filmmakers had sense the sublime absurdity the film conjures for played straight thus making even funnier for the main feature forbidden planet deserves all its kudos not perfect film but great way spend couple hours and far better than star wars which although made twenty years later seems much more outdated and juvenile only such films like 2001 space odyssey solaris alien and aliens and the first two terminator films have really equaled surpassed this classic depth and effects worth knowing that despite forbidden planet happy ending there the possibility that the moti still dormant within alta well after all she her father daughter and had even more vivid nightmare than her father when the moti attacked the ship second time also the film wisely only shows the moti once and never shows the krel for the imagination can always conjure greater scares than the best special effects the film also makes good use narrative ellipses condense the tale something that far more realistic art films often fail forbidden planet one those rare films that both defines yet transcends its era unlike other sci films which were rather obvious cold war allegories watch and you will agree well sleep little less easy but even you don there still the scene anne francis skinnydipping that alone timeless
