1 |text secret sunshine marks the return director lee changdong the film making world after multi year absence having three critically acclaimed films already under his belt recruits now veteran thespian jeon doyeon and her considerable cannes winning talents for the primary role lee shinae what follows journey through one woman tragedy and exploration her coping mechanisms one the things that becomes apparent while watching secret sunshine that doesn really care follow any specific genre but rather picks genre traits when necessary convey what trying convey the story itself follows lee shinae she moves with her son the city milyang whose sino corean translates secret sunshine she moves milyang the aftermath the death her husband was his hometown the film born from tragedy and you think things might just get better she opens piano shop and encounters bit bumbling nice guy mechanic jongchan played song kangho but this isn romantic comedy and jongchan doggedly follow shinae she encounters milyang and the fate that has store for her the cracks her armor quickly become apparent she troubled woman trying grasp onto her own strength overcome tragedy and watch she finds that not enough secret sunshine still manages follow mostly aristotelian dramatic arc but pulls back the catharsis which might confound some viewers especially the ending but the novelistic symbolism present the name milyang the discussions sunshine and the imagery used the film very well left satisfied once started think over the film some more jeon rather impressive throughout especially considering that the role were any less well played would quickly turned into rather painful melodrama but she captures the nuances shinae attempts deal with her losses with layer subtlety song has much smaller role this film than other films but performs adequately appropriately giving stage jeon technically the film well done classical sense flashy aesthetics are employed here the director clearly trying let the story tell itself think only real complaint and one that might not able fixed that despite all the time spend with shinae there bit distance between shinae and the audience least think some this stems from the nature the work because total empathy were pushed then wouldn able see the problems that shinae has objectively the other hand never felt moved along with shinae plight despite her many tears and increasingly erratic behavior all the same the film still stands quite impressive especially that stimulated think about the further meanings present and its ruminations tragedy coping self deception isolation and faith stuck with well after the credits had finished running propelled strong lead performance honestly didn notice its hour runtime and that says something well done
