1 |text louise brooks gives wonderful performance this well made french melodrama she plays typist named lucienne who despite being love with man named andre dreams rising above her position life she sees opportunity beauty contest for miss europe but andre furious when discovers that she entered then demands that she withdraw she tries take back her entry only discover that she already been chosen miss france and will now the main pageant this story love loss and decision played out its passionate end the movie very energetically filmed director augusto genina and cinema tographers rudolf mate and louis nee the filming style more like modern movies than the hollywood flicks the 30s and shows the different style employed europeans there are many fast cuts and traveling shots mostly done with great skill and verve the high energy the movie first third dwindles bit the middle but picks again the last minutes the performances were very good all the principals but that louise brooks especially memorable louise leans heavily her silent screen skills even though this talkie but because her silent style had surprisingly contemporary understated feel she makes the transition talkies very well the long early scene the fair was especially poignant louise used her remarkably expressive eyes convey her growing sense misery and alienation being trapped life she longer wants doubt ever been done better the film builds superb finale artfully shot powerful and stylish this really some the best stuff the early days film and the tragic storyline only underscores the greater tragedy that this the final starring role for louise brooks she wasn just great beauty who looked fantastic swimsuit she really was major acting talent who basically threw all away are all the poorer for that this movie less well known than her german films with pabst but think better one think this crew just better storytelling than pabst and while prix beaute may lack the deep moral complexity the pabst films much easier follow and overall more streamlined focused piece work and doesn hurt that louise singing parts are done edith piaf either bottom line this classic louise brooks film well worth looking for
