1 |text saw this film the toronto international film festival loved this and not just for the obvious reasons blindsight documentary about group blind tibetan teenagers who attempt climb one mount everest sister peaks now this kind thing usually can miss inspirational moving pretty standard right and even the film were just that still have liked but was much more blind herself german sabriye tenberken established school for blind children tibet culture that sees blindness curse evidence that person did bad things previous life many the children the school have been shunned their whole lives and best are burden their families part their education tenberken shares with them the story american erik weihenmayer the first blind person reach the summit mount everest she sends him letter inviting him come and visit her students instead comes with plan arrange expedition for them climb 000 foot lhakpa and provide all the guides and equipment sabriye finds six willing participants and this when the fun starts erik team are mostly american mostly male and mostly sighted experienced mountaineers they type personalities very gung and goal oriented sabriye european female and blind and the students for her are more than project matter how well intentioned additionally the students are tibetan and not old enough confident enough always stand for themselves the expedition unfolds they become pawns between the two adult sides wanting please both while the same time wanting gain the confidence that comes from accomplishment additional obstacle other than being blind that they are speaking english second most cases third language and struggle understand and make themselves understood when turns out that none the students have any climbing experience and that some are much more coordinated than others begins unravel erik original plan for them all reach the summit together both students and teachers begin suffer the effects high altitude decisions must made whether continue send some down the mountain among the effects high altitude increased irritability and you can see how this feeds the conflict between the adults the risk oversimplifying one side are those for whom the destination all and the other are those who just want enjoy the journey won tell you how all turns out except say that this was one the most surprising and thought provoking stories seen long time the film also weaves bits each climber story into the narrative and this was sorely needed since once the climb the kids tended keep their heads down and their mouths shut with all the drama going around them that wasn surprising the backstories are turns charming and heartbreaking and found very strange that found myself closer tears the beginning the film than the end this was contrary expectations and another pleasant surprise addition all the human drama cover director walker and her small crew had contend with the frigid and oxygen deprived conditions herself lugging equipment the mountains and hoping wouldn break down with all great documentaries the filmmaker was just lucky enough smart enough prepared enough the right place the right time and she captured very special story that has much say about people who want what best for the kids does about the kids themselves
