1 |text have you ever felt like your being watched like someone keeps tabs every move you make well just remember before you decide break the law the fbi will always there least that the feeling you get after watching the gripping but slightly mellow crime drama the fbi story traces the roots the organization from small bureau one the most modern facilities the world 1959 telling the story through they eyes one its agents chip hardesty james stewart chip was with the fbi from day one and gladly puts his job above everything else the world even occasionally his family the fbi story tracks his life depicting what does agent and how being one affects his personal life the film does spectacular job showing what kind cases the fbi handles and how they handle them the audience gets see chip stop klux klan riots undercover solve indian murder estate scandal bring fugitives into custody rescue hostages and helped fight wwii even helped bring communist spies justice stewart vaguely complex performance stellar always the slightly neurotic agent who loves his job maybe little too much one the best parts about this film that get see the inside workings both chip family life and his job witness him suffer through the death his best friend and then his son also observe his wife having miscarriage and his marriage having rocky times almost all his personal problems are caused love his job vera miles gives spotty performance but very convincing none the less she was never brilliant actress but there was always something very attractive and alluring about her well maybe that just sadly none the other performances are worth mentioning but the attention grabbing story managed keep exceedingly interested the cinematography this film was impressive especially the scenes the south american jungles the colors all had texture that really set the atmosphere the film perhaps the greatest part this movie was mervyn leroy fabulous direction every scene was fluid they just rolled together tell brilliant story chock full ingenious camera shots some with very hitchcockian feel all all the fbi story spectacular but overlooked film clocking two and half hours some viewers might intimidated but you get the chance recommend jumping into this one enjoyed jimmy stewart spectacular performance and the captivating story
