1 |text until the 1990s there had never been film based upon jane austen emma then two came along the same year 1996 you count 1995 clueless which updates austen plot modern american high school three two years the main character emma woodhouse young lady from well family regency england she financially considerably better off than most austen heroines such elizabeth bennett fanny price and has need find herself wealthy husband instead her main preoccupation seems finding husbands for her friends she persuades her friend harriet turn down proposal marriage from young farmer robert martin believing that harriet should setting her sights the ambitious clergyman elton this scheme goes disastrously wrong however elton has interest harriet but has fallen love with emma herself the speed with which emma rejects his proposal makes one wonder just why she was keen match her friend with man she regards with good reason unsuitable marriage partner for herself this being jane austen plot emma turns out less committed spinster than she seems and she too finds herself falling love leading further complications today 2008 kate beckinsale hollywood star but 1996 despite being only year younger was not nearly well known internationally gwyneth paltrow she however just convincing austen well intentioned but often wrong headed heroine beckinsale seems have gift for classical roles she made delightful hero kenneth branagh version much ado about nothing and sometimes find myself wishing that hollywood could have found more suitable roles for her rather than wasting her turkeys like pearl harbor underworld preferred jeremy northam mark strong emma love interest knightley largely because came closer own conception the character gentlemanly chivalrous older man some ways more father figure emma than lover his surname probably meant indicate his gentlemanly nature nineteenth century gentlemen liked think themselves the modern equivalent mediaeval knights with their elaborate codes chivalry strong tends downplay the question the age difference she and makes knightley more passionate lover and less wise mentor than does northam samantha morton another actress who would bigger things perhaps closer the harriet the novel than was toni collette this was the more small scale the two versions being made for television rather than the cinema and the sets and costumes seem less lavish and there are fewer big names among the cast costume drama however generally something that british television does well and this version can certainly hold its own with the cinema version both are entertaining and well made versions austen novel
