1 |text when this film was originally released was promoted with the notably unimaginative tagline dirty harry again whatever this pitch lacks originality more than compensated for complete and total accuracy sudden impact retains all the aspects that made the previous three dirty harry movies successful tight pacing compelling plot strong supporting characters endless gunplay and bone dry humor some these elements are not only retained but amplified this easily the darkest bloodiest and most overtly right wing installment the franchise the plot somewhat intriguing after killing ridiculous number hoodlums inspector callahan sent forced vacation his superiors the sleepy coastal town san paolo tasked investigate the background recent homicide victim who was shot the genitals before being put out his doubt considerable misery second shot the head early the film the audience made aware the identity the killer artist named jennifer spencer sondra locke who hunting down the thugs who gang raped her and her sister fun fair some ten years earlier this incident shown very disturbing flashback snippets which recur before each new murder more bodies start appear with the same becomes clear harry that both the local police chief and his new love interest guess who know more than they are telling make matters even more complicated the one time rapists realize who hunting them and start hit back hard sudden impact offers relentless action from beginning end clint eastwood directed this film himself and expertly handles series set pieces that culminate exhilarating climax sondra locke performance effectively conveys the blend ruthlessness and fragility that define her character that having been said fair wonder another actress who was not eastwood off screen companion the time could have brought more charisma and dramatic weight the role theresa russell and cybill shepherd jump mind possible candidates members the supporting cast that punch significantly above their weight include albert popwell harry partner horace paul drake the psychopathic mick and the truly scene stealing audrie neenan who portrays the vicious ray parkins however the film has some notable problems some the subplots the animosity between harry and gang twentysomething hoodlums mob vendetta against him take too much screen time and don really have any bearing the larger story their only real use raise the body count absurd levels the first half the film sometimes appears that dirty harry shoots people more often than has use the restroom however the film moves into top gear progresses and the triangulated cat and mouse game between callahan spencer and her former tormentors assumes prominence this second hour makes clear that more stripped down and slightly refocused screenplay would have given sudden impact the potential first class neo noir style thriller that could have taken the series new levels but still have contained more than enough magnum heroics satisfy the harry loyalists instead get the film that eastwood and warner bros clearly wanted make superbly executed but prototypical eighties action flick that mostly declines particularly challenge the intelligence intended audience this was far the biggest grossing the series the box office and not hard see why though not the film that could have been this still big trigger happy fun even after repeated viewings going make your day
