1 |text though not the biggest fan wirework based martial arts films when film goes straight for fantasy rather than fighting get lot more fun out and this film one the best terms fantastical plotting and crazy flying shenanigans ching siu tung has crafted here enchanting treat with fine performance and much ethereal beauty the great tragic leslie cheung plays tax collector hero who stays the night haunted temple and gets involved with stunning fox spirit and wacky taoist cheungs performance filled with naive but dignified charm and pleasingly off the wall the taoist monk who shows off some swordplay and even gets musical number perhaps best off all joey wang the fox spirit truly delight behold with every movement and gesture entrancingly seductive the film takes elements fantasy horror comedy and romance all stirred together into constantly entertaining package ching siu tung directing and handling the choreography gives some neat wirework thrills and fills the film with mists shadows and eerily enthralling benighted forest colours giving every forest scene wonderfully bewitching atmosphere also notable are the elaborate hair stylings and gorgeous flowing garments the female characters with not mistaken joey wang sporting hair done like fox ears times marvellous touch though the film features relatively little action and some perhaps ill advised cheesy pop songs times this beautiful piece entertainment with swell characters and plotting even the odd neat character arc near constant supply visual treats and copious dreamy atmosphere ethereal treasure highly recommended
