1 |text deliverance stunning thriller every bit exciting any good thriller should aspire but also stomach churningly frightening though not horror movie just terrifying any classic horror film the very thought being normal red blooded male enjoying adventure weekend miles from any form civilisation only captured and sodomised couple violent hillbillies surely the worst nightmare the world population would have been easy for deliverance slip into exploitation territory but john boorman has cleverly avoided the temptation down such route and has made film that explores questions and challenges the very meaning masculinity with many films you come away wishing heaven that you could step into the hero shoes performing heroic deeds and saving the day and getting the girl but with deliverance you come away praying god that you never have experience what these four protagonists through four city guys jon voight lewis burt reynolds drew ronny cox and bobby ned beatty head out into the wilderness spend few days canoing down soon dammed river the guys are riding the rapids pairs and and bobby inadvertently get little too far ahead the others they pull the riverside and await their pals the adjacent woodland here they fall foul two local woodlanders bill mckinney and herbert coward who tie tree while one them strips and rapes bobby instructing him perversely squeal like pig lewis and drew arrive unseen and lewis being fair archer kills the rapist while the other hillbilly beats hasty retreat into the forest under great emotional stress the four canoeists decide conceal the event and get out the area but they find the river increasingly dangerous negotiate they journey downstream and the risk their lives heightens when the surviving hillbilly returns take shots them with his rifle from some unseen vantage point the rocky cliffs beside the river deliverance very powerful survival tale but even more powerful and disturbing study macho attitudes being torn apart and left humiliated tatters though all the performances are remarkable one must take particular note beatty efforts role that many actors would turned down the film very similar thematically the 1971 film straw dogs both films deal with terrifying sexual violence isolated locales and both the eventual violent revenge exacted the victim does not result any sense satisfaction the backdrop the rugged countryside deliverance beautiful look but also adds the tension placing the four canoeists setting where they are the mercy the hillbillies and the landscape with nobody rely other than themselves this truly suspenseful film making its finest
