1 |text all films made before 1912 really need viewed with sense time and place 1894 the lumiere family men father antoine 1840 1911 sons auguste and louis owned and managed factory that manufactured photographic plates and paper not small enterprise the factory had more than 200 employees who received pension and social security benefits innovative for that time was located montplaisir the suburbs lyon france what caused louis lumiere become interested building cinematagraph 1894 remains open for speculation suggestion that the appearance the edison organization kinetoscope peep show machine paris during the fall 1894 provided the catalyst dickson edison staff invented motion picture camera about the size upright piano that was patented february 1893 was electrically operated using power from from heavy storage batteries this massive machine pumped celluloid film strip newly developed the eastman company past lens about frames per second fps was ensconced almost immovable object the black maria essentially the first movie studio the kinetescope machines showed staged presentations less than one minute long that were filmed this studio during 1894 louis lumiere applied himself the task inventing moving picture camera had determined that even fps celluloid film the persistence vision the human eye brain would allow for normal motion perceived his camera dubbed the cinematograph was about the size large shoe box and was provided with detachable film magazine that provided storage for enough film make shoot last about one minute when was had cranked past the lens fps the size and light weight the camera could converted into printer projector the addition light source made portable enough that could taken any location record event provided there was enough sunlight available the spring 1895 louis filmed trick riding some cavalry men house fire with firemen arriving and dousing the engulfed building with water and number other scenes and around lyon using molteni bulb turned the camera into projector and presented his films scientists assembled the reception room the revue generales des science the images were projected screen five meters distant from the lens the screen was stretched doorway between two rooms meeting professional photographers that same year louis photographed the arriving delegates and the same evening showed them motion pictures their arrival with accolades from both the scientific and photographic communities louis decided have public exhibition his invention the end the year since each his films would about one minute long would need least dozen films make good presentation for one these films set his camera the entrance his factory photographing the egress employees quitting time the public venue chosen antoine who offered himself the fairground barker for the cinematograph was the salon indien the grand cafe the boulevard des capucines paris was wintry saturday night december 1895 the first audience sat they were presented with projected view the exterior the lumiere factory with closed gates some were chagrined that they were just going see routine slide show lumiere photographs but then the crank the camera projector was turned and movement began louis had innate sense for motion picture taking this film has beginning middle and end the beginning the doors are opened and people begin leave their workplace during the middle the people stream out with many trying ignore the camera and the cameraman they seem happy leave day labor behind them the end the gates the factory are being closed and this was the first film projected for the entertainment the general public
