1 |text audiences today will probably watch film like ossessione and not really consider how unprecedented was during the time when came out the structure the film really divorces from sap happy hollywood conventions xc2 x97as well other major theatrical elements relies more upon depicting reality very grim and sober light films this nature xc2 x97the neo realist films xc2 x97were made reflect the darkness felt during post world war times ossessione tackles some fairly provocative issues that were probably unseen screen prior the war including adultery conspiracy murder pregnancy etc aside from the one crane shot and certain musical swelling moments the film aesthetic very raw and gritty shot location uses natural lighting and most likely non popular actors all these elements helped convey the issues explored the film yielding the following theme negative karmic repercussions will haunt those who deliberately act immorally the two leads xc2 x97gino and giovanna xc2 x97are polar opposites yet both carry the mentality bored and want entertained gino drifter lone traveler who embraces life and its constant fluctuations giovanna bored house wife cemented the familiarly marital permanence she doesn want leave her home and husband but would rather remain where she because safer gino lifestyle represents the ideal lifestyle giovanna craves the only difference that she too afraid live herself xc2 x97that why she falls love with gino represents everything she wants but doesn have the courage get she wants live world free from the monotony living with her corpulent husband xc2 x97gino the perfect ticket into that world the affair that ensues between the two most likely left audiences back the feeling somewhat uneasy mean films prior the neo realist age never showed such scandalous behavior screen before say the least was probably bit alarming conjunction with the theme the neo realist style helps show the negative repercussions adulterous behavior succinctly put adulterous behavior shown the film leads depressing and ultimately deadened lives when gino and giovanna conspire with each other eliminate giovanna husband karma comes haunt them like plague after the deed done they return their home the atmosphere dark and biting can expected from the neo realist style they are not happy they actually more depressed they thought that eliminating giovanna husband that they live happier lives but they were duped the film ends with giovanna death xc2 x97it being karmic similitude her husband death think this very satisfying ending for several reasons here why there lot talk whether not evil should depicted screen and what extent think depicting evil very necessary and only the evil depicted not being glorified but rather shows what negative consequences evil actions have the subtext ossessione asks adultery and murder evil think the film eagerly responds yes the adulterous behavior between the two reveals how unhappy they are ironically though towards the end the film when they seem healed their depression and are seen basking each other arms inside the car the author the film shows that their happiness fact xc3 xa7ade the car crashes off the cliff and into the river killing giovanna the police arrest gino think was the author intention say that even though people sometimes try and justify their immoral behavior the end karma will come back haunt them agree think the two got what was coming them because they both were incredibly selfish xc2 x97always wanting instant gratification and not willing endure through hard times this was especially made clear after the first sign difficulty that gino and giovanna experience their relationship can handle the pressure living giovanna husband shadow leaves giovanna and sleeps with another girl such typical the insatiable hedonistic personality all all the film seemed very risky for its time the audience however was prepared see such film because the sobriety the war brought those pre war happy lucky films were longer being believed movie going audiences were ready see and contemplate difficult films with complex characters they wanted see characters whose lives were entangled called sin because was reflection their own life problems ossessione then acts great catalyst for where the future film was heading that lot the naturalism pieces see today can said have been influenced the neo realist film movement
