1 |text rented this film from netflix for two reasons was the mood for what thought would silly 50s sci asco and because the first feature length superman film needless say after about minutes found myself thoroughly engaged and very pleasantly surprised experimental oil well has penetrated about six miles into the earth and being shut down the sponsor lois and clark show get the scoop but are disappointed that the deepest well ever drilled will longer operation day later strange events the well make for story more appropriate for superman than clark kent seems that the radioactive mole men have invaded from their six mile deep home near the earth core supermen and the mole men simplistic but well made piece social realism released 1951 starring lead actor who served world war the moral the story seems that americans are just capable becoming fascists anybody else drive this point home typically straightforward superman manner reeves even accuses the lynch mob hunting the mole men being nazis one point even the 1950s the science underlying this film was nonexistent six miles drilling through continental crust would not have even penetrated the upper mantle let alone the hollow center the earth which any case does not exist forgivable keep mind that this film based golden age comic book the film little unevenly paced although the molemen are interesting bit creepy and nicely portrayed there are several corman esquire scenes which spend too much time redundantly showing their odd behavior the script intelligent and economical today standards the costuming poor fair but for its time this film special effects and costuming were quite good the cinematography also generally very good and the acting much better than one might expect was particularly impressed with reeves jeff corey and walter reed
