1 |text emilio miraglia first giallo feature the night evelyn came out the grave was great combination giallo and gothic horror and this second film even better got more the giallo side the equation this time around although miraglia doesn lose the gothic horror stylings that made the earlier film such delight miraglia puts more emphasis the finer details the plot this time around and result the typical giallo labyrinth with characters all over the place and red herrings being thrown every few minutes this definite bonus for the film however while can get little too confusing times there always enough hold the audience interest and miraglia storytelling has improved since his earlier movie the plot opens with scene that sees two young girls fighting before their grandfather explains them the legend behind rather lurid painting their castle the legend revolves around woman called the red queen who legend has returns from the grave every hundred years and kills seven people few years later murders begin occur even though only made two giallo miraglia does have his own set tributes obvious that the colour red important him features heavily both films and appears have something against women called evelyn likes castles gothic atmospheres and stylish murders too which fine miraglia may argento when comes spilling blood but certainly knows how drop over the top murder into his film and here have delights involving volkswagen beetle and death iron fence that one all time favourite giallo death scenes the female side the cast excellent with the stunning barbara bouchet and marina malfatti heading eye pleasing cast ladies that aren afraid take their clothes off the score courtesy bruno nicolai catchy and even though doesn feature much the psychedelic rock heard the night evelyn came out the grave fits the film well the ending something turn off although miraglia revs the gothic atmosphere comes across being more than little bit rushed and the identity the murderer too obvious but even this delightfully entertaining giallo and one that highly recommend fans the genre
