1 |text _waterdance_ explores wide variety aspects the life the spinally injured artfully from the petty torments faulty fluorescent lights flashing overhead sexuality masculinity and depression the experience disability laid open the diversity the central characters themselves underscores the complexity the material examined joel the writer raymond the black man with murky past and bloss the racist biker first these men are united nothing other than the nature their injuries but retain their competitive spirit over time shared experience both good and bad brings them together friends support one another most obvious the transformations that experienced joel who initially distances himself from his fellow patients with sunglasses headphones and curtains comes accept the changes that disablement has made his life joel discards these props and begins involve himself the struggles the men with whom shares the ward the dance referred the title reference this daily struggle keep one head above water give the dance reject life _waterdance_ moving and powerful film many levels and not hesitate recommend
