-1 |text tend love everything the great late paul naschy ever was while not all films starring naschy are great they all have specific charm that can found nowhere but naschy flicks and they are always entertaining there rule without exception however mariscal del infierno aka the devil possessed 1974 proves while the film does have the specific naschy flick charm sadly drags far too much and gets really really dull between naschy stars the evil baron gilles lancr xc3 xa9 who oppresses the people and uses black magic and bloody rituals stay power when gaston malebranche guillermo bredeston who fought side side with gilles lancr xc3 xa9 against the british learns about the baron evil behavior decides turn against his former comrade arms and help the people free themselves from the satanic baron tyranny directed xc3 xb3n klimovsky who best known for directing naschy noche walpurgis the werewolf the vampire woman 1971 the film was scripted naschy himself naschy often scripted his own films and one must say that mostly did better more original job than the case here mariscal del infierno mostly built historical adventure rather than horror film and gets quite boring throughout the middle often resembles the sword and sandal films from the 50s only that this film set medieval times the satanic part was probably only added because the great paul naschy name linked the horror genre the film has its good parts paul naschy giving weird speeches paul naschy looking weird paul naschy doing satanic stuff paul naschy torturing innocent victims etc but sadly most the film concentrates the boring hero and the good guys and these moments are boring the female cast members are nice look but unlike most naschy films this one features nudity and sleaze there some gore but mostly looks clumsy and isn fun too look the case with most other naschy films overall mariscal del infierno only worth look for fellow naschy enthusiasts there are dozens films starring the spanish horror deity which should seen before this one such jorobado morgue the hunchback the morgue 1973 orgia los muertos the hanging woman 1973 espanto surge tumba horror rises from the tomb 1973 latidos panico panic beats 1983 rojo sangre 2004 any the waldemar daninsky werewolf films paul naschy legends never die
