1 |text the matador strange film its main character julian played with unusual mix charm and unbalance brosnan not your typical hero julian hit man who experiencing late mid life crises having spent years the profession cold blooded murder now finds himself stressed out and desperately lonely and after chance meeting bar with danny greg kinnear latches and begins halting awkward friendship danny the quintessential nice guy dealing with some stuff his own life and truth told could use friend well the two make unexpected connection and danny sticks around hear julian story even after learning the unsavory truth about julian work matador approaches subject not completely unheard cinema the anti hero assassin films like assassins and grosse pointe blank come mind but matador differs several key ways first all the killing and gore implied but never really shown any detail meaning that you are action movie buff looking for adrenaline rush this movie will probably disappoint you and second unlike most anti hero films matador makes attempt show remorse and redemption from its main character julian job simply presented what kind thing this unusual given that would consider killing for money horrific and yet this unorthodox approach perhaps what makes the film feel authentic although don like admit almost anything could become mundane after did long enough maybe even murder did julian victims deserve die who paying have people killed who knows the movie never deals with these questions the focus julian and his stumbling shuffle into genuine friendship you read about someone like julian the paper you would have passing thought that people like him should ripped out society like cancer but forced watch his life you are drawn his intense humanity sympathy for the devil guess brosnan take julian well done and deeply unsettling doesn completely divorce himself from his james bond good looks and smooth charm but rather just adds disturbing quirks into the mix weird crude remarks the middle polite conversations and sudden shifts from suave charm childish tantrums and sad desperate pleas for acceptance keeps you guessing about his grasp his sanity and how will affect those around him bit like listening piano player that occasionally and unexpectedly hits wrong note while plays but works the films only other major role that danny not nearly meaty kinnear turns solid unspectacular performance regular joe with regular joe life and problems the film doesn really have any huge shocks night shyamalan twists but wasn able guess the ending and felt satisfying doesn have any deep philosophical spiritual insights and yet felt very human and didn have any heart pounding car chases gun battles and yet thought the pacing was well done and was never bored maybe the only real message here about the human need reach out and make connections with one another and how those needs have moral prerequisites even murderer needs friends and even good people can friends with bad people comment the strange random world live good film worth seeing
