-1 |text you know all those letters father christmas and jesus that are sent every year well turns out that they are not actually delivered but dropped off half forgotten corner the post office rot unless some bright spark figures out way posting them bizarre settings winner and one which perfectly fits the strange movie that dead letter office having said that this obviously australian film opposed british one was royal mail most letters get this sort treatment anyway haven been this flat for two years and still getting letters for wang some female priest the church latter day never heard you and various catalogues for industrial equipment addressed plumbing company dead letter office the name given the place where undeliverable mail ends follows the story alice miranda otto who grows seriously divided home writing her absent father she only learns adulthood that her letters haven been delivered for one reason another logically she gets job the and finds herself working alongside other social rejects including the brooding chilean immigrant frank lopez george del hoyo slowly she finds herself drawn him but can she find out where her dad without bringing the self contained world the dead letters office its knees nothing against this film but was reminded the god awful heather graham film committed while watching this however this much better than that pile horse crap but then again that ain difficult for start this film much more logical true the metaphors are somewhat blatant and the underflowing symbolism quickly becomes flood but least this cohesive and quirky without being complete drivel also well acted both otto and del hoyo are very good the lovers looking for something they know they never find while other characters are peripheral best part the trouble that seems wrap far too quickly leaving this viewer somewhat disappointed the other part that when you consider australia draconian immigration policy you don speak english rack off such story unlikely take place reality the other characters sadly also help destabilise the realism proving little more than odd ball stereotypes despite that dead letter office certainly something little different might not everyone taste but liked yes was hackneyed and predictable but sometimes nice watch film without guns violence heavy duty swearing and nudity chance that australian film there ain any major laughs there bullet time and the characters are usually one dimensional but the story that counts here and while not earth shattering its magnificence pleasant enough way passing the time the movie equivalent sheryl crow nice listen now and again but you wouldn really miss wasn there
