1 |text anchors aweigh sees two eager young sailors joe brady gene kelly and clarence doolittle brooklyn frank sinatra get special four day shore leave eager get the girls particularly joe lola neither joe nor brooklyn figure the interruption little navy mad donald dean stockwell and his aunt susie kathryn grayson unexperienced the ways females and courting brooklyn quickly enlists joe help him win aunt susie over along the way however joe finds himself falling for the gal thinks belongs his best friend how brooklyn going take this betrayal and does joe end with susie who loves him too the first and second times saw anchors aweigh also saw the same time did the town the kelly sinatra collaboration from 1949 both times felt that anchors aweigh was the better film terms plotting and structure all the dances and songs fit the moment the plot and they develop the characters and story rather than hamper them yet both times came away feeling that the town the better film overall having now seen both films third time still stand that judgement somehow the town film and piece entertainment just lighter gayer purely and simply happier the numbers are more outrageous and less integral the plot and yet somehow works better than all the dances and singing anchors aweigh not quite sure why this the typical argument that the latter film over long almost two and half hours this certainly valid criticism make certainly felt the length the first two times saw however also film that grows you the more you see the shorter feels and the more you appreciate the technical mastery involved its making and yet something just doesn hang together quite right feels almost the script was pored over and every single moment when kelly could break into dance sinatra into song was noted and that exactly what happened opportunity shoehorn musical number was given and that probably the film biggest weakness has numbers give take few and matter how big fan you are kelly sinatra this really starts turn one numb after while contrast this for example with the ten numbers the town you might well feel that each song each dance can taken out the film without leaving lacking and that true but that also because the writers weren more restrained adding them the first place all this long preamble doesn mean there nothing good about anchors aweigh the musical splashy with great songs bursting out all over like the duets between kelly and sinatra hate leave begged her and you knew susie the singing sinatra what makes the sunset the charm you and the best all fall love too easily and without doubt the always inventive always breathtaking dancing kelly also hard miss with cast this calibre grayson sweet and seems improve each viewing her voice becoming stunning rather than frightening jose iturbi role written sympathetically and does great job with even clarence own brooklyn pamela britton cute and charming close one could get betty garrett without being garrett herself sinatra adorable with those blue eyes and curls his and plays the innocent boy man wonderfully role reprises the town his singing usual simply faultless from enunciation through timing and phrasing his solo numbers might seem drag little but when you got the voice century showcasing probably good reason any slow the rest the film gene kelly sheer genius this film worthy its own paragraph third the billing behind sinatra and grayson respectively anchors aweigh really kelly film his joe brady believable real character tough the outside glib and willing lie when necessary win gal but actually the biggest softy the inside kelly makes this charming rather than cloying but also gives joe real edge that you see the scene when joe chases brooklyn around the room with genuinely murderous look his face and his breakfast tray his hands and the dancing again the film suffers from the too much good thing spoils the effect syndrome does with sinatra singing but once again gene kelly doing the softshoe tapping across the screen sailor outfit dressed bandit chief might well err the side overdoing all kelly dances are breathtaking the pared down simplicity his tap number with sinatra begged her his mexican hat dance with the sweet wide eyed little girl his lavish spanish influenced dance cumparsita course the classic image left audiences minds for all time would kelly his red white and blue sailor suit dancing with jerry mouse tom jerry fame well deserved golden film memory sure not often that one can say you impressed the special effects film made 1945 given the saturation cgi the contemporary film market but gene and jerry still look great with kelly always hitting his spots and looking exactly where needs look would turn out that just about the only people who could really keep with gene kelly would kelly himself cover girl and cartoon animation doubtless that this first daring inventive kelly dance with jerry has reserved place for anchors aweigh film history and the hearts classic film buffs but also notable for being the first three kelly sinatra film collaborations and though rather too drawn out still great couple hours entertainment watch first then again and maybe again grow you before you realise
