1 |text came watch guerrilla part two steven soderbergh biopic che guevara without having seen the preceding film and without more than cursory knowledge che life the same time was rather apprehensive that this would both heavy going history lesson and unrepentant love letter the iconic revolutionary turns out this film far exceeded expectations guerrilla works remarkably well standalone film the story che failed attempt lead revolution bolivia then under military rule compelling tragedy the initial impetus brought che arrival incognito lead the guerrilla war lost misfortune follows misfortune the odds stack against the revolutionaries backing for the bolivian army hostile conditions the rainforest suspicious locals and che failing health are just some the difficulties which beset the nascent rebellion soderbergh portrayal che largely uncritical but this film hagiography the style refreshingly undramatic with subtle and effective soundtrack alberto iglesias adding quiet drama many scenes che undoubtedly the centre the film but there are very few close ups his face and are encouraged see the people fighting alongside him and sometimes against him too where soderbergh wishes demonstrate che virtues see small episodes such the loyal acolyte who upbraids two fellow guerrillas when they question che leadership and emphasises the sacrifice that has made leaving behind cuba fight again for revolution the direction throughout superb part two feels tightly edited despite its narrow focus and able communicate great deal through images without the need for narrator spell things out for the audience the start the film see few short clips lavish parties post revolutionary cuba immediately furnishing with ideas why che would sacrifice his old life fight again another country later the portrayal guerrillas marching through the unending rainforests stands out strikingly beautiful scene and helps create feeling the enormity the task before this tiny band revolutionaries there problem with the film the distance between the viewer and che which though does allow appreciate the context the insurgency and the people around him makes hard for understand him better person true benicio del toro utterly convincing the lead role xc2 x96 much that difficult remember that you are watching actor and not the man himself however watching guerrilla standalone film means that are given precious little insight into what shaping che thoughts words and actions hoped that this more the fore the first part soderbergh biopic cannot comment that yet and certainly the strength part two making look forward eagerly seeing the prequel
