n revealed the audience pierre and louis respective relationships with nora this seems cheat desplechin part thrusting the idea upon unmediated form rather than illustrating more subtly the natural course the narrative one two darkly surreal touches imply the presence alternative but largely unconscious world persons stripped frighteningly bare but again these are felt more pretentious intrusions film making technique rather than eruptions from deeper reservoir truth inherent the story fact for all its heavy handed hints depth the characters are curiously undeveloped and unnuanced they function more ciphers for their creator many ideas about people rather than real people their own right much the detail their lives seems arbitrarily applied rather than organic for example ismael are constantly reminded viola player but more than two hours pass before actually see hear him play and the effect his chosen instrument profession upon his personality never elaborated hence may just well marine biologist trapeze artist amalric brings certain manic charm the unhinged but ultimately sane ismael but found devos cloying and monotone which may intentional however the elusive nora meanwhile jean paul roussillon ismael father elsa wolliaston his psychoanalyst and magalie woch the psychically wounded but defiant sinologist befriends hospital make the biggest impact amongst the supporting actors catherine deneuve too though her role little more than self referential cameo ultimately rois reine very much acquired taste should fail push your buttons very likely that desplechin undisciplined and florid approach will frustrate and exasperate even you somehow keep watching
