1 |text put yourself into carla shoes she overworked unappreciated administrative drudge who invisible you know her she trained three her last three bosses knows where all the bodies are buried and might even look back you the mirror when you brush your teeth always having time for another thankless task and does better than most despite serious disability she has the desk the way the restroom that becomes the repository half finished cups coffee begging spilled what you don want hear well she can and neither can you until your hearing aid place prepare experience life from the perspective the hearing impaired carla emmanuelle devos needs change her life work leading nowhere friends are relying her meet their domestic needs and the only way out starts with collapse that goes virtually unnoticed she won take vacation contract going critical the only alternative hire assistant carla submits requirements that convey her real needs well groomed man this brings applicant for approval that reminds that should careful with our wishes paul vincent cassell does everything wrong from the start his job interview and his getting hired clearly demonstrates carla interest his non job related qualities she sees potential this former thief and the story unfolds their relationship grows very unusual pattern dependence paul has difficult transition returning the world outside prison walls and finds himself another sort prison one the office variety and another indentured servitude pay off old debt his skills thief help carla win political battle the office but paul sees grander opportunity with carla skill lip reading and draws her even further into world intrigue this brutal film noir unrated and probably suitable for older teens carla grows more powerful professionally well personally the story progresses and her disability gives her clear advantages over the rest she grows woman discovering her sensual side while she uses her resources overcome the obstacles competing man world the two main characters are meant for each other strange way without paul carla will remain her role doormat she has our sympathy hopes and best wishes even she doesn make the best decisions along the way you will hear the world through carla ears from awkward adjustments your hearing aid muffled sounds all but inaudible without relatively distinct voices when you can see who talking with one major sense disabled see carla heightened intuitive power compensate and can all use that sense hear not only what people say but also what they really mean
