tics overly long needlessly layered purveyor gender stereotypes manipulative with music the usual raps too long but found this film austere powerful spontaneous and entirely convincing voice protest from the women who kept the vigil outside the place rosenstrasse where their jewish relatives and others were detained found nothing flashy contemporary manipulative this depiction the very absence extreme violence one shot otherwise physically brutalized intensified tension which increased incrementally the film progressed you keep waiting for some vicious attack begin any minute the somberness the film stayed with afterward awoke often later the night saw the film mind filled with bleak melancholic chaotic images and feelings conjured the film for that happens rarely german and english rating seen you like read more reviews send message for directions websites add the rosenstrasse protest swept from their forced labor jobs what was meant the final roundup the national capital 1700 2000 jews mostly men married non jewish women were herded into rosenstrasse welfare office for the jewish community central berlin because these jews had german relatives many them highly connected adolf eichmann hoped that segregating them from other prisoners would convince family members that their loved ones were being sent labor camps rather than more ominous destinations occupied poland normally those arrested remained custody for only two days before being loaded onto trains bound for the east but before deportation prisoners could occur this case wives and other relatives got wind what was happening and appeared the rosenstrasse address first ones and twos and then ever growing numbers perhaps many six thousand participated the protest although not all the same time women demanded back their husbands day after day for week unarmed unorganized and leaderless they faced down the most brutal forces the disposal the third reich joseph goebbels the gauleiter governor district leader berlin anxious have that city racially cleansed was also charge the nation public morale both counts was worried about the possible repercussions the women actions rather than inviting more open dissent shooting the women down the streets and fearful jeopardizing the secrecy the final solution goebbels with hitler concurrence released the rosenstrasse prisoners and even ordered the return twenty five them who already had been sent auschwitz both hitler and goebbels the decision was mere postponement the inevitable but they were mistaken almost all those released from rosenstrasse survived the war the women won astonishing victory over the forces destruction adapted from article posted the university south florida website teacher guide the holocaust
