-1 |text unless sadly mistaken rented nightmare elm street several years ago and there was music video pretty sure which was called dream warriors the end and rented this one dvd hoping that the video would there because was one the funniest things ever seen amazing how stuff from the 80s funny now but nothing funnier than 80s rap videos there was this rap group singing that song dream warriors the vhs version this movie after the credits and they all wearing like denim jackets with shirt underneath and form fitting jean shorts that are all frayed the bottoms like daisy dukes what could make rap group look more foolish can imagine spoilers any rate was disappointed looking for that video the dvd version all had was this mediocre installment the freddy krueger series the movie sort starts off with the same idea part with the main character witnessing all kinds gruesome murders and then sort coming out trance and finding himself with the bloody hands kristen parker patricia arquette has nightmare about the infamous house that nancy thompson used live then runs the bathroom the sink handles turn into freddy hands and attack her and then she wakes standing her bathroom having slit her own wrists from there the movie turns into the usual mental hospital installment larry fishburne tired always playing the bad guy his roles was happy take the role this film nice guy orderly stern but accommodating when the patients want bend the rules little not surprisingly turns what leaps and bounds the best performance the movie arquette later goes become accomplished actor but had not perfected her acting skills when she starred this film the characters the movie are mostly all patients the mental hospital that kristen placed into after cutting her wrists all them are cynical and uncooperative almost none believing that they really belong there all eventually they realize and are able convince the staff that they are all having dreams about the same man and not just some kind group hysteria heather langenkamp has returned her famous role nancy thompson this time grown into dream researcher result her childhood experiences involving freddy krueger not surprisingly she able quickly relate the hysterical kristen and the rest the patients since she had experienced exactly what they going through there are some interesting murders this installment and the technology used for the special effects have taken huge jump there gigantic worm like freddy that tries swallow kristen whole there scene where television turns into freddy and with mechanical arms picks one the patients there for some late night entertainment and punishes her for sitting too close the but there also unconvincing motion scene where couple guys have fight with freddy krueger skeleton which has been rotting the trunk some car car junkyard and one the more groan inducing scenes was one where freddy attacks one the patients his dream the one famous for sleepwalking tearing the muscles and tendons out his arms and legs and leading him around like puppet ouch get peek into freddy past this installment not only meet his mother but also find out the circumstances that led freddy being fathered more than 100 maniacs fighting freddy the patients all band together and their dreams use their special powers most which reflect their shortcomings real life fight him one student bound wheelchair able walk his dreams another has the hilarious powers what calls the wizard master another beautiful and bad she has lots makeup her hair stands foot high mohawk and she has knives clever but the movie falters when has only one the patients the one who can speak not have any powers his dreams until the climax the movie when suddenly realizes that can talk his dreams just the right moment save the day his dream power was little too obvious have been left out for that long but collectively now you see why the movie was subtitled dream warriors altogether this not entirely weak entry into the series the acting pretty shoddy but actually pretty good for horror movie larry fishburne vastly overshadows the rest the cast displaying wonderful acting skills early his career and the movie not simply rehash either the first two xc2 x96 problem that plagues the friday the 13th movies much more than the elm street films the characters are never developed enough allow for the later creation much tension which why most the deaths come across more creative ways kill off someone horror film than the tragic loss the life one the characters that come know and root for their triumph over evil but then again not lot horror movies take the time really develop their characters the point where you throw your hands defeat when they are killed are the edge your seat they run for their lives but important note that the few horror films that actually that are almost invariably the best ones xc2 x85
1 |text kolchak was series that really didn fit into any category part horror part comedy some social awareness thrown and what have something that think people weren ready for shame really started watch these shows the chiller network never saw the originals realized how different and interesting really was starring darren mcgavin kolchak reporter for the international news service and simon oakland his always angry boss tony vincenzo the show followed the exploits chicago news reporter who more often than not became part the story himself searched the windy city for modern day creepies that bump the night the underlying charm macgavin really sets the show apart somewhat goofy guy who always wears the same suit you cannot help but love him his jokes are great and the back and forth between him and the skeptical editor oakland are downright hilarious the stories are for the most part pretty good and the acting very good the were not great period for special effects and the show suffers for but you suspend disbelief what you have fun series that was ahead time
