1 |text the original movie the odd couple has some wonderful comic one liners the entire world seems knows the story neurotic neat freak felix ungar and funny obnoxious slob oscar madison this paring mismatched roommates created one the most successful series all time well countless not anywhere near good imitations the odd couple movie has some wonderful jokes about oscar apartment and his sloppy habits says who wants food one his poker player buddies asks what got oscar says got brown sandwiches and green sandwiches what the brown either very new cheese very old meat also love the line about oscar refrigerator been out order for two weeks saw milk standing there that wasn even bottle there question that walter matthau oscar madison joy watch screen almost good jack klugman version the series the problem with the movie jack lemmon felix ungar jack makes very very honest effort the role the problem that makes felix depressing and down trodden that becomes more annoying than comical tony randall performance the series brought the kind humor warmth and sensitivity felix character which lemmon portrayal lacks tony felix unger obviously could annoying some the time however the series related specific situations where the annoyance was needed the storyline jack felix ungar note the different spelling the movie seems never happy fun interesting the movie felix ungar roommate that drives you the wall all the time the movie still has great moments that withstand the test time the famous meatloaf fight one the greatest scenes ever one the other great examples felix little notes oscar pillow will remembered forever however there are some darker sides where oscar goes over the top his crying near the end after bawling out felix and scene involving felix linguine dinner although lightened funny line seem more depressing than comical perhaps there wasn enough time see the lighter side these characters that made the series memorable the movie the beginning minutes are very boring the same issue occurs with felix conversation with the pidgeon sisters the movie ending predictable and too pat there very little care compassion for each them the other the result that the darker side the film leads lot depression and anger rather than comedy unless you are watching the great scenes described above appears that jack lemmon monotone persona felix brings the film down rather than enhances embraces the comedy between the characters really took the 1970 series make the odd couple the best that could the original film still very good however the series much better
