1 |text xizao the tale about the clash modern life and ancient traditions and its effects family china ming quanxiu businessman who returns home when letter sent his brother ming jiang makes him believe that his father liu zhu has died founds that his father still alive well his old neighborhood and his father old business the public bathroom the movie centers around ming family and how has learn the importance his father job something always had considered old tradition that had die soon also the movie explores his relationship with ming who mentally challenged and the problems the small community and how the bathroom place that purifies not only their bodies but also their souls the two main themes the movie the family and the problems progress are incredibly well handled and the movie never loses the point trying make both themes are very good developed and get glimpse chinese society and customs the director yang zhang tells his tale simple way letting the characters characters the job very simple approach but fits the movie perfectly and highly doubt that another style would fit the movie this good zhang has enormous potential can tell story without the aid visual flare camera tricks the acting outstanding its naturalistic approach everyone acts very natural way and almost looks they were real persons being filmed the three lead characters give remarkable performances and jiang ming surely steals the show even when the movie could had sticked patronizing old days were much better message instead takes attitude equilibrium like saying that progress good and must move but must not forget where came from and keep equilibrium between modern life and the traditions old awesome and touching film
