1 |text made 1946 and released 1948 the lady and shanghai was one the big films made welles after returning from relative exile for making citizen kane dark brooding and expressing some early cold war paranoia this film stands tall film noir crime film the cinematography this film filled with welles characteristic quirks odd angles quick cuts long pans and sinister lighting the use ambient street music precursor the incredible long opening shot touch evil and the mysterious chinese characters and the sequences chinatown can only considered the inspiration many ways roman polanski chinatown unfortunately welles obsession with technical filmmaking that hurts this film its entirety the plot this story often lost behind sometimes incomprehensible clutter film techniques however despite this criticism the story combined with wonderful performances welles hayworth and especially glenn anders laughter make this film joy watch orson welles pulls off not only the irish brogue but the torn identities the honest but dangerous sailor rita hayworth who was married welles the time breaks with her usual roles sex goddess and takes role real depth and contradictions finally glenn anders strange and bizarre portrayal elsa husbands law partner nothing short classic
