-1 |text jack london life was certainly colorful enough for dozen films about different aspects him sad say though that what his life was used for film was some wartime propaganda that put the best face some the least attractive parts his character jack london who barely saw the age when died wrote some the best stories around wrote what knew but also wrote does everyone else bringing the baggage his own life experience with him some that experience another day and time would have been condemned racism but this was world war and london was big believer the yellow peril was called back the day two thirds the film covers his life author see his years seaman from where got the inspiration for the sea wolf see him the yukon miner cabin with dog that was doubt his inspiration for the call the wild london was able capture the spirit adventure that his own life was all about right paper for the world enjoy ever since the final third dealt with his time war correspondent covering the russo japanese war london was socialist but his socialism did not encompass folks who were oriental like few million others saw the rising immigration the chinese and japanese our pacific coast threat jobs for the white people advocated strict immigration policies for orientals the film puts the cart before the horse london presented man who saw because was hand the russo japanese war what japan ambitions were and for that reason was xenophobic was actually the kind atrocities present world war were not existent during the russo japanese conflict japan had her imperial ambitions but did everyone else including the usa that time but our immigration policies caused pressure from our west coast politicians was big contributing factor the deterioration relations with japan over couple generations london was part the cause not prophet crying the wilderness this film was the first independent production samuel bronston who later did some films with bit more budget than jack london had bit more money bronston might have gotten james cagney spencer tracy both who would have been right for the role instead they got michael shea who was making his second film after lady burlesque shea fine the part but certainly was box office london covering the war meets with captain tanaka who played leonard strong actor who specialized orientals and played ton them world war from the vantage point 1905 strong outlines the best manchu tradition japan imperial aims right taking the usa eventually must have gone over great with the swing shift crowd lot course left out london life including first wife playing the second and only wife this film susan hayward who only comes into the movie when half over wish have seen more her charmian kittredge london survived her husband almost years dying 1955 shea fact met and married the leading lady his life jack london virginia mayo has small role jack london and they married for years until shea died 1973 maybe one day get view jack london that will lot better than this one
