ttles down jannings performance incredibly sedate and measured and when the players around him begin mirror this the effect his mere presence has restored order sternberg appears show distaste for violence allowing the grimmest moments take place off screen and yet implying that they have happened with flow images that almost poetic fact really seems have all round lack interest action the scene the prisoners revolt sternberg takes aloof and objective stance his camera eventually retreating fly the wall position compare this the following scenes between jannings and evelyn brent which are complex medley point view shots and intense close ups thrusting right into the midst their interaction personality set would seem that sternberg was much like the cold and callous director played the screen william powell and fact powell portrayal probably something deliberate parody that even sternberg himself would have been unfortunately this harsh attitude did not make him easy man work with and coupled with his focus his technical resources over his human ones the smaller performances his pictures leave little desired while jannings displays classic hamming the charles laughton mode that works dramatically appears one told his stars they were not comedy evelyn brent fairly good giving some good emoting but overplaying here and there the only performance that comes close jannings that powell himself little odd see the normally amiable star the thin man and the great ziegfeld playing figure stern and humourless like male ninotchka but does good job revealing smouldering emotional intensity beneath the hard hearted exterior the last command could easily have ruffled few feathers studio offices tends happen with any disparaging commentary the film making process even relatively tame example like this the very least believe many studio heads would have been displeased the behind the scenes view threatened the mystique movie making which was still very much alive this point turned out such was the impact the picture that jannings won the first ever academy award for best actor well best writing nomination for lajos biro and according some sources although the issue little vague nomination for best picture this significant since the academy was tiny institution this time and the first awards were more than ever bit self indulgent back slapping the hollywood elite but elite not they recognised good material when they saw and were willing reward
