1 |text the gingerbread man the first thriller ever done xc2 x96 robert altman 1955 charles laughton directed the night the hunter spooky slice southern gothic which robert mitchum plays scary serial killer one the film more famous sequences consists two kids escaping from mitchum rowboat the kids frantically paddling whilst mitchum wades after them like monster seven years later mitchum played equally spooky killer cape fear another film set the american south that film featured local attorney trying protect his family and likewise ended with mitchum terrorising folks boat 1991 martin scorsese trying branch out and tackle something more mainstream remade cape fear boat scene and all now have robert altman the gingerbread man another slice small town southern gothic altman says consulted the night the hunter for inspiration and tackled such mainstream film purely because wanted spread his wings and try popcorn picture but what secretly attempting here deconstruct the canonical films the southern gothic genre instead showdown small boat get showdown giant ship instead two kids being kidnapped get two kids being safely returned the police instead money being hidden have money being readily given via last will and testament instead the righteous attorney the 1961 film and the deplorable attorney the 1991 remake get rather three dimensional lawyer kenneth branagh instead the monster chasing the family get the hero chasing the bad guys instead the monster breaking into the family house boat have the hero hunting the monster board the monster house ship similarly instead murderous serial killer get innocent weirdo played robert duvall etc etc etc altman goes and reversing everything just little slightly pulling the edges and doing his own thing his touch most apparent during the film first half hour the film existing uneasy space between conventional plot driven movie storytelling and altman fondness for overlapping dialogue casual narratives prowling camera movement and the way that characters aren much introduced they are simply part what going still despite altman best intentions the film never rises above mediocrity altman too bound the conventions the thriller format much damage his style too lethargic generate tension and the film simply not radical enough counterpoint other canonical films the genre gingerbread man thus too mainstream work more pure altman film and too altman work mainstream thriller the film not complete waste though robert downey junior kenneth branagh and the usually intolerable daryl hannah all turn juicy performances the film also has nice atmosphere set against approaching hurricane and the final act contains some interesting twists and turns while not the complete disaster that scorsese cape fear was the film still never amounts anything special xc2 x96 the late 90s altman made successive films set the american south kansas city gingerbread man and cookie fortune unlike gingerbread man both kansas city and cookie fortune tackle the genre the broader more looser canvases that altman was most comfortable with kansas city the more important these two films its hierarchies class politics and crime and its desire break radically away from typical gangster genre frameworks would prove influential all serious 21st century film crime writers see for example the wire that said cookie fortune while much slighter tale perhaps the better picture note altman claims that this his first thriller but directed images art house thriller 1972 worth one viewing
