1 |text tigerland 2000 out four blake french tthroughout the years audiences have seen and understood war films with every point view possible and somehow producers and writers always come with new and innovative methods portraying various soldiers the battlefield joel schumacher 8mm time kill easily one the riskiest directors currently working has found resemblance with the thin red line the way his new drama tigerland steps individual soldier shoes this movie written ross klavan and michael mcguther has more guts and irony than the thin red line even saving private ryan although the movie dramatic impact somewhat lessened due the perversity the material present certainly enlightens new perspective young men training for war would want know joel schumacher experiences with the army are the men really this unabashed and brutal sure some them are but the movie views its uncompromising world through the eyes young man named roland bozz colin farrell who rebellious against the ideas war his personality instantly counteracts with several other characters one who becomes his best friend paxton matthew davis and another wilson russell richardson whose flamed temper often exasperates bozz tension with the idea going war the war depicted this production not found battlefield but training grounds louisiana based instruction camp between conceptions and fears the soldiers training this film specifically about the preparation for war nothing more nothing less ends when the soldiers finally war kind disappointing since witnessing the characters action would have served supurb payoff shot location about days using 16mm stock and minuscule budget joel schumacher accurately displays gritty perverse cruel and unmerciful atmosphere using hand held cinematography unique lighting techniques and direct sound schumacher grainy and blown out images make the movie feel like documentary feature this unusual style filmmaking only contributes the hard core realism the movie quite graphic its use coarse language perhaps little too disturbing waves four letter words pound the audience some shock what they are hearing even the extreme amount vulgarism does not keep the dialogue from prevailing heartbreaking true and emotional tif anything tigerland provides with minor appreciation how much our soldiers through for our country the beginning stages combat such bravery must take enlist the army during times war knowing the hardships and risks that are being taken such thought provoking ideas are made possible through the heartbreaking performances the young aspiring actors who portray the various trainees this movie not for all audiences but one that young men should take look before enlisting themselves the army and adult audiences should watch appreciate the courage needed such
