1 |text new york love you finally makes our shores but its short stories love somehow didn find reason enough released over valentine probably due the fact that this year festival also falls lunar new year and with that comes the usual lny blockbuster films from the likes jackie chan not the spy next door and local filmmaker jack neo who has traditionally released his latest film over that period resounding success why fix formula that hasn been broken continuing concept where paris aime had begun spawning the city love franchise shanghai will next says the end the closing credits here the buzz here definitely about the intertwining stories set one the cities the world allow for various interpretations from filmmakers all over come with stories based love theme although someone probably forgot tell scarlett johansson some the finer points the sandbox ground rules and her short was unceremoniously dropped from the theatrical edition for being unable fit into everything else well was shot black and white but here hoping that would make the dvd least structurally this series less compartmentalized compared its predecessor which memory serves right had individual stories set within its own confines and never really breaking out its artificial borders created here little more leeway given where characters from various stories interact short filler segments used bridge scenes together and not just solely reliant pick shots made buildings and landscapes hopes making things look little bit more serendipitous with the idea chance encounters amongst strangers though one story craftily adopted this mindset for its own narrative deliver surprise though already seen paris one the top draws for sitting through film like this one definitely the creative forces behind the stories from writers directors and cinematographers from various geographies and backgrounds mirroring the makeup the cosmopolitan city coming together for concept film and what more the star studded cast too with big names amongst the lesser known ones all upping the ante through picture perfect performances for the entire length the short support build upon you can deny the initial star gazing recognizing the notables from irrfan khan natalie portman who also had writing and directing duties rachel bilson looking quite like bardot spielberg blue eye boy shia labeouf who surprisingly can act and shows off more his few minutes here than his entire filmography date story wise like any anthology you find some which will automatically appeal you and with others that don some are straightforward nature while others have come with gimmicky twists that thankfully worked but these stories plus because randall balsmeyer was given duties integrate everything together for more organic feel instead just plain pick shots lesser known areas and established landmarks somehow lacked the more anything goes spirit from its predecessor with stories more rooted reality compared some fantastical elements the previous film elijah wood dalliance with vampire anyone even less adventurous with its narrative style christopher doyle and tom tykwer starring natalie portman here seemed that the filmmakers opted very much for safe with none venturing into that spirit adventure and experiment minor quibbles aside still enjoyed almost all the shorts here contrary what many others have felt about the short film format still very much alive and having them strung together into feature under the city love banner works fine and left wondering which other cities are have been included its lineup hoping that perhaps the franchise will catch and spread its influence here surely have enough prolific filmmakers stringing together singapore love you here crossing fingers that maybe something will materialize down the road otherwise there always the sawasdee bangkok route just making without any attachments franchise house rules
