1 |text sammo hung 1989 film pedicab driver considered many his masterpiece have agree some extent the film its greatest parts really gets incredible and fantastic any hong kong film ever has combination pretty good and well written drama interesting and sympathetic and also non sympathetic characters some genuinely funny humor and truly over the top hyper kung that guaranteed make many jaws drop when someone not familiar with hong kong cinema watches the film well does the experienced enthusiasts the unique industry sammo and max mok siu chung play two pedicab drivers who live hong kong the middle part the last century think they drive their cabs and are also desperate for love sammo interested local baker girl ping nina chi while max one day meets mysterious and beautiful fennie yuen kit ying falls madly love with many other characters get introduced too and they remain pretty clear all the time the viewer really concentrates the film and its plot cannot say the film confusing could much worse especially hong kong soon get know for instance that ruthless gangster family terrorizing the neighborhood and course their violent acts affect our protagonists too and the premise for some the most incredibly choreographed kung fight sequences has been created well some nice drama the film has great cast the leads are all very good and restrained not painfully awful over acting and humor sammo otherwise great eastern condors 1987 for example and they are also thanks the carefully written screenplay pretty likable and easy identify with the cast includes many familiar cinema faces and directors small roles like corey yuen kwai the legendary action director and director films like saviour the soul and ninja the dragon den and fong sai yuk and the masterful composer lowell koon ting john woo the killer and ringo lam school fire and prison fire among many others pedicab driver included the shaw veteran liu chia liang whom with sammo has furious fight with sticks alfred cheung kin ting the director dark noir classic the run from 1988 the late great lam ching ying best known for his friendly face various vampire horror kung comedies name just few fact the cast pedicab driver one the most interesting seen any other production the film has some interesting peaceful moments most notably about the love affair between max mok and fennie yuen and one crisis they confront thanks lowell character they really could have done this completely serious piece they had wanted the discussions about human values and meaning love matter what your past what you done for living get serious and genuinely effective the middle part that the film immediately gets much more noteworthy than our average kung spectacle actioner also the other characters efforts cure things very touching and tells delightfully much about right human relations and friendship and course love still think what fennie says max about the future bad cooking very unnecessary and tones the potential the whole segment and its themes down pretty effectively unfortunately but then get the thing the film makers were interested the most which the action the outrageous and over the top action the fight scenes include traditional kung some sticks meat cleavers and the like and they used here hysterically the most mind blowing kung scene seen any film ever jackie chan drunken master 1994 they really are that great there are wires and they used very cleverly and people literally fly the opposite corner the room when they get kicked punched simply amazing and again something only hong kong cinema can deliver also the dangerous stunts make the viewer hold his her breath the film has one fast car pedicab chase sequence and various dangerous looking jumps and twisting bodies flying through the air and crushing with force the hard destination still the film makers seem not accept the violence the film sammo like the late bruce lee willing give himself after the final murderous mayhem the gangster villa and think this kind morale matter how obvious shallow may good thing even harmless film like this cinema meant much more than just brainless entertainment the film has also some very witty bits humor that not sure everyone hollywood america for example would understand like all the hilarious star wars gag the beginning definitely among these and literally forced laugh when realized what was seeing also some funny scenes are created out sammo passion for ping still the greatest amazement filled laugh came during the scenes depicted the former pharagraph the imagery big and tall men flying with great force over the screen the walls furniture simply insane and breathtaking just cannot hide feelings and thoughts about these eastern film makers when witness something like this and this nothing but positive and appreciating reaction course pedicab driver among the most incredible hong kong action films that have ever seen and easily among sammo greatest achievements the few minor flaws were not there this could rate even brighter and higher
