1 |text imagine turning out the lights your remote farmhouse cold night and then going bed there need lock the doors the only sound the wind whistling through the trees sometime after midnight car with lights off inches the driveway moments later intruder beams flashlight into your darkened living room what makes this image scary the setting remote farmhouse night based truman capote best selling book and with lighting comparable the best 1940 noir films cold blood presents terrifying story especially that first act the plot takes place largely night and rain drenched country roads the stuff nightmares but this dream the events really happened 1959 two con men with heads full delusions kill entire kansas family looking for stash cash that doesn exist director richard brooks used the actual locations where the real life events occurred even the farmhouse and its interior makes for memorable and haunting film both the lead actors closely resemble the two real life killers robert blake more than convincing perry smith short and stocky with bum leg who dreams finding cortez buried treasure scott wilson almost good dick hickock the smooth talking con artist with all american smile after their killing spree the duo head mexico things awry there they come back the stealing cars hitchhiking and generally being miserable they roam from place place but fool life and the two outlaws soon regret their actions the film final twenty minutes are mesmerizing the rain falls the rope tightens and all hear the pounding beating heart even with its somewhat mundane middle act cold blood stages riveting detail real life story that still hypnotizes nearly half century later that setting that does you suppose people rural kansas still leave their doors unlocked night
