1 |text this film has powerful philosophical ending but that ending has meaning only you watch the movie from the beginning youth alienation the late 1960 from the viewpoint young man and young woman the obvious theme zabriskie point neither mark frechette nor daria halprin had much acting experience fact that actually enhances the film message having untrained actors conveys sense realism both players seem emotionally detached from the turmoil around them this not script driven film except for the first ten minutes mostly visual with stunning cinematography the beautiful naturalistic images seem other worldly and perfectly sync with the emotional detachment mark and daria would have replaced the thematically weak pink floyd music with the more cogent music the doors many scenes cry out for riders the storm even like this film different unique artistic and imaginative and the desert badlands are beautiful the years zabriskie point seems more and more attractive conveys the mood the late 1960 america amazingly artistic bohemian sort way and the film last eight minutes are philosophically mesmerizing
