1 |text studied charlotte bronte novel high school and left with stunning impression here was beautiful novel about young woman struggle find love and acceptance the dark times victorian england this young woman was jane eyre poor and plain character with strong mind and will her own her story which bronte told through jane own eyes was both sad and inspiring part our study watched the 1983 adaptation the story and blew away the mini series not only made the effort stay true bronte original text and the essence the story but the actors who portrayed the characters were just great both zelah clarke jane eyre and timothy dalton jane lover the name rochester captured brilliantly the essence their characters cannot imagine anyone else their roles the other performances rochester other versions such the 2006 version lack the passion energy and tenderness needed portray rochester accurately say that timothy dalton comes out top because possesses all these characteristics his portrayal rochester zelah clarke not only looks like jane eyre but she captures jane quiet but firm and passionate nature brilliantly she holds her emotions like the jane the book the appropriate moments the story but allows her fire come out jane passionate scenes the chemistry that clarke and dalton portray their scenes together also credible and true jane and rochester devoted relationship well the supporting actors also fit their roles perfectly and the sets fit the gothic nature the story strongly recommend this version the classic bronte tale you have not read the book before then you can watch this production faithful introduction this beautiful story
