1 |text the seemingly endless quest find well made well acted horror films all too rare find one that even comes remotely close hitting the mark needless say was very pleasantly surprised when stumbled across burned the stake cable network while was flipping channels the premise reasonably simple 1692 young ann putnam swift the most vocal witness against alleged witches leveling baseless charges against anyone who earns her displeasure manipulating her for his own ends reverend parris peters who also serves the court guide matters pertaining witchcraft and satanism things get complicated when ann starts accusing members the goode family witchcraft salem 1980 loreen graham also played swift begins having unusual visions shortly before she visits the salem witch museum strange man seventeenth century garb tries accost her there and the building continues stalk her while strange phenomena begin involve her more and more soon appears that she becoming possessed the spirit ann putnam unfortunately further description gets rather involved and would give too much away though the film not action oriented and would likely little interest many viewers the performances are good and the seventeenth century dialogue used the film many flashbacks sounds very convincing the production values are solid with the possible exception some the special effects side note the film technical advisor was laurie cabot salem official witch viewers who appreciate well made atmospheric but understated horror film may appreciate this the writer director bert gordon has had long career horror and science fiction filmmaking and best known for his work number big bug films and similar works years earlier
