d sometimes matter how hard you try you will fail just his father did they are living the same world the same apartment even but they understand things completely different level the theme alienation one that common this era very apparent this film neither joe nor ratso fit into the culture surrounding them joe feels trapped texas and moves nyc where still very much outsider ratso living the cold nyc wishes move sunny florida where thinks will able find good life even though this his ideal the fantasy get from ratso perspective apparent that knows will never really fit into society said fantasy turned the people living around him yet again outsider alienated from society not until the end that the gap between joe and ratso begins narrow joe resorts violence takes the mentality this city order get money fund means escape for florida for himself and ratso the journey see joe coming out store not wearing the cowboy clothes that never without the rest the film dressed someone who looks like they are headed florida for vacation dresses ratso the same way tires make them fit into the new society they are entering but avail upon ratso death the bus their fellow passengers once again look them upon outsiders even this new culture they have entered they cannot escape the alienation they have met every turn this film despite the ratso death and joe continued alienation the film ends with the hope that joe can take his new knowledge how the world works and create better life than would have had hustler nyc midnight cowboy excellent film portraying the harsh reality society and alienation with stellar performances both voight and hoffman
