 wonder how they could have been explained sequel also there the delightful one favorites score leonard rosenman who also scored barry lyndon and star trek the score for which clearly based his lotr work bombastic and audacious and dare say perfect stands own orchestral triumph but when coupled with the images the film enters whole new world symphonic perfection far from the typical hollywoodland fare that turns many people off the voice actors are wonderful particular note john hurt aragorn who just oozes the essence strider the character design also wonderfully unique though not often everyone taste but remember that the duty the director adaptation show you what she imagines not what you might have imagined and aragorn realized with distinctive native american feel and boromir appears viking inspired garb this perhaps not what you imagined but can only applaud bakshi for showing what saw also might noted that spent significant amount time with priscilla tolkien developing the character outfits for the film one farther word the flight the ford sequence opinion one the most subtlety beautiful sequences ever caught celluloid bakshi not afraid slow down the pace for moment and his mastery clearly shown the incredible tension able build bakshi artistic ability and tolkien incredible work fuse this sequence glorious peak which has yet equaled the recent dvd release 2001 warner brothers sorely lacking while can offer our eternal thanks that the film finally available widescreen format the package woefully short extras how glorious would have been have had director commentary been able see the minutes extra footage that were removed for the theatrical release another delightful addition could have been the assembled the live action footage which was later animated over also present the dvd release the utterly horrible voiceover the end the film which departure from the simple voiceover which occurred the very final frames the film this version plastered and poorly rendered right over the musical climax the score course the greatest tragedy all that the sequel was never made will never able see bakshi interpretation gondor shelob faramir the cracks doom eowyn battle with the witch king gandalf confrontation with him will never graced with bakshi image denethor the palatir the paths the dead shame beyond all shames that will the end have accept peter jackson glitz and glitter hollywood action film version these later events tolkien masterpiece but suppose even that better than having cinematic version all david
