rruption that has been behind the full story progression this not detriment all however allows for more fights and car chases that work full context the plot admission this film worth for the apartment fight between bourne and the cia second asset alone the chase jumping through windows madrid cool its own but when they finally meet get ten minute fight that invigorating watch any scene you see also rather than using massive car chase climatic set piece like the first two films instead get around three small scale road races just intense but staggered enough never bog the action down into monotony after five years waiting also find out the origin our favorite operative with heart and feeling the end the film will find out what has been the cause all the espionage and destruction that has taken place around him one could have done better than matt damon has the physique and attitude believable the action sequences but also the range pull off the moments intelligence and cat and mouse correspondence with those against him joan allen reprises her role with the same amount dedication her job but also bit more disenchantment for what going around her after how brian cox character from the first two films took matters into his own hands needing role that mold are given nice turn from david strathairn like cox working the top the food chain and answers one when making decision with much trying cover any connections his bosses the blackbriar program trying his duty his country you can never quite gauge what will capable doing even the little guys wonderful job like paddy considine the reporter who starts the leak the center everything albert finney man from bourne past and possibly key his origin and edgar ramirez one the cia operatives sent take bourne out ramirez nice addition the role that has been successfully played clive owen identity karl urban and martin csokas supremacy doesn talk much all but has the look and robotic efficiency down pat and hopefully will get more roles show what can post nice turn domino the end one has applaud paul greengrass for continuing exceed expectations and bring this series conclusion that builds the success its predecessors rather than destroy them his skill the close hand held look astonishing and has the same kinetic energy tony scott but without quite the seizure inducing cuts rather than feel like over production his use hand held enhances the environment and puts you directly into the action let also credit cinematographer oliver wood who shot all three bourne films was able work with both directors and work his style into nice harmony with them
