1 |text sergio martino the case the scorpion tail scenic giallo from the early heyday the genre explosion aeroplane results one million dollars insurance money for bereaved but unfaithful wife the money subsequently snatched black clad assassin and series brutal murders follow scorpion tail plays the mystery element written giallo specialist ernesto gastaldi fairly straight but being giallo the murders themselves are memorable and well staged fact the violence this movie very strong places scene with broken bottle being particularly graphic the emphasis the violence doubt influencing the giallo genre move into more and more extreme territory but like the best films the genre the brutality offset good score and attractive photography the music bruno nicolai times reminiscent ennio morricone avant garde work the bird with the crystal plumage but also strong its own right the photography helped the nice use foreign locales this case london and athens where martino manages get respectively the houses parliament and the acropolis there also some inventive camera work too the most effective being the use slow motion sequence where woman runs towards the door where the maniac prowling outside this particular scene martino has the killer hack through the door with knife manner influenced dario argento crystal plumage however also has the killer attempt flick the latch open with the blade knife which something repeated later argento suspiria martino film influential its own right this good solid giallo that both genre and non genre fans can appreciate the performances are good and the production values are fine although the plane explosion shall say somewhat low budget the dvd release noshame nice has both the english and italian language options which real bonus however worth pointing out that times you need fast reader fully appreciate the english subtitle option this applies both the movie and the documentary the extras this minor point though the dvd release worthy addition any giallo collection
