1 |text american paris was many ways the ultimate mixture art and hollywood musical made the height mgm powers musical powerhouse the film features memorable music from the gershwins who rightly have been called the 20th century equivalent beethoven and mozart gene kelly was also the height his powers this film though could rightly argued that this movie was just the warm for his best work singin the rain 1952 the two films are actually closely linked aside from the arthur freed connection the broadway melody segment rain owes its existence the incredible american paris ballet sequence this film this might well have been the only time dance number specially mentioned the opening credits the film and deserved showcases gene kelly skills dancer and choreographer their utmost degree the film cast uniformly excellent leslie caron incredibly making her film debut shows maturity that makes you think she been making films for years her introductory dance sequence and later her work the ballet provides some surprisingly sexy moments rivalled mgm musicals only cyd charisse work singin the rain and the band wagon oscar levant hilarious kelly stoic pal who gets two the film best moments during the end party sequence which will not give away for anyone who hasn seen the film and one the film most memorable musical numbers which couples his incredible piano skills with state the art for the time special effects less memorable are georges guetary kelly romantic rival though does get few musical highlights and nina foch leslie caron romantic rival the may december relationship between kelly character and nina reminded the same kept man relationship seen between george peppard and patricia neal breakfast tiffany there are few elements the film that made less satisfying for than singin the rain the ballet though lavish and well produced doesn really fit with the rest the movie without giving away the plot the ballet just happens with real rhyme reason and unlike the broadway melody sequence really doesn have anything with the plot and the best musicals the songs always have some sort raison etre making matters worse the ending the film which happens immediately after the ballet although the ending shouldn surprise this mgm musical after all was hoping for bit more movie after the ballet ended director vincente minnelli felt that couldn follow the ballet with anything else the film literally left the lurch that negative aside american paris rightly ranks alongside the best hollywood musicals doesn quite reach the heights singin the rain but comes close and remains testament gene kelly skills one the greatest dancers all time
