1 |text saw this film the toronto international film festival filmed during actual qualifying match for the 2006 world cup offside works brilliantly both comedy and tragedy the film follows the fortunes group young women who are caught trying sneak into football match tehran azadi stadium the country islamic religious leaders have decreed that women may not sit with men sporting events lest they exposed cursing and other morally questionable behaviour this hasn stopped the country young female fans who continue sneak using various tricks but panahi focuses small group who have been caught and are being detained agonizingly close the action they beg the bored soldiers guarding them let them least let them watch the match the soldiers tell them they shouldn have tried get that they could have watched the game home they banter back and forth almost real time the game continues just off camera there one very funny sequence where young soldier accompanies one the girls the restroom since there are female restrooms stadiums has clear the room any men before can allow her plus makes her cover her face one can see she woman this accomplished using poster iranian soccer star ali daei mask with eye holes punched out you get real sense that even the soldiers are baffled the prohibition and are only carrying out their orders hasten the end their compulsory military service one soldier complains that was supposed leave could take care his family cattle the countryside little little the girls and the soldiers talk each other and there are numerous small acts kindness both sides show that these are basically good people living terrible circumstances however the soldiers constant reminder that the chief his way lends sense menace since don know what sort punishment the women will face unlike most iranian films which are known for their strong visuals offside filmed realist style with artifice fact the film was made during the actual qualifying match against bahrain that took place june 2005 the plot many ways was determined the result the pitch iran won the match they would qualify they lost they would not since the world cup has come and gone don think spoiler say that iran won the match the scenes celebration the end the film were real and spontaneous which gave the film real authenticity seeing how much this meant the people iran was deeply touching well one the young women makes reference the end the film seven fans who died during the iran japan match march just few weeks before they were trampled death after police began spray the crowd with water move them certain direction knowing that this was real life tragedy added another level poignancy the celebrations don want off long political tangent but this film gave real hope that there are those iran who are hoping for change and working iran nation young people and only matter time before they take the place their elders the political sphere films like this one show the proud spirit the iranian people spite their present difficulties and sincere hope that there brighter future for them
