1 |text this series could very well the best britcom ever and that saying great deal considering the competitors fawlty towers good neighbours name just two what made butterflies superior even the best the best that did not just exemplify great classic classy and intelligent comedy but also expanded horizons reflecting flawlessly gently and every detail the great social change that was occurring britain the time remember watching this show teenager and being awe everything about the lifestyle depicted was remarkable itself this was the first time saw real people using cordless phones and the wardrobe all the characters was far removed from the goofy seventies attire still seen north america the time then there were the decors shop fronts cars these people even the layabout sons with their philosophical approach life and epigrammatic humor were sophisticated they were examples the new europeans that would come have impact life and style throughout the world the coming decade 1980s course the premise was strange and fantastic the idea that someone who was living the suburban dream could discontent and restless was revolutionary particularly north americans for whom happiness was always defined money and things sure the situation was depicted american movies and but not with the intensity butterflies the movie montenegro and the premise was not surprising enough the means which was expressed took the extreme potential affair that was not really about sex even romance butterflies dazzled many but must have left some people smacking their foreheads disbelief the time anyway butterflies turned out many ways prophetic documented ahead its time post modern ennui all pervasive lifestyle the notion emotional infidelity and generational disconnect and male discontent portrayed perfectly the strained father son relationships too bad this series has not been rediscovered big way and all those involved given credit for creating meaningful snapshot certain time and place and foreseeing all the slickness and angst that was come
