1 |text cold blood adapted director richard brooks from truman capote famous novel deals with the brutal and senseless murder family four pair hapless criminals the film excels character study the killers particularly trigger man perry smith robert blake the cast includes few recognizable names but they nevertheless bring the story life with ease robert blake and scott wilson are excellent together two criminals with disparate personalities they play off each other effortlessly while blake also gets plenty opportunities explore his character idiosyncrasies the rest the cast merely average and isn worth remarking richard brooks received oscar nominations for both his script and his direction opinion both were excellent though the script does miscalculate with some ill advised narration the late stages the oscar nominated cinematography conrad hall also top notch the editing also worthy note the jazzy score quincy jones which secured the last the film four oscar nominations unlike many other crime films this one doesn glamorize violence brooks turns the killers into pitiable characters rather than flatly condemning them whether not you agree with that sentiment the film does present interesting alternative the usual hollywood approach recommend the film for this reason and also for the expertise with which the technical aspects are handled
