1 |text had the pleasure attending screening the pacific and eddy last weekend the santa barbara international film festival this film had caught attention little while back when stumbled across article about jalouse magazine seemed interesting the time but nothing too exciting anyhow saw the festival program and decided check out all can say that was speechless when the ending credits began roll this one the most beautiful and refreshing films that have seen some time the photography art direction acting and especially directing were seamless and impeccable nothing spelled out for you this film and actually makes you think something that vast majority films today the exact opposite the dialogue carefully crafted and although this script not wall wall chatter the characters words are very deliberate and meaningful definitely one those films that deserves second viewing and the more you see the more things you notice very layered and intelligent film not sure when where playing again but definite must see for film enthusiasts
1 |text they did and boy did they fantastically what the bbc finally brought the doctor back our screens saturday evening where belongs and they did with style episode one rose one the strengths the new series russel davies writer and executive producer fan the show and knows what the other fans want but also experienced writer his own right knows what other people want another strength perfectly shown here this first episode billie piper and her character rose tyler finally the doctor companion gets credible back story and strong character also nice see the return the autons nice nod the classic series there episode two the end the world the start this double bill show off the tardis strengths end story where special effects everything they now have the technology create real believable environments and monsters more rubber suits sorts also the hints the end this episode regarding the new doctor past very intriguing kill off all the time lords and make him the only one episode three the unquiet dead had the future now lets have the past the first non davies written episode little flat some places but this made for simon callow charles dickens and the sudden twist the plot when revealed the pitiful gelf are not pitiful after all episode four aliens london the consequences the doctor actions are fully explored this series not least with the repercussions rose running off with him also have our first cliffhanger not the best ones admittedly the slitheen are interesting villain though they can look too cgi for their own good episode five world war three the second part this story about the slitheen suffers mainly from the same problems the first also the clips from the next episode coming the end the current episode are annoying and spoil for people episode six dalek yes had the future the past and the present ish but now get the good stuff the return the doctor arch nemesis here think can complement christopher ecclestone was brilliant the doctor and more then this episode where see the pain his face recollects the time war and the alien nature him almost turns into dalek himself episode seven the long game really only story act prologue for the series finale saved simon pegg the smarmy editor and tamsin grieg amusing cameo the media are controlling that never been done before has episode eight father day this great episode full human emotion and heartache for rose and the true consequences what happens when you really muck history full marks billie piper here episode nine the empty child don find this kid very scary sorry but don good episode though but the cliffhanger still could have been better those next time bits that spoil them john barrowman introduced here captain jack the dashing conman good actor who been around for while but only seemingly noticed now episode ten the doctor dances part two this ww2 story very well made historical context terms nice upbeat ending though little confusing perhaps for younger viewers when the mummy revealed episode eleven boom town probably the weakest the series but that doesn mean its bad nice return for the slitheen and also interesting character study the doctor and rose episode twelve bad wolf this starts off quite silly with some good hearted humour and cheeky fun making popular shows over her blighty things turn deadly serious quickly though and the revelation the end the best cliffhanger the series episode thriteen parting the ways goodbye christopher ecclestone fantastic doctor many ways david tennant having really work his socks off good him the regeneration scene the end beautifully played and the daleks are back the extreme god bless cgi because they never able pull this off normally overall brilliant
