1 |text wow wow wow have never seen non preachy documentary globalization until saw mardi gras made china this film has zero narration and combines verite footage with sensitive interviews with four teenage workers china who live inside factory compound they play with toys jump rope and dance yet the majority their days and nights consist work work and work but the footage their work illuminating and mesmerizing watch the owner the factory china amazingly open much that hits home the effects globalization while punishes the workers astutely following mardi gras beads from china the carnival the film reveals how the local connected the global through humor and interesting compelling footage from both cultures one the most interesting parts this film the cross cultural introduction factory workers and mardi gras revelers each other through pictures here the film comes full circle and shows how images can point communication and transformation the film never preachy not guilt driven and allows everyone point view present the end the viewers make our own conclusions about the complexity the film and globalization
