1 |text the first step getting off that road that leads nowhere recognizing that you the first place then becomes matter being assertive and taking positive steps overcome the negative influences your life that may have put you that road begin with which exactly what young latino girl does girlfight written and directed karyn kusama diana michelle rodriguez eighteen year old high school senior from the projects brooklyn facing expulsion after her fourth fight the halls since the beginning the semester she affects whatever attitude which masks deep seated anger that threatens take her into places she rather not she lives with her father sandro paul calderon with whom she has very tentative relationship and her younger brother tiny ray santiago with her life teetering the brink dissolution she desperately needs outlet through which channel the demons that plague her and one day she finds without even looking for when she stops the gym where tiny trains ironically tiny wants nothing with boxing wants art school but sandro determined that his son should able take care himself the streets and pays the ten dollars week costs for his lessons when diana convinces tiny trainer hector jaime tirelli take her and approaches her father for the money under the guise calling weekly allowance she doesn want him know what she wants the money for sandro turns her down and tells her out and earn her own money ultimately with tiny help she finds way and the ring soon becomes her second home environment which she readily adapts and appears that her life about take turn for the better and the fact that she will have fight men not women gender blind competitions does not faze her the least diana has found her element tfirst time writer director karyn kusama has done terrific job creating realistic setting for her story presenting honest portrait life the projects and conveying that desperation familiar many young people who find themselves dead end situations and that road that leads nowhere and there candy coating either hector tells diana when she asks him how came where was fighter once lost then looking around the busy gym like most these guys they going lose too but all they know and that honesty attitude well the way which the characters are portrayed that makes this movie good bleak world underscored the dimly lit run down gym you can fairly smell the sweat the boxers and that sense desolation that hangs over all like pall blanketing these people who are grasping and hanging the one and only thing they have all that they know tmaking her screen debut michelle rodriguez perfectly cast diana infusing her with depth and brooding intensity that fairly radiates off her waves she real that makes you wonder how much really rodriguez exactly where does the actor leave off and the character begin whatever works powerful memorable performance actor from whom will await another endeavor with great anticipation she certainly makes diana positive role model one whom many hopefully will find inspiration and the realization that there are alternative paths available life least those who would seek them out tas positive this film however ends something ambiguous note though diana obviously has her feet the ground there indication where she headed this short term fix for her she destined become the female counterpart hector after all realistically and light the fact that the realism one the strengths this film professional boxing isn exactly profession that lends itself nor opens arms women and keeping with the subject matter the film and the approach the filmmaker affirmation the results diana assertiveness would have been appropriate tthe supporting cast includes santiago douglas adrian elisa bocanegra marisol alicia ashley ricki and thomas barbour ira though delivers very real picture life which many will able identify there are certain aspects girlfight that stretch credibility bit regarding some what happens the ring that aside positive film that for the most part satisfying experience rate this one
