1 |text after brief prologue showing masked man stalking and then slashing the throat older gentleman deserted urban turn the century australian street meet julie rebecca gibney and peter john adam they out house hunting they manage get loan for fixer upper posh sydney street but turns out that physical disrepair not the only problem with their new home just may haunted gantry row combines memorable somewhat clich xc3 xa9d story with good average direction catherine millar into slightly above average shocker the biggest flaws seem partially due budget but not wholly excusable that hurdle crucial problem occurs the beginning the film the opening thriller scene features some wonky editing freeze frames and series stills are used cover the fact that there not much action suspense should created from staging not fancy fix the mix techniques there great atmosphere the scene from the location the lighting the fog and such but the camera should slowly following the killer and the victim cutting back and forth from one the other track down the street showing their increasing proximity the tracking and the cuts need slow the attack needed longer clearer and better blocked stands the scene has strong made for television feel and low budget one that after this scene move the present and the flow the film greatly improves the story has lot similarities the amityville horror 1979 though the budget forces much subtler approach millar and scriptwriter tony morphett effectively create lot slyly creepy scenarios often dramatic nature instead special effects oriented such the mysterious man who arrives take away the old slabs iron which had been bizarrely affixed interior wall for some horror fans the first section the film might little heavy realist drama least the first half hour the film primarily about julie and peter trying arrange financing for the house and then trying settle but morphett writes fine intelligent dialogue the material done well enough that often suspenseful the more traditional thriller aspects that arise later especially you gone through similar travails while trying buy your own house once they get settled and things begin get weirder even though the special effects often leave much desired the ideas are good the performances help create tension there isn abundance death and destruction the film there more abundance home repair nightmares but neither menace really the point the point human relationships there are number character arcs that are very interesting the house exists more metaphor and catalyst for stress romantic relationship that can make sour and possibly destroy that posh neighborhood and that the relationship between two successful yuppies shows that these problems not only afflict those who can place blame with some external woe such money health problems peter character evolves from striving corporate employee with normal work based friendships someone with more desperation becomes subversive scheming attain something more liberating and meaningful the same time learn just how shallow those professional friendships can julie goes through almost literal nervous breakdown but finally finds liberation when she liberates herself from her failing romantic relationship although gantry row never quite transcends its made for television clunkiness movie this pretty good one with admirable ambitions anyone fond haunted house films psycho films horror thrillers with bit more metaphorical depth should find plenty enjoy certainly isn worth spending for dvd that was the price local pbs station was asking for copy the film after they showed factoring shipping and handling but worth rental and definitely worth watching for free
