1 |text wow stacy peralta has followed dogtown and boys with equally stunning documentary about the history the big wave surfing culture america piecing together insider archival footage along with interviews from surfing legends are transported into the daring and free spirited life the early pioneers whose sheer passion for the sport spawned industry that today touches the lives millions getting know these icons and their stories that gives the film its warmth you can feel the respect peralta has for this group hear accounts greg noll striding from pack awestruck fellow surfers the beach singularly challenge foot swells off hawaii north coast jeff clark surfing the outrageously dangerous maverick off the northern california coast all alone for years before was discovered and became the surfing destination california and the storybook history laird hamilton today surfing icon hearing greg noll reverently refer hamilton the best surfer ever sent chills spine aside noll clark and others were the sundance screenings noll humbly described himself old over the hill surfer was deeply moved the audience reception him and film both and clark were likable person they were the film riding giants pays homage these extraordinary athletes while the same time rewarding with insight into the magnitude and terrifying power the waves they seek conquer the gut wrenching vertical drops required get into them and the almost unfathomable combination adrenaline and fear that the surfers experience each time they take monster swell all this and the movie has more for those that didn live california the get insight into the impact surfing american pop culture and surprise the impact the movie gidget surfing peralta also weaves primer some the technical aspects the sport and the history innovation equipment not surfer but like the rest the sundance audience was absolutely captivated this film peralta staking his claim the big kahuna american documentaries
