1 |text was lucky enough catch this movie while volunteering the maryland film festival always been fan classic horror films and especially the gimmicks william castle this was definitely must see for this about the life and work william castle who opinion was underrated director true made some cheap budget schlocky horror films but added something these films real live theater gimmicks that you don see anymore for example had nurses case someone had heart attack his movies and put vibrators the bottoms chairs the tingler this truly well made documentary and brings this rather shadowed director into the light and celebrated his contributions horror cinema also paints castle larger than life character who was very well liked and had smile his face unlike most film documentaries that mostly show testaments from film historians spine tingler shows interviews mostly from his family members and directors who were influenced his work such john waters john landis and joe dante must see for classic horror and sci fans
