1 |text the only reason knew midnight cowboy was because was the afi critic top 100 for top 100 not very well known movie indeed had look hard find copy got the dvd version for about half price surprisingly was only rated m15 the uncut version doubt many will take notice this review more like comment make brief this perhaps one the strangest movies seen partly because the use montages artistic filming very art house and the unusual theme there are many things the film still don understand seen twice and makes for emotionally confusing film the filming and acting were very good and the larger than life characters which make this film memorable the main character joe buck cowboy from texas who moves new york become male prostitute meets the crippled conman enrico ratso rizzo and course they become friends going through the usual escapades what makes the film interesting the two characters are different felt the film didn really develop the relationship between buck and enrico rizzo for the audience have any real emotional connection although the ending certainly quite sad and tragic you probably already know what happens reading the reviews but its pretty obvious from the start personally think the film beautifully and poignantly explores its main themes the deprivation humanity shown the darkness the city streets the breaking down tenements most the characters the film exist beyond the law conman giggolo etc yet you can help liking them joe buck endearing because naive and optimistic while begin feel pity for ratso later the film think the film was rated high because was certainly very ground breaking for its period the time and even now was definitely not typical movie quite art house time when the cinema was dominated tired westerns musicals and dramas film with such unusual theme midnight cowboy pops personal level must say quite liked the film the imagery conveyed dream like quality particularly liked the scene the party the music images etc stay your mind for long time after watching however movie for entertainment sake was bit lacking not really style movie thrills this film savoured and appreciated rather than cheap thrills action flick although would hardly consider myself qualified analyse this film the characters and their motives were quite interesting from what understand from the flashbacks joe buck was sexually abused child his grandmother although still doesn seem relevant the story happy lucky young stud who suppresses his darker memories the religious connotations the film are also puzzling some have suggested homosexual connection between buck and ratso although fail see where they have got the idea from the theme homo sexuality general more than touched upon their conversation and later joe buck encounter with lonely old man but has little with the main story certainly from technical point view one the finest films the decade has more 70s feel than 60s feel and revolutionary for its time touching subjects few other films dared while has simple sentimental story disguised hard edge the beauty the film the strange often psychedelic sequences
