1 |text you cannot enjoy chick flick stop right now however you enjoy films that illustrate complex characters and provide extraordinary acting read ann grant lord dying her two daughters arrive her bedside ann begins talking about people from her past whom the daughters are unaware and they question whether these lost acquaintances are real imagined they come realize that these people from their mother past are indeed real the story shifts basically between 1953 and circa 2000 with few glimpses ann life between those years was 1953 that ann met the love her life and experienced her life greatest tragedy one ann two best friends from college lila being married ann other best friend lila brother buddy lila and buddy are the children rich newport family whereas ann cabaret singer living greenwich village who wants free spirit but still bound many those 1950 conventions soon after ann arrives maid honor lila wedding she meets the person who will become the pivotal character the lives the three harris the adult son former servant the family who grew with lila and buddy and has gone become physician small new england town ann immediately becomes enamored harris which adds complication the fact that lila has always been love with harris and continues buddy also love with harris but being 1953 has redirected that homosexual desire for harris his good friend ann for cannot admit himself that has sexual craving for another man buddy exhibits his inner frustration outwardly being the alcoholic wise cracking bad boy the family much the chagrin his very proper and uptight parents needless say all these expressed and repressed emotions lead tragedy after all this chick flick the present time ann daughters have become distant from their mother and are suffering their own life realizations and doubts constance working emotional exhaustion trying keep her roll perfect mother and wife nina having always felt inferior cannot maintain relationship stir all these relationships into span fifty years and you get intriguing look society its values and its effects upon the personalities and actions the complex people involved all the acting evening excellent but there are some extraordinary performances and scenes along with two unique family relationships that make this film very very special claire danes plays the 1950 ann and she does style that clearly shows intelligent woman those times who conflicted what she supposed opposed what she wants her performance not easily forgettable vanessa redgrave plays the dying ann whose mind shifts from the present the past flights fantasy and course redgrave pulls all off with sterling style natasha richardson redgrave real daughter plays ann daughter constance the film the scenes between this real life mother and daughter playing fictional mother and daughter are insightful treat watch toni collette plays ann other daughter nina nina spends good deal her time being depressed and feeling sorry for herself while shutting out good man who loves her well her mother and sister collette perfect for part such this but have never seen her give bad unbelievable performance matter what part she plays mamie gummer plays 1950 lila and shows woman even more conflicted her expected role life than her good friend ann she very good meryl streep gummer mother plays present day lila what there say about meryl streep other than she always gives insightful and rewarding performance director lajos koltai states the dvd extras that sought out glenn close play the relatively small part lila mother because felt she was the only actress could think play one scene the film certainly was right and close performance that one scene etches your mind all the other scenes which close lila very proper mother and you get another performance treasure there are three other scenes the film combined with the one featuring close described above that make the whole movie worth watching lila wedding day ann comes into her room and crawls into bed with her friend discuss lila misforgivings about her upcoming wedding man she clearly does not love this scene repeated fifty years later when lila comes and crawls into bed with her dying friend ann talk about the lives they have lived this latter scene streep and redgrave are enthralling the other memorable scene least when buddy declares his love for ann hugh dancy buddy gives heartbreaking performance young man torn apart his conflicting sexual feelings his performance superior chick flick yes very special film with unbelievable acting directing and scenery definitely cannot recommend evening too much
