1 |text this 1981 comedy still sparkles thanks the combined efforts writer director steve gordon and stars dudley moore and john gielgud sadly gordon only his early forties died soon after completing this his only feature film especially unfortunate loss since shows truly deft hand character driven farce that makes the whole film irresistible plays almost like 1930 style screwball comedy revamped for contemporary tastes the plot centers arthur bach drunken diminutive millionaire playboy who risk losing his 750 million inheritance doesn marry the dowdy and boring susan johnson heiress handpicked his old money father and dotty grandmother course doesn love her and chance runs into linda marolla working class waitress and course aspiring actress after she pilfers bergdorf goodman tie for her father the standard complications ensue but most endearing way with loads alcohol fueled slapstick executed with classic xc3 xa9lan moore that makes such spoiled character likable credit not only his comic talents but gielgud feisty acidic turn hobson arthur devoted but reality grounded valet the type role could play his sleep but gielgud makes hobson such truly memorable character that his fate the film brings welcome injection poignancy the proceedings probably her most likable film role liza minnelli hands the picture her male stars toning down her usual razzle dazzle personality and making linda quite genuine motivation pre law jill eikenberry plays susan just the right passive aggressive note while barney martin jerry dad seinfeld steals all his scenes linda slovenly father ralph the one fly the ointment veteran actress geraldine fitzgerald who overdoes the eccentricities the grandmother and have admit that still can stand the very dated overplayed christopher cross song that inevitably won the oscar for that year best song unfortunately the 1997 dvd certainly need remastering has extras worth noting except some photos and production notes
