1 |text sherman set the wayback machine for 1986 the united states was just climbing out its worst postwar recession while japan was enjoying unprecedented industrial boom manufacturing industries were still significant part the economy and factory workers were good example the average american the word downsizing hadn entered the general vocabulary yet but everyone knew the phenomenon bruce could heard the radio singing foreman says these jobs are going boy and they ain coming back your hometown chrysler had just been bailed out uncle sam bumper stickers could seen saying buy american the job you save may your own gung does better job capturing the mood the american industrial workforce than just about any other popular movie made during that period certainly the movie has its flaws some loose plot threads and mediocre acting jobs everyone except michael keaton and gedde watanabe but the story really about the meeting east and west keaton hunt stevenson personifies america brash and confident the outside yet insecure underneath watanabe kazuhiro personifies japan top the heap with successful system but wondering there more learned from their western rivals the movie plot flawed simply provides framework for the conflict and eventually synthesis their two personalities keaton acting overshadows everyone else and practically makes the movie itself always admired keaton for his ability deliver lines that feel improvised matter what script following his character hunt stevenson likable affable everyman natural leader with wise ass streak but has fatal flaw common many doesn want disappoint anyone distract the crowd with inspirational anecdotes and even lie rather than point out the ugly truth kazuhiro the mirror image stevenson shy and introspective but also because his japanese upbringing reluctant the bearer bad news the scene which stevenson first comes kazuhiro with the employees grievances captures perfectly the japanese approach workplace conflict kazuhiro replies stevenson complaints with understand what you are saying but won refuse his requests out loud stevenson misinterprets this agreement and goes away saying okay got that settled this still problem japanese american business relations the 21st century ultimately kazuhiro and stevenson have the same problem get the factory working smoothly meet production goals and fulfill their responsibility the workers under them working towards this goal they each have take page from the others book kazuhiro family becoming more americanized obvious example also note that stevenson thinks odd when kazuhiro explains how had make public apology his workers for failing them and yet later the movie stevenson does exactly that himself the plot and its resolution are little cornball but hey this comedy you can overlook the movie flaws there great story about self realization and open mindedness here
