-1 |text relative latecomer the transcendent work film auteur yasujiro ozu whose masterfully understated views japanese life especially the post wwii era illuminate universal truths having now seen several his landmark films such 1949 late spring and 1953 tokyo story convinced that ozu had particularly idiosyncratic gift conveying the range feelings arising from intergenerational conflict through elliptical narratives and subtle imagery taiwanese director hou hsiao hsien keen aspiration pay homage ozu his centenary with this generally enervating 2003 film among with screenwriter ien wen chu hsiao hsien appears get the visuals right but does not capture the requisite emotional weight that would have made the glacial pacing tolerable the story concerns xc3 xb4ko young japanese writer researching the life mid 20th century taiwanese composer jiang wen tokyo after coming back from taiwan where she taught japanese after drawn out minutes character set she reveals her father and stepmother that she pregnant one her students taiwan the same time xc3 xb4ko coffeehouse friend hajime who runs used bookstore has obsession for trains and seems likely love with her hsiao hsien connects this slim plot line with series shots held for inordinately lengthy takes the frame composition changes there are also long stretches silence well abundance scenes featuring trains while these techniques are consistent with ozu style hsiao hsien cannot seem dive into the characters psyches the way ozu did with maximal fluidity and minimal theatrics particular xc3 xb4ko plight seems rather non committal the scheme the drama presented and her parents reaction overly passive hold much interest fact the whole film has atmosphere exhaustion about which makes the film feel interminable the performances are unobtrusive though hardly memorable pop music star hitoto brings natural ease xc3 xb4ko while tadanobu asano something cipher hajime the rest the characters barely register even nenji kobayashi and kimiko xc3 xb4ko parents cinematographer lee ping bing provides expert work though violates cardinal rule ozu films not keeping the camera stable during shots hitoto speak sings the fetching pop song used over ending credits hito shian the dvd includes hour long french made documentary xc3 xa9tro lumi xc3 xa8re which actually does help provide some the context for hsiao hsien approach the film includes excerpts from ozu films particular equinox flower show the parallels with this film though surprisingly mention either tokyo story early summer the obvious basis for some the scenes and situation set ups there are also edited interview clips hitoto asano and hsiao hsien well the film trailer
