1 |text the year reign queen victoria perhaps one the most documented and popularly known historical reigns british history the one hand her story lacks the theatrics earlier royals thanks change social climate and attitudes and the other her story one that perpetuates because notably human taking the earlier years her life where the budding romance between herself and the german prince albert was taking forefront director jean marc vall xc3 xa9e who has only until recently remained the unbeknownst shadows the industry here takes victoria story and captures that human element vital her legacy story that feels extremely humble considering its exuberant background and yet that partly what gives distinct edge here that separates from the usual fare taking very direct and focused approach that centres brief five year period between her ascension and marriage albert the young victoria does what little period pieces this nature offer instead attempting sprawling encapsulation such figure entire life vall xc3 xa9e instead opts show one the lesser known intricacies victoria early years which are easily overlooked favour the more publicly known accolades the result feature that may disgruntle historians thanks its relatively flippant regards facts and the like yet never let document get the way extracting compelling story writer julian fellowes sticks his guns and delivers slightly romanticised yet convincing portrayal vall xc3 xa9e takes this and runs making sure fully capitalise those elements with enough restraint maintain integrity regards both the history involved and the viewer watching major part the joy watching the young victoria play out however simply lies the production values granted here that bring early 1800 regal britain life with vigorous realism rarely achieved quite strikingly genre films everything from the costume designs sets hair styles lighting and photography accentuates the grandiose background inherent victoria story without ever over encumbering indeed while watching vall xc3 xa9e interpretation come life here very hard not sucked solely through the aesthetics that permeates the visual element and then there the film score also which works tremendously further the very elegant yet personal tones that dominate fellowes script entwining the works schubert and strauss into victoria and albert story not only works point reference for the characters play with but also melds the work with elegance and refrain that echoes composer ilan eshkeri original work just well yet for all the poignant compositions lush backdrops and immaculate costumes that punctuate every scene the single most important factor here xc2 x97and indeed most period dramas xc2 x97are the performances the cast and how they help bring the world they exist life thankfully the young victoria blessed with equally immaculate ensemble thespians both young and old that fantastic job doing just that between the sweet budding romance victoria emily blunt and albert rupert friend and the somewhat antagonistic struggles her advisors and the like spearheaded terrific mark strong and paul bettany the conflicts and warmth prevalent fellowe screenplay are conveyed perfectly here all involved which helps keep the movie from being plastic nice look but dim underneath affair common with these outings the end hard fault work such the young victoria got perfectly touching and human sense affection within its perfectly paced romance plus some historical significance that plays intriguing source interest for those the audience keen such details course may not take the cinematic world storm and there lacks certain significance its overall presence that stops from ever becoming more than just poignantly restrained romantic period drama yet sense this what makes enjoyable vall xc3 xa9e never seems striving for grandeur nor does seem content making run the mill escapist piece for aficionados somewhere within this gray middle ground lies the young victoria sure cater genre fans and those little more disillusioned the usual productions beautiful memorable but most all human review jamie robert ward http www invocus net
