-1 |text saw chan missing when first came out about four years after moving from san francisco new york maybe was the perspective few years away but this movie seemed capture the essence the city and its people better than anything else ever seen still does concentrates one particular community the chinese but that fine because much the city soul refracted through the settings the faces and the maybe above all the voices the characters this isn the tourists san francisco the settings are humble and everyday taxi cab the kitchen chinese restaurant richmond district row houses little chinatown apartments and small business offices the piers philippine elder center this what the city looks and feels like day day the people who live there even now the era silicon gulch urban redevelopment unlike say dirty harry its own way excellent san francisco movie well everything filmed street level come understand the characters points view from the perspective their surroundings give them not from some fancy vertiginous shooting wang apparently filmed because didn have the money otherwise yet one the strongest visual elements the movie the natural light achieves the often harsh pervasive quality the sunlight one closest associations with san francisco seems expose everything bringing the buildings the hills the other landmarks down scale and funny way making the people you pass the streets seem more individual and potentially closer you than they might another place wang photography perfectly conveys this and even helps the story along points wang captures the speech and conversational style chinese and other san franciscans better than anyone ever has think there such thing true san francisco accent what you hear from the balding taxi medallion broker think who appears talking the phone one scene listen the way calls the person the other end dingaling the story poignant and despite few very small missteps makes its points beautifully about the longings that pull the hearts people living old immigrant communities including the justified political and ethnic resentments and little ironic amusements that help fuel them all this communicated delicately perhaps why some respondents here think the film meanders doesn suffice say that the two cab drivers quest for chan becomes quest for something more personal chan missing finishes with chinatown travelogue sequence backed goofy novelty song from the 1930s guess about san francisco and all its crazy diversity american caricature yes but somehow not entirely off the mark either
