1 |text retitled from its original japanese name laputa for being offensive phrase something which director hayao miyazaki was oblivious the time castle the sky the master animator third film and one his most beloved all time initially box office disappointment its 1986 release has since been embraced critics and audiences around the world inspired jonathan swift gulliver travels castle the sky steampunk themed action adventure tale about two young orphans young miner pazu and mysterious girl sheeta who wears magic crystal around her neck who team find the long lost island laputa which rumored have great riches and gems they are aided band bumbling yet sympathetic air pirates led the feisty dola who first chase them yet turn out true allies and pursued the government headed its villainous topmost secret agent muska who wants the power laputa for his own benefit for anyone looking for exciting way spend two hours this film excellent choice featuring just the right amount humor exploration wonder and mystery keep one interested the artwork although not spectacular some miyazaki later movies fantastic and gorgeous enough watch with imaginative characters and locations incredibly exciting action scenes and breathtaking flight sequences that will make one feel giddy and while the characters that populate this tale are less complex than miyazaki other works each has memorable endearing personality that stays with the viewer long after the film over dola particular makes for terrific comic character shouting orders her dimwitted sons one moment and being protective sheeta the next muska one the few miyazaki creations ever come across irredeemable villain but like dola commands every scene with sinister charisma that both alluring and chilly anime fans have often compared this movie gainax sci adventure series nadia the secret blue water after all both works share similar story and character elements not mention that they were both created miyazaki himself where both differ their execution nadia although charming for the most part suffered from taking wrong turn its midway point devolving into cartoonish nonsense which all but distracted from the main plot even though did have strong ending castle the sky the other hand remains consistently entertaining and focused for its two hour running time and all the better for while the film epic tone sometimes broken some cartoonish moments like brawl between pazu boss and one dola sons never the point that detracts from the film about eleven years ago disney released english version featuring cast big names such james van der beek anna paquin cloris leachman mark hamill mandy patinkin well some cameo appearances veterans such tress macneille and jim cummings also features ambitious reworking joe hisaishi gorgeous musical score for performance the seattle music orchestra interestingly the man behind this rescore none other than the composer himself much purists have cried blasphemy over this version for its occasional extra dialogue and the aforementioned rescore miyazaki had such problems fact said have applauded the reworking and for good reason because the newly rerecorded music truly the star the new dub while there are some instances where filling some critially silent scenes from the original japanese bit jarring notably the journey through dragon infested storm cloud the overall reworking fantastic and many ways improves the original particularly scenes such when robot attacks fortress and the climactic moments toward the end here hisaishi displays his musical versatility and genius for matching music visuals far the performances the dub the leads are probably the short end the stick james van der beek pazu sounds significantly more mature than his character while anna paquin sheeta speaks with odd accent that fluctuates times problem which actually works favor the character that said both good jobs overall and provide fairly believable chemistry throughout the lively supporting cast however that really make this dub much fun particularly cloris leachman dola and mark hamill muska both are perfectly cast and steal every scene they with the rescore these two really warrant listen the disney dub the script adaptation borders the loose side times there quite bit extra lines and commentary some which are pricelessly funny and others somewhat overdone but aside from least one debatable alteration sheeta speech the climactic showdown the world cannot live without love opposed the original you can survive apart from mother earth the overall characters story and spirit remain fairly faithful the original the whole there little point comparing the disney version the original language track each puts their own stamp this legendary masterpiece and like them both they also better than streamline jal more literal but frightfully robotic lifeless abysmally acted and poorly written older dub from the late 1980 don believe anybody who says this version superior disneys trust the opposite true either way though you can wrong with castle the sky one miyazaki all time greatest and highly recommend
