osition for apparent reason and comedy interlaced into dramatic scenes confusing intent while obstacles appear and disappear seemingly random for the comedy let say this willing accept that lot the humor probably cultural not familiar with korean humor maybe things were lost translation however asian studies major college and someone who has been living japan for the last years still here like think have better grasp asian humor than the average white guy that being said there were many parts the movie that understood were supposed funny but weren spoiler for example after the initial attack where the young daughter lost the family the funeral everyone mourning new character introduced brother and tension raised even higher becomes obvious that the two brothers are odds with one another they both begin grieve for their loss and wind competing with each other over who grieving harder this competition core funny two brothers who dislike each other much they even compete funeral shows the prickly nature familial love common asian comedy this subtle slap stick comedy poking fun family and ritualized mourning supposed funny but seemed really out place the context lost little girl end spoiler then come the plot holes there are many points brought this movie that are never explained worse are explained and fretted over only proved impotent and pointless the end finding out obstacle isn obstacle can good thing for character but you expect some comment that nature instead the audience barraged moments anti climax when problems just aren there anymore and one gives indication that was ever problem start ask you why even bring the first place this was prevalent through out the film problems gave rise new problems and suddenly the world the movie filled with opposing forces that never resolved each other course introducing new and greater problems time tested story telling tradition but the introduction new arc leads the the forced shortening another you would expect least that the new arc gets full explanation not this movie instead was you get several stories each only explained the way and the end the parts never converge complete the whole again willing accept that lot this might cultural maybe its korean story telling tradition put comedy inside tragedy maybe normal for stories all over like child who colors outside the lines every page but never finishes one maybe present problem order develop the plot but then remove that problem randomly without any apparent solution catharsis maybe these are all hallmarks sloppy work and bad storytelling rampant movie that seems have much better reputation than deserves
