1 |text hitokiri which translates roughly assassination tenchu which translates roughly divine punishment showcases hideo gosha the top his form not miss this one gosha other classic goyokin hitokiri not only one gosha best films one the best samurai chambara films ever made and perhaps one the best japanese films ever exported warned all the intricate plot details hitokiri can little hard follow for those unfamiliar with 19th century japanese history even the underlying human drama obvious and open all viewers per the norm for gosha hitokiri provides yet another variation his traditional theme loyalty one lord doing the right thing however gosha develops his favorite theme with such sophistication that really _the_ movie see along with goyokin course suppose breaks down like this you want simpler more action oriented tale you might want see goyokin however you want more thoughtful multilayered albeit grim drama see this one essentially the historical backdrop massive power grap between many different samurai clans who are either working reform yet retain the tokugawa shogunate and those who are trying install the emperor meiji the supreme ruler japan course those clans working for emperor meiji were often less interested reforming japan than ensuring their own clan more power the new world order ironically the entire feudal system was officially abolished one the first reforms the meiji government ironic twists like this gosha big irony that make the entire plot all the more bittersweet what distinguishes hitokiri from gosha other movies gosha mature sense cinematography every shot thoughtfully composed and much like kubrick barry lyndon each frame the movie could hold its own still composition course this typical gosha hitokiri really stands out with stunning backdrops including with goyokin many riveting seascapes just watch the opening sequence and you hooked make mistake this english period piece hitokiri extremely violent don say you weren warned what else other than cool camera work makes hitokiri stand out the performances seem bit more subtle this one katsu shintaro zatoichi hanzo the razor fame turns star performance the conflicted protagonist antihero okada izo katsu manages instill humanity character that seems almost more wild animal than villain throughout the movie you never quite sure you engaged revolted okada character the same time katsu portrayal okada ravenous hunger for respect and his later pathetic attempts redemption seem human that you can help but feel empathy sympathy course after seeing nakadai tatsuya play the tortured hero goyokin great see him play such ruthless villain hitokiri just perfect there nothing more say final note perhaps more interesting buffs than casual fans don miss the last screen appearance mishima yukio yes the closeted gay right wing ultranationalist novelist who committed suicide seppuku before the crowd jeering japanese military personnel kidnapped 1970 and had movie his life and work made paul schrader who actually does pretty solid job portraying the honorable for assassin shinbei tanaka
