1 |text much like the comedy duo its title the sunshine boys has become forgotten classic odd years later hardly mentioned alongside other great film comedies the 1970s this makes sense given the singular specialness this film perhaps the best neil simon ever wrote walter matthau plays willy clark once half legendary vaudeville comedy known lewis and clark now bitter year old solo act who can get job potato chip commercial his nephew and agent ben richard benjamin sure can get work willy will only agree reunite with his estranged partner lewis george burns for abc celebration show business nostalgia nostalgia what sunshine boys has going for spades right from the start when series 1920s film clips showcasing various entertainers from long ago flickers before the accompaniment cole porter clown then there the film present day setting manhattan where flared trousers and wide polyester ties abound the periods collide willy glorious mess manhattan apartment where framed photos and cartoons long dead celebrities stare out from the walls lurid tabloid headlines and empty zabar grocery bags you were alive the 1970s like you might even feel like you were that apartment willy clearly has been living there too long sleeping front the television when the kettle the other room boils willy wakes and picks the phone hello who this pause never mind the tea old men living alone can sad material almost anyone else hands but simon deft wit and unerring feeling for character turns this adaptation his 1972 stage hit into comedy gold the amazing thing about the sunshine boys how much rubs your noses willy almost existential condition without turning you off all years old and just like that dies nothing willy says one old songwriting friend before deciding the man probably died from writing song that rhymed lady with baby burns won oscar for his understated performance the gentle but steely lewis but matthau who brings this one home his make and proud but ragged bearing really selling you the idea was already when made this willy obnoxious the extreme fully deserving ben description crazy freakin old man but you root for him throughout enjoying his small victories even when they come the cost others patience his lines kill you too especially when trying kill lewis for whom the reunion turns out bad idea you out touch willy tells lewis one point still demand still hot this room was fire you wouldn hot lewis replies director herbert ross shoots everything very casual and understated way with low lighting and mid range shots even emotional moments leave room for the comedy and the film overall zen message grace through quiet acceptance you never get the feeling you are watching movie one the sunshine boys many charms and ross direction like the acting the three principals goes long way toward achieving that end comedy hard especially when the subjects are people watching life pass them but the sunshine boys makes all seem pleasure because for watching
