1 |text introduction into yoji yamada cinematic world through his famed and recent samurai trilogy with the twilight samurai the hidden blade and love and honor had enjoyed all three films and looking the prolific veteran director filmography think take very long while watch all his films especially the tora san series needless say when kabei our mother has finally reached our shores jumped the chance watch what would ode mothers everywhere celebrating their innate love for their children based the autobiography teruyo nogami kabei our mother tells close knit family four xc2 x96 mother kayo kabei sayuri yoshinaga father shigeru tobei mitsugoro bando eldest daughter hatsu mirai shida and youngest child teru miku sato from the get their lives would changed forever when shigeru gets arrested under the peace preservation law for his morally controversial writings against the nation set the late 30s where japan had begun their crusade china and thereafter their participation wwii begins kabei struggle hold down jobs feed her family and the frequent difficult meetings with her husband behind bars help comes from relatives especially shigeru side since kabei own dad had adopted told you attitude with her choice spouse shigeru one time student yama arthouse buffs should recognize tadanobu asano here provides laughter bumbling man who slowly becomes confidante and surrogate guardian the children and kabei sister law hisako rei dan from hiroshima which believe would have sounded some hindsight alarm bells her unfortunate fate the film progresses through its timeline while the film centers primarily how the kids are growing under the presence their mom and distant relationship with their dad what enjoyed how the microscopic family events unfold under the macroscopic worldwide events that have impacted the common folk japan against the historical backdrop japan push regional dominance and there are characters here that don mask those ambitions even discussing what the country would eventually should successful holding onto conquered lands this something rarely see japanese films being that frank their discussion that era and also get glimpse how the common man have struggle against domestic issues made all the more difficult with resources channeled toward the war effort the actresses casted here are pitch perfect their delivery and roles they the veterans the child actors actress sayuri yoshinaga deserves special mention for her role the motherly figure who has dig deep and find that inner strength carry the household through under trying circumstances while mirai shida and miku sato are lovable the understanding children who have learn make and compromise each scene with the three them together just makes heart wrenching when the going gets tough fill your heart with joy should they celebrating before long you soon find yourself being attracted want part this family thanks the primary cast powerful performances with yoji yamada coaxing some really natural performances from the kids kabei our mother boasts some stunningly beautiful art direction and classy its delivery both happy and sad moments without going over the top relying cheap melodrama cheapen the emotions seeks from the audience there are plenty little things here done right which makes pitch perfect with every scene not being wasted and with every nuance very meaningful conveying its message across compassion love aside from the very abrupt ending had hoped that could have continued for lot more despite its more than hours runtime kabei our mother comes highly recommended and you find difficult holding back either your tears that thought about your own mom and her sacrifices she makes for you everyday basis just what those sacrifices are should you need another reminder then the scene during the end credits roll will remind you the stuff that you probably have taken for granted
