1 |text the shop around the corner 1940 pleasant romantic comedy not the sort that will hold dear until the end days but nonetheless film thoroughly deserving its reputation 1940 director ernst lubitsch had long ago taken hollywood storm and his famed lubitsch touch had become sparkling commercial trademark this film was planned for 1939 release but scheduling conflicts meant that james stewart and margaret sullavan were unavailable for filming rather than substituting either his main stars lubitsch decided postpone production the meantime directing greta garbo ninotchka 1939 when was finally completed the shop around the corner appears have been met with relative indifference receiving zero oscar nominations despite excellent screenplay samson raphaelson and fine performances from its two leads and frank morgan supporting role time nevertheless has betrayed the film massive and enduring influence with high profile remakes including the good old summertime 1949 and you got mail 1998 its surface one might assume the shop around the corner simply the story two lovers klara novak sullavan and alfred kralik stewart who love each other without knowing however lubitsch film runs much deeper than that the story matuschek and company stylish gift shop budapest and the various human relationships that make the store such close knit family when store owner hugo matuschek frank morgan begins suspect his oldest employee having affair with his wife witness the breakdown two families both home and work there absolutely reason why the story should not have been set the united states xc2 x96 perhaps the blustery streets new york xc2 x96 but lubitsch was deliberately recreating the passions and memories his former years europe the quaintness love and life before war brought terror and bloodshed every doorstep this subtle subtext brings more meaningful personal touch the film xc2 x96 fact even write this review beginning appreciate the story even more sullavan and stewart are both lovely their respective roles but think that the supporting cast that really make the film each character brings distinctive personality the mix and their interactions are always believable and enjoyable especially liked how lubitsch knowingly directed much our sympathy towards hugo matuschek who any other film would have been restricted underdeveloped two dimensional portrayal matuschek may have lost the love his family but recaptures the affection his employees and you feel heartwarming glow when the bitter cold christmas eve snowstorm finds companionship freckle faced young errand boy charles smith this genuine warmth towards supporting character strikes being similar several billy wilder later creations for example boom boom jackson the fortune cookie 1966 carlo carlucci avanti 1972 course doesn really need saying but billy wilder learned from the best
