1 |text sat down watch midnight cowboy thinking would another overrated 60s 70s movie some favorite films come from the 70s the same vein midnight cowboy taxi driver mean streets panic needle park etc but there are many many overrated ones well that have gained strong reputations amongst critics for being groundbreaking unfortunately vast majority them don hold well today sort feel this way about easy rider although too one favorites didn expect much from midnight cowboy but got lot back touching story well made and well told with some the best performances all time dustin hoffman enrico ratso rizzo gives one his best bit funny times sounds like cartoon character when speaks maybe because the lenny simpsons connection but hoffman entirely convincing half the film budget went towards his paycheck was just becoming major star hollywood opposite him the second billed jon voight joe buck the cowboy who travels north the big apple the hopes becoming male prostitute soon his naive ways land him trouble and pairs with crippled scam artist named ratso who offers become joe manager for certain percentage profits the movie quite long two hours but never really seems very long some films can tend drag especially some the films that were made the 70s because been said easy riders raging bulls the directors were the stars the movies the 1970s and occasionally they got bit too infatuated with their material going too long examining characters scenes etc that aren important just about the only scene felt was bit too long and unnecessary was the drug party makes the film seem extremely outdated similar the drug odysseys easy rider and really harms its flow because not needed other than that midnight cowboy almost flawless motion picture was pleasantly surprised does have its flaws flashbacks are bit tacky and never used well they could have been for instance and some the scenes are bit uneasy such the gay movie theater sequence but you can handle its content midnight cowboy truly great motion picture uncompromising examination life the streets the late 60s early 70s depressing movie yes and today standards might seem bit outdated and heavy the liberal perspective life horrible etc but still love and particularly the extremely touching ending will stay with for long long time highly recommended one the best films the 70s was technically released late 1969 but still categorize 1970s film also won the best picture oscar being the first and only rated motion picture was later rated appeal
