1 |text legendary movie producer walt disney brought three the world greatest fairy tales the screen they remain among the most popular animated films all time the first was his groundbreaking classic snow white and the seven dwarfs released 1937 the last was the then under appreciated sleeping beauty which made debut 1959 between these two was perhaps his most satisfying adaptation classic fairy tale cinderella 1950 the three films cinderella the one most faithful its origins ironically unlike snow white which for better worse became for many the definitive version the story cinderella did not follow the same path although was hit and like snow white was responsible for restoring the dwindling disney fortunes never achieved the same audience recognition which certainly deserved disney for once did himself proud electing not tamper with classic instead elaborating and adding substance the tale rather than rewriting for the screen the result was enchanting combination superb animation beautifully soft technicolor and the perfect voice talents brought the story life with radiance that endures this day ilene woods who was radio performer recorded demonstration discs the songs favor the authors the material hoffman mack david and jerry livingston when disney heard them knew had found his cinderella and indeed had woods heartfelt renditions dream wish your heart makes this love and sing sweet nightingale are perfect eleanor audley who would voice maleficent sleeping beauty masterfully captured the icy cruelty the stepmother while rhoda williams and lucille bliss were convincingly nasty stepsisters luis van rooten admirably performed both the king and the grand duke and james macdonald was endearing both jaq and gus cinderella devoted mice william phipps has little dialog the prince future talk show host mike douglas provided his singing voice but film and disney veteran verna felton was born play the fairy godmother and she made the best number the oscar nominated bibbidi bobbidi boo her own show stopper among the artists responsible for the look the film was mary blair whose inspired use color was greatly admired disney her elegant french period backgrounds add tremendously the quality the movie but most important all are the believable characters from cinderella right down lucifer the stepmother deliciously evil cat they bring both life and vibrancy the often told story something very difficult create animated film conjunction with the film year anniversary and not coincidentally the coming holiday season cinderella has just been released special edition dvd simply has never looked better the fully restored film must seen appreciated suffice say looks wonderful enhanced stereo soundtrack has been added and serves the music well the dvd extras now standard part disney platinum editions are too numerous list here but usual some are directed towards children some are slanted adults and the rest fall somewhere between but real fans will want get the deluxe gift set because along with actual cell from the film and eight character sketches includes 160 page hardback book which not only incorporates most the material found the book with the 1995 special edition home video release but much more well usual for disney cinderella will only available for limited time like you are cinderella lover get now this edition truly dream come true
