-1 |text roger corman undeniably one the most versatile and unpredictable directors producers history was single handedly responsible for some favorite horror films ever like the edgar allen poe adaptations masque the red death and pit and the pendulum well some insufferably cheap and tacky rubbish quickies like creature from the haunted sea and she gods the shark reef corman also made couple movies that are simply unclassifiable and xc2 x96 simply put xc2 x96 nearly impossible judge properly the trip for example well this imaginatively titled gas can somewhat labeled psychedelic exploitation other words they incredibly strange hippie culture influenced movies half the time you haven got the slightest idea what going who these characters are that walk back and forth through the screen and where the hell this whole thing going the plot simply and yet highly effective strange but deadly nerve gas accidentally unleashed and promptly annihilates that the entire world population over the age this could the basic premise atmospheric gritty and nail bitingly suspenseful post apocalyptic sci landmark but writer george armitage and roger corman decided turn into trippy road movie comedy none the characters even trying prevent their inevitable upcoming deaths they just party out the streets and found little juvenile crime syndicates gas disappointingly boring and tries overly hard bizarre the entire script appears improvised the spot and not all funny definitely not cup tea but the film does have loyal fan base and many admirers who say that not worth your time money
