-1 |text five years after the original creepshow another inferior horror sequel penned george romero and stephen king creepshow this time there are only three stories instead five none the three stories really original distinguished either the first story horror staple formulaic story about wooden indian statue seeking revenge against the killers its owners the effects are really neat this story but just too familiar compelling enough george kennedy and dorothy lamour play the elderly store owners the second story the raft stephen king story about four teenagers that unwittingly spend the day wooden pallet the middle isolated lake soon the kids are screaming for their lives watery blob does each them for apparent reason however instead being suspenseful the kids are saddled with bad dialog and dopey headed behavior preventing from really caring about what happens next there also some unintentional humor this segment the third and final story the hitch hiker which actually retread adapted for creepshow the original story lucille fletcher was filmed 1953 film noir suspense film then was adapted for famous twilight zone episode featuring inger stevens the hitch hiker works the best out these three offerings but not without its problems either lois chiles plays cheating spouse who ends running over hitch hiker she thinks however don know whether sympathize with her condemn her many average stories this type the characters exist merely tell the stories with their twists and turns the wrap around story with the bullies seems bit out place tom savini appears the creep this installment the good thing there haven been any more sequels stars
