1 |text has said that the movies and baseball both thrived during the great depression appears that the grim realities nation caught the aftermath this economic disaster created need for occasional relief for the populace temporary escape could found the going soap opera that baseball likewise occasional excursion hours into the darkened auditoriums the cinema the presence radio just about everyone house hold kept depression era america once attuned world events and provided many drama and especially comedy shows for pleasant interlude from harsh reality the literature the time also flourished all levels the juvenile reading habits helped create the comic book know what with all the fantastic characters and super exciting adventures but the comic book just did not magically appear all fully developed with all the colorful color pages all itself there were mediums that were ancestral them obviously the newspaper comic strip was one parent providing the visual narrative method story telling the other direct ancestor was the pulp magazine the inexpensive prose story publications that carried great deal stories the same adventure characters going though not necessarily serialized tales the pulp medium had been around for some decades and introduced edgar rice borrough tarzan and johnston mcculley zorro the 1930 brought forth bumper crop feature characters like the shadow the avenger battle aces and the spider master men all found their way the news stands among many others one other was doc savage full blooded super hero the written story the covers the pulps had perhaps the only picture the hero possessing extraordinary strength super keen senses and protean genius class intellect doc was the prototype super hero also assembled his former army buddies into small free lancing team adventurers each them was expert given field had top rated chemist lawyer construction engineer electrical engineer geologist archaeologist paleontologist etc the doc savage stories were very popular the 1930 and and were published into the middle then they went into hiatus for good years then the brainstorm came about repackage the old novels new container the paperback book fresh look the cover art was introduced featuring highly stylized series paintings very muscular doc with perpetually ripped shirt the introduction proved highly successful with the publication title month and for while more soon there was rumor doc savage movie but when what producer well the venerable man bronze was back the news stands for over years before any real project got put together was veteran stop action animator and producer top special effects films geoprge pal who did the film along with warner brothers when doc savage man bronze arrived the movie houses boasted well casted team actors albeit largely name far familiarity with the viewers with former tarzan ron ely nearly perfect casting the lead and coming beauty starlette pamela hensley the female lead and veteran character paul wexler the villainous captain seas other name would have been recognized and just maybe that was plus this case the story does fine job both getting most the audience acquainted with the incredible group and the same time get plot going use narration paul frees and short film clips are the method pursued move the introduction along the main body the story from the very start there are hints that this story will with the same sort manufactured camp humor the batman series some really great looking early scenes involving doc and the whole crew doing their individual specialties are thrown toward humor the paul frees narration and the unexpected unlikely outcomes for example experiment doc with miniature rocket missile turns out part method catching fish small one that the whole story unfolds like that hitting the viewer with little camp every often keep reminding not take too seriously are also puzzled about george pal being the producer his last who had been well known for special effects surely factor that could put good use sci action setting the pulp character world can remember seeing quite vividly mrs ryan deanna was the hospital just having given birth our 2nd child michelle our older girl jennifer was visiting her grandmother after visiting hours were over the maternity ward was straight over the old marquette theatre 63rd kedzie here chicago having seen and being guy with good familiarity with doc was sort let down the final product could accept little this camp business but would not have objected pal would have seen fit let all hang out and have some real neat dinosaurs and volcanoes give all little more pulp comic serial type excitement and yet the cast headed ely and the others made the whole film likable not lovable the sets and locations were far can see very much like those serial adventure flick which would enjoyable about anyone and maybe that just what they were trying for with this doc savage man bronze
