1 |text noted cinematic phenomenon the late eighties and early nineties was the number oscars which went actors playing characters who were either physically mentally handicapped the first was marlee matlin award for children lesser god 1986 and the next ten years were see another best actress award holly hunter for the piano 1994 and fewer than five best actor awards dustin hoffman 1988 for rain man daniel day lewis 1989 for left foot pacino 1992 for scent woman tom hanks 1994 for forrest gump and geoffrey rush 1996 for shine for portrayals the disabled matlin who played deaf woman herself deaf but all the others are able bodied this phenomenon aroused some adverse comment the time with suggestions being made that these awards were given more for political correctness than for the quality the acting when jodie foster failed win best actress for nell 1994 some people saw this evidence backlash against this sort portrayal view however that the majority these awards were well deserved thought the 1992 award should have gone either clint eastwood robert downey rather than pacino but apart from that the only one with which disagreed would have been hanks and that was because preferred nigel hawthorne performance the madness king george that film course hawthorne played character who was mentally ill left foot was based upon the autobiography the irish writer and painter christy brown brown was born 1931 one the thirteen children working class dublin family was born with cerebral palsy and was first wrongly thought mentally handicapped well was for long time incapable deliberate movement speech but eventually discovered that could control the movements one part his body his left foot hence the title learned write and draw holding piece chalk between his toes and went become painter and published novelist and poet life working class dublin the thirties and forties could hard and the city jim sheridan himself dubliner shows here many ways grim grey cheerless place very different from our normal idea the emerald isle sheridan and day lewis were later collaborate another film with irish theme the name the father against this however must set the cheerfulness and spirit its people especially the brown family much christy success was due the support received from his parents who refused allow him institutionalised and always believed the intelligence hidden beneath crippled exterior and from his siblings see how his brothers used wheel him round specially made cart and how they helped their bricklayer father build christy room his own their back yard the film could easily have slid into sentimentality and ended just another heart warming triumph over adversity movie that does not due number factors principally the magnificent acting the course his career day lewis has given number fine performances but this together with the recent there will blood his best never less than 100 convincing christie his tortured jerky movements and strained attempts speech persuade that really are watching disabled person even though intellectually are well aware that day lewis able bodied the other performances which stand out are from fiona shaw his mentor eileen cole from hugh conor the young christy and from brenda fricker christy mother which won her the best supporting actress award the other reason why the film escapes sentimentality that does not try sentimentalise its main character christy brown had difficult life but could also difficult live with and the film gives warts and all portrait was heavy drinker given foul language and prone outbursts rage could also selfish and manipulative those around him and the film shows all these aspects his character course also shows the positive aspects his courage his determination and his wicked sense humour day lewis acting not just physically convincing that persuades believe his character disability but also emotionally and intellectually convincing that brings out all these different facets christy character his oscar was won the teeth some very strong opposition from the likes robin williams and kenneth branagh but was well deserved
1 |text this film about life the triumph over adversity and the wonders the human spirit defy anyone not shed tear the end the movie this more than just tear jerker its engaging thought provoking drama with excellent performances from all the cast but especially derek luke and denzel washington years amazed that luke still virtual unknown and washington only directed one other film nevertheless apart from slow build the story this foster child trials and tribulations and how still affects him adulthood the sort movie that stays with you long after you have seen like many fox searchlight pictures this was more sleeper hit and didn get the mass critical acclaim deserves the scene where antwone finally meets his mother summed the movie for there were many ways that could have been done and could have been all schmaltzy could have been unrealistic but washington struck exactly the right tone his mother never said word and could only shed tear while antowne asked simply why her overwhelming guilt prevented her from saying anything what could she say defend herself one the most moving cinematic scenes have seen
