1 |text british comedies tend fall into one two main types the quiet introspective usually romantic study and the farcical social satire settings characters and concepts vary but certain characteristics place the vast majority shows into one the two categories butterflies perhaps the epitom xc3 xa9 the first type the scripts are very verbal including long interior monologues the main character ria basically happy but unsettled housewife curious about what she might have missed out when she embarked thoroughly conventional life when she meets successful but clumsy and emotionally accessible businessman who makes his interest her quite clear she toys with the idea finding out what the other path might have offered the acting and scripts are always the money which makes one reaction the show almost entirely personal one was neither blown away nor turned off mother the other hand adored this show think the degree which one identifies with ria dilemma the most important factor determining one reaction butterflies
