1 |text when good times premiered 1974 was one the first black family sitcoms centered the poor chicago based evans family and their struggles make ends most the early episodes focused the parents james and florida evans and their struggle provide for the family john amos and esther rolle were the best part the show they were terrific actors and had great chemistry james and florida evans they had three kids thelma and michael was the skirt chasing but well meaning teenage son who made for his lack subtletly with artistic talent thelma was attractive bright girl who was constantly trading insults with michael was near child prodigy who was well educated social issues and was destined become lawyer 1976 the producers made huge mistake firing john amos literally killing off his character this really changed the focus and not for the good might add the shows began focus more and his buffoon like behavior which angered black viewers well series star esther rolle who left after the next season instead show that focused key african american issues that existed society the time viewers got shows that were overloaded with skirt chasing and fat jokes once esther rolle left the quality the show suffered even more although was still watchable was longer the great ground breaking show that once was although esther rolle came back for the 1978 season became obvious that the show was its last legs all loose ends were tied during that season and the show quietly faded off the air first three season last three seasons
