1 |text the premise the story simple old man living alone the woods accidentally stumble upon murder small child and tries convince the police that the murder has occurred though very little dialog provided throughout the film the visual narrative told the camera eye alone made the film quite engaging the setting the gray woods conveys feeling loneliness which complements the quietness the characters themselves can also sense helplessness the old man inability convince the police the murder which parallels the silenced child inability tell her own story true horror lies feelings hopelessness helplessness and irrationality this film successfully addresses these elements visuals alone rather than relying cheap sound effects blood and gore that other bad horror films use when the narrative weak cleverly the story unfolds slow pace build tension for few creepy and startling moments the ending also unexpected and believable reminiscent japanese horror films such the ring and dark water english horror films such lady black and the innocents this film provides viewers the experience true atmosphere horror recommend anyone who enjoys good chilling the bone scare give this film try the way you haven seen the films just mentioned above you might want give them try well
