1 |text pendragon pictures new film wells war the worlds the first faithful adaptation the original novel has been development for about years theatrical release was intended for earlier this year march 2005 but this never happened the dvd was rushed out coincide with the release spielberg version which hits theatres june liked this film with certain reservations how faithful the adaptation not quite 100 faithful wells book but faithful good enough for least several scenes were totally new such ogilvy the astronomer confrontation with farmer and the unnamed writer narrator awkwardly having tea with his cousin but the whole this film follows the book very closely certainly much more than the classic 1953 version george pal its greatest fault that was obviously made very cheap budget the majority seems have been shot blue screen and composited with digitally rendered backgrounds this particularly annoying during most the interior shots and scenes crowded city streets the overviews 1898 london look like something from video game numerous scenes horse carriages were faked guess they couldn afford rent horse the only scenes shot for real seem those open fields forests but within those budget restrictions they managed quite lot artistically the film looks right the martians and their tripods are quite well done and very true wells descriptions was particularly impressed with the heat ray although the thunder child sequence which should have been one the film highlights very disappointing great shame that they couldn afford more actual sets better quality animation the acting and direction won win any oscars for the most part they are competent not bad but not outstanding the music quite good also though not par with any the major hollywood composers actually glad this didn get theatrical release because the budget limitation would have made look much worse big screen stands would rate this similarly bbc adaptation classic literature few nitpicks most the scenes are presented with various colored filters mostly red this may have been artistic choice but used very inconsistently and seems more like sloppy job mastering the dvd and the writer narrator obviously fake moustache mutates from scene scene bottom line worth seeing you can look past the technical and budgetary limitations and get into the story think you will enjoy this especially you actually read the original wells novel however you are easily put off cheap production values you best pass this unless you mst3k fan warned however that the film runs full hours don recommend watching all one sitting btw entirely different version war the worlds aka invasion came out dvd the same month that spielberg hit the theatres http imdb com title tt0449040 this was also made budget but updated the present day like the spielberg film but much better and top off jeff wayne making animated film his best selling album from 1978 but that won out until 2007
