-1 |text kings and queen bloated french drama that rambles for interminable two hours and thirty two minutes discernible point purpose the film features two stories that seem unrelated first but which eventually connect with one another about halfway through the movie the first centers around nora and her struggles with various men her life including elderly father who discovers has only few days left live the other story involves young man named ismael violinist who finds himself placed unfairly believes mental institution through the machinations unknown third party after traveling along separate tracks for awhile these two narrative strands eventually come together when learn that ismael former lover nora and the man she has chosen adopt her son from earlier tragic relationship with bit more focus and considerable amount streamlining kings and queen might have been potent engrossing drama about modern day relationships certainly has moments tremendous insight and emotional power and the performances are for the most part complex and touching but taken whole the film meanders and maunders such extent that quite frankly begins wreak havoc our patience and wear out its welcome early even more distressing the fact that even though spend what seems like mild eternity the company these people really don know quite what make any them when the show finally over for instance nora father his deathbed writes withering diatribe against his daughter character that simply doesn gibe with the woman been looking for well over two hours nora admittedly mother theresa then again who but she certainly doesn deserve the invective thrown her her very own father nora could accused being confused indecisive bit self absorbed times but evil enough have her father wishing could give her his cancer and make her die his place don think perhaps this film simply operating level depth that was unable fathom but suspicion that even writer roger bohbot and writer director arnaud desplechin would have trouble fully explaining their purpose here this well acted pretentious bore film that takes the viewer long rambling voyage through sea personal crises journey that leaves him wiser more enlightened the end than was the beginning
1 |text you like horror movies with lots blood and gore tons jump scare moments and unrelenting escalating scenes excruciating death then look elsewhere you like quiet moody thoughtful horror which casts blood aside favor genuine feeling dread then wendigo for you thoughtful stressed out george his psychoanalyst wife kim and their young son miles are heading out the snowy countryside for long weekend vacation away from the city the way george hits stag with his car the hunters who had been pursuing the deer are not thrilled when they find that george has ended their chase particular deranged hunter otis takes personally follows the family their vacation home making sure they see him spies george and kim they have sex fires through their windows with his rifle when they aren home letting them discover the ominous holes their windows and walls when they return when kim takes miles the drugstore town miles attracted small sculpture display case carved resemble man with the head stag native american man tells miles that this the wendigo spirit the woods who has taste for flesh and always hungry miles takes the figure home with him already haunted the death the deer the day before that afternoon when and his father sledding george shot and miles pursued through the woods creature barely glimpsed just shock and imagining the whole thing hours later george rushed the hospital and miles still clutching his statue either faints dreams goes vision quest which the wendigo returns this time the angry flesh eating god part tree part stag and part man hunting for otis who has finally gone over the edge wendigo beautifully made film almost totally silent but for the wind howling through the snow covered trees okay the monster itself kind fakey looking but small flaw more than made for the genuine feeling tension and dread that creeps through every frame the film and the eerie backdrop the silent snowy countryside the performances are great particularly jake weber the moody and thoughtful george and patricia clarkson his sweet but nonsense wife they are happy couple with their share common problems and the strength their relationship and their love for each other that makes this film powerful watching this film often like watching someone home videos realistic are the performances this movie not for everyone lot people may find themselves totally bored waiting for the hideous lovecraftian beast and bloody revenge that never come can never really sure the wendigo even exists seen through the eyes sensitive child and also later through the eyes madman this more psychological drama than horror film but has more than enough creepy elements satisfy fans subtle horror
