1 |text what more can said have not been this fascinated with young actress since cate blanchett burst upon the scene over ten years ago and although both blanchett and blunt have played queens now seems the benchmark for and coming actresses the roles are complete polar opposites simply put you are looking for high passion compelling drama and machiavellian intrigue this not the movie for you this isn say that the script direction was bad its just that the subject the film did not lead too dramatic life when compared other notable royals like elizabeth anne boylen henry viii henry henry and elainor acquitane these are people whose lives were the stuff such good soap operas are made and whose policies and decisions altered the course british and most cases world history victoria contrast ascended the throne without incident she quasi governed nation that was fast becoming global power due industrialization and the rise the navy her state had stable government led competent and dynamic politicians and she married young had harmonious family life the facts her life are not the sturm und drag such powerful dramas are made the heart the film aside from the attempt dramatize her stultifying upbringing and the machinations surrounding her throne the story the one thing that was truly shocking and surprising about her reign love story marriage made for financial political reasons with reason not necessarily the place look for world shaking passion yet victoria will always remembered history being sort patron saint marital fidelity happiness and ideal family life thus central the film the budding love victoria and her prince albert was very taken with rupert friend characterization albert whom portrayed kind patient somewhat earnest and maybe touch naive young man looking good the world and help short good man with good heart not the most dynamic figure base drama around but that not the point the story that does not matter the heart the character shines through thanks friend understated yet earnest performance for the queen well emily blunt sublime her beauty cannot denied but she more than something pretty look her face like quicksilver because her expressiveness the slightest arch the eyebrow glance the eye slight wry smile delivers much again this not bombastic performance heavy speeches and impassioned pleas its not that kind movie but what blunt does with the role show the simple humanity the character with potent subtlety for example see the joie vivre that has been kept check victoria mother miranda richardson and her scheming adviser lover conroy expressed the simple things like victoria trying sketch her dog see her delight and fascination upon first meeting albert her eyes being continually drawn him see her nervous and overwhelmed when addressing parliament upon her ascension and favorite scene all the film see her nervous happy and hopeful she steels herself what really most women never have their life ask the man she loves marry her proposition ridiculous for those times and some would say now that victoria bursts out nervous laughter before she can even say marry again this not movie for over the top larger than life expressions but more study the subtleties character and making the little things say much overall judge the film what and what tried and such give felt that some the politics could better explained and that some very fine actors were wasted with little and little character development namely miranda richardson the duchess kent and the characters conroy and lord peal again the film need not have spent large amount time those characters but little more exposition would have helped explain the political environment also would have loved have seen more the adjustment married life between victoria and albert but that may just greed for more scenes between friend and blunt summary don view this film terms historical drama but for what really love story between two characters that happen historical figures give this film solid for wonderful lead performances brilliant costumes and scenery and the magnificent victoria emily blunt and anyone who has any shred romance left them you will touched the end this movie god save the queen
