1 |text more than twenty years before peter jackson visionary adaptation the lord the rings there was this 1978 animated effort from director ralph bakshi ambitious and reasonably faithful version the story this has sadly been rather over shadowed the jackson trilogy indeed many reviewers here the imdb mainly those who saw the newer version first seem fiercely unkind this version but one applies little common sense and takes into consideration the time when was made and the technical possibilities that existed that time then they will realise that this pretty good film indeed was shortly after seeing this animated movie back the early 80s that sought out tolkien book and immediately became lifelong fan these richly detailed middle earth adventures some respects owe this film degree acknowledgement the film which shaped literary tastes forever sauron the dark lord middle earth forges all powerful ring that gives him incredible power following great battle during which sauron defeated the ring falls into possession king named isildur xc2 x85 but instead destroying foolishly chooses keep for centuries the ring passes from hand hand eventually coming into the possession hobbit named frodo baggins who lives peace loving community known the shire frodo learns from wizard named gandalf that his ring fact the one ring the very same that was forged sauron all those centuries ago and that its master once again searching for order restore his dark power over the entire land frodo embarks perilous journey protect the ring with three other hobbit companions but every step the way they are hunted sauron ring wraiths the black riders there follow many adventures during which company nine adventurers formed guide the ring the only place where can unmade xc2 x96 mount doom the land mordor the film concludes with frodo and his best friend sam the borders mordor closing ever nearer their horrifying destination meanwhile gandalf and the other members the company fight off huge army orcs the legendary fortress helm deep this version covers just over half the original book second instalment was planned bring the story end but was sadly never completed while the ending feels abrupt does least end sensible point the story one has feel little frustration and regret that sequel exists which might follow these animated heroes their eventual goal the animation passable with nice variety locales and characters presented interesting detail the music leonard rosenman suitably stirring and fits appropriately with the epic narrative the voice overs are decent too especially john hurt aragorn and peter woodthorpe gollum the other hand michael scholes who provides the voice for sam rather campy and goofy which not well suited the character the lord the rings commendable attempt visualise the staggering book which based
