g princess margaret hers obviously the pivotal role and she has absolutely trouble dominating the film despite strong performances from jim broadbent miss miranda richardson and miss harriet walter all immeasurably more experienced the music suitably regal and forms cohesive part the whole movie without being any way obtrusive the fact that britan flourished more under its two great queens elizabeth the first and victoria than any other time matter feminists might like make more but suspect like prime minister margaret thatcher really powerful women make them feel uncomfortable you can work out why there might
