1 |text this has one the best movies about serial killers that ever seen and this coming from someone who absolutely loved silence the lambs hbo has hit the jackpot here this film compelling from the first moment until the last this film has many underlying themes its hard tell exactly what about chronicles the decade long search for the russian serial killer andrea chikatilo stephen rea gives brilliantly reserved performance the inexperienced forensic expert who put charge the investigation and donald sutherland gives even more involving performance his cynical superior and the only person the russian government willing help him both their performances are subtle masterpieces rea begins naive and unwilling compromise while sutherland begins detached and almost amused the situation towards the end rea becomes more world weary and beaten the system while sutherland finds himself more passionate and idealistic any other movie would have said that sutherland performance stands out above the rest but here even rivaled jeffrey dumann the serial killer himself dumann brilliantly creates character here who inspires empathy rather than the hatred think would find monster but doesn want and get the idea that just disgusted with what does are tortured ashamed but vicious well you can take the incredibly dark subject matter and very disturbing then you should see this movie
