1 |text wasn born until years after this wonderful show first aired but luckily managed catch the reruns the mid and the rest history was hooked the premise was pretty simple two hardened nemesis agents richard barrett and craig stirling william gaunt and stuart damon are partnered with expert not young doctor and biologist sharron macready head behind the bamboo curtain retrieve dangerous biological agent from being used red china whilst making their escape their plane hit machine gun fire and they crash the heart the himalayas where their lives are saved mysterious and previously undiscovered civilisation who heal and enhance the senses the trio thus setting the scene for many exciting adventures come the series lasted for hour long episodes and guess was its relatively short lived one season run that has set for cult status monty berman the producer was notorious for making things cheaply possible and sometimes the show suffered for this with incredibly tacky sets particularly episodes such happening studio deputising for the australian outback and the snow sets operation deep freeze and the beginning but you can get past this and focus the characters and the story lines the show was really lot fun had great mix adventure and plenty deadpan humour mainly from some terrific one liners from william gaunt the chemistry from the three leads was fantastic you get the sense that they were really having lot fun making the show and this borne out the 2005 reunion documentary where the three reunite after over years reminisce about the show and laugh about anthony nicholls awful wig they all shared equal screen time and all had their moments shine have say was always richard barrett fan loved his sardonic humour along with that dangerous edge was certainly man you didn cross and those eyes the bluest eyes you would probably see have also followed bill gaunts career with interest since however craig stirling certainly would have had his legion female fans and sure alexandra bastedo had whole queue male fans swooning over her too the show also had plethora guest stars entice with including donald sutherland jeremy brett peter wyngarde burt kwouk anton rodgers kate mara jenny linden paul eddington and colin blakely notable episodes for were auto kill the interrogation the fanatics the mission and the gilded cage but sure every one has their personal favourites you get chance watch this show for the first time watch after many years remember watch the context the time was made and just sit back and enjoy the characters and the chemistry from the three leads what made this wonderful show for and don think will ever tire enjoy
