-1 |text nell shipman must have been paid hefty sum money promote the maxwell automobile off road capabilities the plot the movie pretty simple nell plays writer who has bad case writer block and needs inspiration she goes visit mexico absorb the atmosphere there she meets the hero bert van tuyle cowboy who chooses drive car rather than ride horse while nell visiting with her father partner his mining camp gang local bandits kidnap her and bring her their camp deep the wilderness the hero needs get her quickly decides drive there his car this where the film takes weird twist bert proceeds drive over every terrain imaginable huge rocks small streams heavy brush scraggly tree stumps steep inclines etc etc for the greater part the film get see this car struggling crawl over obstacles now mind you this isn modern day atv 1920 maxwell automobile looks very out place off road vehicle and clearly has limitations for some the terrain encounters get see stuck more than once this film but the filmmakers made effort show beating the odds and eventually passing all the obstacles once the hero gets the hidden camp and rescues the girl jumps the car with her and drives off with the bandits hot pursuit horseback and this point became hysterically funny watching this car slowly rolling over huge rocks getting stuck gravel and mountain brush going forward and back get momentum enough pass over fallen tree limbs the bandits should have had ample time catch but they never even though are believe this wilderness chase goes throughout the night and silly climax the car climbs mountainside and helps nell and the hero push huge boulder down the side crush the pursuing bandits after seeing this film you would think the army should invest 1920 maxwell automobiles because they clearly have better off road capabilities than hummers and bradley tanks combined watch this film just for laughs worth just see nell cuddling the car grill and saying you did your best brave little car
