he cinematography elmer cossey adds extra layer realism the world the miniseries yet the highlight the miniseries really the script screenwrtier arthur hopcraft tackled the job adapting the six hundred page novel excellently the novel was largely least its early parts autobiographical that pym early life echoed much john carre life the script for this miniseries exception traces the development magnus pym from young boy perfect spy never once does the miniseries deviate from its purpose telling fine human drama the context the world espionage one ever wants proof that spy thriller can tense and fascinating without ever having one gun fight fist fight james bond style car chase this would the proof while the miniseries six plus hours long never wastes moment and all the better for though might overlong for some for those who don have very short attention spans here must see from the performances peter egan and ray mcanally fine production values and fine literary script perfect spy one the finest miniseries who can expect see fascinating trip down the history the cold war yet more then that also trip down what john carre has called the secret path the path the spy the man who must lie and betray survive much human drama spy thriller perfect spy isn missed
