olute response sulu who voices his lack understanding about any these events just after mccoy death kirk will get the bottom all this come what may but doesn get much easier for kirk what follows probably the longest staged mano mano fight for the series kirk tussles with his nemesis from his academy days struggle that seems take place over half the planet yet this counterbalanced scenes extraordinary tenderness with another kirk past acquaintances this episode runs the gamut all human experience rather fitting light what learn about the actual purpose this weird planet gratifying that the script really does explain all what happened opposed some nonsensical approach which permeates many other fantasy sci series with similar plot lines unexplained appearances persons who could not possibly there and there actually subtext the story that humans need work off our tensions and fatigue particular fashion just don function normal natural way also note the appearance the very cute yeoman barrows and the sudden absence yeoman rand who did not return until the first trek movie believe that after this episode even more trek fans couldn wait for the next appearance all their favorite characters but leave this episode with final perhaps tantalizing thought mccoy was killed verified spock how know was our real mccoy who beamed back the ship perhaps this explains why this mccoy was still inspecting starships about century later and getting along very well with data
1 |text the shining weird example adaptation has very little common with the source novel written stephen king yet widely remembered one the best cinematic renditions the horror master work this due two factors stanley kubrick masterful direction and jack nicholson chilly acting nicholson plays jack torrance writer who accepts take care the overlook hotel canada during the winter period unaffected the gruesome stories surrounding the place claims nice isolated location just what needs finish his new book therefore the overlook becomes the new home the torrance family jack his wife wendy shelley duvall and their five year old son danny danny lloyd the boy particular senses right from the beginning that something wrong has been told the cook dick hallorann scatman crothers that endowed with mysterious psychic energy the titular shining which allows people like him and dick see flashes from the past and the future among other things because this gift the forces that inhabit the hotel immediately take interest danny even though quite capable resisting them that not jack case however gets increasingly paranoid regarding his wife affections and seeks comfort the company what can best defined ghosts triggering chain insanity and dread which very hard break the shining works horror movie because kubrick though having never worked this kind film before knew exactly what was effective and what wasn hence the larger focus atmosphere and psychological shocks than gore and creative bloodbaths king criticized the director for changing most the story omitting most the jack danny subplot merely hinted the film that led the book emotionally strong climax and while his disappointment valid the omission was actually necessary the novel dealt with redemption albeit unconventional way and redemption theme kubrick one the most famous analysts human decay never had soft spot for what interested the mental and subsequently physical unbalance that threatens the characters and keeps the creepy tone even thanks very cold approach and expert use the steadicam shot danny encounter with two ghostly twins being the best example another criticism king raised was about the actors especially nicholson the writer opinion his trademark grin the start the movie seemed indicate jack already was insane thus undermining the rest the story now true that nicholson looks bit goofy from the very beginning but equally true that martin sheen king ideal choice for the role probably would not have been able deliver performance terrifying nicholson from the moment starts grinning more unsettling way than before the immortal here johnny scene impossible picture another actor playing that part and even though the version the shining from 1997 isn bad the torrance character indelibly linked the one flew over the cuckoo nest star for duvall and lloyd both add terrific support the latter especially deserving place alongside harvey stephens the omen damien and haley joel osment cinema great horror child icons one might complain about duvall being completely different from the book counterpart blonde and beautiful and not having much else but scream and run but two things ought considered back 1980 the scream queen clich xc3 xa9 wasn one yet rarely has any actress looked genuinely terrified camera making the book movie differences secondary compared the real fear that emerges from wendy eyes irvine welsh the author trainspotting once said there such thing completely faithful adaptation any literary work and should know given the liberties danny boyle took when his junkie masterpiece was brought the screen yet that doesn mean the movie necessarily bad the shining proves said point perfection very little from the novel approximately included the film but kubrick and nichlolson hands this masterclass loose cinematic translation becomes one the finest most original horror pictures all time which really saying something given the genre current poor form
