1 |text welcome oakland where the dead come out play and even the boys hood can stop them this low budget direct video production seems timed coincide with the release land the dead the latest installment george romero famed zombie series the ghetto setting and hip hop soundtrack may provide additional appeal for inner city gore hounds ricky carl washington works medical research facility while raising his kid brother jermaine brandon daniels but the teenager bored macaroni and cheese dinners their tract house would rather spend his time hanging with street friends marco and kev apparently there not lot for african american high school dropouts this side the bay except deal drugs and scuffle with the homeys including rival latino gang bangers ricky plans sell their late parents house and move inland the castro valley more middle class and presumably safer environment unfortunately before this can happen drive shooting leaves jermaine dead the porch grief stricken ricky tries last desperate ploy tells scotty his lab assistant steal some the experimental cell regeneration formula they have been testing rats when double dose fails revive jermaine there choice except call 911 but funny thing happens the way the morgue the boy reanimated sputtering growling zombie chews the ambulance drivers and staggers off into the night bent revenge and hungry for fresh meat the feeding frenzy infects more victims and before the night over the east bay battleground between the living and the blood spattered undead the horror genre has seen more than its share cheap movie makers from wood herschel gordon lewis charles band but low budgets not necessarily mean bad films consider val lewton programmers cat people the leopard man isle the dead roger corman poe quickies romero night the living dead and john carpenter halloween the difference between memorable and awful has more with talent and ambition than money hood the living dead more fun than several hundred million dollars worth recent high priced horrors cheapness has its charms truly cheap films actors wear their own clothes amid real settings here the tract houses have freshly painted walls neutral matte tones lending bleakness oppressive douglas sirk bourgeois melodramas the 50s lines seem more improvised than scripted what the hell are gonna now just keep your eyes open for any thing that looks out the ordinary ricky and scotty call their boss who calls military man named romero have huge bitch problem that have take care fast not problem says the merc closing his phone and grabbing his guns everybody has guns and even when fighting zombies they their cell phones who isn nowadays information exchanged with naturalistic understatement what happened got into with some crazy motherfockers deja that park zombie again ricky even has blow his twitching girlfriend away saying only she gotten out hand unlike most zombie movies this one provides motive for mayhem jermaine takes revenge the gang bangers who shot him who turn continue the rumble this urban film making that implies its own social commentary near guerrilla production suggesting future for low budget horror that reflects real life instead supernatural clich xc3 xa9s the brothers quiroz who have trademarked their name anticipation new movement may inspire others tell stories arising from personal experience rather than imitating tired hollywood product considering their limited resources jose and eduardo quiroz have made cheap but technically acceptable feature about people they know photographer rocky robinson gets the job done music eduardo quiroz simpler than carpenter haunting halloween theme and hip hop songs the darkroom familia and others add atmosphere the result promising not exactly exhilarating they are learning their craft and unlike lewis and wood who never got any better their next may one watch
