1 |text footlight parade among the best the 1930 musical comedy extravaganzas snappy script and all star cast including jimmy cagney the lovely joan blondell dick powell and ruby keeler make this film cut above the rest directed and choreographed the creative genius busby berkeley this film will have you grinning from ear ear from start finish busby course the undisputed master the hollywood musical with gold diggers 1933 and 42nd street his credit dance director footlight parade graced hundreds scantily clad chorus girls berkeley trademark the elaborate dance numbers were shot with only one camera and busby was the first director film close ups the dancers his obsession with shapely legs and rear view shots amply demonstrated here the overall effect highly erotic and mesmerizing our boy jimmy cagney plays chester kent producer prologues short musical stage productions that were performed movie theaters entertain the audience before the talkies were shown surrounded crooked partners corporate spy and gold digging girlfriend although cagney had solid background vaudeville this was the first film which showed his dancing talents joan blondell memorable cagney wise cracking lovestruck secretary and ruby keeler adorable always the film climaxes with three outstanding production numbers honeymoon hotel the waterfall and shanghai lil each one masterpiece and not likely duplicated today hollywood where called special effects have replaced creative cinematography claudia bottom line clever and erotic with some the best musical production numbers ever put celluloid thoroughly enjoyable depression era romp
