rtrayal makes perfect complement eastwood harry and becomes philosophy and deed something his counterpart supporting roles two performances stand out paul drake mick creates the best psycho since andy robinson dynamic portrayal the serial killer the original dirty harry with actually very limited screen time drake establishes genuinely disconcerting presence that believable and convincing which adds much the purely visceral response the audience this the guy you can wait see harry take care the end also effective audrie neenan who makes her character ray parkins the epitome the proverbial low life who can found any bar any city performance that evokes gut level response and adds greatly the credibility the film that helps provide that necessary sense realism the supporting cast includes albert popwell horace mark kevloun bennett and nancy parsons mrs kruger with perfect blend drama and action sudden impact dispenses justice that fulfilling respite from reality the perfect justice not perfect world that makes for satisfying cinematic experience
