-1 |text the bygone days the catholic church sin eater was individual that through ritual would take the sins dying person upon themselves often these people were excommunicate similar individuals who the church would not absolve thereby denying them entrance into heaven the sin eaters were seen blasphemous circumventing the chruch monopoly redemption sex this bit with some overt supernatural mojo let the concept wander where may and you have the order movie that combines stigmata religious anti authoritarianism the files paranormal investigation and the thorn birds sexual spirituality into odd melange that sometimes works alex heath ledger rogue priest one the last members the order the carolingians semi heretical order knowledge seeking demon fighting priests when alex mentor found dead under bizarre circumstances bishop driscoll peter weller sends alex investigate tagging along are fellow carolingian thomas mark addy and mara shannyn sossman who was subject one alex exorcisms year prior the three rome investigate and are drawn into dark underworld bizarre catholic heresy ominous prophecies demonic intrusions and man claiming the last surviving sin eater benno furmann written and directed brian helgeland who worked with the same principals the scattershot and half hearted knight tale the film odd one and difficult classify wants several things once supernatural thriller religious intrigue dramatic television pilot and only sometimes succeeds any them this isn helped the slow pace the fact that most the actors seem sleepwalking through their performances with occasional bursts brilliance ledger particular has particularly stunning scene despair otherwise monochromatic performance sossman however displayed the same disconnected performance that she given all her films most notably the rules attraction the plot itself meanders back and forth between several different story arcs leading you wonder which the main one with each arc containing its share red herrings large gaps narrative appear lost between scenes times which can confusing for many but this also one the film saving graces the structure the film coupled the fact that there never truly clear antagonist until the very end the film forces the viewer analyze and reason time when most films are blatantly obvious about everything the exception this historical background the carolingians and the practice sin eating both which are explained dry exposition even the beginning the film character relationships and history are inferred instead explained combine this with the location shooting and judicious use special effects and you have very old world supernatural thriller with even the opening credits reminiscent something from the late early brief mention here well for the subtle and organic score david torn combination minimalist orchestration and lisa gerrard style exotic vocals very nice score that evocative without being bombastic and exists very deceptive simplicity confusing plot lack purpose and sometimes sleepy performances would often damn movie but for some reason the order remains watchable many people will very turned off the movie for its odd sensibilities and some may even become angry that they are forced engage the higher functions their brain understand still the film sheer intangibility will prevent from being either critical commercial success until the dvd which sure will stocked with copious amounts deleted scenes recommended film only for people who like think while they watch out
