1 |text saw heartland when was first released 1980 and have just seen again improves with age heartland not just for lovers indie films time when most american films are little more than cynical attempts make money with cgi pyrotechnics and vulgarity heartland holds slice american history also reminder how spoiled most modern urbanized americans are nothing this film overstated stagey one declaims any hollywood movie speeches the actors really inhabit their roles this really feels like small film but really bigger than most multizillion dollar hollywood productions the film based the lives real people 1910 elinore randall conchata ferrell who has never done anything better than this widow with year old daughter jerrine megan folsom living denver but wants more opportunities she advertises for position housekeeper the answered clyde stewart rip torn one our most under appreciated actors scots born rancher himself widower with homestead outside burnt fork wyoming elinore accepts the position seven dollars week and moves wyoming with her daughter she and her daughter move into stewart tiny house the property rolling treeless rangeland place endless vistas where the silence broken only the sounds made these people and their animals guaranteed make person feel small the three characters for long periods without seeing another human soul what worse stewart turns out taciturn the point being almost silent can talk the man elinore complains grandma landauer you better learn before winter replies grandma grandma lilia skala one the only two other characters who are seen more than fleetingly she came out wyoming from germany with her husband many years before and runs her ranch alone now that she also widowed grandma their nearest neighbor and the local midwife and still she lives ten miles away the other supporting character jack the hired hand barry primus elinore routine and her employer one endless backbreaking labor where there are modern conveniences and where everything must made fixed done hand this the real meat the film watching the ordinary life these ranchers they struggle against nature wrest living from the land but despite the constant toil and fatigue elinore always looking for other opportunities she learns that the tract adjacent stewart unclaimed impulsively she files claim the property twelve dollars almost two weeks pay meaning that she lives and she must actually live there and works for ten years she will get the deed naturally stewart learns what she has done with merciless logic points out that with money livestock credit and assets she has chance succeeding then offers solution proposes marriage the stunned elinore realizes that this the only real alternative and accepts think that stewart proposal purely machiavellian wants the land and the free labor but see that fact genuinely fond elinore and they grow together couple she becomes pregnant she goes into labor the middle midwinter blizzard clyde travels for hours horseback through the storm the ten miles grandma and the ten miles back only announce that grandma wasn there this more like real life than pleasant folks elinore has the baby all herself with help whatsoever their son still infant when gets sick and dies they lose half their livestock the vicious winter they struggle the last sequence the film supposed optimistic the birth calf clyde calls elinore urgently help him deliver the calf instead being head first the calf footling breech presentation and elinore must physically pull the calf out the birth canal there cgi animatronics trickery fakery special effects what you see what happened folks calf born bed straw wooden barn lamplight with that the film does not much end simply stop leaving the viewer unsatisfied but after while you appreciate the film whole not just for its ending this little gem rewards patience and thoughtfulness will watchable long after most the films the last generation have long been forgotten
