1 |text the mid 1930s hollywood was regaining its confidence after the difficulties the talkie transition although all the technical problems sound had been solved very quickly took longer resolve the questions how talking pictures should look how they should structured and how they should acted the informer key picture that shows the extent which wordless moments can convey story asserting the power images without ignoring the necessities sound and dialogue this not say the informer truly throwback the golden days the silents for one thing many silent pictures were not purely visual their narrative and were overburdened with title cards but what the informer has the self assuredness extend moments between dialogues focus reactions more than speeches and let shots play out simply for atmosphere director john ford for all his capability was filmmaker who appears have put effort proportion how interested was the material thought story was silly just did half arsed luckily the informer with its depiction community honour working class life and most importantly irish setting was everything ford loved and the result one his finest works ford only really employs too kinds shot the first places xc2 x96 the dublin streets shrouded mist and darkness their furthest depths cannot seen dingy interiors where the walls and ceilings seem press the second faces striking close ups against plain backgrounds usually without dialogue focusing upon the inner conflicts these people lead man victor mclaglen fits perfectly within this character and this manner filming him mclaglen performance does not look like much being about drunk act but the other heartfelt emoting here and there his gypo nolan has what alcoholics refer moment clarity with such performances are oscars won mclaglen backed spot supporting cast among whom there are weak links particular nice have donald meek and una connor usually only seen comic relief roles playing straight dramatic parts for once although meek appearance does contain one two jokes the tone the scene and much his manner serious not only these two deliver incredibly deep performances their familiarity most viewers comedy players gives added note poignancy their part this tragedy rko who produced the informer were perhaps the most adventurous and willing take risks all the major studios thanks this are able see dismal story with despicable anti hero its centre which could easily have been clunky over earnest mess instead filled with moody atmosphere and depth character which keeps watching and draws into its world
