1 |text this story the winchester rifle model 1873 the gun that won the west cowman outlaw peace officer soldier the winchester was treasured possession indian would sell his soul own one winchester the first collaboration between director anthony mann and actor james stewart duo that would create run superior westerns that added new psychological depth the genre the story sees stewart lin mcadam pursuing the man who killed his father riding into dodge city with his trusty friend johnny williams millard mitchell lin runs into dutch henry brown stephen mcnally the man wants but with wyatt earp will geer having taken all the guns from those entering the town both men are unable have the shoot out that they are ready for the men instead square competition win winchester rifle competition that lin eventually wins but before can leave town with the magnificent prize dutch ambushes him steals the rifle and skips town fast lin sets off hate filled pursuit both man and rifle the rifle will changed hands number times with each time adding another dimension the day reckoning for all approaches very much benchmark for what became known the called psychological western winchester basically story decent man driven borderline insanity event his past tho shot black and white the only one the duos westerns that was the landscapes are still breathtaking feasts for the eyes the tone set with the opening scene lin and johnny horseback and silhouette amble over hillside they make their way dodge city just the starting point that would see mann use his vistas way running concurrent with his characters emotional states stewart gives one his finest and most intense performances mcadam proving once and for all that was one americas finest and most versatile actors the support cast isn too bad either shelley winters excellent the sole female amongst the machismo while mitchell mcnally geer and the always great dan duryea add further class proceedings there even bit parts for tony curtis and rock hudson here tho the latter playing indian brave stretch too far originally the film was project for fritz lang who even had the script ready run but lang walked away from something that proved blessing for western fans for great director that lang was with mann directing and with new script from borden chase robert richards hands set the wheels motion alter the course the genre not only with the further efforts that mann stewart produced but also who they influenced the likes budd boetticher nicholas ray and sam fuller were all taking notes and gleefully for the western purists they followed suit and carried the psychological torch still further big hit the box office back release winchester magnificent film that still packs punch the modern age
