ose save lives gideon naudet decides leave the firehouse and walk down the impact area once there captures the impact the second plane united airlines flight 175 with world trade knows jules with chief pfeiffer inside the towers watching and capturing the crowds reaction the unimaginable gideon begins capture tape the growing fear lower manhattan inside tower one jules records the last view the world loved ones will have their sons fathers uncles grandfathers husbands boyfriends friends one one each firefighter carrying lbs equipment begin the long arduous climb stories rescue the injured and trapped jules also catches the last glimpse chief pfeiffer will have his brother kevin leaves his selfless duty also caught video the gutwrenching sound falling bodies hitting pavement from victims choosing jump from the higher floors above the impact zones sooner than face death the hands the flames and smoke but jules respectful never once does capture sensationalistic moment the money shot his work professional through his baptism fire also catches the sight debris falling from tower two after hit the second plane and the ordered way the firefighters evacuated civilians from the building then jules caught the collapse the south tower and the first official victim taken father michael judd the chaplain for the fire department then jules and chief pfeiffer make their way from the fallout the collapse tower two tower one begins its structural collapse what results breathtakingly poignant view from inside ground zero jules and gideon work separately document that day not knowing either alive each fearing the worst each firefighter arrives the firehouse they greet each other with joyous hugs having made back and one moment overwhelming emotion jules and gideon are reunited jules cries his brother shoulder gideon embraces his younger brother hanlon makes the filmmakers the subject there one fearful moment when tony benetakos who left the station with former chief believed have been lost but returns the fold this probie has proven himself shown with only three interruptions stunning achievement documentary filmmaking ranks there with the hindenburg footage showing history unfolds the naudets are commended for their deft handling the subject lesser hands the tendency would toward the sensational but the naudets temper their eye toward dignity and compassion narrated hanlon get the feel his words takes the audience through the events september robert niro hosts the program sombre restrained way never seeks the camera for his own glory rather lays out the scenes you are about see also commend cbs for their bravery airing this special chastised for their attempt grabbing ratings they temper their editing toward the emotions the relatives those who perished this must see for anyone who needs reminded what true heroism isn about dribbling basketball selling album hate lyrics about humanity its best heroism its finest and the cost freedom
