1 |text the tenants began 1971 short novel the now deceased bernard malamud writer philosopher examining the conflicts between jews and african americans the incendiary atmosphere brooklyn the time the book was written novel the story was gut wrenchingly real transcribed into screenplay novices david diamond and danny green who also directs more cerebral dissertation that gradually erupts into action the final moments harry lesser dylan mcdermott jewish novelist with one book under his belt but currently attempting finish his newest book ten years into the writing convinced that must complete the novel the same environment where was started the sole tenant condemned brooklyn tenement owned levinspiel seymour cassel who constantly tries buy out harry lease that the filthy dilapidated building can demolished into this atmosphere enters another black militant quasi anti semitic writer willie spearmint snoop dogg whom harry befriends hides and offers help the nascent novelist attempt write about the death all white people harry attempts help willie lead conflict not the least which harry meeting willie girlfriend the white jewish irene bell rose byrne less than friendly gathering willie militant black brothers and sisters willie and irene are the skids and harry gradually falls love with irene and they plan leave new york soon harry finishes his novel when willie hears the assignation and further critiqued harry willie explodes and begins the downward descent not only delicate friendship but also competition between writers the ending reveals the slippery nature the human condition and the human capacity for violence and undoing the actors their best with script that bit awkward but despite scripted lines that border preaching they create believable characters the cinematography enhances the story keeping the mood dank and dense and primarily confined the condemned building the musical score appropriately makes use the solo jazz trumpet and blues piano underline the ten