1 |text this final entry george lucas star wars movies often regarded the weakest the lot however this not say that totally worthless entry the series the contrary sure not groundbreaking its predecessors and bit more slow going times but return the jedi still offers lot warrant the price admission the first third the movie where luke and his friends rescue han from the palace jabba the hutt classic jabba truly disgusting blob bloated flesh who speaks his own language not only makes great villain but memorable one too must have been nightmare construct this giant puppet much less give the spark and life that see the finished product actually what also makes this sequence fun the clever use puppets for the various members jabba court including the intimidating slavering rancor and scary sarlaac pit monster builds masterfully its climax and pulls punches all the while things get little bit slower around the second act where luke discovers that and leia are related blood and when travel the forest planet endor home the cuddlesome yet stalwart ewoks most the complaints about return the jedi that read seem centered these furry creatures that they somehow disrupt the tone the saga don totally agree with that although this moment probably played out bit longer than should however their leader wicket played warrick davis delightfully memorable creation and watching how they handle the imperial troops technology with their simple natural weapons provides nice contrast the time get the third act though the pace picks again intercut between the ewoks battle against the troops lando and the rebel forces launching attack against the empire all new half completed death star and luke final showdown with darth vader and the emperor the latter ties with the jabba palace sequence the highlight the movie mark hamill flexes his acting chops once again luke skywalker these scenes and watching him fully matured jedi knight makes for unforgettable performance also iconic james earl jones voice darth vader rivaled only the shriveled crone like emperor played with deliciously raspy frightening evil ian mcdiarmid the tension between this trio heightens the excitement this climactic moment which appropriately darkly lit and menacingly underscored the star wars movies have always set standards for special effects and the technical work return the jedi can easily hold candle its predecessors the space battle fights are exhilarating always and the speeder bike chase through the forest knockout course given that this movie was made after new hope and the empire strikes back probably shouldn surprising that the special effects have reached even greater level excellence the acting classic star wars fare hamill harrison ford and carrie fisher all mature and deepen into their roles and anthony daniels provides more hilarious moments 3po frank yoda only appears two scenes but makes the most and yes there also john williams music all told while return the jedi falters little bit the middle the first and third acts deliver style making this rather satisfactory finale one the greatest sagas ever 1997 george lucas released the classic star wars digitally restored and revamped special editions which featured added effects and shots well some enhancements the three return the jedi appears have caused the most commotion with star wars fans perhaps can due the jarringly out place albeit funny you not easily offended jedi rocks musical number jabba palace which although technically amazing does disrupt the flow the film however did like the ending montage scenes where see victory celebrations occurring the various planets the galaxy this dvd version features yet more tweaking get see more montage finale scenes notably naboo where hear what sounds like jar jar binks screaming wesa free and what probably the most controversial change hayden christensen the specter anakin skywalker the closing scenes probably due the intense and unfair disdain fans have for his somewhat shaky work episode attack the clones seems inevitable that fans would put this edition down for that alone however you watching the star wars saga chronologically and contemplating about chances are you may react little differently nonetheless issue that fans have raised probably best warned beforehand nice would have lucas release the original versions these three classic films nonetheless stands what said about these revamps being the definitive editions his classic trilogy and when viewing the star wars movies altogether one complete saga lucas intended actually makes sense keep them technically and aurally consistent the original films will always engraved our memories but these new incarnations are just much fun one can give them chance
