1 |text filmed mgm the same sets the english version but german garbo second portrayal anna christie benefited from practice and her apparent ease with german dialog garbo appears more relaxed and natural under jacques feyder direction than under clarence brown and her silent movie mannerisms have all but disappeared which made her transition sound complete the strength she brought the character remains here although has been softened and garbo reveals more anna vulnerability the entire cast with the exception garbo different from the previous version the film and garbo benefits from not having compete with marie dressler who stole every scene she was during the english language version feyder film garbo holds the center attention throughout although the three supporting players particularly the father gave excellent performances feyder direction was more assured than clarence brown and his use the camera and editing techniques did not seem constrained the new sound process did those brown the film moves with more fluidity than the english language adaptation and the static nature the first film has been replaced with flow that maintains viewer interest even william daniels cinematography seems improved over his filming the brown version captured garbo luminescence and the atmospherics the docks with style also the screenplay adaptation for the european audience made anna profession quite clear from the start and the explicitness clarifies for viewers who were unfamiliar with the play what was only implied the brown filming however the film was made before the production code was introduced which made the censorship puzzling garbo oscar nomination for anna christie was always somewhat mystifying and suspected that the nod was given more recognition her relatively smooth transition sound films than for her performance however some the academy voters may have seen the german language version the film and they realized will contemporary viewers that her anna christie under feyder direction was definitely oscar worthy
