1 |text what platoon from the japanese army were send back time 400 years right the middle the feudal wars that led the formation the tokugawa shogunate great pitch right the movie does exactly what says the tin thankfully the writers didn bother explain the usually ridiculous sci movies scientific mumbo jumbo time transport how why they just did however the time transport sequence itself trippy hell and quite beautiful not bit dated not silly one would imagine the rest the movie follows the premise but while loses bit steam with the various subplots that follow the arrival medieval japan picks with devastating battle sequence undoubtedly the main order the day the whole concept and extension the movie itself was probably originated from this simple pitch what equipped with the latest modern warfare were fight samurais and boy does deliver the main battle sequence that spans more than half hour probably one the best its kind action war movies not only relentless and exhausting pace and length also terrific mish mash styles and techniques that only unique premises like samurai can deliver mean where else would you get the chance feature tanks ninjas complete with shuriikens helicopter and samurais the same shot the platoon led lieutenant iba tears literally through hundreds extras gunning them down with machine guns mortars grenades and tanks this mish mash styles with one foot firmly rooted the sprawling jidai geki epic kurosawa kagemusha hiroshi inagaki samurai banners while the other western action and war movies there are stylistic touches like the wonderful slow motion shots and bloody violence that bring sam peckinpah enzo castellari circa keoma mind japanese cinema has always been influenced westerns and other hollywood works and vice versa and samurai effortlessly turns this east meets west melting pot into exciting film the film makers thankfully take the whole thing seriously and the movie benefits immensely from not that tongue cheek mentality completely absent just that doesn try pander bad good audiences that enjoy laughing their movies the budget was probably hefty evident the hundreds extras elaborate costumes very decent for production that not traditional jidai geki and special effects the camera work and editing are all top notch almost better than movie with higher artistic ambitions deserves not withouts its flaws either course there are many song scenes where all sorts japanese rock disco and country songs play over montages there bonding scene love interest scene war hell scene etc the songs themselves are pretty lame and corny and detract from the whole thing although clocks whooping 140 minutes flies like bullet for the most part still some scenes flashbacks and subplots the first half could have been clipped for tighter effect the cast also deserves mention featuring such prominent names sonny chiba isao natsuyagi goyokin samurai wolf tsunehiko watase the yakuza papers and hiroyuki sanada all them hitting the right notes
