1 |text paul verhoeven has one the strangest oeuvres any major director started off making art house films his native netherlands before moving hollywood where began making subversive genre pieces which are often seen mere entertainments the mainstream crowd 1983 the fourth man was the last film made before moving the and seems have been transitional film for him from the beginning the fourth man clear that the film will seen from the perspective the famous albeit impoverished author gerard seeming homage carol reed similarly titled 1949 film the third man the film begins with author making trip speak crowd literature enthusiasts the similarities end there however gerard runs into major complications before arriving the auditorium and the speech itself goes fairly smoothly spite the relative ease with which completes this function know that the author somewhat troubled has realistic fantasies about murdering his roommate before leaving his house and also has surreal fantasy involving hotel sees advertised and detached eyeball growing out door peephole that sometimes has trouble keeping his fantasies separate from reality made all the more clear when anecdote tells exposed untrue and admits that lie the truth until longer knows whether something did didn happen the fourth man full surreal fantasies and dreams which are made all the more disturbing because very easy see how they relate events which have seen occur and because they sometimes foreshadow events which haven occurred yet between the effectiveness the unreal sequences and verhoeven careful editing style this ends being the most atmospheric film this side don look now and like that film this one full ambiguity unlike that film the fourth man also perversely funny gerard deeply held catholic beliefs seep into every aspect his life including sexuality naturally associates female hair stylist knows intimately with the biblical delilah though fears she remove even more important symbol masculinity with her scissors erotic fantasy sequence that would make luis xc3 xb1uel blush substitutes man attracted for life size statue christ the cross the fourth man horror film which manages bring the viewer into the mind the protagonist while still maintaining certain ambiguity certainly seems gerard danger but may just more his lying the truth the film also full both subtle and not subtle visual symbolism which helps make unique and satisfying cinematic experience
