1 |text slight spoilers way back before evangelion was made before hideaki anno was idol and household name for many anime fans and before gainax had reached the status fanfavorite gunbuster was made with only wings honneamise made gainax that time and the famous otakon shorts course gunbuster had some tough acts follow didn make easier itself picking out genre that was already done countless times before space opera luckily gainax decided put out six part oav direct video series this allows the series have bigger scope than would have been possible was made into film this also prevents from becoming too boring and overly long with lots pointless battles and filler along the way besides that they made some effort stay clear from the tested space opera mechanics used macross gundam and many other popular space operas for one the shows starts out pretty light with noriko the okinawa high school for mechapiloting noriko the daughter respected ship commander who died battle when she was still little kid this makes her life the academy quite hard some her fellow classmates start suspect that noriko favored the professors the first episode pretty much comedy drama with very tight focus the characters and setting the school things quickly change when the threat alien invasion announced and noriko and kazumi best girl class are chosen help the assembled fleet out the middle bulk gunbuster leaves our female lead space focusing both personal drama and action couple more characters are introduced and parts noriko past are dragged again besides that the alien threat becomes more imminent every minute and the gunbuster mankind final hope presented smart writer okada was incorporated the principles time dilation spice things bit short time moves slower for those who travel the speed light this means that noriko can part war that takes almost century complete also the dramatic aspect this accentuated when noriko sees her friends again her return base who have aged considerably more than her the science might not perfect but presented pretty believable way with even some science theatre shorts between the episodes where noriko kazumi and their coach give short description the scientific principles used the series the animation for series made the 80s definitely good the designs are retro 80s style course but has charm animation fluent enough and the character designs are nice although the costumes betray some the fanservice fascination gainax will later exploit the fullest the mechas throughout the shows are pretty cool too with the gunbuster the ultimate killing machine strong and vast the last episode was entirely done black and white while generally believed but not confirmed that this was done for budget reasons lends whole different atmosphere the series which suited perfectly for the latter part the music very typical space opera fair too bombastic places very generic and definitely not worth buying does fit the series for the most part but can become quite annoying times tanaka not really famous composer and the only other respectable series worked dragon half you think 80s anime music you will know what expect the series progresses the focus slowly shifts from drama space opera epic battle but such way the viewer will hardly notice this step step the drama will toned down and the battles will take the front row neither aspect ever left completely out though with the last episode sight noriko and crew are fighting for the further existence human kind and with the last battle sight certain questions are presented the audience concerning position the human race the galaxy and how far can guarantee self preservation while they are never answered later they still present some interesting food for thought the last episode very epic with nice but quite predictable ending though not all endings should contain numerous outlandish twists course again fits the series gunbuster may sound like your average space opera anime first with alien invasions huge battles and some personal drama and for the bigger part but done exceptionally well for change instead going for steady mix former elements six episodes long gunbuster presents change from small scale drama large scale epic heroism along the way meet with some various interesting and well fleshed out characters which mutual relationships changing heavily due the time dilation phenomenon the show very tightly written although does tend slip some points overly dramatic occurrences and too cheesy mecha attacks could have been easily avoided overall the trip gunbuster takes you very relaxed sometimes sad sometimes heroic one might not have shattered the boundaries and limits the space opera genre but least bend them little highly enjoyable anime classic but not without flaws
