1 |text with the release peter jackson famed lord the rings trilogy even easier dismiss ralph bakshi 1978 animated lord the rings film inferior agree with the majority that jackson trilogy the essential film adaptation tolkien work but that does not prevent from enjoying bakshi ambitious pioneering effort jackson has admitted that received least some inspiration from seeing bakshi film and there are some clear similarities between their adaptations the film colorful picturesque backdrops are excellent and the score memorable was for the most part satisfied the drawings the characters the pairs pippin and merry and eowyn and galadriel are mostly indistinguishable from each other visually the balrog and treebeard were unimpressive but these points didn bother very much however the nazgul are aptly drawn and made sufficiently eerie the only character representation was bothered was sam was made look unbecomingly silly this film novel for its animation techniques addition hand drawn characters live actors are incorporated into the animation through rotoscoping quite apparent which characters are hand drawn and which are rotoscoped but none the less found that the film style was novelty the use rotoscoped live actors for the battle scenes was good decision and helped these scenes turn out well the voice acting was generally high quality particularly good was john hurt who provided authoritative voice for aragorn aragorn isn favorite character mine from the stories but backed john hurt voice was favorite character this adaptation other favorite was william squire whose voice appropriately strong for gandalf the only actor who seemed inappropriate was michael scholes sam whose voice acting was irritating and added sam unfortunately silly image the only other bothersome part the voice acting the mispronunciation character and place names particularly strange was the decision frequently have saruman referred aruman producing this film ralph bakshi expected have the ability produce two films hence this film contains about half the story from the start the fellowship the ring the end the battle helm deep the two towers the obvious implication this that the film story highly condensed version the story from the books enjoy the original stories and more thorough adaptations but the liberties taken compress the story didn bother even the choice leave arwen out the story enough the key elements the story were this film keep engaged for the duration and there was even novelty being able breeze through half the lord the rings story 132 minutes the battle scenes were impressive and particular the orc march and battle helm deep were tremendous ralph bakshi version the lord the rings isn perfect and doubt number lord the rings readers lament the cuts the story however for the drawbacks this film were minor compared the thrill seeing effective adaptation half great trilogy only strong lament that unable see the second part this first great tale the lord the rings since bakshi was not given the budget create sequel
