1 |text this movie amazing for several reasons harris takes extremely awkward documentary and turns into relevant social commentary groovin gary small town kid who assumed well liked for his many impersonations when decides play olivia newton john local talent show for whom very passionate gary actions show that odds with the conservative social environment which lives this results him making various justifications for his actions that people will not think that fact transvestite other such social outcast the second installment harris exploites the struggle between gary and beaver novice attempt make narrative out the original documentary the third and final installment the trilogy truly amazing for harris extreme sensitivity with the subject unlike the second installment the orkly kid shows gary truly troubled character struggles gain acceptance within his own community avail his secret passion for dressing like olivia newton john distances him even further from the people that already consider him social outcast the movie depicted realistically that like reality lends itself many reactions surely one can see gary ridiculously pathetic character but may also identify with him outcast
