1 |text there director like more than mamoru oshii but sadly even though directed quite few films that gained huge international attention there are still fair few his films that have slipped through the cracks tachiguishi one them and even though loved bits not hard see why distributors the west are somewhat reluctant release between his big and serious films oshii known some smaller and quirkier projects while tachiguishi definitely falls into this category oshii has really outdone himself with this one creating something that very hard classify even freaky japanese flick figure its very core lies documentary not quite unlike otaku video but rather than make fool existing subculture oshii invents his own and delves into the lives culinary heroes scrounging away food for free and upholding the japanese culinary level oshii approach the subject has close ties with dai nipponjin the subject handled with deadly sense gravity while the images screen look ridiculous can deadpan humor taken the extreme but that not all rather than simply shooting his mockumentary oshii decided make using new visual technique baptized superlivemation weird mix live action photography digital animation and puppets stick performed and acted out posed you want the greats the japanese animation industry less the project was supposed low budget possible and you think that just about covers know that the film extremely dialogue heavy making good companion piece for innocence the influence the grifters analyzed from all kinds cultural political and even philosophical angles fired the audience through continuous stream monologues and dialogues and make even worse the whole film completely grounded actual japanese history and customs making even harder for foreigner get good grip the material needless say multiple viewings are advised make the best all the details tucked away inside the film that said conceptual level the film easy follow and already pretty hilarious various grifters are introduced were they the most influential historical figures post war japan the film plays like you expect serious documentary any other important figure unfold but somehow the big and crudely animated cut out photography limbs which figures are assembled don quite make all that serious the range characters introduced sublime shinji higuchi taking the cake cow creature wearing nose ring while taking the fast food chains with his gang bull people oshii regular kenji kawai provides besides pretty comical performance score ranging from atmospheric and dark wacky strange and comical lot fun had from the exaggerated noises and effects complementing the animation and totally contradicting the tone the rest the film visually the film very atmospheric though must said that the animation pretty scarce and while effective remains toned down only burst out hyperactive weirdness from time time which not exactly bad thing seeing how tachiguishi dialogue heavy despite that the film still visual masterpiece each frame looks absolutely lush and tailored match and improve the general atmosphere the film beware though because tachiguishi does demand lot from the viewer you don speak japanese there lot reading done and there are many cultural references that demand some attention top that the monologues the film area quite extended and can hard follow the film still lacks english subtitles and even though french was largely sufficient get what was all about sure missed many the finer points the film tachiguishi not easy film get into but around halfway through reaches full steam and doesn let off from there still hope see this one again with english dutch subs dub would actually best for film like this much like container though guess quality anime dub bit too much ask for with all that said can only congratulate oshii another marvelous film rare find film that blends and mixes many styles and influences create something that unique and still works the film smart looks and sounds great and filled the brim with creativity immensely funny even you can catch all the details the first viewing but sure least get this with decent subs the automated english translation that floating out there completely worthless and does the film justice all tachiguishi caters very specific audience and not surprised the french got their release while the rest europe and the rest the western world still waiting for sign this film but for those that like oshii appreciate dry and deadpan humor and crave creative spirits film that cannot missed even though could just well misfire
1 |text having have someone hold your hand whenever walk down stairs having others taste your food before you eat facing over bearing mother these are only few the obstacles which the young victoria has deal with this film there also the various power struggles going well attempts her life needless say makes for very fascinating and informative viewing had only previously seen emily blunt the devil wears prada and little else she was that film she once again the standout here was extremely impressed with her portrayal the young victoria and thought she handled the role very well she makes the transition from the young victoria meet the start the film the queen victoria she becomes later entirely believable blunt perfectly cast the role showing all the different sides from the vulnerable the strong from the young victoria who makes mistakes the queen who takes control not enough can said about emily blunt this role she quite simply exquisite commanding your attention every second she screen she keeps you transfixed and including the final shot the film rupert friend proves also well cast victoria love interest and eventual husband prince albert the actors have nice chemistry and you absolutely believe their developing relationship they have their disagreements but you can tell that they are love blunt and friend are excellent every scene that they share and keep you interested what happening between victoria and albert the other actors the film are also very good paul bettany lord melbourne miranda richardson the duchess kent mark strong sir john conroy and jim broadbent king william there not single bad performance this film the less focused upon people are well portrayed also given what little screen time they have even victoria dog cavalier king charles spaniel named dash memorable and makes impact the film although the movie does tend skip more than few aspects victoria life especially the end and instead tells what happened with her and albert screen what matters the most what actually see this after all film about the young victoria not the middle aged victoria nor the old victoria while there are some embellishments made history with this film remains focused what sets out which tell the story how the young princess rose power the movie looks amazing the costumes emily blunt wears are visually stunning and the music only adds the film never detracts from exceptionally shot and unlike lot films these days this movie actually good length doesn run long that you lose interest feel that needlessly being drawn out goes without saying that what makes this film great emily blunt she fine form here turning another excellent performance and elevating this film above what might have been had another actress been cast this rather important historic role this one finely crafted film with excellent performances that should definitely seen you have appreciation for fascinating look woman who was extremely significant history this must see
