1 |text when small hobbit named frodo baggins inherits magic ring from his uncle the wizard gandalf investigates and discovers that the ring ancient creation evil dark lord should the ring end back his hands will regain his power and destroy middle earth frodo and his loyal friends set out quest destroy the ring with band warriors this underrated adaption the classic novels only covers the first half the story regardless this epic and wonderfully animated film the animation superbly done with rotoscope which tracing over live action footage ralph bakshi worked well with the low budget was given the film also boasts grand music score leonard rosenman that fits every scene there are few plot holes with the script but that has excused considering the original deal was make the book trilogy into two films much had crammed the first one biggest gripe some the character design samwise was bit too goofy while the other hobbits act completely normal the other characters are actually well written for the screen and the voice actors great job was pleased that legolas actually bit more helpful the plot the rotoscoped orcs are more comical than frightening while the ringwraiths are eerie and nightmarish another problem that the evil wizard saruman called aruman thanks the writers overall think little more money and better writers would have done this lot justice but there something charming about ralph bakshi made valiant effort making screen adaption these classic stories the film suffers terribly from being overshadowed the live action films but still great movie for animation lovers all ages
