1 |text although was released way back 1967 cold blood still remains the benchmark which all true crime films are matched veteran writer director richard brooks elmer gantry adapted truman capote non fiction book into chilling docudrama that retains disturbing power even today thirty five years later robert blake and scott wilson portray perry smith and dick hickock two cons who tip from hicock old cellmate floyd wells broke into the holcomb kansas home herbert clutter looking for wall safe supposedly containing 000 but safe was ever found and the two men instead wound killing clutter his wife and their two children getting away with only radio pair binoculars and lousy forty dollars two months the run including aimless vacation northern mexico ended las vegas when cops caught them stolen car but eventually comes out after merciless grilling kansas law enforcement officials that these two men committed that heinous crime holcomb tried and convicted four counts murder they stew jail over five year period appeals and denials until both are hanged death april 1965 blake and smith are absolutely chilling the two dispassionate killers who show remorse for what they done but are concerned about getting caught john forsythe also does good turn alvin dewey the chief detective investigating the crime does gerald laughlin his assistant tactic that both faithful capote book and good artistic gambit all around brooks does not show the murders the beginning instead shows the two killers pulling the clutter house the last light goes out then cuts the next morning and the horrifying discovery the bodies only during the ride back kansas when blake questioned forsythe and narrates the story see the true horror what happened that night don see that much blood being spilled these scenes but don need the shotgun blasts and the horrified look the clutters faces they know they are about die are more than disturbing enough there need resort explicitly bloody slasher film violence brooks wisely filmed cold blood stark black and white and the results are excellent thanks conrad hall expertise the chilling jazz score quincy jones the capper the end result one the most unsettling films any kind ever made devastating its own low key fashion 134 minute study crime that shook entire state and indeed entire nation and should seen though viewer discretion advised the rating there for reason
