1 |text noteworthy that mine only the third review this film whereas patton lust for glory producer frank mccarthy earlier biography controversial american general from the second world war has date attracted nearly hundred comments like previous reviewer intrigued why one film should have received much more attention than the other one difference between the two films that patton more focused concentrating relatively short period and immediately after the end the second world war whereas macarthur covers not only this war but also its subject role the korean war well his period american governor occupied japan during the interlude the main difference however lies the way the two leaders are played gregory peck dominates this film even more than george scott dominated patton whereas scott had another major star karl malden playing opposite him general bradley none the other actors macarthur are household names least for their film work scott course portrayed patton aggressive and fiery tempered man who times was war with the rest the human race not just with the enemy suspect that real life general macarthur was volcanic individual patton but that not how appears this film peck macarthur more reflective thoughtful bent comparable the liberal intellectuals played some his other films times even seems man the political left much his speech the occasion the japanese surrender 1945 could have been written paid member cnd and his policies for reforming japanese society during the american occupation have semi socialist air them attempt show something macarthur gift for inspiring leadership peck makes him fine speaker but his speeches always seem owe more the studied tricks the practised rhetorician than any fire the heart atticus finch from kill mockingbird had put general uniform whereas scott attempted warts and all portrait patton the criticism has been made that macarthur attempts gloss over some its subject less attractive qualities think that this criticism fair one particularly far the korean war concerned the film gives the impression that macarthur was brilliant general who dared stand interfering militarily ignorant politicians who did not know how fight the war and was sacked for his pains when victory was within his grasp many historians course feel that truman was forced sack macarthur because the latter conduct was becoming risk world peace and had choice but accept stalemate because stalin would not have allowed his chinese allies humiliated even during the korean scenes peck macarthur comes across more idealistic than his real life original probably was see little his rashness and naivety about political matters truman remark knows much about politics pig knows about sunday was said about eisenhower but could equally well have been applied macarthur approach international diplomacy perhaps the film attempt paint out some macarthur warts reflects the period which was made the late seventies after the twin traumas vietnam and watergate was difficult time for america and public looking for reassurance might have welcomed reassuringly heroic depiction military figure from the previous generation another criticism would make the film that falls between two stools was intended full biography macarthur something should have been shown his early life which not covered all the first see the general when leading the american resistance the japanese invasion the philippines one theme that runs throughout the film the influence general macarthur father himself military hero would have liked see what sort man arthur macarthur was and just why his son considered him such hero and role model another interesting way making the film would have been concentrate korea and macarthur clash with truman with equal prominence given the two men and with actors similar stature playing them the way which the film actually was made seemed less interesting than either these alternative approaches would wrong however give the impression that disliked the film altogether although may not have agreed with peck interpretation the main role there denying that played with his normal professionalism and seriousness the film whole good example solid workmanlike biopic thoughtful and informative good film but one that could have been better one pedantic note the map which macarthur shown using during the korean war shows the dmz the boundary between the two korean states that did not come into existence until after the war the pre war boundary was the 38th parallel also think that macarthur was referring the tocsin war war may toxic but difficult listen with thirsty ear for toxin
