-1 |text wish spike lee had chosen different title for his film summer sam conveys the impression that the film about the infamous serial killer david berkowitz not gritty earthy portrait nyc street life during the hot summer when berkowitz terrorized that city the film follows several young fictional characters italian american neighborhood and their reactions the son sam threat there vinny and his wife dionna there richie and ruby and several other characters the problem that these characters are not likable they are routinely annoying and times unbearable lee then belabors their high energy chaotic lives which are filled with anger lust and general turmoil there are least two protracted fight scenes between vinny and his wife redundant disco dance scenes countless gabfests over and over kept wondering where the film editor meanwhile with all that bulk the film passes the chance convey any real sense fear dread arising from the son sam menace which too much the background lee more successful showing different kind menace that arising from neighborhood vigilante groups the acting uniformly good that combined with disco music and lavish attention costumes and production design make you really feel like you are italian american neighborhood nyc 1977 the film atmospheric authenticity however not nearly enough offset rambling overblown script about the lives grossly irritating people
