1 |text had the pleasure screening the big bad swim the 2006 new london film festival last week the festival highlights some the best independent and non mainstream films from the past year was assumption that the big bad swim was chosen for screening this festival for the simple reason that was shot locally and around eastern connecticut however the credits began roll could only think about how well the big bad swim compared the others featured during the festival far topped list followed the puffy chair who killed the electric car and transamerica the the big bad swim engaging truthful and often humorous look several adult education swim class pupils and their likable yet troubled instructor that has depth that not seen screen quite while the interweaving character development and plot lines derived from something absurd adult swimming lessons works subtle and endearing ways which found refreshing the plot doesn beat you over the head with direction rather builds and grows organically with pace that was spot was never bored never cringed never stepped out the story the screen the humor the film something like napoleon dynamite meets old school the acting from group relatively unknown actors was credible and their dialog never seemed awkward contrived obviously not being multi million production the camera shot weren all awe inspiring and clear but adequate and well done for the budget the lighting and filming technique for scenes filmed the strip club setting were particularly eye catching because more realistic approach than similar themed scene found closer also found shots filmed underwater the class from the waist down seemed just much portrait character shot from the shoulders could sure said over and over from many the independent film industry but have say the big bad swim isn picked for some kind distribution would extremely disappointed the big bad swim needs seen you have the chance see this film see disappointment impossible
