nk she deserves lot more roles well decent roles than she gets david strathairn newcomer this series noah vosen definitely the bad guy the movie and really excels definitely the nastiest character met and some the decisions makes are truly nasty strathairn relishes the role and too gets some superb scenes the movie special mention must also albert finney who makes the most his all too brief screen time will not say anything about the character that best left surprise but trust his scenes are some the highlights the movie the bourne movies have always had strict focus the storyline more than the action sequences this isn say the trilogy lacks action sequences good god there loads them dotted all throughout the movies but running throughout the movie very well written and well acted storyline this storyline concludes the best way imaginable this movie watched supremacy the night before saw ultimatum was nice because could notice certain little parts that very final scene supremacy new york lot more important that ever imagined the time won spoil for people but recommend checking supremacy before you see ultimatum unfortunately though for lot people they will see ultimatum purely because the action sequences this the part where should condemn such people and say they should see for the storyline but lying didn say that favourite parts the bourne series whole are the car chases the mini car chase identity one favourite car chases all time well the action ultimatum has the best the bourne series fact the movie kicks off with action sequence moscow the duration the movie get numerous punch ups all very violent and shockingly brutal bike chase that absolutely amazing many foot chases which are even more amazing thrilling car chase that unforgettable and much more but the highlight for has the scene waterloo station won ruin but for some reason had gripped any flaws for the movie eyes but you are not fan the bourne series have not seen the previous two then wouldn recommend