1 |text while the title before the devil knows you dead comes from irish proverb the film plays out like greek tragedy all starts with botched robbery and continues spiral out control two brothers attempt escape the mess they gotten themselves into the cast well assembled with philip seymour hoffman ethan hawke playing the aforementioned brothers notable support includes albert finney their father and marisa tomei the wife one brother and lover the other beyond these principals the acting unremarkable the story compelling and told with certain degree verve the narrative structure keeps things interesting providing different points view and frequent time shifts that being said the film unpredictability somewhat muted since becomes apparent early that this story tragedy through and through all all pretty impressive debut for first time screenwriter kelly masterson sidney lumet direction well handled but more impressed the fact that still directing over eighty years old was less impressed the score carter burwell but isn major distraction the end the film proves compelling viewing and while the story presentation may have superficial similarities other films this one remains unique experience
