1 |text this was the third muppet movie and the last one jim henson was around take part the making before his premature death 1990 the first three films starring the famous characters were all made and released into theatres before was born originally saw the first and second installments the original trilogy the muppet movie and the great muppet caper around the mid nineties kid but didn see this third one the muppets take manhattan until april 2007 this was shortly after had seen its two predecessors and 1996 muppet treasure island for the first time many years this third muppet movie definitely didn disappoint the first time saw and second viewing nearly three years later may not have impressed much but not certainly didn too far downhill the muppets stage musical manhattan melodies turns out big hit their college campus they are graduating from college they will soon leaving but decide they will all stay together and manhattan try and get their show broadway after their arrival they begin searching for producer but after many rejections they finally decide part and find jobs most them leave town but kermit stays and still determined find the right producer and reunite the muppet gang gets job new york restaurant owned man named pete the frog quickly befriends pete daughter jenny aspiring fashion designer who currently works her father restaurant waitress kermit continues his attempts reach stardom now with the help jenny doesn know that miss piggy has secretly stayed new york and now spying him she begins see kermit and jenny together and her looks like they getting close which leads jealousy when saw this movie for the second time looked disappointing first seemed little rushed unfocused and maybe even forgettable around the beginning there are some funny bits during this part the film such animal chasing woman through the audience the college campus but for little while the film seemed bland compared its two predecessors fortunately wasn long before that changed the film entertaining for the most part with saying goodbye the poignant song the muppets sing they part and lot that happens after that the two funniest parts might miss piggy tantrums after she sees kermit and jenny hugging but there were definitely many other times when laughed such poor fozzie trying hibernate with other bears the muppets still have their charm and comical antics which obviously also helps carry the movie for the most part does the plot simple but intriguing one for all ages there are some weaker moments such the muppet babies sequence and juliana donald performance jenny lacklustre but neither these problems are too significant and are far from enough ruin the entire experience would say the muppet movie the film that started the franchise 1979 the best the original trilogy and that seems the most popular opinion this third film probably the weakest the three but all them are good unlike muppets from space the third the theatrical films the franchise made after henson sad passing least the muppets take manhattan still the muppets won into details about what think the muppets 1999 film released twenty years after their first one since already explained review why found disappointing and even though does have some appeal clearly not alone however every theatrical movie starring the lovable muppets that was made during henson life good entertainment for the whole family even the second and third installment each showed slight decline quality after the one that directly preceded
