ave ever seen film the big surprise the enigmatic character sarah played with great depth and originality actress sarah smart she takes character who could have been insufferably tedious and sheer acting magic turns her into deeply mysterious and intriguing person about whom wonder tirelessly for the entire five hours she good that end wondering about sarah smart frankly guess that what happens when you really your job properly that people wonder where the character ends and the actress begins she knows herself that and many not she has some deeply unnerving tricks with her eyes which wobble and let know she unhinged but are not sure how why though eventually learn that she had extremely violent and traumatic childhood her mastery ambiguous facial expressions extraordinary rory kinnear amazingly convincing apparently hopeless fellow who lives with his mum and isn much but who turns out have hidden depths suppose most people have hidden depths but want plumb them that the question his mum played very well indeed margot leicester superb performance given lucinda dryzek who plays snotty revolting teenage girl the sort all dread meet but who crucial moments collapses helpless tears and turns out pathetic with all her arrogance just pose three other children are also very good lucinda friend and her younger half brother and half sister the younger siblings may very dim indeed characters the story they seem unable say anything particularly articulate being hopeless witnesses the disappearance with little recommend them but their sweet natures but that conveyed wonderful effect lee massey the boy and tyler anthony the girl harriet walter has small role but not get see much her which shame she such fine actress that she was wasted here one could but one must draw line somewhere the series manages strangely fascinating because the depth portrayal all these essentially uninteresting people caught web intense anxiety and suspense
