1 |text this definitely one the best kung movies ever and may one the best movies ever got great plot that functions like puzzle with lots intrigue and suspense this film full cat and mouse games and deceptions with people hiding their identities and their natures the characters this film live and breath much more than your average kung movie characters they are all interesting and compelling and the movie does good job giving them scenes show their personality and desires the fight scenes play out like little stories and many them are very original and exciting has cool training sequences and martial arts skills that are awesome they enter the realm fantasy there are members the poison clan each one with his own style that mimics the special skill venomous animal the styles each these characters are fun watch and you can see the techniques they use training applied during the film when this happens the director uses quick cutting back the training scene draw parallel these cuts are accompanied music changes and sound effects and the whole thing really works nicely one thing about this movie that very original the way treats death the director chang cheh was obviously very concerned that the film not trivialize death this makes some the scenes the movie much more effective actually care when people are killed this film this because the camera lingers the horror death even when the bad guys are killed some the sequences this movie are truly gut wrenching when characters search vengeance you really feel their anger and pain the same time this also fun movie has all the typical things you expect from traditional kung film there bad dubbing the characters are willing fight the drop hat some the sound effects are hilarious and times the behavior the characters incredibly unrealistic all this just adds the greatness the film and lets not forget that this director was visual stylist much more gifted than most his contemporaries you watch this movie closely you will notice that the technical prowess display virtuostic everything goes fast because the quick cutting style and the rapid camera movements the genre that easy overlook how beautiful the movie really the lighting and composition are spectacular times the camera work and movement extremely sophisticated along with very interesting fast paced editing the scenes that portray suspense and intrigue for example imagine hitchcock moving about twice the speed chang cheh was truly master craftsman and artist who knew his genre and was able produce important material while working within confines doesn rattle the boat the kung genre film but subtle way his skills permeate every scene and every shot and they add greatly the quality the work important filmmaker who continues influence many people this the real package kung movie that delivers every level art trash emotionally moving and fun has true sense morality but doesn allow that morality get the way delivering good action recommend everybody whether you are fan this genre not
