1 |text don get wrong goldeneye was revolutionary and definitely the best fps game based the 007 franchise but the series had fallen into fps rut enter everything nothing which puts bond third person when wrote earlier review for from russia with love had finished frwl and just started eon and judged eon bit harshly even though frwl definitely has the edge nostalgia and capturing the essence the movie franchise eon definitely superior terms depth controls and gameplay variety missions range from standard running and gunning driving suv driving aston martin driving limousine that wired explode commandeering two different types tanks goldeneye riding motorcycle flying helicopter repelling down shaft guarded laser tripwires and free falling after plummeting damsel sure vehicle controls are little clumsy but the issue here the variety movie adaptations goldeneye and frwl were all that could have hoped for but eon original storyline adds the feeling controlling james bond adventure this helped the impressive cast list willem defoe shannon elizabeth heidi klum and misaki ito judi dench and john cleese reprise their movie roles and respectively and pierce brosnan while sean connery adds credibility the game proceedings all characters resemble the stars with the disappointing exception heidi klum who game model doesn the real life model justice mya theme song par with least some the big screen bond title tunes the game also plays tribute some the older bond movies willem defoe character former colleague christopher walken baddie from view kill richard kiel appears jaws the hulking henchman from the spy who loved and moonraker three fight scenes the first and best which proceeds the same fashion fight the movies would have single player gameplay mainly consists standard foot missions bond like bond you will able choose whether use stealth out with guns blazing the game provides plenty opportunities utilize stealth with plenty wall and object cover unfortunately unlike frwl only one button eon controls both crouching and wall clinging bond may end crouching low when supposed peeking around corner and vice versa the game also allows players into bond reflex mode while you browse your inventory everything around you will into super slo allowing you analyze objects around you that can interacted with while this takes some getting used eventually this mode will allow you perform many spectacular bond moments such shooting down chandelier take out four goons underneath and greatly add the bond movie feeling there are available difficulty levels operative agent and double operative you can breeze through few hours agent few weeks double few months the difficulty level can changed for each individual mission garnering high scores missions will unlock gold and platinum awards and effect features such vehicle upgrades and the skimpy outfits the bond girls wear some missions can extremely frustrating due scarcity checkpoints but when all said and done mission any longer than single action scene bond movie multi player unfortunately not thrilling goldeneye still has the best multi player mode any bond game eon main multi player campaign mode that puts players charge lesser mi6 agents less important mission than bond more standard third person death match can unlocked from this mode but the single player mode the most complete bond experience date the ending with most bond games anticlimactic while the final mission one the most aggravating the game the final confrontation with the villain disappointing also levels that require bond speedy become largely matter trial and error still for any serious bond fan not playing this game tantamount missing one the bond films
