1 |text the effects job related stress and the pressures born moral dilemma that pits conscience against the obligations family business albeit unique one all brought head perhaps the catalyst midlife crisis are examined the dark and absorbing drama panic written and directed henry bromell and starring william macy and donald sutherland telling look how indecision and denial can bring about the internal strife and misery that ultimately leads apathy and that moment truth when the conflict must necessity last resolved talex macy tired has loving wife martha tracey ullman precocious six year old son sammy david dorfman mail order business runs out the house well his main source income the family business shares with his father michael sutherland and his mother deidre barbara bain but empty years plying this particular trade have left him numb and detached putting him mental state that has driven him see psychologist josh parks john ritter and make matters worse maybe better depending upon perspective parks waiting room meets young woman sarah cassidy neve campbell whose presence alone makes him feel alive for the first time since can remember she quickly becomes another brick the wall the moral conflict his job has visited upon him the days after their meeting simply cannot stop thinking about her his whole life seems has become situation one from which seemingly unable successfully extirpate himself without hurting the ones loves can deny his age and the fact that has indeed slipped into genuine midlife crisis but about discover that the problems facing are simply not going away their own crossroads and going have decide which way and going have very soon tfrom concept that intrinsically interesting bromell has fashioned engrossing character study that insightful and incisive and presents way that allows for moments reflection that enable the audience empathize and understand what alex going through makes very clear that there are simple answers that real life there easy way out his characters are well defined and very real people who represent the diversity found life and moreover within any given family unit the film resoundingly implies that the sins the father are irrefutably passed the progeny with irrevocable consequences and effects when you growing you accept your personal environment being that the world large and often years into adulthood that one may begin realize and understand that there are actually moral parameters established every individual who walks upon the planet and that the ones set the father may not conducive the tenets the son and that point that alex finds himself the story unfolds ergo the midlife crisis more specifically the crisis conscience from which cannot escape powerful message succinctly and subtly conveyed bromell with the help some outstanding performances from his actors tfor some time william macy has been one the premiere character actors the business creating such diverse characters quiz kid donnie smith magnolia the shoveler mystery men and jerry lundegaard fargo and that just sampling his many achievements one point this film sarah mentions alex sad eyes and very telling comment therein lies the strength macy performance here his ability convey very real emotion understated believable way that expresses all the inner turmoil experiencing consider the scene which lying awake bed staring off into the darkness that one restless moment clear that grappling not only with his immediate situation but with everything his life that has brought him finally this point that scene you find the sum total life guilt confusion and uncertainty all which have been successfully suppressed until now all the things that have always been the core alex life only now gradually breaking through his defense mechanisms and finally surfacing demanding confrontation and resolution complex character created and delivered macy with absolute precision that makes alex truly memorable character whom anyone who has ever faced situation seemingly insurmountable odds will able relate terrific piece work one the finest actors around tsutherland extremely effective well his michael despicably sinister way that real chilling frightening fact consider that there are such people actually walking the earth this not some pulp fiction james bond type villain but true personification evil hiding behind outward appearance that normal could the guy next door which what makes all the more disconcerting and sutherland brings all life brilliantly with great performance tneve campbell looks the part sarah but her performance the usual case with her seems somewhat pretentious although her affected demeanor here just happens fit the character and actually positive aspect the film only she would occasionally turn her energies inward would make tremendous difference the way she presents her characters panic however one her best efforts powerful film that the end journey well worth taking
