1 |text the late dudley moore had the most famous role his too short career 1981 arthur raucously funny and alternately touching tale that generates warm smiles big belly laughs and occasional tear you the right mood moore received best actor oscar nomination for his performance arthur bach drunken playboy who races cars plays tennis fondles women but has weekends off and his own boss arthur destined inherit 750 million dollars when marries snooty society girl named susan johnston jill eikenberry who the spoiled daughter undercover gangster things get sticky when arthur meets linda morolla liza minnelli waitress struggling actress from queens who steals neckties for her father birthday moore lights the screen one the single funniest performances the last years the late sir john gielgud won best supporting actor oscar for his flawless turn arthur acid tongued butler and best friend hobson whose outward disdain for arthur behavior covers more paternal feelings there are other funny contributions barney martin linda father stephen elliott susan father and geraldine fitzgerald arthur demented grandmother the film was directed with keen eye for comedy first time director named steve gordon who sadly died the following the year there was also forgettable sequel several years later but this instant classic not missed
