1 |text the scottish artist andy goldsworthy fashions natural materials into ephemeral artworks assembling rocks into egg shaped cairns filling riverside rock pools with fiery flowers and stitching thorns and twigs into intricate web patterns original work and few photographs his other creations are tucked away corner southampton art gallery near where live but although found these pieces intriguing only realised the wonder goldsworthy work when was lucky enough catch screening rivers and tides thomas reidelsheimer film accompanied beautiful instrumental soundtrack fred frith brings goldsworthy and his art life showing the artist work the opening scene captures him fusing icicle fragments into snake like thread set atop tree stump working with his teeth and bare hands goldsworthy crafts beautiful ephemeral work before long this delicate sculpture melts away nothing the brilliant nova scotian sunlight this scene among the most beautiful the film but the breadth and inventiveness goldsworthy work remarkable reidelsheimer shows both the successes and the failures capturing the frustration pieces that collapse before they are completed well the glory those that shine even for just few hours minutes seconds goldsworthy himself provides the narration speaking slowly but thoughtfully about the themes his work makes plain his need work with nature alone and further his understanding through trying work with natural materials even when they seem working against him times down earth and humorous other times struggles for the words express his purpose xc2 x96 something which quite understandable when witnessing his astonishing work first hand the rivers and tides the title become increasingly pertinent see the natural materials pass through the artist hands flowing from one form the next the capture the creation and dissolution goldworthy work itself striking piece art although goldsworthy works with widely varying materials and covers territory across north america and europe the presentation artworks one after the other this film exhausting gave the same feeling fatigue that get when spend too long art gallery and struggle take anything new brief interval which are introduced andy family and hometown all that breaks the long succession his artworks nevertheless reidelsheimer does superb job photographing goldsworthy and his creations locating them their wider environments from meandering canadian rivers rainy scottish hillsides fittingly the film ends with goldsworthy casting handfuls earth and snow into the sky fleeting patterns emerge from the dust particles even they dissipate into the air this the purest expression the beauty found the work this remarkable artist
