1 |text home room deals with columbine like high school shooting but rather than hashing over the occurrence itself the film portrays the aftermath and what happened the survivors their trauma guilt and denial spoilers the shooting itself treated foregone conclusion with action footage other than the reaction almost teenage swat commando after shooting the high school killer the film has three protagonists the detective investigating the crime which guilty parties are left convict and two teenage girls surviving the incident played very young erika christensen and busy philipps the two girls having nothing common besides the shooting are put together because and the drama ensues erika christensen though only has been around the block much that film viewers are pretty much acquainted with her solid and reliable style acting busy philipps three years older than christensen and altogether unknown blew away with her overwhelming dramatic strength and screen presence this girl was the part great movie and connects you with its intimate focus the fragile yet growing relationship between the two traumatized girls gus van sant elephant 2003 though good seems almost superficial and paltry compared home room when comes dramatic flair and acting what can see this film got very little screen time and exposure much more loss for equally traumatized america ten out ten
