-1 |text many the lead characters hideo gosha 1969 film hitokiri manslayer aka tenchu heaven punishment were actual historical figures western name order format ryoma sakamoto hampeita takechi shimbei tanaka izo okada ____ anenokoji the name hitokiri historical term refers group four super swordsmen who carried out numerous assassinations key figures the ruling tokugawa shogunate the mid 1800s under the orders takechi the leader the loyalist ultra nationalist pro emperor faction the tosa clan what was this struggle about sad say you won find out this film brilliant history lesson indeed gosha much more interested showing you the usual bloody slicing and dicing and absurd length the inner torment the not very bright killer izo okada than revealing actual history sakamoto for example was someone historical significance considered the father the imperial japanese navy the closest gosha comes providing history lesson the scene which sakamoto whom takechi considers traitor the loyalist cause comes takechi mansion try sway him ideologically begins talking about the international political situation with foreign warships japan ports and japan that too weak militarily defend against them want know more sorry gosha cuts off this potentially fascinating lecture mid sentence much for informing his audience about turning point japanese history the film left utter confusion about the aims the two sides this struggle for the two and half centuries that the shogunate held central power japan was institution dedicated preventing social change preserving the feudal relations society was fearful outside contamination both ideological and technological keeping with this spirit outlawed firearms those instruments leveling europe and the americas with which peasant could have stood samurai throughout this period the emperor was nothing more than spiritual figurehead but the towns which stood neutral zones between the feudal fiefdoms new class merchants landlords and craftsmen was developing the class known europe its french name the bourgeoisie inevitably this new class gained strength chafed against the many confines feudal society europe the king emperor became the central figure the bourgeoisie struggle for power against the feudal aristocracy but political leadership does not always fully understand the interests the class serves when the outside world arrived with bang 1853 the form admiral perry black ships the ruling elite japan was thrown into crisis their military was match for these foreigners also they had heard about the havoc the british and french imperialists were wreaking china what should japan save itself from the fate its weak neighbor surprisingly some elements within the usually isolationist shogunate were inclined open trade with the foreigners order obtain some their advanced technology this the point view represented just barely the film sakamoto the other hand the emperor loyal ultra nationalists represented takechi believed they could keep out the foreigners force only they could prevent the other faction from selling out the country sound familiar thus the assassination key shogunate figures order and away takechi motivations were for the film biggest puzzle gosha suggests that fighting mainly for his personal advancement rather than for the loyalist cause can take this represent the tenor the loyalists whole you care several reviewers have compared this film favorably with goyokin which gosha made the same year but where goyokin crackling suspenseful adventure yarn with hero worthy sympathy hitokiri plodding nowhere near compelling and lacks such hero sakamoto could have been this film hero but are not allowed know him nor what stands for well enough for him achieve that status view his wonderful scores for five previous kurosawa films masaru sato score here was very disappointing sounding like something rejected from bonanza episode barry freed
