1 |text pretty good film from preminger labyrinthine times explores sets and locales from various angles and perspectives were nature film the denizens the modern city and how they live this sense visually and spatially satisfying its hero good cop with bad temper gets into very hot water when accidentally kills guy with plate his head dana andrews plays the lead were hamlet and has never been better the story may pure melodrama but andrews gives weight and almost raises the level tragedy his girl gene tierney attractive but unremarkable gary merrill makes for very interesting villain with his natural warmth providing nice contrast andrews coolness his smiling amiable seeming bad guy seems continually challenging his nemesis the mere fact his being emotionally open opposed the tightly wound and moralistic cop who pursuing him there are major surprises this film which seems transitional for all concerned for director preminger reunion sorts with his laura stars andrews and tierney who were passing their career peaks around the time the movie was made the supporting cast merrill karl malden neville brand are understandably more optimistic they were all their way preminger serene observer ever lets the events unfold without expressing strong point view the morally ambiguous ending somewhat disappointing for the cat and mouse game between the two antagonists seems larger and more archetypal than any mere movie could contain much less resolve
