-1 |text many have stated that orca xc2 x96 killer whale jaws rip off this not really true though the enormous commercial success jaws undoubtedly made these man beast stories more attractive propositions for film makers the second half the 70s orca xc2 x96 killer whale would better described modern day retread moby dick story about obsession one hand whale obsessive quest avenge the death its mate the other bounty hunter obsessive quest kill the whale before can claim any more lives sadly orca killer whale emerges very disappointing film its fundamentally interesting ideas somewhat ruined hammy performances and preposterous plotting shark hunter nolan richard harris encounters marine life researcher rachel bedford charlotte rampling diving off the atlantic coast canada their meeting almost ends disaster when rachel team are attacked great white shark but killer whale arrives the nick time stop the shark after this nolan becomes increasingly obsessed with capturing killer whale and selling aquarium but his plans backfire when accidentally kills pregnant female the species while the distraught male looks rachel tells nolan that killer whale incredibly intelligent mammal with strong memory and feelings just like human worse still native umilak will sampson warns him that the whale will always remember its grief and everything can have revenge nolan initially tries forget about the whole regrettable incident but the whale causes havoc the fishing town and the disgruntled locals begin demand that nolan puts sea track down and destroy eventually nolan forced pursue the killer whale xc2 x85 the hunt leads all the way the desolate ice floes the arctic ocean where man and beast play out their final fatal battle against each other two things stand out this film one the haunting score ennio morricone perhaps the greatest composer film music all time his talents wasted various tenth rate clunkers during the 70s and 80s the other the amazing widescreen photography ted moore which makes the film consistently pleasing the eye every other department orca xc2 x96 killer whale shoddy film that does nothing enhance the reputation its talented cast and crew harris appears extremely ill throughout the film his hair bedraggled black rings around his eyes and skin deathly pale his performance lacks the usual vitality rampling strikes lot sexy poses but fails convince with her long winded and ill informed explanations about the ways whales the rest the actors are wasted brief and undeveloped roles the most memorable which sees derek getting her leg bitten off the vengeful whale the plot total nonsense from start finish with such preposterous sequences the whale deliberately starting fire the fishing village that engulfs and destroys the local refinery although credible suppose that whales are intelligent creatures with genuine emotions the idea that whale could plot revenge against single human adversary and carry out calculatedly utterly absurd orca xc2 x96 killer whale really one for completists the man beast cycle from the late 70s most will come away from the film shaking their heads disbelief and grinding their teeth with despair
