1 |text ahista ahista one little small brilliant started watching and the beginning got little bored since the pacing was slow and the main idea one guy meeting girl who lost was not really new but the film went started getting increasingly and gradually engaged the film the fantastic writing and the charming romance the film was extremely simple and natural and after some time felt was watching real documentation one guy life there one very good reason the film got this feel and the fresh talent called abhay deol extremely convincing the simple kind hearted and struggling ankush whose new love motivates him make amends and fight for better life throughout the film presented ordinary mischievous prankster but also helping and loving person who like anyone else will anything protect his love deol portrays all the different shades his character whether positive negative naturally and with complete ease shivam nair direction very good his depiction the life people the rural neighbourhood excellent but what gets even more impressive his portrayal ankush relationships with the different people who surround him including his friends and his love interest megha who ready anything for also immensely liked the way nair portrayed his interaction with his friend loud and plump mother whom calls khala aunty likes drive her crazy and annoy her every occasion yet see that she occupies very special place his heart and like mother figure him evidenced several scenes except for abhay the rest the cast performed well though soha ali khan did not stand out according she was good and had some her mother charm the actors who played ankush friends were very good was the actress who played ankush khala apart from the performances the film writing was outstanding the dialogues were sort ordinary yet brilliant and the script was also fantastic that mainly because despite not new story was never overdone melodramatic and there were attempts make look larger than life the film biggest weakness was himesh reshammiya uninspiring music which was unsuitable for this film otherwise ahista ahista was delightful watch and got only better with every scene the concept may not new but the film manages look fresh and becomes increasingly heartwarming the story goes the ending was bittersweet kind sad yet optimistic short this movie really grows you slowly and this can easily attributed the wonderful writing the moving moments the charming romance the realistic proceedings and course abhay deol memorable performance
1 |text rented zero day from the local video store last week had never heard the film and had reservations about just from looking the box knew the film was indie film and therefore the quality was going less than mainstream film can tell you that after finished watching zero day immediately started from the beginning again the film was clearly following the basic outline what happened columbine high school april 1999 but what struck was how believable the two lead actors were first time through watching this film wasn entirely sure what was watching were actual tapes left behind the shooters columbine the back mind knew what was watching could not real but the same time the acting was convincing you had keep giving your head shake the film disturbing absolutely are you going see things that will make you question the merit the film probably think what most people will find disturbing they will actually have feelings for the two lead characters calvin and andre played cal robertson and andre keuck why that problematic for some people calvin and andre are planning massacre their high school know for myself felt immense sadness for andre and calvin had empathy for them because their lives had come such horrific point they had fallen deeply through cracks that they had begun journey down road which could have been stopped only people around them had taken notice their plight zero day phenomenal film gives you close and personal look events that most will only ever see the conclusion the news leaves you thinking about the lives involved and leaves you perplexed how people get this point week after seeing this film still think about those you who have not seen zero day please keep mind the following the film independent with little budget and the film shot camcorders the material the film disturbing this not mainstream hollywood and there happy ending but you can put all that aside zero day film that will stick with you and just maybe help you open your eyes little
