1 |text remember watching the disney version and watching now makes think has somehow lost its magic touch plenty other renditions ever after put aside cinderella have fact lost their touch throughout the years then found this production with flawless performance kathleen turner the evil stepmother and was blown away the phantasmagorical essence this fantasy story that has cast under its spell since childhood all know the story cinderella young girl who father died and was dominated her wicked stepmother and stepdaughters and longs the ball for one last chance for freedom but this plot line takes different twist the classic fairy tale causing cinderella whose real name zizola and only called cinderella her family because her slavery trapped situation her father who still lives slowly losing himself dominant wife who manipulates him into playing favorites with his wife and step daughters against his own and tries poison him thus zizola goes out save her father stopping her stepmother from finding another suitor the ball distracting the men who come her way there the bored prince valiant has change heart from his dull life and falls love with the mysterious lady the strange dress forged water nymph named mab with rose petals for slippers what drew this film most all was original take the old fairy tale that none can compare does not weave web lies like most cinderella stories does not ignore any reason why cinderella would want attend the ball and nor does show shallow side the prince the disney version did instead shows more cinderella selfless heart more than any other production and the artwork simply stunning the costumes are all beautifully made especially zizola sapphire blue ballgown match the marcella plunkett fantastical beauty and soft spirit like voice would highly suggest this film for anyone who interested dream like sequence the classic fairy tale with interesting twist only problem that the producers and director did not make full collection other fairy tales with this same element and the fact that the film now out print
