1 |text watching ossessione today more than decades later still powerful experience especially for those interested movie history and more specifically how italian filmmakers changed movies forever roughly from ossessione and sica bambini guardano both 1943 years later with fellini antonioni pasolini visconti makes amazing directing xc3 xa9but taking the uncredited plot the postman always rings twice guide the development his own themes strikes even today how ahead its time ossessione was shot fascist italy during world war think about depicted scenes and themes that caused the film immediately banned from theaters and the fact that used the plot famous american novel and payed copyright didn help ossessione alarmingly reveals poverty ridden war time italy far from the idealized italy depicted fascist telefoni bianchi movies but also extremely daring its sexual frankness with shirtless hunk gino massimo girotti who definitely precedes brando kowalski streetcar named desire taking giovanna clara calamai married woman bed just minutes after they first meet watch calamai unglamorous matter fact undressing and the subtle but undeniable homosexual hints between gino and spagnolo elio marcuzzo very appealing actor his face not unlike pierre xc3 xa9menti who was shot the nazis 1945 years old few words sex lust greed and poverty relentlessly had rarely ever been shown before italian cinema all the copies ossessione were destroyed soon after its opening was called scandalous and immoral visconti managed save print and when the film was released after the war most critics called the front runner the neo realist movement preceding rossellini roma citt xc3 xa0 aperta and sica sciusci xc3 xa0 some other critics perhaps more appropriately saw ossessione the italian counterpart the poetic realism french cinema remember visconti had been renoir assistant especially marcel carn xc3 xa9 quai des brumes and jour xc3 xa8ve and julien duvivier xc3 xa9p xc3 xa9 moko while ossessione may neo realistic its visual language the depiction war time paesan life italy with its popular fairs poverty child labor prostitution bums swindlers etc the characters and the themes were already decidedly viscontian was always more interested tragic passionate obsessive greedy characters social political sexual apartheid the decadence the elites than realistic everyday life characters and themes favored desica and rossellini ossessione already find elements drama and tragedy later developed many his films especially senso visconti definitive departure from neo realist aesthetics and rocco suoi fratelli even his most neo realist film terra trema makes his fishermen rise from day day characters mythological figures ossessione good opportunity confirm the theory about great artists whose body work approaches analyzes and develops specific themes and concerns over and over again from their first their last opus matter the scenery background time setting may change visconti may play with the frame but the themes and essence his art are well obsessively recurrent ossessione not missed you surely fascinated this ground breaking powerful film
