1 |text this film never received the attention deserved although this one the finest pieces ensemble acting and one the most realistic stories have seen screen clearly filmed small budget real hospital the center the story joel very well played eric stoltz joel has been paralyzed motorcycle accident and comes the hospital ward with other men who have spinal injuries joel love with anna his married lover played helen hunt who shows early signs her later academy award winning work although the joel anna relationship the basic focus there are many other well developed characters the ward wesley snipes does tremendous job the angry raymond even more impressive william forsythe the bitter and racist bloss think forsythe two best scenes are when becomes frustrated and angry the square dancers and later when feels empathy for young korean man who has been shot liquor store hold favorite scene with snipes the the roundtable discussion post injury sexual options the chemistry between stoltz and hunt very strong and they have two very intimate but not gratuitous sex scenes the orgasm the ward both sexy and amusing there also another memorable scene where joel and bloss and the korean boy take the specially equipped van the strip bar truly comedy errors they make their feeble attempts get the van going see the naked ladies the story made even more poignant the fact that the director neal jimenez paralyzed real life this basically his story this film real not glossy flashy have the amount talent film such small budget amazing recommend this film everyone see because one those films that even improves second look shame that such great piece work gets overlooked but through video perhaps can get the attention richly deserves
