phone and hears from his girlfriend portman for once not annoying that she breaks with him and reflects their relationship tywker style the story dizzyingly fast paced kinetic and repetitive featuring screaming and running lola rennt making the most adrenaline pumping segment paris aime and possibly also the most touching once tywker starts wielding his most powerful tool xc2 x96 music fill the negative account clearly not all directors manage touching tywker van sant cohens coixet and xc3 xa9pardieu sylvain chomet scrapes the bottom the pile carving out truly disposable segment which little boy retells the story how his parents met they are two lonely mimes this part your face french and desperately quirky that insulting international viewers suwa also directs poor and fluffy segment with unusually haggard looking juliette binoche whom mourns the loss her son nothing else happens finally the wrap and interweaving the stories the end feels somewhat rushed and half hearted yet paris aime truly spoils you with quality for all the other stories are well crafted with crisp acting and amusing writing certainly one the highlights 2006 not saying much suppose and very personal film the sense that unavoidable pick favourite and least favourite highly recommended both mainstream pretentious heh audiences out
