1 |text this very much not the sort movie for which john wayne known plays diplomat man who gets things done through words and persuasion rather than physical action the film moves with quiet realism through its superficially unexciting story for the open minded the patient and the thoughtful this movie rich depiction intriguing part history there are two intertwining stories the big story internalised isolationist japan and externalised expansionist america clashing when their interests conflict the small human story outsider barbarian wayne and civilised geisha initial hostility and dislike turning mutual respect and love the human story reflection the greater story the two nations the movie very well done and all actors play their roles well the two lead roles are performed perfection john wayne excellent townsend harris striking exactly the right blend force and negotiation his dealings with the japanese eiko ando likewise excellent the geisha the title charming and delightful the interaction between her character and john wayne particularly well portrayed this exactly how these two individuals they are depicted the film would have behaved the script very well written lacks all pomposity and realistic depiction the manner which the depicted events may have occurred the characters are real people not self consciously great figures from history furthermore the clash cultures and interests portrayed with great skill and subtlety indeed the clash traditionalist and traditionally powerful isolationist japan and rising newly powerful nation from across the ocean summarised very well one exchange between john wayne and the local japanese baron wayne complains that shipwrecked sailors are beheaded they land japan and that passing ships cannot even put into port for water the baron responds that japan just wants left alone wayne character replies that japan increasingly important crossroads international shipping and that things continue before the nation will regarded nothing more than band brigands infesting important roadway very real summary the way which the two countries each saw themselves being the right and saw the other being the wrong the resultant clash between two self righteous peoples with conflicting interests has its reflections throughout history continuing theme that echoes into the present and into the future cinematography and the depiction mid nineteenth century japan before the accelerated growth towards industrialisation that was follow later the century excellent visual treat and enlightening insight into japan ancient civilisation highly recommend anyone whether john wayne fan not watch this film you get the chance just aware that isn action film representation interesting place and time history and slow boiling love story which much their surprise comes dominate the personal lives the two main characters watch this film its merits without preconceptions allow yourself immersed its story and you will thoroughly enjoy all all excellent film
