1 |text kolchak the night stalker hugely entertaining series which pushy sarcastic forty something reporter repeatedly drawn into mortal combat with supernatural and occasionally extraterrestrial forces based very popular pair movies featuring the kolchak character this series died quick death the mid 1970s due low ratings but nevertheless maintains strong cult following today but will the average modern day viewer able dig kolchak and his weekly clashes with the undead that actually tough question answer fairly detractors this series tend argue that formulaic and hopelessly dated the other hand fans argue that cleverly written well acted and sometimes genuinely spooky and got foot both camps thoroughly enjoyed watching all episodes kolchak dvd recently though can plainly see that the series has major flaws address the question kolchak being formula fiction first now think can all agree that most shows have formulas just about every episode columbo unfolds according the same pattern for example repetition not necessarily bad thing itself fact critics have long recognized that audiences often enjoy and actively seek out repetitive entertainment however the problem with kolchak that its formula simply too rigid too repetitive even the most generous standards almost every episode kolchak investigates murder and figures out that was committed some form monster tries publish story about said monster but his editor vincenzo blocks him always the grounds that kolchak doesn have sufficient evidence support his claims that supernatural forces are work and alas kolchak also obstructed the police the end kolchak does some independent research the monster figures out how kill and then kills without ceremony reward writing big story about you can see where this ever strict formula might get tiresome right particularly mystified vincenzo kolchak always raving about monsters and vincenzo never believes well then why doesn vincenzo fire kolchak have him committed that what any normal boss would but the series eschews such realism and prefers keep vincenzo and kolchak comical antagonists result many their scenes together are profoundly unbelievable though they are also quite funny the very best episodes kolchak manage vault over the limitations this formula however usually because they contain some kind unexpected twist these select episodes are good enough that think they largely immune typical criticisms the series some favorites include horror the heights episode that noteworthy for being grimy inventive and socially aware kolchak dialog has unusually sharp and cynical edge though adheres closely the kolchak formula the script written hammer studios veteran jimmy sangster remarkably literate and delves deeply into the monster backstory the devil platform possible inspiration for the omen films this episode stands out because the villain very young tom skerritt tempts kolchak with satanic contract full goodies and doing reveals lot about the reporter character firefall this episode appears have bad reputation among fans but enjoyed because got great red herring and really creepy almost unstoppable seeming monster though singled out these three episodes for praise say that most the stories are entertaining the very least for money there are only two complete turkeys the episode run primal scream which about monkey men running rampant chicago and the sentry which features the dumbest looking creature makeup the history filmed entertainment and this assessment coming from lifelong doctor who and godzilla fan balance then this good series little repetitive little cheesy perhaps but has elements greatness even during the weaker episodes darren mcgavin wonderful performance the caustic world weary endlessly funny kolchak truly shines carries the series effortlessly way that for example sarah michelle gellar never managed buffy mcgavin was one great character actor and this series worth watching for him alone
