-1 |text from actor and independent writer director john cassavetes woman under the influence gives the viewer look working class family with problem mental instability the husband nick played peter falk blue collar worker who has trouble showing his wife mabel played gena rowlands the amount attention that she deserves from the onset the film obvious that mabel very quirky and strange but only few minutes later clear that she much more than that crazy bonkers out her damn mind nick tries his hardest hide this from his workers and after she has particularly strange incident dinner asks her she okay trying deny mabel illness her problem only spirals from there did find some particular problems with this film guess these problems were mostly present the story and the way some the character acted toward the end mabel has been committed because frankly she nuts then six months later she ready come out the hospital and her husband throws party welcome her back never acts stupid the beginning the movie why would invite all these people some them strangers mabel over his house when his wife such fragile state simply idiotic later after mabel comes the house mabel father has huge outburst nick screaming the top his lungs about not wanting eat spaghetti his daughter has just gotten back from six months rehabilitation and the thing you want keep her calm and goes nuts over spaghetti few minutes later the film nick brings mabel into the stairwell and forces her the things she did when she was mentally unstable make her weird noises and gestures didn send her there make her better and not those things there were various other parts that occurred after this but would just redundant look them more detail guess just had serious problem with the decision cassavetes have his characters act this way simply didn make sense however although had problems with the ending the film there was one aspect that really redeemed the acting gena rowlands played amazing crazy woman there were times when forgot she was acting where got caught her wild gesticulations and crazy talk that was actually scared her she was amazingly convincing and intense however was also impressed the rest mabel family peter falk played very strange character and almost thought was crazy himself because the awkward way handled his children his job and especially the situation with his wife also usually don appreciate child actors but the young people who played nick and mabel children this film were phenomenal really felt like they were mabel children because they seemed attached her and were interesting helping her with her problem think their performances are one the things that kept this film together and without them would have made the film less realistic and less intense general wasn impressed this film the story was jumbled and unclear and the characters acted ways that made wonder who wasn insane the movie the only saving grace were brilliant lead acting roles the longhetti family their realistic dialogue and powerful acting kept the film together and are probably the only reason the film has ever amounted anything
