e primus secondus sextmus and septimus the other sons where killed the other brothers humorous competition see who lives get the throne anyway tosses his ruby charm the sky and voila that what brings the star earth the star crashes the form beautiful woman named yvaine clare danes and she course wearing the charm but little does she know she now being persuaded tristain the princes and also aging witch named lamia michelle pfeiffer who wants cut out the stars heart regain her own youth complicated yes but all comes together the adventure unfolds tristain the first find yvaine but blinded his devotion victoria doesn recognize the growing bond between and yvaine his initial interest lie only returning yvaine victoria proof his love but must get past the princes and lamia first the princes aren that big issue they are constantly trying kill each other and just pirates the caribbean never has death been funny but tristain also encounters the witch who enslaved his mother though doesn know his mother and band flying pirates led robert deniro his the most important character the movie and deniro plays tee steals the movie with his toughness and soon learn undercover secret that will leave audiences the floor with laughter though his role small length deniro extraordinary michelle pfeiffer wonderful lamia sexy evil witch claire danes most appropriate the confused and distressed yvaine she makes perfect damsel jason flemyng adam buston rupert everett and mark strong add the perfect dose levity the fighting princes whom they die return ghosts ala blithe spirit and high spirits moreover director matthew vaughn whose only other directing experience was layer cake weaves enchanting tale that everyone will enjoy stardust may too complex for young children but anyone over the age will want see this movie multiple times that good stardust what movies are supposed perfectly written perfectly cast perfectly directed and perfectly acted other words perfect
