1 |text surprise that writer director michael powell considered matter life and death his and emeric pressburger spellbinding fantasy from 1946 his favourite their films together released during the aftermath world war this colourful romantic adventure would have provided just the tonic for traumatised recovering nation need good uplift following string other patriotic war films the archers made this one their quirkiest skittish and most patriotic the lot quintessentially british for upholding british heritage shakespeare beer fair play good manners also visibly americanised its baroque compositions technical inventiveness and fine multi ethnic cast oddly echoing another 1946 classic wonderful life amolad opens grand firmament with one those jolly voice overs preaching about the earth and the heavens and what big wonderful world live then cuts the inside british cockpit badly hit flames and with the pilot already dead sounds misconceived but the connection soon made lucid with the events that follow clocking nearly minutes the rapid fire exchange between british pilot peter david niven and american radio contact june kim hunter breathtaking its intimacy resigned dying peter nevertheless exhausts plenty vigour charm and outpouring confessions and his warm affiliation with june closes with mutual exchange love you keeping with the magic the moment peter oversight his conductor whose job was transport him the other world escapes death and finds himself stranded beach later encounters june riding bicycle and instantly matches the body with the voice but realising their error the high court want peter sent back and order the french conductor maurice goring down earth retrieve him but peter adamant live because june and the conductor mistake and wilfully guards his corner peter fate ultimately lies with the heavenly court and american prosecutor raymond massey whose jury consists several deceased war heroes and posh british delegates the surreal trial which dissolves from back into rich technicolor once the verdict announced may well dream but the final shot the hospital validates the predictable outcome the abstract frame filling stairway heaven the american title the film used twice the first time when elevates peter and his enigmatic french guardian upwards crossing giant statues peter potential attorneys for the trial including abraham lincoln and plato the second time the softly lit colour stairway provides the setting for what iconic image cinema peter and june frozen side side their marvelled eyes fixed forward the frame their fate sealed the unlikely affection shared between peter and june never turns mushy verbose treated with nobility and the perception that the couple are already suitable enough married and simply need convince people their love can keep them together the french conductor who can freeze time and people bodies obtrudes many their key moments together lecturing peter about history and among his mischievous tricks pinching peter top 100 game tricks book and his coffee cup visually inspired other powell pressburger collaborations this was the first time they combined colour with xc2 x96 the latter having cheerful quality when used for the heaven scenes and both are equally captivating the outstanding script more than matches the imaginative set design with dialogue that sounds immediate that doesn feel like was written performed for the screen amusing and witty powell pressburger writing deserves equal acclamation with their forte for colour and composition made 1946 matter life and death one those films that defies age looking fresh and inventive even this age where cgi would vamp its artificial effects probably stripping them their emotional wonder other jarring changes would include the need for reduced average seconds for cutting and the inevitable plea shorten dialogue can preserve the low attention spans most audiences powell weaves spell that subconsciously absorbs the viewer from the first frame giving him freedom experiment with images without betraying the logical development peter predicament
