1 |text hotel nord gripping drama guilt which marcel carne portrayed entertaining tale ill fated love which also functions revolt against the cruel world the film based entirely pair hapless lovers pierre and renee were mistaken when they believed that suicide would put end their misery hotel nord has its own inimitable charm its inhabitants have become essential part the establishment there element togetherness everyone flocks hotel nord eat chat etc marcel carne has remained true the spirit the films produced 30s and 40s hotel nord has certain kind nostalgic feel carne while recreating the life parisian roads was able create sort nostalgia for black and white giving unique genre poetic realism his oeuvre hotel nord can termed quintessence cinematographic populism the 14th july ball scene the banks saint martin canal remains magnificent sequence the film immense popularity can judged from the fact that hotel nord has been declared national monument
1 |text ching siu tung and tsui hark chinese ghost story aside from being one the greatest wuxia pian films ever made beautiful and romantic love story well impressively choreographed martial arts film that should belong every film lover collection the sorely missed hong kong superstar leslie cheung plays traveling tax collector who spends the night haunted temple while staying the temple meets colorful cast characters that include the swordsmen yin and hsiao hou the tree devil and the beautiful ghost lit sin seen played the lovely joey wong free her from the clutches the evil tree devil must reincarnate her body and travel the underworld defeat even more powerful demon enough good things can said about this film the pacing perfect with great combination romance action fantasy and humor and the feverishly paced finale should leave you with little chance breathe the chemistry between the wonderfully tragic joey wong and leslie cheung whose legendary career ended much too soon really allows the viewer feel for both them indeed the acting the whole vivacious and full life would say this one the most fun viewing experiences ever had much the credit goes his portrayal the mysterious swordsman yin his over the top persona disillusioned swordsman hell bent vanquishing evil leads some great moments humor and traditional drama wonderful score lush cinematography with eye popping colors and frenetic action pieces courtesy ching siu tung round out this wonderful film find copy anywhere you can
