1 |text 1987 hong kong had given the world such films sammo hung encounters the spooky kind chow yun fat john woo iconic better tomorrow warriors and the classic vampire jackie chan was having international success video but was with chinese ghost story that cinema had its first real crossover theatrical hit the west for many years western filmgoers had never seen anything like was film that took various ingredients that cinema had used for years flying swordsman wildly choreographed martial arts and the supernatural and blended them create film that was unique its look feel and execution forget the poor and unnecessary sequels spawned this the original and best director siu tung ching still best known action choreographer such films woo better tomorrow the killer has under the watchful eye legendary producer tsui hark created masterpiece fantasy horror cinema and with such expert crew his disposal less than martial arts coordinators the chances the film being anything but wonderful would unthinkable the editing the amazingly prolific david who wrote directed the bride with white hair and edited such classic titles better tomorrow hardboiled and the cult hit the club quite simply work genius his crafting the perfectly choreographed high flying tree climbing sword fights makes them some the best cinema has ever created fast moving outlandish but never confusing they are even today the pinnacle their art the crew cinematographers have also done miracles this film where every shot expertly crafted painting where wonderful blue tinged night sequences shrouded ever present ghostly fog are the breathtaking platform for our story unfold film where everything used weave dreamlike beauty even the silken robes and dresses worn hsiao tsing become living parts the movie whether romantic sequences battle scenes the ever present silk flows across the screen even simple scene where hsiao tsing changes robes turned into thing fluttering beauty every skill the set combines create most memorable scene from such simple act the sets are also amazing giving other worldly sense the forests and the temple and harshness the scorched flag filled wasteland hell for the amazing finale the production design zhongwen deserves the highest praise another major factor the films success the music romeo diaz and james wong hong kong films have given some fantastic music and songs that have added much the success sequence but chinese ghost story the music quite simply vital from the opening song onwards the music becomes important the characters the score perfect mixture modern and traditional instruments drums bells and guitars pound away over the action sequences great effect but the slower achingly romantic pieces that comes into own here flutes strings and female choral effects create what are possibly the finest pieces music heard film add this the female vocal stunningly beautiful song that plays over tsau shen and hsiao tsing love making nothing ever seen but the effect wonderful this lovingly innocent movie romance and you have shining example the power film music can have and course have the acting talent leslie cheung better tomorrow and very popular singer outstanding the innocent tax collector his work the thankfully mild comic sequences never over the top and his scenes with joey wang are played with just the right amount passion and innocence joey wang who would later mostly relegated support roles films like the chow yun fat andy lau classic god gamblers has never looked more radiant than how she does here she the epitome ethereal beauty her portrayal the tragic hsiao tsing stunning she shows her characters sadness what she has become and what she made but also gives off subtle eroticism the scenes where she luring the men their gruesome deaths veteran actor vampire swordsman great fun the wise brave but ever grumpy yen treads fine line between the eccentric and the annoying with practised ease and what easily could have been character that could have harmed the film actually wonderfully entertaining and memorable but what about the monsters and beasties hear you cry well they range from the rather crude but fun stop motion animatronic zombies that inhabit the temple resulting great running gag with constantly thwarted attempts munch the amusingly unsuspecting tsau shen the rather cheesy but surprisingly effective lord black complete with arsenal vicious flying heads and quite outstanding wire work most which has this day never been topped but the most outstanding effect and creation the tree spirit killer tongue first encounter this thing with evil dead style rushing camera effect powers down its victims throats deliver lethal french kiss that turns the victims into zombiefied husks but later shown all its crazy glory can grow big and long that shoots through the forest after prey rips apart trees wraps itself around buildings and coils slimy length around people before picking them and throwing them against tree trunks can even split open reveal fang filled mouth outrageous idea that given the deeply romantic main plot shouldn work but does fantastic and unforgettable effect what all this adds classic example hong kong movie making true team effort that has given truly ground breaking movie film packed with wit invention action monsters martial arts ghosts fantastic ideas lush visuals beautiful music and most important enduring charm one cinemas most moving romances
