ill surely please all with fantastic animation and wonderful dialogue plus somewhat twisty surprise think this film simply remarkable and does hold for the two hour and four minute run time the story wonderful peak into hayao miyazaki animation which has limits the setting the film combo many time periods does seem take place the end the 1800s but some alternante universe which has advanced technology and weapons laputa also surprisingly funny film the film has tons hilarious moments almost equal the drama and action the film holds think the funniest part fight scene where pazu boss faces off against pirate and soon after riot breaks out funny see the men compare their strength and the music fits right with perfectly now let talk about how the dub rates excellent cast give some great performances bring these characters life teen heartthrob james van der beek plays the hero pazu who has much more mature voice then the japanese version where the original sounded more childlike either way think his voice nice fit with pazu anna paquin the young oscar winner from the piano plays sheeta this also nice performance but the voice bit uneven she doesn stay true one accent times she sounds american apple pie but other times she sounds like someone from new zealand the performance most enjoyed however was coris leachman who played mama dola not only this excellent performance but the voice and emotion she gives the character really brings life there was ever live action laputa movie forbid she would the one play her you can just imagine her the role well somewhat luke skywalker himself mark hamill muska and this another top rate hamill performance you may familiar with hamill from long line voice work after did the original star wars movies but renders muska full evil his voice sounds like his regular voice and mix the joker who played for many episodes the animated batman series rounding out the cast voice character actor jim cummings who does great gruff job the general and andy dick and mandy patakin members the dola gang now let talk about what really makes this dub special joe hisaishi newly arranged music for those who have never heard him hisaishi does the music and like all miyazaki films the music very memorable each his scores has own personas which fits the particular film perfectly now these new arrangements has done are more american like which think was the goal the new recordings don worry the classic tunes the japanese version are still here great form the score sounds arranged like this hollywood blockbuster has more power has more emphasis clearer and deeper the film prologue the first seconds where are introduced the airships has some new music not sure but believe when first saw the ships there was music all but majority the music has new backdrops and more background music enjoy things seem very enhanced powerful scene the music more stronger then the original versions calm scene more calmer overall think many you will pleased with the new arrangements mixes highly did myself and personally think helps improve the film prefer the new score over the old one and hope disney will release license the music rights full blown soundtrack another plus side the dub that the story remains faithful and much the original japanese lines are intact kiki sure few lines where changed and this the same way lines have been changed but majority are close exactly the original lines and dialogue miyazaki has written was afraid some excellent lines would butchered but they were there intact some new lines have been added well which help out but not sure whether consider this good thing bad thing disney did not translate the ending song was japanese was mortified when they did completely new songs for the kiki dub but with this version the original song japanese guess good still the original but bad since majority people seeing this dub speak english there big down side this dub and deals with how the voices match the character lips course any dub won perfect but think kiki and mononoke the dubbing lines match were much better executed and disney had little bit more time with this one some the time everything matches perfect some the time doesn completley match and rare case someone says something and the lips don move all there scene where sheeta chuckles and her mouth doesn move one bit far things about the film itself these are thoughts thought the most amazing part laputa was the animation from the opening sequence the ending the animation lush and detailed you just have watch awe you see the true nature each character true detail their face with extreme close ups and action you have give ton credit for the effort that these animators put into this film everything well done and beautifully hand drawn like moving piece art and think this was done the mid 1980 the animation quite different from disney ghibli has own distinctive flare which very different but very good and after all these years the colors look vibrant ever laputa also has tons action sequences lots plane dogfights plus few ground these sequences are well done and intriguing scary that they are comparable big budget action film and the finale just something you must see the sound effects are pure and classic and fit explosions guns firing and everything else well and like all miyazaki films each one focuses different theme kiki confidence this one has great lesson greed and power people don realize how greed can take over you and how having too much power isn good people are obsessed with power and are greedy and the main villian muska greatly shows this all all laputa castle the sky was great film begin with and now improved for the most part glad more mainstream audience now have the chance see this classic animated film all glory with great voice cast who put lot into the film with the excellent redone musical score from joe hisaishi disney has done nice job this dub and quite worthy though think the voices matched the mouths better the kiki and princess mononoke disney dubs castle the sky still great dub and worth the long delays because now more can expierence fantastic film
