-1 |text the 1930s saw vogue for documentary films about remote corners the world with emphasis wild animals exotic terrain and primitive people with unusual cultures despite the logistics transporting film crew distant and dangerous place and then bringing back alive with the film footage such films were often much cheaper make than were conventional hollywood features because there were expensive sets costumes high priced movie stars the most successful makers such films artistically and financially were the team martin johnson and his wife osa who made several documentaries sometimes with blatantly staged events africa and asia the johnsons safari films were extremely popular inspiring several parodies most notably wheeler woolsey this africa which the very sexy esther muir plays character named mrs johnson martini instead martin johnson geddit although several other filmmakers were producing safari documentaries this time the johnsons films were the most popular this genre because they relied heavily humour viewed from our own more enlightened hope standpoint this serious flaw the johnsons documentaries there are too many scenes which the funny little brown yellow people are made look complete idiots who are easily outsmarted the clever white bwana johnson and his wife one definite asset these movies the presence osa johnson ten years younger than her husband she manages seem young enough his daughter while certainly not attractive the shapely blond esther muir osa johnson was pert brunette who gave ingratiating performances front the camera all the films she produced with her husband congorilla probably the best the johnsons films the shots the congo are interesting and have some historical value evidence what this environment looked like 1930 the shots the pygmies and other natives are also interesting although these suffer from the johnsons penchant stage events manner that makes the natives look wild and alien the best and funniest scene congorilla improvised sequence which osa johnson attempts teach jazz dance some pygmy women the dance the black bottom less the same dance which bob hope famously taught daisy and violet hilton the conjoined twins wearing jodhpurs riding boots and pith helmet osa johnson starts scat singing while she does high steps and slaps her knees her attempt teach this dance the african women meanwhile they just stand there staring her apparently wondering what this crazy white woman trying accomplish very funny scene but has unpleasant undertones osa johnson doing dance that was invented black americans the implication seems that black africans should instinctively able perform this dance after brief demonstration using natural rhythm guess because their blood something rate congorilla points out this film says little bit about african life the 1930s and rather more about american cultural perceptions that same decade
