1 |text discovered this film after reading the book that inspired not strictly biographical film loosely based the facts but found compelling and eerie exploration evil and madness and michel serrault gives unforgettable performance petiot there are many memorable images this movie petiot traveling through the night like vampire his black cloak flapping behind him almost iconic there are also several touches expressionism petiot crooked silhouette mounting the stairs leading from the cellar where the butchered remains his victims await cremation reminds some scenes from nosferatu but found the primary appeal this movie aural the soundtrack loaded with ominous sounds starting with the foreboding music the opening credits accompanied wordless wailing petiot lives and runs his medical practice complex with many small shops and there persistent background noise knives being sharpened somewhere well peddler playing eerie tunes saw there are animal noises well the concierge keeps goat unseen cats howl and later the film see hapless cattle being herded through underpass the whole atmosphere unsettling with overtones violence and slaughter not only animals but human voices are often heard the screams gestapo victims petiot patients his waiting room monitored listening device just the same the suspected collaborators after the war are monitored their cells even the action the film often arranged that hear the voices the participants without seeing them when petiot goes see mme kern hear her singing she works her voice echoing the theater before ever see her and even when she does appear she often filmed from behind her voice calling out her husband whose voice calls out her conversation disembodied voices echo large halls and their owners when seen all are photographed distance cannot actually see them speaking this ghost story and these are the voices ghosts many them petiot future victims yet petiot himself often only voice his frightening laughter echoes retreats from the camera throwing comments behind him into the air nobody way much ghost those murders always frantically busy scurrying from appointment appointment never rest but his activity that machine lifeless and imperturbable interesting that among all the horror and danger occupied paris petiot alone unafraid amused enthusiastic angry irritated contemptuous but never afraid unlike those real people lures their deaths surprise that boasts his mechanical inventions including perpetual motion machine true detail from the book did claim have invented many machines sort perpetual motion machine himself and mechanical imagery everywhere the film from the opening giant wheel the movie house petiot bicycle with its squeaking wheels echoing the sound sharpening knives the victrola keeps winding play music before makes kill even his routine with his victims mechanical write note your wife let disguise you before you leave you need vaccination barcelona casablanca dakar like well oiled machine the routine always the same just the record always the same maeder the author says that was the clockwork perfection his crimes that weighed heavily against petiot his trial his system was smooth and efficient nazi concentration camp and this may why the movie invents subplot petiot involvement with the french gestapo and the occupying nazis unfortunately doesn quite work part the story because very hard figure out just what petiot doing for the collaborators what going when ends their headquarters the middle the night disposing bodies hiding stolen goods hard say and harder believe not likely the state would turn freelancer like petiot but does remind the duality evil people petiot robber and murderer but also devoted father and husband just learned that hitler loved dogs and that nazis guilty the worst war crimes could also loving fathers and family men have recognize that petiot could commit unspeakable horrors and yet also function normally his insanity easily camouflaged the insanity and horror the wartime situation paris when killing robbing and disappearing are happening all around nobody pays attention petiot tosses more corpses the pile
