1 |text what arguably the best outdoor adventure film all time four city guys confront nature wrath story survival the setting backwoods georgia with its forests mountains and wild rivers the director john boorman chose use local people not actors portray secondary characters these locals imbue the film with depth characterization unequaled film history central casting actors could ever come close these people remarkable faces voices actions don recall film wherein the secondary characters are realistic and colorful much anything else this gritty realism that makes this film amazing another strength the film theme nature the wild can violent how appropriate that the setting should the american south very few places the are have been violent redneck country story about darwinian survival the fittest the film conveys the idea that humans are part nature not separate from deliverance very much product its time when unlike today americans expressed concern over vanishing wilderness the film magnificent scenery the sounds birds frogs crickets and the roar the river rapids combined with the absence civilization all convey environmental message and that another strength the film entertainment level the tension gradually escalates the plot proceeds not even half way into the film the tension becomes extreme and then never lets not until the final credits roll very few films can sustain that level intensity over such long span plot finally the film technical quality topnotch direction and editing are flawless cinematography excellent dialogue interesting and the acting terrific burt reynolds has never been better ned beatty perfectly cast and does fine job and jon voight should have been nominated for oscar there weak link the film the music which strikes timid overall deliverance almost certainly will appeal viewers who like outdoor adventure even for those who don the gritty characterizations the acting and the plot tension are reasons enough watch this film one the finest cinema history
