1 |text probably the best film the year for this small french film centers put upon office secretary carla emmanuelle devos who spends her days doing other men jobs uncredited and being the source their scorn and lunchtime conversation which all too clear her being partially deaf she reads lips change set motion when she hires newly paroled con paul vincent cassel her assistant the relationship which develops between them the centre the film mutual dependency for vastly different reasons bonds them carla becomes attracted paul and the fact that makes her feel attractive for what seems like the first time paul does nothing dispel her feelings because needs her help owes money local gangster and forms plan steal from him which will involve carlas skill reading lips think the main thing that pushes the film way above average suspense drama the amazing chemistry between the two stars throughout the whole film matter what other characters are screen you can feel this amazing bond between carla and paul cannot remember when have witnessed such sexual chemistry between two actors emmanuell devos gives brilliant performance she won the french cesar for best actress you never feel like you are watching piece acting this really carla the chameleon like vincent cassel also wonderful makes somewhat unappealing character both appealing and attractive loved this film because these two people and both times when had finished watching wanted back into the cinema and become involved with them all over again
