1 |text really enjoyed this episode which was great surprise given the bad reputation seems have acquired from pure writing perspective the 16mm shrine absolute treat with fantastic dialogue and character analysis typical sterling particular really enjoyed the philosophical indulgences the episode tackling themes existence and reality whilst balancing with more psychological topics such denial pride and desire the sixteen millimeter shrine episode about how these ideas based around unwillingness accept change can seemingly alienate person from the rest the ever changing world also fantastic example cerebral twilight zone one that explores the mind rather than the world outside these elements all come together very nicely create thought provoking and incredibly interesting minutes the episode not without its faults however which mainly lay lupino and leisen shoes ironically felt lupino was unconvincing throughout with only few scenes that could count memorable this course being absolute shame considering how well sterling had written her character furthermore leisen didn seem know what with most his characters sometimes having them stand around set doing next nothing which probably explains why accepted the poor performances from lupino half the time thankfully balsam does good job covering lot weak spots helping redeem the show from acting perspective least said previously however you fan classic film and cerebral science fiction this shouldn bad sometimes made out addition the writing that mentioned above the episode also features some fantastic photography still amazes that the show looks this good nearly fifty years later and decent enough set design overall the sixteen millimeter shrine great episode and above all certainly one make you think
