1 |text cry the dark cry the dark was film that anticipated would offer phenomenal performance from meryl streep and solid unremarkable film this assumption came from the fact that aside from streep best actress nomination the movie received little attention from major awards groups little did anticipate that cry the dark would such riveting drama well constructed every level you ask this under appreciatted classic the film opens rather slowly letting the audience settle into the chamberlain relaxed pace and really notice that the core they are incredibly loving simple family fred schepisi the director selects random moments capture family vacation that give looming sense the oncoming tragedy while also showing the attentive bliss with which lindy streep and michael sam neill chamberlain care for their children while the famous line dingo took baby has become somewhat punchline these days the movie never even comes close laughable the actual death azaria horrifyingly captured subtle and realistic leaving the audience horrified and asking questions the majority the film takes place courtrooms and focuses the chamberlain continuous fight prove their innocence the press and the court which suspects lindy murder the fact that clear from the beginning that they are innocent makes the tense trials all the more gripping audience member was fully invested the chamberlain plight and was genuinely angered and hurt and saddened when they were made look terrible the media but the same the media public opinion understandable loved the way the media was means made sympathetic but they always had valid reasons hold their views the final line the film very profound and captures perfectly the central element that makes this film much different from other courtroom dramas terms performances the only ones that really matter this film are those streep and neill and they deliver every way for this ranks one not meryl streep best performances for all her mastery different accents which course are very impressive their own right streep never loses the central heart and soul her characters find this one streep more subtle performances and she hits out the park and neill actor who has never impressed beyond being charismatic and appealing jurassic park perfect counterpoint streep performance from what seen this undoubtedly neill finest work date shame wasn recognized the academy with leading actor nomination match streep the two them play each other brilliantly more emotionally gripping than most films and also incredibly suspenseful cry the dark far exceeded expectations highly recommend that people who only know the movie the flick where meryl screams the dingo took baby watch the film and see just how much more there cry the dark then that one line
