1 |text watching the commercials for this movie was fairly convinced that was going loathe for one thing was one those loosely based the novel movies which usually means that the book author saw the script hated and refused associated with the film worse the trailer showed only the most mundane slapstick imaginable kid gets squirted the face with garden hose and falls over when little brother got into his mind that this was the must see film the season course thought the same thing about cars over the hedge the ant bully monster house etc etc was admittedly less than thrilled but once the theater the film won over for variety reasons first and foremost the writers capture kid dialogue better than just about any other children film ever seen prime example this comes directly after the boys principal accidentally eats worm stuck egg omelet the boys lame over exaggerated impression the principal lecturing them which makes realistic since all little kids think mistakenly that they great mocking expressions their adult tormentors then one the boys asks why did say alley oop another boy responds maybe crazy and the entire group laughs uproariously not overly witty rejoinder but exactly the kind thing young kid would come with the spot and exactly the type remark other kids his age would find hilarious confirm kid brother laughed right cue when they were spoken screen could practically hear his voice spouting the same exact lines was placed similar situation another reason the movie works that the writers manage work issues like bullying sibling relationships the new kid school and peer pressure conformity without making any them seem though they were subplots for some after school special for example the bully joe isn stereotypical definitely bad but not pure evil and just enough his home life revealed that the audience feels sympathy for him and understands his bullying origins there also cue the dramatic music moment where billy worm boy realizes what complete tool being his younger brother woody and yet the end the movie some type minor transformation has been made there some realism here the way the characters resolve situations and the way they relate each other and very little comes across corny the only drawback the movie comes the form absolutely laughable dance scene that even the creators the infamous mcdonald dance party mac and would scoff why why was put into the movie did austin rogers adam pull macaulay culkin and refuse take the role unless was given vehicle showcase his impressive dancing skills the entire sequence definitely did not need there and had slightly less comedic value than any given show the history channel overall though this movie was excellent and the length about hour and twenty minutes was just about perfect one the best most realistic live action kid films you ever see you ever around children just remember what being kid was actually like
