1 |text name julia ross mesmerizing 1945 thriller from joseph lewis arguably one the very finest directors hollywood noir films this minute gothic oddity from columbia pictures came after lewis lengthy apprenticeship the helmer string poverty row westerns east side kids comedies horror melodramas including the incredibly bizarre bela lugosi shocker the invisible ghost and standard studio product secrets bombs over burma the falcon san francisco etc all which set the stage rather nicely for what was come from the enormously talented and inventive lewis name julia ross well dark the night from the following year introduced director who had mastered the rare and delicate art telling dark and probing tale swiftly and efficiently the most modest budgets later lewis productions like gun crazy 1949 and the big combo 1955 despite the expanded scope their narrative structure continued rely upon deft lucid camera work and effective low key lighting and very modest resources name julia ross probably owes more the tradition british mysteries set studio bound england than does conventional film noir attitudes and trappings young woman nina foch agrees take position the home elderly woman dame mae witty two days after her arrival she awakens from deep sleep completely strange house and mysteriously enough with brand new identity that the old woman daughter law told that she been the victim nervous breakdown she struggles grasp the utter and seemingly hopeless nature her predicament but before long she begins piece together the strange and troubling truth behind this dark mystery that her husband the always menacing george macready most probably murdered his real wife and that she been duped into participating harrowing and sinister scheme much what distinguishes this otherwise modest tale are the indelible touches that lewis brings the production marking the first his truly serious endeavors film director
