1 |text this rather poorly named western series won emmy for best syndicated program and certainly interesting series was produced republic the studio which did action better than anyone and they put their best into each episode was built around real historical figure the old west railroad detective named matt clark similar the later elliot ness with the gangsters the 1920 and managed become involved with almost every notorious western outlaw between the middle the 1800 and wwi the series best asset was jim davis tall rugged ruggedly good looking prime shape with authentic western accent and great riding skills which made him utterly convincing the action scenes davis was every inch the western hero was teamed with two lovely and active stars mary castle frankie during the first season and kristine miller jonesy during the second each worked well with davis what separated this show from its contemporaries and much what came later was the professionalism invested the action scenes ace action directer william witney directed episodes franklin adreon the rest both filmed the action with polish republic vast store stock footage from serials and was utilized give scope the level individual episodes rose fell with the quality the guest stars brought the play the outlaws among the really good ones were marie windsor belle starr lee van cleef jesse james fess parker grat dalton jean parker cattle kate and joe sawyer and slim pickins butch cassady and the smilin kid the cream the western and comers pickins parker denver pyle james best and richard jaeckel honed their craft veterans with decades experience under their belts harry woods glenn strange kenneth macdonald earle hodgkins steve darrell and chief yowlachie provided the old leather feel vintage westerns the weakness the concept was that there are only many famous western outlaws the second season the famous figures were becoming mite obscure for all the most dedicated history buff nevertheless few the later shows were match for any due the guest stars henry brandon portrayed rustler nate champion and former republic star don barry was outstanding small time outlaw milt sharp western fans history buffs will want see this
