d serious completely shuns others except for his family meticulous and precise about everything does and for while appears the prime mover the plot attack the school yet likable his own way does not embrace teenage nonsense and part feel compelled agree with him yet these moments are shattered andre fleeting gestures violence towards the audience treating both confidante and potential victim cal the other hand seems more relaxed than andre more accepting reality yet his own way dominant have many personal moments introspection with cal video diary scenes when alone and apart from andre cal seems struggling with his own personal demons and using their plan exorcise himself them andre jealous cal going the prom with old friend wants cal all himself cal placates andre and encourages him for the first time his life andre seems have found someone who believes him and who admires him cannot lose whilst cal has found someone offering him way out the movie certainly picks pace and improves nears its grim conclusion there excellent moment when cal attends the high school prom suddenly the star the movie becomes shy and introverted not all ease with his peers yet are inclined feel more connection with cal than with the raucous bawdy crowd screaming juvenile obscenities whilst drinking heavily their limo theirs episode all too common and recognisable not want relate them when over and cal back with andre silently preparing one their final videos like the characters feel once again ease safe the fantasy world they created feel like shunning the masses they have the penultimate scene superb the final video sees andre and cal arming themselves their car just moments before attacking all too real and truly creates sense impending doom know know cal and andre and are realising they are about actually with kind morbid fascination are also relishing the films catharsis the massacre shot cctv fashion times shocking and whilst was certainly the perfect choice depict the massacre were going not void flaws what most significant the sudden radical change perception have cal and andre looking them the this person suddenly they are the callous killers knew they would become yet refused acknowledge that they would violent and real our heroes have become monsters and the reality their fantasy terrible tragedy which costs them everything the final scene shows group teens filming themselves burning the crosses erected for andre and cal disgust that they have been memorialised having known andre and cal can only feel almost sadness that they are actually gone forever and that they certainly did not win anything zero day must see for anyone interested these violent acts sensationalised the media character study well worth experiencing
