1 |text clever script from the late sebastian japrisot and smart performances from the two male leads alain delon and charles bronson should the other way around result engaging and entertaining thriller add the above the competent direction from veteran jean herman and sparse but effective score francois roubaix becomes easy why this film has odd timeless quality this buddy buddy bonding story with two loners both disillusioned and world weary returning presumably from algiers like the other colonial powers this time post leading into the 60s france had struggled keep appearances overseas losing algiers was bitter blow adieu ami the original title chronicles the actions our two anti heroes they struggle make after their discharge one thing happens after another and the viewer really has pay attention because japrisot lean and economical with his script there then there must reason suffice say these two men battle out physically and psychologically one long weekend their motivation quite different their goals are different their survival depends entirely each other that alain delon and charles bronson are outwardly different the former arguably pretty boy and the latter ugly thug adds the chemistry that quest makes for great story which turn makes for great film lest forget there are women this film and true the japrisot method they too are memorable though not nearly fleshed out say much more would spoil one delight discovering their true nature farewell friend has been released the anamorphic image enhanced english only not even subtitles for the hard hearing running time 110 minutes mono soundtrack but the roubaix music has lots punch highly recommended
