1 |text this unusual laurel hardy comedy with something split personality times feels like two movies made different styles spliced into single short happily each portion funny its own right and the boys seemingly effortless clowning carries the day and synthesizes the film disparate elements into entertaining whole while never heard fan cite dirty work his her favorite laurel hardy comedy nonetheless one that everybody seems like our story set the home professor noodle who represents one key element the story line wildly over the top parody mad scientist scenarios this marks rare venture into sci territory for abbott costello and the three stooges tangled with mad doctors far more often than stan ollie any event the professor obsessed with creating rejuvenating serum that can make people younger while his sarcastic butler jessup expresses the viewer skepticism with rolled eyes and the occasional dry quip meanwhile stan ollie are chimney sweeps who show the professor home the very day perfects his solution their portion the film consists characteristic but first rate slapstick involving the chimney the roof shovels and number unfortunate mishaps you don enjoy watching these guys screw task then you probably won like dirty work but for fans the team this movie feast the highlight comes when ollie plummets through the chimney lands the fireplace and then pummeled with bricks that fall onto his head with maddening rhythmic precision one one also like the shot ollie tumbling off the roof into greenhouse the process work slapdash suspect was something inside joke the way fields movies would feature the world worst rear projection screens the slapstick stuff great fun but the mad scientist motif that makes this film offbeat and two supporting players deserve tip the bowler hat prolific character actor lucien littlefield terrific the professor delivering his overripe lines with relish and cackling with hammy glee while sam adams stitch the less showy role jessup the butler great stan laurel and oliver hardy were their prime always worth noting that their supporting casts the hal roach studio gave their films enormous boost too usually did the background music roy shield but dirty work marks rare occasion from this period that roach comedy has musical accompaniment all after the opening credits mood music might have enhanced the proceedings but matter this highly enjoyable comedy anyhow and prime example what made laurel hardy popular their day
