1 |text hundstage intentionally ugly and unnerving study life particularly dreary suburb vienna comes from former documentary director ulrich seidl who adopts very documentary like approach the material however the film veers away from normal types and presents with characters that are best described extremes xc2 x96 some are extremely lonely some extremely violent some extremely weird some extremely devious some extremely frustrated and misunderstood and the film combines several near plot less episodes which intertwine from time time each following the characters over couple days during sweltering viennese summer very few viewers will come away from the film feeling entertained xc2 x96 the intention point the many things that are wrong with people the many ills that plague our society general thought provoking film and its conclusions are pretty damning the whole fussy old widower fantasises about his elderly cleaning lady and wants her perform striptease for him while wearing his deceased wife clothes nightclub dancer contends with the perpetually jealous and violent behaviour her boy racer boyfriend couple grieving over their dead daughter can longer communicate with each other and seek solace having sex with other people abusive man mistreats his woman but she forgives him time and again security salesman desperately tries find the culprit behind some vandalism work site but ends picking innocent scapegoat and mentally ill woman keeps hitching rides with strangers and insulting them until they throw her out the car the lives these disparate characters converge over several days during intense summer heat wave the despair the film palpable many scenes are characterised long awkward silences that are twice effective whole passage dialogue might then there are other scenes during which the dialogue and screen events leave you reeling particular scene during which the security salesman leaves the female hitch hiker the mercy vengeful guy beaten raped and humiliated thankfully all off screen for some vandalism she didn even arouses sour almost angry taste another scene man has lit candle wedged his rear end and forced sing the national anthem gunpoint all part his punishment for being nasty his wife while might want cheer that this thug receiving his come uppance are simultaneously left appalled and unnerved the nature his punishment indeed such stark contrasts could act summary the whole film every moment light heartedness counter balanced with moment coldness every shred hope countered with sense despair for every character you could like feel sympathy for there another that encourages nothing but anger and hate might want turn away from hundstage dismiss exercise misery but also points some uncomfortable truths and for that should applauded
