1 |text what makes for best picture material the oscars have come for lot stick for rewarding overblown spectacles that have aged poorly and ignoring the auteurs who would deified decades come wasn because hollywood was against art creativity the academy awards are the selections made the industry itself and that why least the classic era they tended reward the greatest collaborations the most sensational meetings creative minds the arthur freed unit mgm had been bound for oscar winning glory for several years this point was only matter time before freed aided his strongest director vincente minnelli and some the finest musical stars the business would land best picture freed had arguably done more raise the status the musical than anyone else crafting pictures which wove story and song together without losing the dynamic spectacle the 30s musicals the point about freed musicals that the lyrics the songs unlike those hammerstein lerner don have tell even relate the stories what important that the tone the song and the way presented fit into the structure the film american paris was the first three freed musicals the other two being singin the rain and the band wagon which took existing classic numbers out their original context and made them work completely unrelated story the words don fit the plot but the routines fit the show when gene kelly sings got rhythm hasn even got girl yet but the way done with the french kids joining great bit characterisation and the upbeat tune and dance gives the movie the little lift needs this point american paris also uses the rule breaking allowed the genre add little unconventional flights fancy tell the story such the series dances which accompany the description leslie caron character and what better director for this project than minnelli himself painter and pianist this time there wasn really anyone who had better feel for technicolor while some directors would saturate each scene one colour fill the screen with clashing shades minnelli colour schemes are tightly controlled but never look forced the opening scenes the tones are fairly muted but not drab and particular there absence red during oscar levant and georges guetary meeting the caf xc3 xa9 few more vibrant shades are introduced then during the first musical number strauss minnelli gradually brings splashes red xc2 x96 table cloth bunch roses xc2 x96 until eventually dominates the song has awoken the picture colour scheme for most the songs the colours are choreographed intricately the people however some numbers such tra keeps the shades the same and instead opens out the space the song swells and the characters become more animated the achilles heel american paris its story personally find the romantic angle particularly unpalatable playing does like last hurrah for the misogynistic love stories that reigned supreme the 30s the headstrong independent woman gets rejected while the meek delicate girl harassed into loving the hero even you don mind that difficult connect emotionally with the story because constantly overshadowed the songs and dances compare this singin the rain which doesn really have many great routines memorable set pieces american paris but has winning storyline singin the rain was overlooked the 1952 oscars yet regarded classic the genre today but think people sometimes forget that cinema all encompassing form visual entertainment not just means telling story american paris not deep engaging tear jerking but like certain demille picture that won the top award the following year certainly great show
