1 |text what movie never imagined richard attenborough could have such movie him gandhi has always left indifferent apart from ben kingsley performance and never considered attenborough particularly good filmmaker but cry freedom held interest like few movies have recent times exciting mesmerizing political movie with great performances kevin kline and young denzel washington kline plays donald woods south africa newspaper editor who befriends the civil rights activist steve biko starts difficult friendship for woods sees biko black supremacist preaching hatred against whites but biko with his kind words upbeat attitude and complete transparency wins over woods and introduces him reality about apartheid that woods knew nothing about biko decent law abiding citizen who altruistically stands against all prejudice and the system that keeps down his people one night coming from illegal meeting arrested and beaten death the authorities try hush the matter because biko has become huge personality south africa but through the efforts woods the truth comes out but what should triumph only becomes nightmare woods and his family become targets for the secret police this movie has interesting structure has fact two narratives first narrates the life and death biko amazing first half completely dominated the charisma washington what may his greatest performance yet the second half less interesting narrates woods attempt escape from south africa publish book about biko woods has become enemy state banned person which means can meet people leave his country plus constantly spied the police kevin kline gives great performance this second half too although the first half quite straightforward the second does interesting things with editing giving flashbacks biko and events that show the repression against the black south africans some may argue this make more interesting but for the second half just captivating woods and his family devise bold plan escape south africa the last minutes were heartbreaking was tears george fenton and jonas gwangwa score certainly had something with although never been much fan fenton cannot stand his gandhi score think the score for cry freedom one the most beautiful ever composed for cinema the movie thanks the music married the powerful images times reached incredible peaks emotion cry freedom definitely not movie just watch because denzel washington this movie cherished its entirety acting writing music editing cinematography come together perfect synthesis create ode the power the human spirit this movie deserve place alongside movies like the pianist life beautiful and the shawshank redemption
