1 |text daniel day lewis does remarkable job playing christy brown the artist who grew with cerebral palsy but managed have productive life dealing successfully with his handicap and becoming respected artist and writer the film however very difficult one review even watch fortunately had the caption feature catch every spoken word which would have been impossible saw the film theater while respect brave piece work dealing with difficult subject matter can say the sort film want view more than once nevertheless attention was held the story telling device flashback framed the present which see christy being honored for his achievements before see the flashback his youth and his struggles communicate with those around him who certainly gave him loving care daniel day lewis certainly remarkable the troubled man who falls love with therapist fiona shaw much his mother fear that when the love not reciprocated his heart will broken there painfully long scene restaurant where confesses his love her before others and then goes into frenzied rage after drinking too much brenda fricker does brilliant job the mother taking care him his father and brood siblings while struggling keep roof over their heads until day lewis begins have success with his work she complements day lewis performance the warm hearted mother and shares many poignant moments with him richly detailed story family that stayed together under the most unusual circumstances with attention period detail every frame the film both fricker and day lewis won oscars but hugh conor and ray mcanally are also excellent conor christy boy and mcanally the father who spends too much time the local pub but loves the boy summing elmer bernstein music added plus factor well worthwhile but definitely not film for everyone
