1 |text spoilers many different comedy series nowadays have one point another experimented with the idea obscure independence early episode cartoon family guy the griffin family find their home independent nation the united states america and the story progresses from there way back 1949 however the ealing studios produced wonderful little film along the same idea after child prank the residents pimlico discover small fortune treasure the inquest becomes clear that the small area small outcrop the long lost state burgundy withdrawing from london and the rest great britain the residents the small street experience the joys and the problems with being independent state based time when rationing was still operation this story brilliantly told and equally inspiring featuring performances stanley holloway betty warren philip stainton and young charles hawtrey the film well stocked with some the finest actors their generation these actors are well aided well superb little script with some cracking lines feeling remarkably fresh despite being over years old the story never feels awkward and always keeps the audience entertained ealing studios was one the finest exporters british film ever existence with films like passport pimlico not difficult see why amusing from start finish the story always fun and always worth watching
