1 |text there are some films that every horror fan owes himself herself see and emilio miraglia dama rossa uccide sette volte aka the red queen kills seven times 1972 definitely one them with gialli and gothic tales being two favorite sub genres horror was looking forward seeing this film for quite while and even though expectations were high this masterpiece surpassed greatest hopes miraglia earlier giallo the night evelyn came out the grave 1971 was already creepy and highly atmospheric film which successfully mixed giallo with gothic horror but couldn possibly compare this instant personal favorite the red queen kills seven times hands down one the most unique and overwhelming italian horror films ever made and lover the genre could possibly consider missing incredibly mesmerizing giallo with strong gothic elements the red queen delivers everything one could hope for either sub genre inventive and incredibly compelling plot spine chilling suspense sublimely uncanny setting and genuinely creepy atmosphere eerily lush colors stylish murders brilliant score and not least ravishing female cast lead the stunningly beautiful barbara bouchet this film simply one the most outstanding combinations elegant beauty and pure terror the film starts out incredibly beautiful gothic castle germany little girls kitty wildenbr xc3 xbcck and her sister evelyn have been fighting when their grandfather tells them the story behind incredibly uncanny painting legend has that fiendish red lady return the castle every hundred years and kill seven people fourteen years later kitty barbara bouchet has become successful fashion photographer suddenly people begin get murdered director miraglia had already proved his incredible talent for style atmosphere and colorful creepiness with the night evelyn came out the grave and makes use these elements even far more effectively this gem the red queen kills seven times feast for the eyes indeed and one the most overwhelming italian horror films both visually and plot wise the haunting painting the grandfather castle alone capable giving the viewer the goosebumps the red lady red queen she called the english title arguably the most fiendish figure ever giallo the spine chilling laughter that the murders are accompanied would even frightening its own sexy female cast always appreciated especially giallo and this one prime example for that the ravishing barbara bouchet one favorite actresses must one the most stunningly beautiful ladies ever appear screen and she great actress too bouchet presence has graded many italian flicks among other appearances she starred three the greatest cult masterpieces italian 70s cinema within one year 1972 fernando leo milano calibro lucio fulci giallo highlight don torture duckling and this unforgettable gem apart from the wonderful miss bouchet the film gorgeous female cast includes sexy young sybil danning marina malfatti the night evelyn came out the grave and other beauties who are not afraid bare for the camera the whole film the murders are stylish and extremely elegant yet frightening and macabre and some them are quite gory bruno nicolai mesmerizing score memorable gets and makes the film intensely eerie atmosphere even more haunting the plot ingeniously convoluted and full red herrings the tension level increses with each passing minute the red queen begins creepy and stays stunning the last second overall this one the films that cannot find enough words praise for the red queen kills seven times absolute masterpiece that easily ranks among the finest gialli ever made and top priority for every fan horror and italian cinema see
