1 |text prisons are not exactly renowned for their kind hospitality and happy vibes what with stories fights chaos murder and course extreme male bonding but the prison this film different beast altogether horror films set cells are you probably know nothing particularly new they emphasis and exaggerate the fear claustrophobia and the inability escape xc2 x96 two the greatest themes horror cinema with such examples the chair waldermar korzeniowsky 1988 the green mile frank darabont 1999 alien david fincher 1992 and course the entire women prison exploitation genre itself another entry into this niche has something inventive and lot fun boot order recognised least that what you have thought prison certainly incredibly fun and enjoyable ride and somewhat shame that isn well known should the film short centres old prison well duh which has been reopened however not just fellow inmates and guards the prisoners have fear but also mean ass demon ghost spirit with only one thing its mind death and boy are treated some awesome death scenes won spoil anything here for you but there are plenty innovative and enjoyable murders all done invisible hands besides the special effects and the murders this film also has another thing going for cast headlining have lord the rings peter jackson 2001 2003 star viggo mortensen and for all those inclined yes does get naked whose performance not only highly believable but done with such skill that his eastwood esquire character both bad the bone and likable very delicate mix add him cast hey wait minute know that guy actors and you got yourself one great set stars the characters themselves however lack three dimensionality and more often than not come across very stereotypical got black oculist hard nails prison warden human rights activist woman and plenty other stock characters but all honesty this fault actually aids the film instead boring character development over long equilibrium are chucked more less straight into the action and once gets going very early there not single scene that filler xc2 x96 balls the wall plot unlike certain shawshank redemption frank darabont 1994 sharing conventions with the slasher genre this somewhat convention itself and good slasher genre tradition prison punishes those who have been bad all all this excellent little horror film and one which sadly overlooked and unmentioned among the horror world with excellent cast and great special effects and rather original death scenes this film highly recommended horror fans don fooled into thinking cheesy little film either just because was made usa 1980s far from cheesy although the very end does ruin this and simultaneously far from gritty and realistic whilst attempts tackle issues such prison rape these are rather subtly done give out luvs very entertaining horror film with some very nice touches indeed
