1 |text year old girl develops her first serious crush the year old boy that lives near while simultaneously trying overcome her feelings inadequacy comparison her older sister that the simple premise this beautiful poetic coming age film from director robert mulligan mulligan famous for previously directing summer 1971 and kill mockingbird 1962 two giants the coming age genre here directs newcomers the principal roles reese witherspoon her film debut the year old girl emily warfield the older sister jason london court the year old boy reese witherspoon astonishingly good her film debut displaying every emotion that year old girl feels experiencing young love and hurt never striking false note warfield and london are both equally good well the film accurately depicts each adolescent thoughts feelings regard love with heartfelt sensitivity never crossing over into maudlin excess even once kudos the autobiographical screenplay from jenny wingfield this one the very few films about young love that honest and consistent tone without being emotionally dishonest sensationalist the music wonderfully simple accentuating the tone and mood from scene scene but never becoming intrusive the beautiful cinematography famed horror director freddie francis who was his when this was shot tess harper and sam waterston play the girls parents with dead aim accuracy for 1957 caring strict and emotionally simple gail strickland good also the boy mother there are feelings sort out lessons learn and truths face this sweet natured film that packs emotional wallop date this robert mulligan last film this one the very best films 1991 stars
