fter paying rent actually jesse james last residence 1318 lafayette street joseph missouri was simple one storey cottage renting for there was upper storey when jesse james killed his wife could not come running from upstairs hope lange does here she was actually the kitchen one continuity error robert wagner with stunt double does impressive job taking slug the jaw and falling over while his hands are tied behind his back but when gets the rope binding his wrists has vanished the screenplay does some weird and unnecessary juggling dates following the northfield robbery attempt jesse says expects get home his birthday the actual northfield bank raid the james gang september 1876 was two days after jesse james birthday maybe meant next year birthday later see jesse and his wife moving into their joseph home fine summer day while jesse tells her what plans when christmas eve arrives but real life and mrs jesse james moved into that house december 1881 this scene should christmas eve these errors were entirely avoidable some the fictionalisations here don make sense according this movie the northfield bank raid failed because one fictional henchman was late cutting the telegraph wires this had actually happened would indeed have hampered the james gang getaway but wouldn have affected the robbery itself which failed for other reasons there are good performances here jeffrey hunter frank james moorehead alan hale jnr cole younger and stage actress marian seldes rare screen role was disappointed robert wagner normally under rated actor elsewhere wagner has proved his impressive range convincingly portraying heroes villains and morally ambiguous characters here can seem decide whether depict jesse james goodie baddie doesn much bother john carradine phones his performance brief role fictional jackleg preacher who baptises jesse and his wife their wedding fact jesse james was baptised childhood his uncle methodist minister but perhaps this second baptism topping jesse jame