1 |text john carpenter halloween the greatest horror film all time maybe not everyone but and always will the film sheer genius and will always hold very special place heart unfortunate didn get see this film until twenty years after release but even twenty years later after many slasher copy cats had come and gone the film still gave the same impact must have done then father suggested before see halloween h20 that whip out and rent halloween and get the full story and after watching halloween was quite clear that defined and set the slasher genre the film plot simple 1963 michael audrey myers killed his sister judith cold blood with large butcher knife incarcerated for fifteen years where was treated sam loomis escapes and returns his hometown haddonfield where begins stalking three young girls laurie strode innocent bookworm annie brackett tough talking sarcastic and lynda van der klok beautiful and sexually vigorous young girl loomis tracks michael here where enlists the help the town sheriff leigh brackett whom remains skeptical his story about the psychotic killer michael watches the girls mercilessly and begins killing them off one one until only sweet innocent laurie left who the prime target michael list the casting this film was brilliant and all the actors and actresses gave top notch performances jamie lee curtis was stunning her first film role laurie strode and donald pleasance gave thrilling performance with his small role loomis nick castle who portrays michael did outstanding job the soulless and evil killer and his walk and body movements were perfect one the great highlights this film chilling score done john carpenter himself who created one the most recognizable horror themes known today the blue lighting was creepy and effective and one the great moments this film when young laurie cowering against wall after seeing her dead friends and the shadows behind her michael face materializes before strikes michael mask was one the thing that sent chills down spine the most the white emotionless face worked perfectly what makes this film great that not gory film unlike the cheesy friday the 13th films fact there little blood this film all and works instead suspense and tension became clear that halloween spawned movies like friday the 13th and characters like jason voorhees whom mere rip off michael myers sum suggest you see this film least once your life landmark film making and without doubt not the greatest then one the greatest horror films all time
