1 |text when saw this movie the theater when came out 1995 via free advanced screening was totally enchanted and would have gladly paid see was sorry when talked many people afterwards who had also seen and who were totally disappointed with and how ended the other hand felt completely the opposite was totally satisfied with the outcome and everything else people talked said there was too much talking plus they were unhappy because they felt that the ending left you wondering about the fate the two characters found these observations absurd and also painful evidence how the majority the american movie going public seems have tendency want easy follow stories films with not too much complex and intelligent dialogue lest they get confused they also like spoon fed tidy endings happy sad this disgusts nobody wants challenged anymore and for the ending and don want spoiler totally content because know heart that these two characters will see each other again all about your own personal faith romance and destiny very personal film that doesn speak all people but certainly spoke give chance patient with richard linklater has crafted very lovely film with beautiful story set against the beautiful background the city vienna watching makes you feel you yourself are strolling through the city streets along with the characters you yourself were tripping through europe eurail pass very intimate plus ethan hawke and julie delpy exquisite job bringing the complex script life they must have improvised during some parts and works well they have great chemistry their roles their awkwardness strangers getting know each other the beginning very believable and you can truly feel the romance and bonding develop between them the movie progresses get the feeling that this was very personal work for linklater and deeply respect him for getting this film made definitely touched and hope touches others just much bravo for romance
