1 |text rawhide was wonderful western series focusing band trail drovers lead the trail boss gil favor most episodes especially from the first seasons were really character studies favor and his men guest stars came and went but unlike wagon train they seldom dominated the episodes they appeared rawhide was true gritty western and gil favor stood out memorable character never forgotten thanks eric fleming performance the show became massive hit course was ably supported wonderful cast good actors clint eastwood sheb wooley paul brinegar steve raines james murdoch rocky shahan robert cabal all these actors left their mark piece television history rawhide captured the flavour that time the west that other series has for yet anyhow managed later seasons tended split the leads and give them individual story lines for some the time this didn work the cattle drive and the regulars provided the best stories however there were still some classic stories and rawhide remained top drawer affair the black and white photography added bleak realistic feel that other western series seldom managed capture rustlers indians commancheroes beautiful damsels distress serial killers they all showed give our heroes problems the end came for the series quietly when the final season was axed less than half way through the reason eric fleming had departed and rawhide was now head without body the gritty realism was gone gil favor commanded respect and exuded authority was never infallible and this made him all the more interesting shall not see his like again watch episode whenever you can they seldom disappoint
