1 |text after not having much luck selling his screenplays the new movie industry during the first decade the 20th century 1908 playwright griffith got the job that would make him legend was hired the biograph company director movies wasn really what griffith had expected when decided enter the movie business but accepted the job and less than year became biograph most successful director thanks his original approach film making and the wild inventive his narrative many years later would direct the birth nation 1915 the movie that would revolutionize film making and make him one cinema first recognized authors however lot what would make him great filmmaker can found the many short films made for biograph company the early years his career 1909 the sealed room one those and also one the few horror movies that very first decade the 20th century the sealed room story set the 16th century which count arhtur johnson has built windowless room his castle small yet nice and very cozy room meant used enjoy the love and company his wife the countess marion leonard more private way however the count doesn know that his wife not exactly faithful she infatuated with the minstrel henry walthall court with whom she having affair soon the count gets busy with his own business the countess calls the minstrel and both lovers enjoy the count new room when the count returns discovers she missing and begins suspect finally discovering the two lovers his room but instead making scene prefers remain hidden decides that there better punishment for his unfaithful wife seal the windowless room with the couple inside written griffiths regular collaborator frank woods the sealed room takes elements from edgar allan poe the cask amontillado and mainly honor xc3 xa9 balzac grande breteche create haunting gothic melodrama based the themes treachery and sadism despite having runtime minutes woods screenplay develops the story very good way and plays remarkably well with the horror elements the story while melodrama heart woods focus the character the count and his sadism creates one the best horror characters these early era the sealed room definitely very simple and basic story but woods handling the dark and morbid thematic its plot makes the story very entertaining film that was very different than most griffith melodramas the sealed room griffith uses his talents experiment with tension and suspense different way than his usual while often played with editing create thrillers that excited his audience this movie his focus was create desperation and horror playing with the inherent feeling claustrophobia that the source stories had interesting how the story starts another his melodramas and slowly the pacing becomes faster the horror themes begin dominate the plot culminating his great use editing for the final scenes not being movie where camera tricks are essential what shines the most the sealed room griffith talent direct his actors the legendary filmmaker manages bring the best out his cast with his usual natural style far removed from the staginess that was the norm his day usual the cast was comprised usual collaborators griffith starting with arthur johnson the count johnson gives great performance and truly conveys the character transition from loving husband sadistic monster his performance not without touch overacting but actually that adds realism the character exaggerated personality the countess marion leonard looks very good and also very effective her acting conveying natural charm that makes hard not sympathize with her her treachery finally the legendary henry walthall appears the handsome minstrel and while far from being one his best performances manages give proficient acting that also adds nice touch comedy the film while not real importance the plot nice see other members griffith stock company the background like his wife linda arvidson and young mary pickford nobles court while not exactly masterpiece the sealed room notable exercise editing create suspense and tension like griffith used those days the movie has very good set design and while very low budget griffith care for details makes look very convincing and works perfectly along with his directing style the change focus horror makes stand out among other his films from that era and johnson performance the sadistic count makes worth watch while griffith will always remembered for his highly influential and controversial the birth nation the early short films made before really give good idea the development the techniques and the style that would make him legend simple yet elegant the sealed room fun movie watch and one the few horrors the first decade the 20th century
