1 |text cunningly interesting western from director who had few peers the genre much like other anthony mann pictures the far country blends potent pot boiling story with adroit knowing impacting scenery both which play out amongst some mann peccadilloes like honour integrity betrayal and course death the story sees fortune hunting partners jeff webster james stewart and ben tatum walter brennan travel oregon territory with herd cattle aware the blossoming gold boom they plan make tidy profit selling the cattle klondike town arriving skagway they find self appointed judge gannon john mcintire ready meet out justice webster account webster having fractured the law all with honest cause along the way punishment gannon takes the partners herd from them but they steal them back and head across the canadian border dawson with gannon and his men hot pursuit here beautiful women and meek and lawless town will fill out the destinies all involved interesting from start finish the far country benefits greatly from james stewart bubbling anti hero waiting portrayal and mann slick direction the tight borden chase script the cinematography from william daniels superlative tho not done any favours current dvd prints and the film has few surprises and will wont core reeling the viewers paying dividends watches for hardened genre fans still remains something essential viewing for first timers venturing into the wonderful yet dark western world anthony mann and james stewart
