1 |text must admit that this the type film that would normally eschew but rented basically because the stars certainly was not sorry fact you see rated five stars this film the perfect combination sharp directing and superior acting andy and hank hanson are brothers who decide commit the uncouth crime robbing their parents jewelry store the crime goes terribly wrong thus beginning examination the three men the hanson family through series flashbacks get know charles hanson and come understanding the strained relationship between father and sons younger brother hank basically screw has always had trouble holding job and pretty much goes the direction the wind hank insecure cowardly and very much under the influence his big brother ethan hawke has the character hank nailed and gives what probably his best performance thus far shows man who basically good hearted but influenced outside forces that unable follow through with any important task andy the surface appears successful businessman but soon discover that addicted drugs and has been embezzling from his company pay for his habit andy who concocts the scheme rob his parents store and gets weak willed hank commit the act philip seymour hoffman surely one the finest actors our time plays andy hoffman actor who has the ability portray man who the surface charming businessman liked his acquaintances but real slime ball underneath absolutely perfect for the part andy might said that through his superior acting skills made andy the perfect part albert finney plays father common his generation charles hanson not bad unfeeling man but has lousy relationship with his sons because never really understood what was necessary nurturing positive bond between his sons and himself has always been too quick criticize and admonish always made clear that favored his younger son over his older thus causing wide emotional rift between himself and andy get know charles and andy the thought andy forming plan rob from his father becomes less unbelievable personal note cannot believe how much charles hanson reminded own father and how much andy and hank reminded own brother and myself perhaps this may one the reasons that enjoyed the film much this story distant critical father more successful older brother and less successful younger brother hit close home fortunately brother and never came the state committing crime against parents guess were made sterner and more moral stuff this complex personalities and actions has been expertly put together director sidney lumet eighty three still has the chops give the audience engrossing characters and edge seat action that hypnotizes angry men was his first film made fifty years prior before the devil knows you dead but hasn lost any bit his magic touch showing characters that will long remembered the events and characters before the devil knows you dead are harsh and unattractive and this definitely not feel good movie however two hours ultimate entertainment which thoroughly recommend
