1 |text ran across this several years ago while channel surfing sunday afternoon though was obviously cheesy movie from the 70s the direction and score were well done enough that grabbed attention and indeed was hooked and had watch through the end recently got the opportunity buy foreign dvd this film oops didn notice domestic one had finally come out couple months prior and was very pleased able watch again and its entirety don wholly understand the phenomenon but somehow the 70s seem have lock horror movies that are actually scary the decades prior the 70s produced some beautifully shot films and the bulk our enduring horror icons but are they actually scary not very likewise the years since the 70s gotten horror movies that are cooler more exciting have much better production values and sophisticated special effects are more fun funnier have effective jump moments and some very creative uses gore but again they aren really scary there just something about the atmosphere the 70s horror films the grainy film quality the spookily dark scenes unilluminated vast high tech lighting rigs the edge dreamland muted quality the dialogue and the weird and stridently scores the odd sense unease and ugliness permeating everything everything that works undermine most movies the 70s the case horror works its favor specifically this film the quiet intense shots the devil dog staring people down fairly unnerving much more effective than they had gone the more obvious route having the dog growling slavering and overtly hostile cujo the filmmakers wisely save that for when the dog appears its full supernatural form the effects when that occurs while unsophisticated today standards literally gave chills the bizarre vaguely defined not quite sure what looking look intuitively strikes more like how real supernatural vision would rather than the hyper real crystal clear optical printer digital compositor confections latter day horror films while the human characters this film are not satisfyingly rendered their nemesis the world they inhabit the actors all decent job the pairing the brother and sister from the witch mountain movies yes brother and sister rather cheesy bit stunt casting but they fine yvette mimieux always manages entertaining unspectacular richard crenna earns more and more empathy from the audience the film progresses his self doubt wonders whether his family alienness truly due supernatural plot whether merely succumbing paranoid schizophrenia pretty well handled though his thought that getting routine physical may provide explanation for what been experiencing absurd its xc3 xafvet xc3 xa9 the movie the end question mark type ending one the only ones seen that doesn feel like cheap gimmick and actually made think about the choices these characters would faced with next and what they likely and how they feel about detractors this film may say merely feature length vehicle for some neato glowing retina shots but hey you could say the same thing about blade runner
