1 |text was easy for sir richard attenborough make gandhi 1982 xc2 x97he was merely narrating story great individual who walked this planet not long ago comparatively must have been lot tougher for director feroz abbas khan making his debut filmmaker make gandhi father pitting shriveled anti hero against international hero both whom were historically real individuals and ironically father and son the events the film are mostly real mahatma gandhi lived shown the film setting high moral standards for the world follow yet these very standards overshadowed the aspirations his eldest son harilal lawyer repute like his father complete his education and get job india and thus provide income for his nuclear family the film does not debunk gandhi and his ideals for gandhi his mission was larger than his family aspirations loved his family and cared for them though his thoughts for their appeasement were blinkered his ideal caring for the masses stood for equality and dignity among all persons and his view give special undue advantages his own son overlooking other deserving persons went against the basis what preached the film looks unusual case parenting xc2 x97where idealist parent places receding goalposts for less than brilliant offspring the film presents unusual scenario that happened son marries his childhood sweetheart upsetting his father the father upsets his son educational aspirations several key junctures the fragile link between devoted son and father breaks the son wants stand his own feet and care for his nuclear family while the father gradually becomes the father nation the son stumbles valiant quest for identity and survival his marriage breaks and seeks solace religion buffeting between islam and hinduism through all his tribulations his link his mother remains until she chides him for being drunk feroz khan essentially director plays making his foray into cinema wrote and directed the play mahatma gandhi that had considerable impact the indian theater community the play and the consequent film were based two biographies one chandulal dalal and another nilamben parekh the success the staged play was evident reason for the commercial bollywood actor anil kapoor produce this noteworthy film every time good director plays attempts direct cinema there evidence lack confidence with the medium peter brook great director plays but less competent film director the opening shots khan film promises great cinema xc2 x97a derelict harilal gandhi brought sion hospital bombay mumbai barely mumbling that his father bapu the popular name mahatma gandhi father entire nation the hospital authorities not recognize him mahatma gandhi eldest son dying poverty and loneliness apart from the dramatic opening the film unfortunately merely presents great story and some superb exterior shots father and son meditating silhouette for indian film does present some high production qualities that hand hand with lack interest for details the clothes most indians the film seem dust free and freshly laundered modern hairstyles actors and even shefali shetty playing mohandas gandhi wife century ago with plucked eyebrows the bane indian cinema since feroz khan theater personality has invested much more effort working with the actors developing the characters rather than cinematic details somewhat like sir attenborough another person who also product theater royal academy dramatic arts knowing quite well that criticize gandhi any manner was asking for trouble even when there was direct criticism the film producer anil kapoor took remarkable decision not putting posters the film accessible heights india fearing that some one could tear the poster disrespect intentionally unintentionally with all its mix greatness and faults gandhi father throws several questions the viewer mother son bonding stronger than father son bonding parenting one immediate family less important than humanity large does one seek refuge religion and alcohol only when worldly troubles are encountered this film harilal buffeted adversities runs from one religion another while his father quotes scriptures forgive them for they know not what they when beaten and thrown the ground south african policeman convinced the value religion and convincing others well the film won the best actress award the tokyo international film festival for shefali shetty shah and indian award from critics feroze khan and anil kapoor have handled sensitive subject very well and elicited above average performances from the ensemble actors hope the international success the film paves the way for some able director film another brilliant indian play girish karnad tughlaq some day meeting international quality standards
