1 |text horror omnibus films were popular the seventies not very fond them myself but this one undeniably excellent slice british horror cinema the house that dripped blood horror omnibus featuring four stories that surround creepy old house the country and are being told scotland yard officer estate agent this film headlined three well known stars horror cinema peter cushing christopher lee and ingrid pitt whom horror fans will recognise one lee stars the greatest british horror film all time the wicker man the first segment the film titled method for murder tells the story horror storywriter whose creation strangler named dominic brought life his own imagination this story builds suspense very well through his girlfriend and the audience lead believe that what seeing figment his imagination this story certainly isn very original but makes for its lack originality through the atmosphere creates and final twist which works incredibly well and came genuine surprise the second story titled waxworks stars peter cushing and least favourite the four this tale follows the story phillip grayson cushing man that discovers wax museum and decides venture inside discovers woman that familiar him and who later find out murderess quite what the woman relationship with phillip entailed never really explained but the tale relies more the mystery build the suspense rather than plot details cushing later joined his friend neville rogers played joss ackland and that when the tale really starts pick the setting waxwork museum full murderers for horror film isn new idea the same setting was used great effect the excellent 1966 horror film chamber horrors although the one here isn grand the one the aforementioned film the power the setting used lesser horrifying effect much which achieved feeling claustrophobia brought about the limited area the museum peter cushing always interesting watch and seeing him avoid axe wielding madman treat for the horror fan despite being least favourite this story still entertaining and interesting enough not let this anthology down the film continues with sweets for the sweet which without doubt the best the omnibus this story stars the legendary christopher lee seemingly overprotective father the beauty this story comes from the way played out leaves the audience guessing know that there something wrong with either the father the daughter but don know who what christopher lee usual portrays his character with great degree sinisterness the audience left simmer over his actions regarding giving his daughter doll and the fact that she isn allowed school have any toys the card exactly why held close the chest until right near the end epitomised the truly chilling line which lee tells his babysitter that fact afraid his daughter the ending this section superbly played out opinion one the finest endings any horror story ever told and will stay with you long after the end credits roll the omnibus finishes with the cloak which definitely the most comedic the four this tale about hammy horror film star that unimpressed his latest film technical side goes out and buys himself cloak naturally this cloak turns out real vampire cloak unlike the other three tales this one seems played out mostly for laughs that bad thing however the majority the humour funny and serves nice contrast the rest the film the ending this tale coincides nicely with the ending the wraparound story the film which very sinister yet humorous ending very good film also look out for the little jibe regarding christopher lee dracula nice touch think overall you want horror omnibus you really cant wrong with the house that dripped blood the third tale alone makes the film worthy your time and this very solid horror film indeed
