1 |text one the less widely lauded recent asian period action affairs gojoe first slow and often curious but overall pretty terrific offering exciting layered and beautiful sad say know virtually nothing the buddhist philosophy japanese history and legend that surrounds this film its deeper meanings are lost but even without contextual knowledge this still rich fare taking traditional fantasy structure into impactful higher plane the story benkei warrior monk and perhaps demon who seeks enlightenment destroying the demon gojoe bridge prince shanao himself mortal seeker after his own higher plane but this time the power demons thus the film becomes matter illusions and benkei case indecision conflict which the real goal self knowledge for benkei come terms with his true nature and for prince shanao come face face with the nature what seeks become benkei even more hampered here the fact that his dark nature makes him fundamentally odds with the world even when not open conflict never ease director sogo ishii handles this one epic with measured pace camera work always stylish and often frenzied without neglecting the need for more sedate moments let the location sink there also great use lighting and fog give ethereal atmosphere there air fantasy much the film but outside the overtly supernatural moments down and dirty fantasy with more period fell than flights fancy the cinematography makoto watanbe important here vivid and detailed richly evocative affair actingwise daisuke ryu dignified and powerful with mysterious savagery benkei while tadanobu asano has driven cold arrogance prince shanao the leads masatoshi nagase rounds things out ordinary man smart and cynical but still unaware just exactly what the stakes are the film all fits together well however touch flabby times begins slowly some shots are little drawn out and the epic fight scenes times longer than strictly necessary for the fighting filmed frenetic rather than for actual moves has artistic impact but may disappoint regular action fans often obscured objects flashing blades and fast moving individuals whirling with deadly force through their adversaries are the order the day invigorating watch but the end could have done with little more traditionalism there some unfortunate cgi bloodshed well somewhat works the context but still distracting overall though found this pretty great film its not one for regular action fans swordplay enthusiasts seeking another azumi rather deeper and more mystical beast its ending particular will not down well with fans the more generic wing such fare but for myself really hit the spot and for those more adventurously inclined might too well recommended any rate
