1 |text terms the arts the 1970s were very turbulent era literature and the visual arts was the closing great fifty sixty year period creativity that has yet restarted music was decade that many see low point due corporate rock and disco television was golden age for situation comedies from the odd couple the mary tyler moore show all the family but film was even greater period creativity all genres that saw the rise the american auteur directors like robert altman francis ford coppola and martin scorsese from the ashes the old studio systems that had dominated hollywood for over half century these directors wanted craft literate arts films for the masses the sort that had been staples europe since the end the second world war yet the studios were trying keep pace with socially aware films the sort not seen since the 1930s but unlike the films the 1930s starring actors like jimmy cagney and john garfield usually starring the dead end kids that dealt with social issues gritty realistic way realistic one could get sound stage the social consciousness the late 1960s and early 1970s manifested itself most science fiction films which allowed the left wing hollywood preach the masses under the guise what most considered little above comic strip entertainment there was precedent for this approach for several the flying saucer films the 1950s dealt with the political zeitgeist the mccarthy era most notably the day the earth stood still and invasion the body snatchers and the early 1960s saw rod serling constantly subverting the political conservatism the time casting social issues into science fiction settings his classic sci television anthology show the twilight zone among the studio offerings this time were the ecologically sensitive silent running george lucas first film thx 1138 which dealt with consumerism group think and existentialism and logan run which hammered away communism and state control versus the rights individual some the film references are quite heavyhanded and reek the then current arab oil crisis and rampant inflation few jarred strawberries cost 150 and soylent rations its assorted colored foods soylent yellow soylent red and the new soylent green reputedly made from the finest undersea growth manner not unlike the gas rationing the time scenes food riots are eerie echoes the oil riots many gas stations during the year the film release and the scenes crowding and bodies live and dead lying all about are still chilling well influential later film like escape from new york obvious progeny the rest the script stanley greenberg however rather pedestrian and fairly standard for dystopian flick but fleischer and cinematographer richard kline great job filling the screen with interesting images and sounds spice things the use soft dimly lit visuals murkily filtered add stygian feel the new york the film almost like colorized version carl theodor dreyer vampyr the only light the film comes from artificial sources and were not for the fashion faux pas the film could truly seem timeless the end the film where thorn sneaks into the processing plant where human corpses are made into soylent green wafers both chilling and oddly drama less the end the soylent minions hunt thorn down but survives long enough utter the film catchphrase chief hatcher yet one does not know enough for hatcher has already been opted and has track record taking the easy way out yet that fact and its ambiguity shows that the film does not recapitulate its characters dilemmas and has depth many later better made films sci not not have also why soylent green still film worth watching
