1 |text the british production company amicus generally known the specialist for horror anthologies and this great omnibus called the house that dripped blood doubtlessly the finest amicus production seen far admittedly there are quite few that have yet see though the house that dripped blood consists four delightfully macabre tales all set the same eerie mansion these four stories are brought you wonderfully gothic atmosphere and with one the finest ensemble casts imaginable peter cushing christopher lee cushing and lee are two favorite actors ever well denholm elliott and the ravishing ingrid pitt star this film which true horror fan could possibly afford miss one course and the film has much more offer than just great cast the house that dripped blood revolves around eerie rural mansion which strange things are happening four parts the film tells the tales four different heirs the first tale method for murder tells the story horror novelist charles hyller denholm elliott who moves into the house with his wife after moving the writer suddenly feels haunted maniac his own creation the first segment great kickoff the film the story creepy and macabre throughout and the performances are entirelly very good the second story waxworks retired businessman phillip grayson peter cushing moves into the house and suddenly feels drawn mysterious wax museum the nearby town the great peter cushing once again delivers sublime performance this and the rest the performances are also very good the tale delightfully weird and the second best the film after the third the third tale sweets the sweet far the creepiest and most brilliant the four john reed christopher lee moves with his little daughter the private teacher and nanny mrs norton whom reed has employed instruct his daughter appalled about her employer strictness towards his daughter and eager find out what reason the overprotective father views upbringing may have this best segment maintains very creepy atmosphere and genuinely scary plot christopher lee always superb his role nyree dawn porter also very good the nanny and special praise goes then year old chloe franks this ingenious segment alone makes the film must see for every true horror fan the fourth segment horror actor paul henderson jon pertwee moves into the house with his sexy mistress star carla ingrid pitt this fourth story satire more than actually horror highly amusing satire however and there are many allusions other horror films one point henderson indirectly refers christopher lee who stars the previous third segment all four segments have delightfully macabre sense humor and great atmosphere stated above the third segment far the creepiest and greatest but the other three are also atmospheric and often macabrely humorous horror tales that every horror lover should appreciate igenious atmosphere macabre sense humor genuine eerieness and brilliant cast make this one must see short the house that dripped blood excellent horror omnibus that lover british horror could possibly afford miss highly recommended
