1 |text the cinematic interests the british monarchy continues with the young victoria 1837 1901 after having seen recent years the efforts with keira knightley the duchess cate blanchett elizabeth films and scarlett johansson and natalie portman take the boleyn sisters with the other boleyn girl more contemporary stories would include helen mirren award winning portrayal the queen the current reign queen elizabeth the turn princess diana death each the films mentioned featured stunning actresses with acting gravitas some may dispute johansson were the flavour their moment and each film had definitive moment their historical character legacy that becomes brainer have those events featured and fact elizabeth had enough span two films however the young victoria the title already suggests lite version the young queen life and you looking for that definitive event the staple political intrigue that plague all royal households and their dealings with shady self serving politicians unfortunately there nothing depth here that not say the young victoria without directed canadian jean marc vallee best known for crazy and written julian fellowes this film chronicles very plain terms the life and times victoria emily blunt soon becoming the new girl when she was child the troubles she faced before coronation such the eagerness her mom the duchess kent miranda richardson and her adviser sir john conroy mark strong appoint themselves joint regent her throne already planned for reigning king william jim broadbent that wasn enough the political power play enters the picture with lord melbourne paul bettany being prime minister waiting trying gain the trust the new queen and subtly plants his own trusted allies into positions within the palace one hand you understand the need for young and new queen have trusted people key positions but the other are they really acting her interests the interests others even this angle intrigue creeps into her romantic story with prince albert rupert friend where their relationship forms the bulk the second half the film and pretty much everything already included the trailers for both they been brought under the influence others and told each step the way exactly what even their union may seem like firm registration alliance not for both lovers recognizing their common need establish their own grounding and with the help each other instead being pawns there this constant search and probing opportunities break out stifling and times absurd rules and regulations trust also becomes much valued commodity and loyalty too can traded for wanting set the slate clean however all these themes become but breeze through the narrative from childhood romance marriage and children fact there much fast forwarding here especially the last few minutes filled with inter titles that actually leaves the audience wanting for more and room course for another movie which suspect would probably not see the light day but perhaps television series might pick the film response and come out with mini series such pity that all the effort here ensuring the gorgeous costumes sets and art direction would confined film that quite lightweight theme and brief mention issues that they don really challenge the protagonists order allow for some overcoming character defining adversary with its star studded cast one would expect more but one would left wanting more instead recommended for those who are ever curious about kings and queens the british monarchy only complement other more engaging stories available the other films already mentioned
