-1 |text the fbi story 1959 was warner bros 149 minute epic tribute the famous criminal investigation agency from book don whitehead came somewhat laborious screenplay richard green and john twist and was directed with only modicum flair mervyn leroy however did have splendid colour cinematography joseph biroc and helpful score the studio musical magician max steiner the movie charts the history the bureau from its lowly beginnings the twenties modern times and its all seen through the recollections aging fastidious agent chip hardesty james stewart relates his investigative experiences flashback class budding young agents but all very long winded and episodic and progresses begins look like mini series instead major movie production the young hardesty runs the american crime gamut from taking such notorious criminal figures baby face nelson barker dillinger etc sorting out nefarious organisations like the klux klan nazi spy rings and the red menace and here has said that only for the screen presence and appeal its star the fbi story would probably have ended forgotten disaster moreover this another problem with the picture stewart left carry the entire movie almost his own with the exception vera miles who has the thankless role being his long suffering but devoted wife surrounded cast minor players throughout you find yourself half expecting someone like robert ryan jack palance even raymond burr make welcome entrance mobster police chief whatever but nothing quite imaginative that ever occurs pity the film does however manage give good look inside the workings the bureau with the help stewart narration learn about the thousands men and women who work for the organisation which includes the hundreds agents the field and are also treated peek inside headquarters which houses the gigantic records section and also get glimpse the chemists and fingerprint experts meticulously going through their daily chores another plus for the movie max steiner remarkable score heard over the titles powerful rousing and determined march while for the picture gentler moments there attractive love theme but quite ingenious the menacing and ominous march theme for the klux klan sequence and better still the rhythmic latin american music the composer wrote for the south american scenes especially the exciting fandango like orchestrations for the arrival the federal troops horseback the fbi story was one five scores the composer wrote 1959 which included samuel bronston naval epic john paul jones the charming rom com cash mccall delmer daves seminal western the hanging tree and daves summer place from which derived the young love theme which was become major hit tune for steiner better known theme from summer place the fbi story just about passes muster movie thanks biroc rich colour cinematography steiner wonderful music and course jimmie stewart who makes anything watchable classic but implausible line from the fbi story the bland nick adams who has just blown plane with people board including his mother being led away handcuffed turns the arresting officer and blurts case get any mail you can send canyon city prison for the next month after that you can send hell wow
