1 |text reign over success due the powerful work adam sandler and don cheadle while comedic actors going dramatic has been seen somewhat distraction sandler stranger playing more serious roles most the characters portrays have unstable temperament and vulnerability that can burst any moment might even typecast for characters with such hidden anger problems however this performance has some considerable dramatic weight unlike his roles less comedic fare like punch drunk love and spanglish the film alan johnson cheadle runs into his old college roommate charlie finerman sandler whom hasn seen several years five years before charlie suffered the overwhelming loss his wife and three daughters plane crash charlie barely even recognizes cheadle character due the repression his memories and consequent reclusive childish lifestyle since the accident isn until alan persists engaging him conversation that charlie remembers who their renewed relationship that follows will allow finerman have friend who doesn speak about his loss eventually enabling him confront the thoughts and feelings has suppressed his own terms though writer director mike binder doesn show much sense individual style and some his shots and transitions are bit awkward does have knack getting decent great performances from his actors while being talented and funny writer shot this film with digital camera more and more filmmakers are doing today enabling the crew shoot the night scenes with limited lighting this kept the colorful backgrounds new york city focus but resulted creating frequent digital grain which resembles blue specks scattered and moving the screen almost every main character reign over gives great performance jada pinkett smith and especially liv tyler are memorable their respective roles frustrated wife cheadle character and psychiatrist however sandler and cheadle that give some their finest work date they completely owned this movie sandler actually plays character that doesn outwardly resemble act like himself all partially credited his bob dylan esquire wig though cheadle character has more screen time than sandler they both should considered leading roles they equally support and help each other throughout the film music also plays great part this film especially the title song reign over love reign the who and later covered pearl jam one the most powerful moments the film binder shows sandler using music shut out his feelings and memories but this particular song provokes such intense emotion that rather than diminishing his anger incites his emotions all all reign over enjoyable sad yet many times funny film driven its amazing leading performances
