1 |text 1909 griffith had been directing films for the biograph company for about year and xc2 x96 working rate two three per week xc2 x96 was rapidly beginning develop his skills filmmaker the sealed room very interesting minute short fascinating piece gothic melodrama that even drifts slightly into the realm early horror the simple narrative was probably inspired edgar allen poe 1846 short story the cask amontillado and concerns powerful king who conceives deliciously sadistic form revenge punish his wife infidelity set medieval times the sealed room begins with the king arthur johnson overseeing the construction windowless room from sequestered dove cote the idea being that and his wife marion leonard will have completely private place enjoy each other company obviously very much love with her always showing his affection this latest act the crowning achievement his endearment however unbeknownst the king his wife has fallen love with the royal minstrel henry walthall during one romantic liaison inside the specially built room the wife and the minstrel are discovered and the heartbroken king conceives means getting his retribution the ignorant couple silently orders his workmen seal off the only doorway with stone and mortar slowly descending into cackling insanity each new stone placed down griffith always had eye for acute detail and the sealed room excellent early example this the lavish medieval century costumes lend the film sense reality and the castle interior looks authentic enough believable the time the director was also pioneering methods creating suspense and must admit that the film progressed became fixated finding out what would happen the hapless young lovers the early minutes griffith restricts his shots lengthy long takes from stationary camera was usual the time but soon xc2 x96 parallel the progressively darker subject matter xc2 x96 alters his editing tactics fascinating way though may not have invented the technique griffith was crucial popularising the use cross cutting xc2 x96 that alternating between different events occurring the same time not only does this create sense continuity but also maximises the level suspense since the audience are well aware not only the king ghastly actions but also that the wife and the minstrel are oblivious all despite these innovations the sealed room suffers from many the shortcomings typical the era the entire film takes place just two rooms with footage captured from total just three positions and prone become dull and monotonous times the acting performances are greatly exaggerated for extra effect however least the case arthur johnson his overplaying actually contributed recognising the escalating madness the betrayed king moment that thought particularly effective was when the two lovers attempted exit the room only find their only doorway replaced with wall solid stone their panicked reactions accompanied the silent maniacal cackling the king serve very well create impending sense claustrophobia did think however that their supply oxygen was exhausted surprisingly quickly
