1 |text blockbuster the time original release was the second highest grossing film 1976 the third screen version star born has always divided critics and fans alike the film open scathingly negative reviews however million budgeted picture went gross over 150 million the box office and won academy award and five golden globes not without some irony that streisand most commercially successful film would also remain her most controversial for every ten fans who state that star streisand best film there are always ten more who claim the weakest film her filmography although both sides have some merit support their claims should still noted that the seventies take star born remains one the most touching and highly entertaining showbiz dramas that hollywood ever produced for money the best version the often told tale the film solidly enjoyable and throughly absorbing changing the setting from the old hollywood studio system the competitive world the music industry was actually great idea and the screenplay forges realistic contrast between the characters romance and their careers this the main area that the 1976 version star born actually surpasses classic predecessors for example the film especially successful when depicting the clashing personal and professional difficulties during recording sessions and the never ending phone calls that interrupt kristofferson songwriting attempts this version the story also more believable portrayal the lead characters for example the female leads the two previous versions were virtuous and self sacrificing that they came off saints the other hand esther the female lead this version not only portrayed being strong and passionate but also flawed and conflicted this makes her feel more real than the janet gaynor judy garland characters felt the previous films and makes the story that much more effective the performances are all target even some the supporting characters aren fleshed out enough you looking for actress singer who can walk the fine line between tough and vulnerable without making herself seem like script contrivance streisand definitely the girl you want she one the few film stars who can make even the most banal dialogue seem fresh and natural and usual she manages make strong emotional connection with the viewer simply put her esther fully realized three dimensional human being kris kristofferson may not get much respect now for his laid back characterization however always interesting watch and displays magnetic charisma here that seldom displayed elsewhere his career kristofferson actually received rave reviews the time from newsweek time and even the new yorker usually vicious pauline kael gary busey and paul mazursky also give believable performances but both have fairly minimal amount screen time the film soundtrack recording was also massive success hitting the billboard hot 200 and selling over four million copies the alone the streisand composed evergreen with lyrics from paul williams unarguably one the most gorgeous songs contemporary pop brought even further life absolutely incomparable vocal performance from streisand the rest the film original songs mostly composed williams and rupert holmes are pretty good well and streisand sounds fantastic her live solo numbers remain the memory long after the rest the movie has faded streisand vibrant performances bring woman the moon and with one more look you thrilling life and make even sillier numbers like queen bee work far better than they have the right kristofferson solo numbers sound somewhat tuneless however that may have been intentional since playing singer decline though naturally dated some respects definitely does reflect the decade which was made the seventies take star born still holds remarkably well the film well mounted and slickly produced the chemistry between the leads extremely powerful and always feels genuine and streisand has two emotional scenes near the finale that are both aching effective conclusion star born not only entertaining and moving but also transcends all criticism
