1 |text midnight cowboy one those films thats been proclaimed masterpiece with good reason really one the finest films ever made america its both artistically valid yet entirely accessible and commercial wonder was huge success when initially released but warned its also one the most heartbreaking films ever made the characters are memorable well developed and ultimately tragic the filmmakers should applauded for not giving the hollywood ending something which was basically mandatory the 80s still this why treasure the years 1967 1977 for american film its time when well made innovative and most all bleak films could made with the big budgets that hollywood could offer all this was over the time star wars was released the direction john schlesinger makes the material work combines simplistic style with some experimental editing unlike many other films featuring these psychedelic effects midnight cowboy has aged quite well its still powerful now was when initially released the acting however what makes this masterpiece the characters backgrounds are never fully explained but the performances make them completely developed both jon voight and dustin hoffman are absolutely memorable and sympathetic despite their sometimes reprehensible actions plus being fan vintage exploitation films loved the scenes set the infamously sleazy 42nd street midnight cowboy close being perfect and one the most powerful films ever made
