1 |text two thirds nearly 000 imdb users who have voted this film have rated and one user reports wearing out six videotapes was this record merely faulty vcr although the film primarily intended period piece clearly has quite unusual fascination but for some reason imagined largely whimsy and until recently never felt the urge watch mind was changed elizbeth von arnim original book wife loves reading but her sight longer allows her read much she borrowed talking book form such books are usually irritating companion who busy with other things but gradually came appreciate that this one was seductively soothing although way syrupy and was also very well written realised wife would enjoy watching the film and decided buy her the videotape now very glad that did and would certainly recommend its purchase anyone else who appreciates quiet reflective work with fireworks but with well constructed character development and very successful pre mussolini italian atmosphere the story set the immediate post ww1 period and starts with two married london ladies who decide pool their savings and enjoy holiday together away from their families rented villa italy force circumstances lead this couple being joined two others with very different characters and backgrounds its theme essentially more than the interactions that take place their holiday progresses not only between these four very disparate mature ladies but also with the occasional male visitor you want action thrills dramatic sex scenes natural man made disasters harlequin style romances this would not the film for you but imdb users have collectively and very emphatically demonstrated that none these are necessary for film prove highly rewarding watch and you care give try you may did come rank among your much loved films fairly rare for watch film book with which already familiar many cases find this takes some the pleasure away from watching the film but here there such strong visual appeal the setting that actually found pleasure augmented the anticipation seeing the next segment the book effectively unrolled before eyes perhaps italy itself has some part this the last time had this experience was when was watching tales from boccaccio decameron generally films books tend increase the dramatic level the original work ensure that the filmed version has even wider appeal but here anything reduced order keep the viewers attention the gradual character development rather than any background events this works very well although changes from the book are few and basically the film remains true the original story great credit due the director mike newell and all members the cast particularly those well known british actresses who play the four principal ladies
