1 |text coinciding with the start the baby boom the years after world war saw unprecedented exodus americans moving out their city apartments into the suburbs where they can fulfill their dreams owning their own homes directed potter and written norman panama and melvin frank white christmas this lightweight but surprisingly observant 1948 screwball comedy captures the feeling that period very well course helps have trio expert farceurs xc2 x96 cary grant myrna loy and especially acerbic melvyn douglas xc2 x96 head the proceedings with their natural likability odds with the escalating frustrations home ownership even though the film sixty years old now there timeless quality the blandings dream and the barriers they face achieving obviously hollywood thinks since been remade least twice first very physical tom hanks comedy 1986 the money pit and again last year with ice cube are done yet one look hgtv programming schedule will show you how the situations explored here still resonate today the plot begins with man jim blandings his wife muriel and their two daughters cramped into two bedroom one bath manhattan apartment rather than pursue muriel idea renovate the apartment for 000 jim sees photo connecticut house magazine and realizes this where they need move with the help opportunistic real estate agent and against the advice their attorney and family friend bill cole the blandings decide buy ramshackle house badly need repair however the foundation sags badly that the house needs torn down favor new one this sparks the blandings push the architect design house excessive that the second floor twice big the first costs rise with each new complication tempers flare and even romantic triangle imagined among jim muriel and bill priorities finally sort themselves out but not before some funny slapstick scenes and clever dialogue that tweaks the not blissful ignorance the new homeowners with his double takes and flawless line delivery grant infallible this type farce and jim blandings epitomizes his more domesticated mid career characters role originally meant for irene dunne myrna loy shows why she was hollywood perfect wife she doesn get many the funnier lines but she combines her special blend flightiness and sauciness make muriel appealing character her own watch her deftly maneuver the overly agreeable house painter with her absurdly idiosyncratic color palette avuncular pipe smoking bill cole xc2 x85bill cole melvyn douglas shows his natural easy going xc3 xa9lan grant foil smaller roles are filled expertly with particularly memorable turns harry shannon the laconic well digger tesander lurene tuttle jim officious assistant mary and louise beavers the blandings lovable maid gussie the 2004 dvd provides some intriguing vintage material including two radio versions the movie the first 1949 version that did end pairing grant and dunne and then second 1950 version coupling grant with his then wife actress betsy drake most appropriate 1949 cartoon the house tomorrow also included giving comical tour futuristic dream house the original theatrical trailers for ten grant film classics complete the extras
