1 |text the war between the states was perhaps the darkest hour the history america war that pitted brother against brother and family against family and left scars that even today have not yet healed and all probability never will and any story about any war beyond any historical significance the personal discord behind the greater conflict that creates the emotional impetus that makes involving the human element that renders the context necessary give perspective which what director ang lee provides ride with the devil civil war drama which focuses the personal travails within the broader depiction the war itself and along the way manages include examination one the bloodiest chapters the war the infamous raid lawrence kansas quantrill and his raiders which succeeds presenting quite objectively from the confederate point view 1863 the union influence predominates the state kansas and even across the border neighboring missouri those with confederate loyalties are finding increasingly difficult hold out against the encroaching northerners especially without the aid what could considered any regular confederate troops and when things begin really heat around their own town jack bull chiles skeet ulrich and jake roedel tobey maguire form band their own and join the fray doing damage the union cause wherever practicable jack bull and jake not like the war and not like killing but they are standing for what they believe right there are others however even among their own men like the young pitt mackeson jonathan rhys meyers who will use the conflict vehicle for personal gain and nothing more than excuse express their own violent nature through unnecessary brutality perpetrated many instances against innocent victims and for jack bull and jake well many just like them becomes time which loyalty and moral judgments will sorely tested time during which their souls will tempered blood and they will have ride with the very devil himself against seemingly insurmountable odds with all his films director ang lee approaches his story through incisive yet subtle examination the traditions cultural aspects and moral attitudes the people and times depicting and doing lee provides his audience with least some understanding his subject that goes beyond the actual story and ultimately offers perhaps deeper grasp the motivations that propel his characters and the drama which they are engaged whether the traditions and customs that account for the relationship between father and his daughters eat drink man woman the effects class distinction sense and sensibility the honor and code which warrior lives and dies crouching tiger hidden dragon the moral ambiguities fostered lack all the above the ice storm lee infuses his films with insights into the human condition that take them higher level this film exception and does with all his films lee presents his story with the aid breathtaking cinematography this film frederick elmes who also did the ice storm brilliantly which under his guidance nothing less than visual poetry that special lee touch and adds wistful reflective sense whatever story telling which one the elements that make his films memorable jake tobey maguire initially brings sense youthful innocence the film that contrasts effectively with the maturity conveys later the story develops and his character along with most importantly maguire convincingly and believably responds the events that unfold around him which adds the credibility the overall film and underscores the realism the presentation his stoic acceptance death and the news those murdered the various skirmishes and battles the moral propriety which those encounters adhere even such troubled times the betrayal which because the nature the conflict almost commonplace and the loyalty and beliefs which and his companions cling adamantly all this that maguire achieves through his performance and small accomplishment however the kind studied understated performance that often taken for granted which unfortunate work like this worthy acclaim and should recognized skeet ulrich effective well jack bull and jewel her motion picture debut turns engaging performance sue lee shelley jeffrey wright however who stands out notable supporting role daniel holt well jonathan rhys meyers who brings chilling christopher walken like menace his role pitt also what amounts cameo role one scene mark ruffalo leaves indelible impression with very little screen time the supporting cast includes james caviezel black john simon baker george clyde tom guiry riley tom wilkinson orton brown john ales quantrill john judd otto roedel and kathleen warfel mrs chiles the civil war will forever open wound upon the nation but hopefully time goes will through the objective contemplations filmmakers like ang lee and films like ride with the devil that will ultimately help close the schism and promote healing light more recent events something that sorely needed worldwide film powerful medium can educational well entertaining and perhaps the future more filmmakers like ang lee will embrace and promote sense unity through the sensitive depiction the events and attitudes that make what are
