1 |text this little seen movie languid and laid back giallo veers away from some the clich xc3 xa9 the genre and adopts looser approach about woman searching for her missing lover psychiatrist who has suddenly vanished for apparent reason her search leads her villa populated group eccentric individuals true giallo style murder never far away the cast really rather good have aldofo celi thunderball alida valli suspiria horst frank cat nine tails and very young sybil danning scream queen the lead actress rosemary dexter and while not familiar with her she does good job leading the picture one the defining features eye the labyrinth its music atypically for giallo features jazz rock fusion soundtrack this score composed roberto nicolosi reminiscent miles davis especially his work silent way excellent soundtrack and really gives this movie different feel than most gialli the fusion groove accentuates the languid atmosphere and compliments the sunny sea front scenery that the film mostly made this giallo really need talk about the murder set pieces well this film falls little short this regard certainly not devoid them but they are few and far between the opening dream murder being probably the best offer well memorable burning car sequence but this really isn particularly violent film still don think should disappoint too many seasoned fans the genre the mystery fairly compelling and has enough eccentric characters the idiot boy saro and that unsettlingly inappropriate dubbed accent and moments the bizarre satisfy while the sleaze factor upheld with smattering nudity throughout eye the labyrinth plays like giallo version agatha christie mystery features group unsympathetic characters villa all under suspicion murder have the obligatory flashbacks detailing their connections with the final hours the highly unsympathetic murder victim while this isn grade example the genre certainly appealingly different one doesn borrow too heavily from other films the sub genre for giallo enthusiasts give this thumbs and hope one day given nice dvd transfer certainly deserves the treatment
1 |text beginning see very consistent pattern form the identity 2007 films 2004 was the year the biographies and 2005 was the year the political films 2007 can identified year featuring wide plethora morality tales films that portray test challenge and question human morality and the motives that drive certain things although this identification rather broad think that there are handful films released this year such yuma eastern promises american gangster country for old men and others that specifically question and study human morals and the motives that drive acts such violence treachery before the devil knows you dead deviously stylish morality tale and quite dark bleak and depressing one that and even better the fact that comes from one the greatest classic directorial forces our time the legendary sidney lumet who many have said has passed his prime but returns full force with this viciously rich crime thriller one those films whose plots are thick that one very reluctant into details movie that best enjoyed entered without any prior knowledge the events about unfold there are twists and turns but the thick and richly wrought plot not all the center this film the true focus mentioned the morality tale the motives that drive these two men the actions they the film plot structured like combination between the filmographies both the coen brothers namely blood simple and fargo and quentin tarantino see two men driven under various shady circumstances pull off fairly simple crime that goes incredibly ridiculously wrong and reciprocates with full force and inevitable tragedy and make all the more interesting the film told fragmented chronology that keeps back tracking and showing series events following different character every time and always ending where left off the last time sizzling sharp thick and precariously depressing kelly masterson screenplay surprisingly poignant and well rounded particular because debut screenplay but the film has much more going for than just delectably sinister and quite depressing plot first and foremost the picture looks and feels outstandingly well sidney lumet has throughout his career consistently employed interesting style cinematography and lighting naturalistic and yet stylish the same time the film carries with distinctive air style and class with wonderful natural lighting that just looks really great editing top notch combining the sizzling drama thriller aspect with great long takes that really take their time portray the action accordingly and vivid dynamic camera angles and movements further add the style the film also backed fantastically succulent musical score carter burwell the screenplay does its part and course lumet does his part but the film dramatic center are three masterful actors who deliver incredibly good performances first and foremost there are the two leads leading the pack philip seymour hoffman who has always been excellent actor but has stumbled upon newfound leading man status after his unnaturally fantastic oscar winning performance capote his turn this film fascinating severely flawed broken manic hoffman has some truly intense scenes the film that really allow his full dramatic fury come out and not just his subtlety and wit his side ethan hawke who has delivered some fantastic performances many films that are almost always overshadowed greater grander actors here bounces off hoffman and complements him incredibly well all the dynamic acting between the two them just utterly fantastic and convincing the audience very quickly loses itself the characters and forgets that watching actors and then there albert finney such supple opulent supporting role like the one has requires veteran professional and here finney delivers his finest performance many years the tragically obsessed father the two brothers who get caught the crime love how the dynamics between the three them play out love how hoffman clearly the dominant brother and shamelessly picks his younger brother even now that they middle aged men and yet despite this clear how finney father favours hawke younger weaker brother also the topic the cast the two supporting female characters xc2 x96 wives the brothers xc2 x96 also feature fantastic performances from amy ryan and marisa tomei whose looks just get better and better the years this film isn revolutionary these themes and this style have already been explored the likes the coen brothers and very easy imagine them directing this film but for film that treads familiar ground simply excels lumet employs his own immense directorial talent and employs his unique and very subtle sense irony and style masterson brilliantly vivid intense and morbidly depressing first time screenplay the lead performances are incredibly intense and the film features absolutely fantastic turns from hoffman hawke and finney but the truly greatest wonder the film that three years after won lifetime achievement oscar much revered the ultimate sign retirement the film business sidney lumet proves that still has the immense talent deliver truly wonderful resonant intense piece cinema reminiscent his golden years
