-1 |text granting the budget and time constraints serial production batman and robin nonetheless earns place near the bottom any cliffhanger list utterly lacking the style imagination and atmosphere its 1943 predecessor batman the producer sam katzman was known king the quickies and like his director spencer bennett seemed more concerned with speed and efficiency than with generating excitement unfortunately this team also produced the two superman serials starring kirk alyn with their tacky flying animation canned music and dull supporting players the opening each chapter offers taste things come thoroughly inane titles robin rescues batman batman wizard mechanical music droning and our two heroes stumbling toward the camera looking all around either confused having trouble seeing through their cheap halloween masks batman cowl with its devil horns and eagle beak fits poorly that the stuntman has adjust during the fight scenes his utility belt crumpled strip cloth with compartments from which still manages pull blowtorch and oxygen tube critical moments any case the lead players are miscast robert lowery displays little charm individual flair bruce wayne and does not cut particularly dynamic figure batman creates the impression that rather somewhere anywhere else john duncan robin has considerable difficulty handling his limited dialogue too old for the part with even older stuntman filling for him out costume lowery and duncan are exciting tired businessmen ambling out for drink without one ounce the chemistry evident between lewis wilson and douglas croft the 1943 serial although serials were not known for character development the earlier batman managed present more energetic cast this one offers group going through the motions not that the filmmakers provide much support not one the hoodlums stands out and they are led one the most boring villains ever the wizard great name actually they are led someone sporting curtain shawl and sack over his head with dubbed voice that desperately tries sound menacing the prime suspects eccentric professor radio broadcaster are simply annoying even the established comic book regulars are superfluous hard discern much romance between vicki vale and bruce wayne despite the perils she faces vicki displays virtually emotion commissioner gordon none too bright unlike the previous serial alfred the butler mere walk whose most important line wayne residence they are props for drawn out gimmick laden incoherent plot further saddled with uninspired repetitive music and amateurish production design the wayne manor exterior resembles suburban middle class home any sitcom the interiors those cheap roadside motel the batcave office desperately need refurbishing the costumes are kept rolled filing cabinet pity that the filmmakers couldn invest more effort into creating thrilling adventure while the availability the two serials dvd plus for any serious batfan one should not fooled the excellent illustrations the box they capture more the authentic mood the comic book than all chapters batman and robin combined now for the good news this not the 1997 version
