1 |text serials were short subjects originally shown theaters conjunction with feature film that were related pulp magazine serialized fiction known chapter plays they were extended motion pictures broken into number segments called chapters episodes each chapter would screened the same theater for one week the serial would end with cliffhanger the hero and heroine would find themselves the latest perilous situation from which there could escape the audience would have return the next week find out how the hero and heroine would escape and battle the villain once again serials were especially popular with children and for many children the first half the 20th century typical saturday the movies included chapter least one serial along with animated cartoons newsreels and two feature films the golden age for serials was 1936 1945 this was one the best the era zorro has been seen many films but reed hadley racket squad the undying brain was excellent the role the action constant and are led chapter chapter the ultimate end where find out the identity the evildoer zorro triumphs always does
