-1 |text the sight kareena kapoor two piece bikini about the only thing that wakes you from your sleep while watching tashan xc2 x97 the mega disappointing mind numbing new film the cinemas this weekend bad films are bad films and see some every week but tashan not just bad film terrible film terrible because takes its audience for granted terrible also because the filmmakers expect get away without plot any common sense only because they got big movie stars onboard written and directed vijay krishna acharya tashan what you describe road movie but one that going all the wrong directions saif ali khan stars jimmy cliff call centre executive who hired teach english bhaiyyaji that anil kapoor playing ambitious gangster desperate cool jimmy got his eye pooja the gangster pretty young assistant played kareena kapoor who uses jimmy swindle her boss crore rupees determined recover his money and also punish both jimmy and pooja bhaiyyaji recruits his most trusted henchman the job you have akshay kumar bachchan pandey the gangster faithful aide from kanpur who tracks down the culprits and recovers the stolen money that hidden across the length and breadth the country much like those bad eighties potboilers tashan too held together threadbare script centred vendetta plot but the treatment over the top indulgent that fails establish any connect instead coherent screenplay traditional three act structure you get handful set pieces around which most the scenes are loosely constructed that garish item song the desert the bullet dodging action scene rajasthani fort kareeena bikini moment even that ridiculous climatic action scene complete with shaolin monks water scooter zipping through dirty naala and believe not even dhanno style horse driven tonga all fairness not all these set pieces are badly done the item song the desert quite neat actually but very little makes any sense the larger picture because you just going from one piece another without any help from the script really little you expect seemingly fast paced road movie find sickeningly sentimental flashback track about childhood sweethearts you see the problem with tashan nobody associated with this film knew what film they were making what more don think they cared either the film reeks arrogance arbitrarily packing elements every genre without actually bothering stop and see the mix does work tashan like overcooked stew there are films that kill you softly and then there tashan film that kills you with excess packaged snazzily with glossy finish camera work exotic locations and fancy costumes every frame the film probably cost lakhs put together but still feels like hollow piece the end because the story doesn hold borrowing narrative from tarantino and style from stephen chow doesn help either because they don blend with the film wafer thin plot one may have complained little less the characters were more engaging but anil kapoor grating hinglish dialogue makes you want slit your wrists and saif ali khan fumbles through the film foolishly unable find his feet kareena kapoor meanwhile queen over the top delivery does decent job but course tashan salvaged some extent thanks akshay kumar irresistible presence and his spontaneous approach the character you cringe when cupping his crotch repeatedly and you scowl when delivers those double meaning dialogues but not for moment can you take your eyes off the screen when there despite some good music from vishal shekhar the songs seem like they only prolonging your misery well that because tashan test your patience case you didn know tashan means style sorry say this film has none
