ar losing funding and control becomes inconsequential finds himself facing the imminent danger losing much more than that now there very real chance that may lose everything including himself verhoeven has crafted what initially exciting even thought provoking film establishes good pace and uses the his disposal great effect though does tend allow the striking visuals overwhelm the character development anyone familiar with the invisible man actually anyone who can logically follow the progression the story will know early that caine not destined for happier times still verhoeven has style storytelling that definitely going capture the attention and engage his audience but seems bent rushing toward the climax and along the way abandons any and all the nuance that has made his film thus far successful opting enter into final sequence that nothing more than mindless blood and gore fest that betrays his audience and everything worked for earlier the film rather than seeking intelligent resolution caine suffering and using some inventiveness and imagination take the film inevitable conclusion verhoeven takes the low road and though may succeed purely visceral level any meaning one could derive from the story dissolves like many ashes the wind along with anything that would have made this memorable film and shame because verhoeven has higher level than much what offered this genre and allows sink unnecessarily one much lower kevin bacon does good job creating character that believable only the surface which seemingly serves verhoeven purposes perfectly there little depth bacon portrayal but has more with his director agenda than his own acting abilities verhoeven simply does not allow bacon the time develop caine any extent the character mainly vessel around which verhoeven can build his story and toward that end works the film would have been better served however had verhoeven and bacon collaborated more closely least developing bond between caine and the audience that