1 |text always sad when fringe movies such this are overlooked the majority filmgoers panic wonderfully compelling and poignant study character who feels trapped the pointlessness his own life william macy alex convincing always this fine actor seems have special talent for pulling your heartstrings matter how flawed his characters may may not always condone the lifestyles the protagonists plays but the emotions fear and confusion that evokes are often all too painfully familiar the title panic initially seems paradoxical given the lack overt emotion one point alex tells his doctor that rarely gets angry yet this story unfolds becomes increasingly obvious that rage and desperation not indifference are the driving forces behind this man existence more than once was reminded his performance fargo another strongly character driven movie both fargo and panic witness middle aged man who somehow seems have stepped out synch with the rest life has lost his way and the only way back deceptively appears though the darkness knows making bad choices but desperation overpowers self control and common sense alex connects with sarah year old woman mesmorizingly played neve campbell whom meets doctor office thematically this union less coincidence more the work fate alex finds certain comfort being with sarah sensing perhaps that she fellow drifter like him someone who has lost her way and floating aimlessly through the rest her life waiting powerlessly for its inevitable conclusion opting for movies such this shrewd and convincing way for neve campbell answer those critics who question her acting abilities too often the characters she has played who are the weakness offering campbell depth which flex her acting muscles this performance however may eye opener for many perfect movie world not only would there many more films like panic but also they would reach and appreciated much wider audience you watch movies for the richness and depth characterization rather than merely the latest state the art special effects then for you panic unmissable
