1 |text the academy awards ceremony march 1957 dorothy malone won the best supporting actress oscar for her torrid over the top portrayal spoiled heiress texas oil tycoon written the wind the 1956 potboiler adapted from robert wilder novel was veritable three ring circus showcasing alcoholism greed impotence and nymphomania malone performance marylee hadley lonely rich girl who picks men assuage the pain rejection from former childhood sweetheart was representative the movie whole mesmerizing watch even resorts the lowest common denominator melodrama written the wind ultimately the work one man the incredibly gifted director douglas sirk xc3 xa9migr xc3 xa9 from pre world war weimar germany who left his european theater heritage behind pursue career hollywood extremely erudite man sirk made name for himself the 1950 universal studios reliable director lavish soap operas most notably with ross hunter productions magnificent obsession all that heaven allows and imitation life independent producer albert zugsmith offered sirk the opportunity work outside the limiting constraints universal demure entertainments and create more adult sensational product hence the sultry wind and its follow 1957 tarnished angels both released under the universal international banner anyone guess why sirk didn pursue loftier themes but apparently directing these exaggerated dramas appealed more his artistic sensibilities written the wind could considered sirk epic soap opera indeed rife with human vulnerability and neurosis depicted among the very rich that compelling watch any real life domestic squabble among the rich and famous perhaps more robert stack not actor typically known for over emoting nearly matches malone intensity with his offering the weak willed brother kyle hadley mere shadow his patriarchal father when finds out that unable impregnate his new bride beautifully leonine lauren bacall hadley goes off the deep end escalating already serious drinking problem with secret gun 