1 |text rousing adventure form director george stevens before would turn more serious fare such 1948 remember mama and 1956 giant that set the standard for all future action yarns follow loosely based rudyard kipling poem the same gunga din follows the journey three military officers 19th century india the noble trio must brave series battles and other various dangers including thuggee cult and temple full gold their screen adventures remain thrilling even after more than six decades and have lent inspiration nearly everything from the cliffhanger inspired space opera star wars 1977 the similarly plotted raiders the lost arc 1981 the biggest reason for the picture success however the pitch perfect performances the film trio extremely charismatic actors victor mclaglen has rarely been better the strapping tough guy cary grant the ultimate comic foil and douglas fairbanks suave swashbuckling hero imaginable perhaps even more than rival errol flynn the chemistry between the three actors simply could not improved upon and such warm and believable comradely precisely what missing from most modern action pictures and they receive tremendous support from the marvelous sam jaffe who overcomes the obvious physical miscasting and makes the title character beacon humane sweetness and quiet strength huge hit its day the film was reportedly the second biggest money maker 1939 behind the outrageously successful gone with the wind and remains arguably the best film its kind
