1 |text normally not compelled write review for film but the only commentary for this film thus far rather unfair feel necessary share point view krisana was titled the theater saw fallen follows matiss lonely latvian archivist tries learn about woman whom didn try stop from jumping off bridge well her reasons for doing that the plot nutshell but this film not concerned with story much depicting the guilt man who failed act detective who investigates the incident tells him usually don bother care about the anonymous faces pass every day until after they die comparisons michaelango antonioni and his blowup will most likely abound any review you read about krisana the influence antonioni philosophical and austere style and the story blowup are clear and fact writer director fred kelemen makes obvious reference that film scenes which matiss attempts come know the woman who jumped off the bridge least who thinks did the only other person share his her views the film detracts the college film class look and sound the film she neglects consider the budgetary constraints that existentialist latvian film most likely faces but the atmospheric black and white cinematography and ambient sound succeeds artistic level depict the solitude matiss the background sound wind and street noises lend ominous aura and reminds one fellini film whether not that was kelemen intention the filmmakers undoubtedly had little money but this constraint used the film advantage krisana succeeds character study with enough humor thrown keep from being too self serious could have easily fell into the trappings mystery story but avoids that and becomes intelligent film about loneliness and guilt you are more concerned with plot this film and its ending may frustrate you otherwise take the time engaged well worth seeking out
