1 |text indeed drug use warehouse shoot ups matrix esque bullet dodging futuristic city with mix asian races and lonely vampire all the same movie seems like story that could only envisioned japanese pop rock star and that exactly what moon child and more while all these elements combined may sound like the perfect subject for campy movie the week moon child pulls off with but few expected bumps and hitches along the way the film has gritty definitely independent feel jumping from one scene the next not smooth transition but rather sporadic leaps and bounds giving glimpses into the characters lives and barely scraping true plot but the film makes excuses instead turning the story into one friendship love trust and betrayal all sugar coated the aforementioned elements futuristic society warring gangsters and vampires hyde the somber vampire kei excellent giving depth the character and balancing out the overly zealous acting gackt sho orphan who befriends kei lee hom wang also shines the vengeful son who becomes friends with grown sho the story revolves around these characters and their extended friends and family through different periods their lives and how simple friendship can easily turned into grief and betrayal while the action times all too unrealistic and special effects appear just show off one thing the film never does presume about the immensely popular asian singers features the superstars actors have their flaws and their characters the movie rarely gets boring and ends where should after jumping about quite bit moon child rather enjoyable humorous times and even very touching definitely worth your time
