1 |text french horror cinema has seen something revival over the last couple years with great films such inside and switchblade romance bursting the scene mal xc3 xa9fique preceded the revival just slightly but stands head and shoulders over most modern horror titles and surely one the best french horror films ever made mal xc3 xa9fique was obviously shot low budget but this made for far more ways than one the originality the film and this turn complimented the excellent writing and acting that ensure the film winner the plot focuses two main ideas prison and black magic the central character man named carr xc3 xa8re sent prison for fraud put cell with three others the quietly insane lassalle body building transvestite marcus and his retarded boyfriend daisy after short while the cell together they stumble upon hiding place the wall that contains old journal after translating part they soon realise its magical powers and realise they may able use break through the prison walls black magic very interesting topic and actually quite surprised that there aren more films based there much scope for things with fair say that mal xc3 xa9fique makes the best assets despite restraints the film never actually feels restrained and manages flow well throughout director eric valette provides great atmosphere for the film the fact that most takes place inside the central prison cell ensures that the film feels very claustrophobic and this immensely benefits the central idea the prisoners wanting use magic break out the cell very easy get behind them often said that the unknown the thing that really frightens people and this film proves that the director ensures that can never really sure exactly what round the corner and this helps ensure that mal xc3 xa9fique actually does manage quite frightening the film memorable for lot reasons outside the central plot the characters are all very interesting their own way and the fact that the book itself almost takes its own character very well done anyone worried that the film won deliver the end won disappointed either the ending both makes sense and manages quite horrifying overall mal xc3 xa9fique truly great horror film and one the best the decade highly recommended viewing
