1 |text the year 1995 when many people talked about the great premiere braveheart mel gibson also saw another very fine yet underrated movie scottish history rob roy although very different film especially due the historical period the story set rob roy has much common not only with marvelous braveheart but also with the very spirit epic movies film that discusses similar themes like fight for dignity courage honor revenge family being key happiness also leads the very bliss scottish highlands where the human soul finds its rest being surrounded all grandeur nature robert roy macgregor liam neeson the main character true hero universal epics sort scottish robin hood who struggles lead his people out oppression imposed cold hearted lords although worsens his situation through the acts has suffer lot two things stay his mind undeniably honor that given himself and love his woman mary macgregor jessica lange that leads him unexpected events except for the interesting content and quite vivid action the movie filled with truly stunning visuals this factor has both with the sets and locations the film well the wardrobe many memorable moments stay the mind any viewer who can allow themselves insight into artistic images for the most splendid scene was the highlands when rob roy tells his boys what honor really means then sends them away and beautifully makes love his woman the scene escapes marguis montrose john hurt the waterfall also worth look stunning visual course there some graphic violence like the duel for instance but don think that this violence would harmful many other modern films its justification like any other epic bloodshed and cruelty those times were really serious and there would point hiding the most disturbing scene for was the rape done rob roy wife the villain the story archibald cunningham tim roth truly disgusting and kids should definitely stay away however all the rest yet there one aspect that made really love this movie the performances all the cast perfect jobs from the leading lian neeson who fits very well the role tall brave strong scottish man the supporting cast brian cox who portrays wicked killearn silent witness terrible acts who feels comfortable with the evil war jessica lange very fine mary macgregor and has some the most beautiful moments the film there chemistry between lange and neeson many their scenes john hurt one the best british actors does terrific job marguis montrose corrupted man for whom money the aim itself achieved any means like that calmness his portrayal but the real villain played tim roth who truly depicts wretched side his character archibald man who mocks love who loves war and who finds true lust rape and slaughter but like any good epic this exceptional evil must find its end and one more aspect the musical score such memorable and sentimental tunes that are bound sound the ears for long the final moment touched tears not only because the beauty conveys but because deeply combined these blissful tunes with the grandeur locations scotland remains the heart its visitor and this movie reminded that permanent effect was second journey scotland rob roy very nice movie very well directed photographed and acted perhaps does not equal braveheart with its spectacular sets and crowds extras battle scenes but fairly long film with much attention placed one very significant feature cinema should have stunning entertainment combined with heartfelt education really enjoyed that film not hesitate call metaphorically highlands entertainment and rate
