ermine any film that attempts serious social commentary without exception the cast summer sam excellent however the acting for the most part uninspired the cast either just going through the motions they have little work with scriptwise additionally there notable miscasting comedian john leguizamo very talented but his vinny character seems stale comedic impersonation john travolta tony manero from saturday night fever and michael badalucco perennial nice guy actor badly miscast serial killer david berkowitz coming across funny rather than frightening the only performance worth paying attention adrien brody the troubled but sincere neighborhood misfit ritchie the brody performance and the typically stylish lee cinematography are this film only virtues out
