1 |text after gorging myself variety seemingly immature movies purchased rental dvds figured that the time was right for little serious drama and who better provide than sam mendes for number reasons american beauty doesn appeal much this film which easily the darkest thing that tom hanks has ever done and probably one the most underrated films the last decade for this not simple gangster tale lifted from its graphic novel origins and simply wonderful watch because and despite usual allergy any film with tom hanks name still can watch big without wanting cat kick glad gave this try because this one those movies that you kick yourself for you miss normally squeaky clean hanks plays michael sullivan devoted family man and father two sons growing during prohibition the early 1930 also professional hit man mob boss john rooney paul newman but has managed keep his job secret from his sons but after his eldest tyler hoechlin witnesses his dad involved mob killing the pair are forced the run john seeks tidy the matter soon father and son are pursued chicago where fellow hit man menacing jude law waiting for them the face reads like pretty standard gangster film but said this isn really about gangsters all about the relationship between father and son thrown together the most tragic circumstances hanks grits teeth superb the tortured man who finds out that everything has its price and little hoechlin also good sullivan son all honesty there not single performance that could single out weaker than the others the cast pretty much faultless the cinematography and costumes and not often praise costumes which recreates the with stunning effect there has been much effort get everything right and pays off spades this could easily have looked rubbish they admit that the early look was difficult put down but doesn and that deserves every bit credit chicago especially looks fantastic lined with hundreds rickety cars from the era and filled with people monochrome suits and hats true time travel even little cgi needed the story also winner offering human face what often seen stereotypical genre movie villain law surprisingly menacing the almost mechanical killer maguire and proves that you don have cagney niro brando play gangster the film decidedly noir ish driving rain and ill lit warehouses predominate but least violence and killing are finally seen have emotional and psychological impact those who perpetrate and those who merely witness such acts the whole thing evocative previous age and previous movies but sweeps away the old and refreshes with modern tale redemption amid the tommy gun shootouts and extortion rackets can feel little slow places especially you used masses gun play movies like most modern audiences like yours truly but sometimes words can speak louder than actions mendes has delivered fine follow his oscar winning debut film which intelligent beautiful watch road perdition may not everyone tastes but this one dvd shall not exchanging anytime soon
1 |text eric stoltz delivers extraordinary performance joel garcia successful young novelist who winds paralyzed and special hospital for the recently disabled after breaking his neck hiking accident while learning cope and adjust with the gravity his new limited physical condition joel befriends slick fast talking charming womanizer raymond amazing wesley snipes and boorish surly racist biker bloss terrific william forsythe who feels threatened the diverse multi ethnic array fellow patients forced share room with joel also receives substantial support from his loyal and loving but married girlfriend anna radiantly played helen hunt but still must come terms with being disabled his own this remarkable movie key triumph its laudably stubborn refusal neither sanitize nor sentimentalize the severity what these men are going through directors neil jimenez who also wrote the thoughtful and insightful script and micheal steinberg relate the story with exceptional taste wit and warmth specifically addressing with disarming candor and matter factness how being handicapped irrevocably alters one lifestyle including and especially your sex life this point most powerfully made striking sequence when joel and anna try and fail make love motel room besides the expected poignancy the film further provides surprising surplus wickedly funny raw earthy humor that highlighted the uproarious sequence with joel and bloss making secret nocturnal expedition strip club the uniformly superb acting qualifies another significant plus stoltz snipes forsythe and hunt are all outstanding with stand out supporting turns grace zabriskie bloss doting amiable mother and elisabeth pena and william allen young compassionate hospital nurses despite the grim subject matter the film ultimately proves very moving positive and uplifting cinematic testament the astonishing strength and durability the human spirit simply wonderful little gem drama
