1 |text french film directors continue amaze with their extraordinary ability simulate the sights and sounds ordinary everyday suburban life this was readily apparent with the release early 2002 emploi temps time out brilliant character study white collar worker descent into melancholy after having been fired from his job the penchant french filmmakers many scenes were shot real streets and public places giving cinema verite feel the story yet emploi temps also possessed elegant look thanks excellent camera work and some stunning location footage most notably swiss mountain retreat running fairly the heels that masterful movie comes another impressive french production jacques audiard gritty crime caper sur mes levres read lips actually tag this film crime caper does disservice because much more than that with the earlier french release incisive character study marginal people using their wits get ahead society that has turned its back them paris construction firm carla shy diminutive young woman sits her desk sequestered area the office that major pathway the xerox machines and restrooms obnoxious coworkers use the front carla desk chat and drop off their half finished styrofoam cups coffee partially deaf carla turns her hearing aids and off will noise becomes bothersome the drone the paper copiers the shrill crying friend baby when her boss calls her into the office suggest that she hire secretarial assistant help her with the work load carla fears she may lose her job the employment office carla lists the specifications she wants for her assistant preferably male she were personals agency should years old and clean cut with extensive computer and filing skills when the agency sends over unkempt menacing looking young man carla both shocked and intrigued they leave the office and have lunch local eatery where carla interviews her prospective assistant when she finds out that has just gotten out prison carla initially wants nothing with paul but has change heart and hires him although she basically kind toward her helper carla now finds herself position authority and possessing newfound sense power paul learns quickly and becomes able worker carla helps paul find temporary place live and even covers for him when his parole officer shows one day the office wondering why paul missed his appointment during one their lunch breaks carla informs paul her hearing deficiency and reveals her ability read lips later when avaricious coworker blatantly takes over project carla has been working furious carla asks paul help seeking revenge the man from here sur mes levres becomes increasingly intense crime drama escalating into some the most violently graphic scenes that have been shown the screen recent years the screenplay borrows elements from hitchcock most notably rear window where carla lip reading talent comes into full play using pair binoculars there teasing again off again sexual attraction between the two protagonists that culminates rather strange homage north northwest but works because the considerable sexual heat that builds slowly between the two stars that being said what one carries away from this movie isn much the similarities classic hitchcock thrillers although those elements are definitely there but the pervasive view modern day city this case paris where life runs the gamut from mundane workdays boozy garish nightlife where sex drugs and laundered money infiltrate the lives several characters unlike hollywood productions this psychological suspense yarn where the people look like the everyday man and woman the street where punch the face groin sounds like sickening thud and where the office place feared hitchcock with the gloves off
