1 |text not quite the timeless masterpiece you would hope would based the acclaim garnered but 1969 midnight cowboy still powerhouse showcase for two young actors just bursting into view the time directed john schlesinger and written waldo salt the movie seems product its time the late 1960 when american films were especially expressionistic but still casts spell because the story comes down themes loneliness and bonding that resonate matter what period the film cinematic influence can still felt the unspoken emotionalism found ang lee brokeback mountain the meandering plot follows joe buck naive young texan who decides move manhattan become stud for hire for rich women full energy but lacking any savvy fails miserably but unwilling concede defeat despite his dwindling finances meets cynical sickly petty thief named ratso rizzo who first sees joe easy pawn the two become dependent one another and rizzo begins manage joe things come head psychedelic drug infested party where joe finally lands paying client meanwhile rizzo becomes sicker and the two set off for florida seek better life this not story that will appeal everyone fact some may still find repellent that hustler and thief are turned into sympathetic figures yet their predicaments feel achingly authentic his first major role jon voight ideally cast brings out joe paper thin bravado and deepening sexual insecurities rizzo dustin hoffman successfully upends his clean post college image from the graduate and immerses himself the personal degradation and glimmering hope that act oddly compatible counterpoint joe the honesty their portrayals complemented schlesinger film treatment which vividly captures the squalor the times square district the time the director also effectively inserts montages flashbacks and fantasy sequences fill the character fragile psyches credit also needs salt for not letting the pervasive cynicism overwhelm the pathos the story the other performances are merely incidental the journeys the main characters including brenda vaccaro the woman joe meets the party sylvia miles blowsy matron john mcgiver religious zealot and barnard hughes lonely out towner the two disc 2006 dvd package contains pristine print transfer the 1994 restoration and informative commentary from producer jerome hellman since unfortunately neither schlesinger nor salt are still living there are three terrific featurettes the second disc look back documentary after midnight reflections classic years later which features comments from hellman hoffman voight and others well clips and related archive footage such voight screen test controversy and acclaim which examines the genesis the movie initial rating and public response the film and tribute the director celebrating schlesinger
