1 |text paul reiser steps away from the standup comedy spotlight write warmly humorous and gently tender story about family what see and what don see what expect and what surprises the thing about folks doesn set any new standards for film but fine little story well told that reminds about the significant bonds that family represents sam kleinman peter falk has been workaholic times pushing his wife muriel olympia dukakis his daughters mackenzie connolly and lydia jordan and his son ben paul reiser into the background one day muriel leaves note that after years marriage she leaving her daughters along with ben wife rachel elizabeth perkins immediately begin the search for her whereabouts leaving the confused and hurt and disgruntle sam sort things out road trip with son ben the road trip becomes time for the two men learn who each other and what they each mean their status father and son and family members sam relaxes for the first time his life and introduces the now workaholic ben the pleasures and fun living the trip comes end with phone call about the whereabouts muriel and why she left and the regrouping the wiser family draws the story warm ending all not what seemed better and well different falk and reiser play off each other like the pros they are but many ways the film belongs the brief moments when olympia dukakis screen reminding that she one our strongest matriarchs film well worth viewing grady harp
