1 |text have admit have always found difficult watch antonioni film from start finish the first try and even for this one ended watching three parts repeated occasions the end realised perhaps was better that way because forced stop thinking the usual terms plot and just enjoy the scenes one one the first part seems lot more fragmentary which not bad thing just requires more effort follow when gets the desert scenes all efforts are repaid full the stunning cinematography only part what really makes all unforgettable how the landscape made into overwhelming presence the silence and vastness the sense sadness and freedom the way fuses and contrasts with the two young characters the desert dead but the same time feels less distant and alien than the urban scenes the first part the dance between the airplane flying over and the girl car makes for series great shots the love scenes the desert are simply beautiful hard imagine this kind approach from film our times there course something very stylish and studied about them but the same time they manage express sense natural spontaneous innocence that very rare these days all feels loose and unscripted thanks also the understated acting but that the result maniacal attention detail and form which comes its climax the series explosions the end really mesmerising spectacle just leaves you awe don really care for some the usual objections boring well yes you want all films follow classic plot development and packed with action twists but then all cinema was like that that would truly dull and sad pretentious maybe but when that kind ambitiousness coupled with actual skills depth and style pretentious compliment the political criticisms make the least sense don see the point approaching film like this with ideological blinders worse patriotic requirements just defeats the purpose perhaps true that like previous commenter remarked antonioni viewed these young hippies and the politics protests and riots with the police with the fascination foreigner but think that adds something rather than detracting from the film not true that hippies did not exist italy the time think the protests like france although they were obviously different from the american counterpart and some ways even more militant but his interest this film was not narrowly political the events seem more like pretext for film whose appeal has universal timeless quality special mention for the fantastic soundtrack amongst other things this film along with easy rider probably one the main earliest precursors the contemporary artsy music video well the concept film soundtrack that would stand its own but unlike the former uses music much more subtle way blending with the landscape rather than the action you want traditional narrative film then don bother you want stunned patient and you won regret
