1 |text the world old school kung movies where revenge pictures came dime dozen took lot for film stand out and even more make fan favorite after all these years what arguably chang cheh finest movie continues hold influence over the hong kong movie industry from the themes loyalty brotherhood and revenge explored john woo who got his start the movie industry working for chang during the heyday heroic bloodshed during the late 1980 more modern movies like man called hero which sports character costume inspired this film the influence has also carried into other areas well from music such the tang clan commercials for sprite and video games such mortal kombat what makes this movie special the plot the surface pretty simple deals with members rogue group known the poison clan who are searching for treasure hidden their sifu all the members the clan have extraordinary kung abilities denoted their animal styles venoms the lizard can climb walls the scorpion has deadly strike etc the twist that since the clan always wears masks not all them known who the others are thus simple plot becomes almost suspense thriller not talking the usual suspects here but far above many other kung movies the time supposedly golden harvest was not too happy with chang script like most his movies they felt was too dark and violent and they actually wanted him add broad comic relief thankfully chang stuck his guns and stayed with his original script which has since has become revered one the best for the films its time not ever completing almost perfect dramatic arc and providing the perfect backbone for the extraordinary action sequences but what really solidifies the movie are the venoms themselves chang cheh hit upon magical formula with the cast not only did gain talented martial artists whose moves competed without the aid wires other special effects put most modern martial artists shame but great actors well the formula proved popular that chang usually had one more the venoms his later movies getting back matters hand most old school movies the actors seem playing out cardboard cutouts but here the actors actually create characters seems that everyone has favorite venom mine philip kwok best known many mad dog from hard boiled lizard and this personal connection the characters that the five deadly venoms generates which makes true classic the genre even you normally not fan old school movies you need check the five deadly venoms out for nothing else see where modern movies got their inspiration from
