1 |text this the first american film successfully adopt the naturalistic style used europeans particularly the french and belgians for least decade and isn about time following three high school girls the crown heights neighborhood brooklyn during the last days their summer break between freshman and sophomore years does what all good art should discovers the universal the particular even though the girls preoccupations are outwardly conventional boys sex popularity money freedom and clothes glimpse how their whole lives are being shaped the universal interface between character and destiny the naturalism whole complete the film breathes stays the moment inhabits real time the story tells itself the medium and its artifacts for once are not the message the film unwaveringly truthfully conveys the childhood perspective its characters does not impose its own adult meanings morals details emerge their own are never pushed and thus seem all the more real and powerful for their understatement even though great pains have been taken capture the authentic social reality crown heights part the largest black ghetto new york city and one the most dangerous violent places the the subject childhood the ghetto not the ghetto itself documentary footage the practice sessions marching band the jackie robinson steppers punctuate the film regular intervals with explosion color movement and sound otherwise the camera stays very close very intimate patient sly and unobtrusive observer the language rich spontaneous the acting transparent some scenes standout such the girls lolling about each revealing her deepest fantasies lanisha confession her acceptance death random violence the most shocking one the deepest scars the ghetto her sharing with her mother her confusion and fear before the stark challenges adult life equally moving and beautifully unsentimentally affirmative social realities are respected not propagandized all three girls are being raised single moms only one lanisha has father active her life and not coincidentally the three she the most emotionally stable and empathetic others and the one with the most self respect two them suffer from asthma disease disproportionately prevalent the inner city gunfire accepted daily occurrence only momentarily interrupts their conversation only one the girls joy feels hope for feels she has control over the future while the other two varying degrees have already accepted despair this far the best dramatic american film seen years see see see
