1 |text walt disney the rookie based the story jim morris former minor league picher who made one the most amazing comebacks sports history ending almost year retirement and making his major league debut 1999 the age the film opens with brief synopsis morris childhood which included series locations his father was military man and even when his family settled for good football crazed texas morris passion for baseball remained strong the childhood segment then jumps ahead about years the adult morris played dennis quaid who now baseball coach and chemistry teacher big lake high school real life was reagan county high school big lake texas mentioned that attempted career baseball player but that didn work out morris team struggling and lectures them about giving their dreams they turn the table him telling him that should try out for major league team several times when pitches them practice they express amazement the speed with which throws morris seems unconvinced but agrees deal with his players which they win district will try out for major league team big lake does win district and adhering his end the deal morris attends tampa bay devil rays try out phenomenally throws miles hour faster than threw during his minor league career and outstanding speed even for major league pitcher after another try out with the team morris offered contract with the devil rays this leaves him with tough decision stay his comfortable life once again pursue his major league dream going through the minor league grind making little money and spending months time away from home and the decision even more agonizing than during his first minor league stint because now has wife and three children morris signs with the devil rays begins the level and moves quickly the aaa level one level below major league baseball but the season winds down the chances him getting called grow increasingly slim for the most part love this movie there are lots great performances and likable characters and easy find yourself really pulling for morris also the movie does great job portraying professional baseball both the major and minor league levels and most all teaches the timeless message holding tight your dreams even when they seem distant and almost impossible achieve still the movie has some flaws while generally accurate exaggerates and even fabricates few things check out http espn com page2 closer 020410 html for some examples also except for one scene which prays with his players the movie completely ignores morris christian faith but considering disney left wing zeal that not surprising presumably lot the exaggerations fabrications were done make the story more dramatic yet the minute documentary morris that included the dvd features some information that makes his story more dramatic but excluded from the movie for example from birth until his family settled texas for good when was morris located times and his initial minor league career ended after four surgeries through which lost half the muscle his left pitching shoulder thus making his throwing mph even more inexplicable fully appreciate and understand the story jim morris good not only watch the rookie but watch the dvd documentary check out the aforementioned link the movie inaccuracies and probably also read morris biography also titled the rookie haven read the book but hope one these days but overall the rookie very good portrayal miraculous story and powerful testament the power dreams and the triumph the common man
