1 |text the beauty this film evidenced the great portrayal the power mother love the exceptional performances the steady execution and the quite innovative script the film tells the story indian woman nandini who lives canada with her husband shekhar and little kid raja all sudden her husband informs her that his family india whom she had not even known troubles and the couple rush india when they get into the village nanadini shocked and terrified witness very wild rural culture shekhar family ruled his cruel highly cynical and merciless father narasimha lives poor and highly violent lifestyle which full murder and terror and where women are subservient and helpless nandini starts nagging shekhar return home but soon killed his father enemies when she wants leave narasimha refuses let her take raja back india here starts the intense struggle which can called nandini narasimha india not presented particularly positive light this film but only shows very tiny minority its rural areas may even correct the portrayal view fair and not one sided because the positive side also presented extent such horrifying sight could shown film about any country the world the locations are amazing the music wonderful and krishna vamshi direction aided very effective cinematography and good editing one thing that must noted the very ear pleasing background score ismail darbar beautiful the characters are very well defined though get see both their bright and dark sides different portions the film portrayed realistically throughout the film flows well and interesting and fairly entertaining watch its dialogues are superb and intelligently written and although the shocking proceedings can very disturbing some points great deal positive moments manage relieve the tension the film biggest strength the performances karisma kapoor breathtaking and very believable nandini her ability strike balance between vulnerability and unrestrained emotion simply incredible she displays much intensity impulsiveness anguish and determination the mother who wants get her son back that this little kid seems her own son her outbreaks while facing off nana patekar which are like volcanic eruptions show how the simplest women can become tigress when comes her child after fiza this her most powerful performance one the greatest actors indian cinema has seen nana patekar indescribable narasimha manages hateful narasimha yet admirable the actor who plays him patekar displays cruelty wittiness and even humanity with total conviction outstanding another great performance comes unsurprisingly from india most underrated actress deepti naval who sensitises her character perfection sanjay kapoor just adequate and shahrukh khan provides great comic relief anyway watch shakti could have been better but definitely must watch
