1 |text sigh xc2 x85 sincerely wonder why all the acclaimed and supposedly profound movie critics hold such grudge against director michael winner surely isn the avatar subtlety his films are practically always hard handed and confronting but what they awesomely entertaining his most famous action movies like the first three entries the death wish series for example are easy targets clobber down because they allegedly glorify violence and the personal use shotguns but even when winner takes far more mature cinema genres xc2 x96 like the religious horrors the sentinel for example xc2 x96 doesn stand chance with any the critics the sentinel generated some controversy and infuriated several people upon its release when leaked that michael winner cast genuinely malformed and handicapped people portray the creatures attempting cross the gateways between hell and earth pretty much the exact same controversy caused todd browning masterpiece and landmark horror cinema freaks remain banned and unseen for over thirty years and why just because certain prudish and easily offended people who shouldn watch the movie the first place claim unethical thing don suppose michael winner todd browning held these people gunpoint forced them appear their films what gives the right feel embarrassed their place another major reason why critics didn warmly welcome the sentinel because jeffrey konvitz novel xc2 x96 and thus michael winner screenplay xc2 x96 hugely derivative other contemporary but far more successful religiously themed horror stories and thus according the merciless pens horror critics little more than pure plagiarism admittedly the sentinel borrows multiple substantial elements from rosemary baby the omen and the exorcist but let face cinema largely thrives stolen formulas and imitating success stories you overlook the slightly unoriginal concept and all fairness handful thoroughly confusing and unnecessary sub plots the sentinel honestly still remains uniquely atmospheric and often downright petrifying horror highlight with impressive ensemble cast and nightmarish imagery you not likely forget easy alison parker ravishing model with some unprocessed mental traumas moves into stunning brownstone apartment brooklyn deeply against the will her boyfriend michael who proposed wed her several times already alison physical existence and especially her mental condition drastically alter shortly after and the ominous apartment appears the root all misery she meets eccentric neighbors and attends birthday parties for their cats even though the landlady claims she and blind priest are the only tenants she frequently faints during her work assignments and has truly creepy visions her bastard father and the night she attempted commit suicide slowly becomes clear that alison got chosen serve higher supernatural purpose inside this apartment building but simultaneously malignant forces try and prevent this truly regrettable how the promotional taglines and even brief synopsis the back the dvd immediately reveal that alison brownstone apartment the earth gateway hell itself and she the chosen one guard because the film script only slowly builds towards this shocking revelation for nearly minutes and throughout some sadly tedious and overlong sequences michael winner successfully maintains the impression that alison own mind playing tricks with her and that the involvement the catholic church and her fianc xc3 xa9e odd behavior are strictly red herrings multiple the horrific scenes come pretty close being genius like alison flashback her first acquaintance with the priest upstairs the whole climax with the controversial guest appearances mentioned here above literally perplexing showcase pure terror and easily one the most unforgettable and nail biting denouements ever witnessed the cast michael winner managed gather deeply impressive especially considering the sentinel still remains legitimate horror movie and this genre isn the most popular among prominent actors but course you also have put the cast listing little into perspective with such extended cast obviously several the roles the film are little more than cameos martin balsam and john carradine for example only appear screen for couple minutes all together several others like christopher walken jeff goldblum beverly angelo and tom berenger perhaps add lot fame the movie nowadays but back when was released they were still too unknown order attract curious viewers personal pick for best performances burgess meredith the uncanny neighbor and eli wallach the satirical police inspector the relatively unknown cristina raines does admirable job carrying the film and chris sarandon neatly back her even though sports ridiculous mustache humble opinion the sentinel marvelously entertaining and frightening horror movie and most definitely must see for true genre fanatics
