1 |text the first side story the universal century gundam universe presents refreshing new look the war between earth and the space colonies the focus longer small group individuals who would play pivotal roles the conflict but the everyday civilian population and how the war seen through their eyes the story does contain some gundam staples its premise being the attempts zeon squad capture experimental gundam but the execution the plot that made this show interesting watch this series focuses the experiences young boy named alfred and the relationship between his neighbor christina mckenzie who secretly federation pilot and newbie zeon pilot named bernie wiseman alfred develops sort brotherly love for bernie while our young zeon pilot also falls for christina war the pocket proves that you not need sweeping epic tale about special individuals make for good war story there are uber ace pilots large scale fleet battles seen here this short episode ova focuses lot more character emotional drama over other themes like politics philosophy and love how realistically portrayed the characters are alfred your typical everyday kid who plays violent computer games and thinks the armed forces cool then given crash course the horrible realities war the unlikely friendship and bonding between bernie and christina each not knowing the fact that they are soldiers different sides the war played very real without going overboard with the romance drama stuff same goes for the endearing relationship between alfred and bernie that being said would not want spoil much the story here but makes whole lot more heart wrenching watch the tragedies that unfold the show moves along all the way its emotionally devastating twist ending despite its lack action this show never falls into the category boring the characters are just that engaging enough carry the whole show not worry there are number mobile suit action scenes scattered here and there each are beautifully animated level that surpasses that ova and are sure satisfy the craving for some mandatory mobile suit battles gundam series normally watching anime japanese english would leave personal preference but this case strongly recommend the english voice track over the japanese one not only the characters whom all except alfred are caucasian sound more believable english but the performances the english voice cast are par and even surpass the japanese one instilling each character with such realistic emotions and intonations that they sound just the acting some live action dramas short this show does not try impress the audience what does conveys numerous heartwarming themes that hit closest home especially the death innocence the battlefield and the horrors war through the eyes child truly moving little story that deserves more credit than being given
