1 |text the house that dripped blood the third series seven amicus horror anthologies the monster club included part the series this would make eight movies although that movie very different from the others look upon the amicus anthologies with great memories used love them when was teens feelings for them today are just strong spent many years trying track down this movie the synopses the stories was appealing that went far paying substantial amount for when eventually found copy great though the movie did feel sense disappointment when finally saw wasn quite good was led believe whilst better than its two predecessors nowhere near good its four successors shall demonstrate the linking story sees john bennett police inspector tracking down missing person who lives mysterious old house his journey begins the local police station where learns the stories previous occupants the linking story later sees him visiting the estate agent who sold the house whilst this linking story seems enticing paper flat and lifeless practice and easily the weakest any amicus anthology couldn help but get the feeling that john bennett poor man version donald pleasance ian hendry would much rather have seen one the two aforementioned actors his role could have even had both here one the police inspector and another the estate agent they could and believe would have brought this weak element the movie life much better the movie contains four stories each which focuses inhabitant the house the first story sees denholm elliott writer crime stories absorbed into exciting story about strangler even going far drawing sketch aid his writing soon after begins seeing visions his own creation some excellent direction peter duffell particularly with the choice camera angles helps detract from the restrained script elliott performance superb the tormented writer and also helps elevate the story the story ends with semi twist but couldn help get the sense script which didn allow live its potential the second story sees peter cushing move into the house lonely man who still pining for beautiful young woman who once jilted him and who keeps picture cushing performance really brings this emotionally moving story life helped the director who chooses include continual focus cushing loneliness this taken further with great hallucination scene that helps see inside cushing mind anyway cushing sees figure nearby wax museum that looks just like his girl naturally his obsession grows but this seemingly romantic story has disturbing twist the end joss ackland plays cushing rival but his performance massively overshadowed the late great peter cushing the third story and easily the best sees christopher lee favourite horror actor all time move into the house with his daughter lee gives one his perfect ice cold performances here shows love attention for his daughter all even brings school governess educate her the governess played nyree dawn porter another her superb performances tries find out what wrong without giving too much away can reveal that witchcraft plays role christopher lee presence truly electrifying every scene chloe franks deserves special recognition for her massively underrated performance the little girl who easily the creepiest character the whole movie the movie worth seeing even for the sake seeing just this one story the final story played almost entirely for laughs but certainly does entertain and that what matters jon pertwee plays horror movie actor who moves into the house very dissatisfied the approach his producers take movies seeing everything cheap and fake particularly the costumes decides buy authentic cloak for his latest vampire role geoffrey bayldon has excellent cameo dealer who sells pertwee ancient cloak when pertwee puts the cloak starts developing fangs and basically transforming into vampire pertwee performance has seen believed truly hilarious ingrid pitt also this story but her talent wasted role that should have been much larger the linking story finishes with loose connection the final story this particularly fitting since the inspector was looking for pertwee and naturally decides visit the house the rest you able work out for yourself weak the linking story does have decent somewhat unintentionally comical ending convinced that the blame for the shortcomings what should have been truly magnificent movie doesn lie with peter duffell the director who really does his best with what got think the script was just too restrained and lacking the ambition that can found the four later movies overall the house that dripped blood despite its flaws must see for fans the amicus anthologies fans other amicus movies fans portmanteau horror movies summary provides the movie with enough appeal your eyes check out you enjoy
