 zarustica for the whole show who gives scratchy but still malevolent turn well the expected evil laughter anthony cruise kashue the other hand too weary and takes about five episodes find his stride oliver gregory probably the most effective orson especially during his final dramatic scenes aside from lisa ortiz deedlit karen smith shiris john knox ashram and muscari slayn the dub best voices come from some the newer characters including crispin freeman spark maar garrack episodes roxanne beck little neese meg frances who voices pirotess the oav but also voices ryna with vulnerability and sassiness well karla and especially angora deb who steals every scene she leaf the half elf the rest the cast isn terrible any means but little more uneven than the oav dub some are all right aldonova greevus while others are lackluster hobb palace guards dragons etc and few were awful particular prince reona too harsh and monotone for fighter justice fact the lack aural continuity some cast members get new voices for some unexplained reason the time get some the later episodes one the problems the dub others include less memorable and more awkward sounding dialogue uneven synchronization and finally apologize advance the fans this the lodoss island segments these offbeat super deformed interludes the end each episode will either amuse drive you batty admittingly first found them major nuisance but they sorta grew after while besides there are some showstoppingly hilarious lines such king kashue and this cashew really quite nut these flaws rank the dub for chronicles just notch just below that for the ova resulting uneven english track summed best one wonders the japanese language track the preferred listening choice well guess what the japanese version has its good and bad points too while some voices are less annoying than the english language track found others less appealing than the english equivalents particular the actress who does deedlit nowhere nearly good lisa ortiz yumi tohma plus should mention that the japanese cast not the same the ova because the series was made seven years after the original all but one sho hayami the cast members are replaced new ones although they respectably good job may major annoyance for those who were used the japanese ova cast shows that not everything japanese better than english despite its flaws chronicles the heroic knight still fine series which deserves hold its own ground its not without its rough spots and doesn always live its predecessor yet there enough good points counter the bad making this moderately enjoyable fantasy anime
