1 |text thirty years after its initial release the third version star born finally comes dvd package that should please the most devoted fans barbra streisand that would include since just saw her concert singing among other numbers the feminist anthem woman the moon from this 1976 film easy dismiss the movie career polarizing story such sturdy pile hollywood style clich xc3 xa9s that variations exist other films including streisand own funny girl this time reset the then contemporary music scene the timeworn plot follows self destructive rock star john norman howard his deep dive career descent just meets club singer esther hoffman who awaiting her big break troubles dog their courtship from the outset john norman both names please responds grasping fans and bloodless djs with random acts violence from which inexplicably escapes prosecution john norman esther represents his last shot happiness and turn she drawn the innately decent creative musician underneath the xc3 xa7ade the movie most pivotal scene gives esther her big break benefit concert and her career takes off inevitably can handle the failure his career light her meteoric success and you are familiar with any version this story you know the rest directed frank pierson although streisand budding directorial talents are obviously display the film still manages draw even though know shamelessly contrived and manipulative still has certain emotional resonance despite its numerous flaws although streisand her prime seems like the ideal choice play rising singing star her screen persona simply too strong and predefined play esther credibly the same can said for her performing style since the script seems make allowances for her softer adult contemporary oriented material accepted within the otherwise hardened world arena rock from the moment she pops her head the middle the oreos she can help but come across established star can forgive the lapse simply because she unparalleled vocal talent but what becomes less forgiving how she makes esther more strident than poignant when john norman woes become overwhelming this creates oddly discomfiting dynamic the last part the film when becomes less about what caused the climactic event than esther response this capped off uninterrupted eight minute close her memorial performance great except when she regrettably mimics john norman style toward the end kristofferson the other hand gives superb performance throughout managing level honesty that grounds the film and makes palpable his concurrent feelings love pride and resentment toward esther makes his vodka soaked onstage growling work within this context otherwise what always strikes strange about this version how all the supporting characters are relegated the background they didn exist unless they were interacting with the two principals the only ones who register are paul mazursky john norman level headed manager brian and gary busey his cynical band manager bobbie veteran cameraman robert surtees provides nice burnish the cinematography though level graininess persists the print big seller its day the soundtrack hodgepodge different styles from the 1970 some songs still quite good everything woman the moon watch closely now some that have moved kitsch queen bee kenny loggins believe love and course the inescapable evergreen the print transfer the 2006 dvd clean and the sound gratefully crisp thanks digital remastering streisand participation the chief lure the extras beginning with her feature length commentary she gives insightful information about the genesis the film the casting and the reportedly troubled production she also refreshingly candid about the megalomania jon peters her hairdresser boyfriend who became the movie producer and her dissatisfaction with pierson director just wish she could have provided more scene specific comments that directly relate what screen she also tends repeat the same anecdotes when the mood strikes her gets tiring hear for the third time how the person playing the chauffeur was friend peters think having second commentator could have drawn out other nuggets from her there wardrobe test reel that shows some amusing 1970 clothes especially kristofferson mixed fabric poncho and orange polyester shirt there are also twelve deleted scenes included with streisand optional commentary one comic bread baking scene which reminded how much like streisand farcical comedies another extended scene which she plays evergreen the guitar front awestruck kristofferson who then falls asleep the most interesting alternate take the musical finale incorporating fast cuts which agree with streisand should have been used fittingly the theatrical trailers for all three versions star born are also included
