1 |text had watched snippets from this kid but while purchased blue underground set immediately due its being limited edition only now did fit viewing schedule and that mainly because bakshi american pop 1981 just turned late night italian see review that film below anyway found the film quite good sword and sorcery animated epic with especially impressive looking backdrops the rather awkward rotoscoped characters were admittedly less with rousing derivative score the plot again wasn exactly original but proved undeniably engaging juvenile level and the leading characters well enough developed especially interesting the villainous ice lord nekron and the enigmatic warrior darkwolf the hero and heroine however are rather bland stereotypes but one can hardly complain when bakshi and frazetta depict the girl well endowed her bra could torn off any second and half naked boot her tiny panties are forever disappearing her ass still clearly action oriented piece and certainly delivers this front that involving darkwolf being particularly savage the final showdown though brief also nicely handled and sees our heroes astride pterodactyls assaulting the villains lair inside cave the long run apart from the afore mentioned frazetta backdrops the main appeal this movie for now its nostalgia factor transported back childhood days watching not just films like conan the barbarian 1982 and the beastmaster 1982 but also animated series such blackstar 1981 and man and the masters the universe 1983 for the accompanying the making fire and ice mark bakshi 1982 vintage featurette the sword and sorcery animated film which only available via the washed out vhs print owned ralph bakshi himself goes into some detail about the rotoscope technique and also shows several instances live action performances studio segments from the script which would then traced blended with the backgrounds and filmed still having watched several such behind the scenes featurettes the art animation the disney tins and the looney tunes sets for instance doesn make for very compelling piece
