idered treason south africa and that could have resulted woods meeting fate similar that biko the real donald woods and his wife acted consultants this film denzel washington only the film for the first hour and was disappointed with that was expecting see him for the entire movie but was amazing steve biko and captured his personality from what read really well and his accent sounded perfect his performance earned him oscar nomination for best supporting actor kevin kline delivers excellent and thought evoking performance donald woods and penelope wilton excellent his wife wendy filming took place zimbabwe needless say problems arose when they tried film south africa while south africa the south african gestapo followed the film crew everywhere they got the bad vibes and they pulled out and went neighbouring zimbabwe instead despite everything and the fact that the apartheid didn end til seven years later cry freedom wasn banned south africa but cinemas showing the movie received bomb threats richard attenborough brings the horrors the apartheid the screen with extreme force and determination doesn hold back the end the movie when showing what was supposed peaceful protest students shantytown turns into massacre when police open fire them the film ends with the names all the anti apartheid movers who died prison and the explanations for their deaths many had explanation quite few were epilepsy which hard believe and many more either fell from the top the stairs were suicide from hanging one will ever know what really happened them but think fair say that none these men died their own hands but the hands others more precise the hands the police cry freedom must see movie for portrayal and story steve biko also searing and devastating portrayal beautiful land divided and the hellish grips racial segregation and violence
