1 |text this movie rates one all time favourite top movies many people seeing for the first time and knowing little about many the themes the movie probably won understand why find enthralling will try explain the movie very rich historical detail and cultural insights and while has few minor anachronisms they are completely forgivable the story retelling the famous duel between the monk benkei and the young prince yoshitsune gojo bridge during the fight according legend yoshitsune bests benkei and the monk becomes the prince loyal retainer this movie revision that story however and involves war dark prophecy and political maneuvering one the main themes the movie mappo which the prophecy the buddha that after 1000 years his teachings would fail and the world would fall into chaos was believed heian japan after the eruption fuji and the civil war between the taira heike and the minamoto genji that the world would fall into anarchy and everything would collapse time demons next you have the way which the movie resolves the issue yoshitsune sword training the tenku raven goblins karuma defeated clans often escaped into the mountains and disguised themselves demons scare the locals off this said where ninja clans began historically yoshitsune depiction gojo nicely accommodates all this then there benkei and the various strains buddhism depicted including lot esoteric buddhism the shingon sect these are all depicted quite accurately and just add little extra the movie manages convey the power meditation and energy way that makes integral the story uses magic realism add extra dimension the film but does such way make tactical and menacing all all filled with fascinating tidbits and rings surprisingly true life for the period the scenery and the costuming are also completely unmissable and very authentic the soundtrack great very brooding and ominous also thought that the actual acting performances were surprisingly good benkei great brooding anti hero shanao yoshitsune depicted young man testing his limits and growing increasingly drunk his own power and tetsukichi the scavenging sword smith makes for and interesting depiction the common man and his less than flattering opinion the killers who fancy themselves his social betters the plot see why good really suggest you dig old book japanese history and see how this retelling turns almost lighthearted robin hood little john story into gory tale intrigue violence and infernal karma
