-1 |text creepshow little more than pale imitation the original designed with little purpose other than cash the name the previous film even amplifies the flaws its predecessor which was often predictable and heavy handed still the first time around there were enough thrills make for periodic lulls resulting uneven but overall fairly entertaining effort the sequel has few worthwhile moments the transparency the stories are even more apparent once while delivers but most the time just lingers there the original all the stories revolve around the common theme revenge and just desserts wooden indian comes life wreaking vengeance upon the killers its owner teenagers are devoured aquatic monster hitchhiker returns from the dead pursue careless motorist none these premises are inherently bad themselves but they are utterly lacking inspiration there are few surprises and scares this textbook example unmotivated the numbers filmmaking doesn help that this cheap looking movie suffers from flat directorial style although honest there wasn much work with the end the second story comes off best but not much for the most part the performances are okay best george kennedy the ill fated general store owner does adequate not particularly inspired job dorothy lamour the other hand quite good the guilt ridden motorist evoking sympathy for her plight despite the predictable redundant material however most the characters are pretty thin overall one would think that creepshow would have turned out better george romero who directed the original returned pen the screenplay based more stephen king stories makeup effects artist tom savini turns some good gory work why the film letdown guess romero didn really want make second film but was forced for financial reasons was decade horror sequels clones rip offs and whatnot this one was certainly inevitable can imagine the guy writing the script hurry picking his paycheck and running off guess had what was necessary get his own projects financed can blame him rating out released new world pictures
