1 |text the traditional western synonymous with wide open spaces clearcut morality inevitable storylines the optimistic faith hero ability shape his own destiny escape his past these qualities reflect directly the american sense self the self shaping dream the pushing boundaries and frontiers which why the genre still alluded opportunistic politicians with some noble exceptions wellman hawks the western was healthily free neuroses real anxiety anthony mann changed all that forever and this first foray into the genre one the most violent vivid complex not say exciting westerns ever made the traditional western depends hero who exemplifies rugged wholesomeness whatever misfortunes may have had the past supporter order and right who dominates the film removes its obstacles restores harmony effect and obvious villain who often ironically drives the plot forces the hero into certain actions the difference between the two often delineated mythically simple the wearing white black hats mann background was film noir genre antithetical wide open spaces and optimism noir was neurotically charged focusing the dissolution unstable protagonist where morality blurred the hero often the villain trapped interior labyrinth his own making passive victim destiny noir about regress not progress the interrogating and denying modes and signs representation not the creation and confirmation them winchester fraught with noir anxiety noir often considered psychological genre visualising the traumas its protagonist head does this too and all the more disturbing that that protagonist lovely homespun jimmy stewart initiating here his great run difficult films with mann and hitchcock many ways good natured and sweet representing right and trying restore disruptions the natural order also near lunatic who will stop nothing achieve murderous revenge whose relentless quest mirrors ethan edwards the searchers its inhuman persistance whose human instincts are frayed this quest and whose bursts violence are genuinely terrifying witness noir his anxiety has psychological base unlike most healthy heroes who have outgrown symbolically killed their fathers mcadam father was killed before could complete the process his chasing his brother less moral revenge than anguished protest against stunted growth the climactic shoot out not cathartic mcadam staggers back into normal society like just witnessed some the world most ghastly horrors what most unsettling about the film that not really about hero villain all but inanimate piece weoponry that drives the action opens with the gun the title privileged display behind glass window while its admirers are trapped squashed undifferentiated framed admiring outside throughout the film human power reduced the most arbitrary signifiers names change lin and dutch mime shooting each other because they guns quests lose their moral vitality and their practitioners veer close madness armies have ask for help from confederate strangers fight battles man becomes worthy respect only when mentions his name another man revealed coward when abandons his fiancee the indians the gun retains its prestige power wholeness not the revenge plot which drives the film but the story the gun this wrenches the film out conventional expectations and creates eerie alienating modern feel become caught the revenge plot that when follow with the gun another plot entirely feel slightly bewildered this emphasis the gun symbol potent masculinity actually allows for critique that masculinity revealing pointless elaborate rituals the expense society and order brute capitalist greed murderous indian traders who defraud both seller and enemy cowards psychotic killers before returning its true owner broken hero thoroughly compromised who has become murderous the murderer seeks the gun never imprinted with the name its owner not only because there fixed owner but because there fixed masculinity insight anathema the traditional western brilliantly invokes western myths wyatt earp dodge city the cavalry the civil war the wide open west only undermine them earp has inflated reputation that all name but never proven dodge city safer against outlaws than anywhere else the cavalry inept custer has just lost little big horn and the bitter feud the war shown irrelevant the myth the open west site for very closed inescapable circular plot which traps its characters refuses allow them shape their destiny but allowing shape them the old john ford silhouette riders vast mountain reprised but signals here not progress but repetition and circularity but for all its deconstruction the film also tangibly vivid way few westerns ever achieve mann incisive technique intrudes his camera crucial positions alternating revealing distance with intense examination making the saloon doors and stagecoaches seem thrillingly alive and lived
