1 |text approach films about talking animals with care for every wonderful one like babe you get equally poor one like the dreadful remake homeward bound the incredible journey the case cats dogs you have great idea for film not living its potential when heard about paulie the premise wisecracking parrot didn exactly fill with confidence but found the film pleasant surprise and manages sneak its way into your heart without you realising russian janitor misha vilyenkov tony shaloub gets job research laboratory one day hears singing coming from the basement and when investigates finds parrot its cage singing its little heart out misha becomes fascinated with the bird especially when turns out the parrot can not only sing can talk and not few phrases either its parrot you can actually make conversation with the parrot called paulie voiced jay mohr and recognises fellow castaway misha wondering how this world the wise bird ended dusty basement misha convinces paulie tell him his life story which all began when was baby and the care marie five year old girl with stutter the two them became birds feather bad pun when marie parents became concerned about her close friendship with bird they considered sending him away and they finally did after marie nearly injured herself fall after teaching paulie fly desperate reunited with her paulie begins long journey across america which includes diverse number new owners flying great distances and even ending behind bars cage that paulie was one number talking animal films released dreamworks the late 90s and although wasn afforded the same recognition box office success babe paulie succeeds quite few levels and occasional work striking intelligence jay mohr stand style acting well suited the part paulie never plays the part too smug even bit smart aleck paulie worldly but also naive his way because lived rather sheltered life with marie when taken away has fend for himself for the first time and when falls into the hands different owners they make promises paulie reunite him with marie which believes only for those promises broken time and again paulie admittedly little episodic follows the eclectic people paulie ends with and how slowly gets brought closer and closer marie first winds pawn shop where adopted ivy gena rowlands kindly woman who teaches him the meaning manners she sympathises with paulie situation and drives across america find marie paulie occasionally very touching film his scenes with ivy are some the best wonderful moments paulie perched her shoulder singing tom jones numbers the way she instills him the need for hope great and some the dialogue quite well written and even thought provoking there are things life you put off because you think you gonna them later but the real thing ivy taught you gotta live like there may not later the scene where ivy passes away route leaving paulie all alone very heart rending moment and the sequence where plucks the courage fly for the first time across the grand canyon soaring majestically such beautifully composed scene stays with you for hours after the film over despite the occasional sad moment there are plenty laughs had paulie falls with group performing parrots spanish outdoor restaurant the animatronic effects here are really excellent four birds perfectly choreographed dance number and paulie even gets have romance which dashed when falls with petty thief played mohr well that may the only complaint have soon you get comfortable with one situation the film then moves paulie another the scene where paulie taught steal money from atm machines funny but little disturbing too amazed dreamworks were granted the chance include such scene kids film and paulie diamond robbery very mission impossible caught the act and shipped off the lab for animal testing where remained ever since the story finally comes full circle the lab where misha vows help paulie course they find marie but the final revelation scene such shocking intensity was left numb for several minutes paulie may never get the longevity babe has but believe its equally brilliant film the same laughs the same flawless effects and the same surprising intelligence minor gem
